window.AKK_FAKE_HEIRESS_THOUGHTS_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_FAKE_HEIRESS_THOUGHTS_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":201,"title":"Chapter 201: Did You Have a Fight with Shen Huaichu","paragraphs":["\"Jing Yi, it's not that I don't trust you, it's that I don't trust myself.\"","If I can't even show up at the racetrack, then I certainly have no place in your choices...","...","Once you figure one thing out, everything else starts to make sense.","Jing Yi looked up at Shen Huaichu, his eyes red but not shedding tears.","She could feel that Shen Huaichu loved her deeply.","Deeply enough to endure the pain just to stay by her side; deeply enough to blame himself first whenever she raised a concern; deeply enough to bury all his emotions inside.","How could she not love someone like Shen Huaichu...","But precisely because of this, she clearly understood that Shen Huaichu's happiness was never truly relaxed.","And neither was hers.","During that period, they seemed to share a mutual understanding and avoided this issue.","Yet this issue was one that couldn't be sidestepped.","For a moment, Jing Yi felt an overwhelming sadness. She had thought that being together would bring them joy and happiness.","Because she wanted Shen Huaichu to feel happiness and joy, but what she seemed to bring him was only endless worry and fear.","The air around them seemed to freeze, and Shen Huaichu felt as if he had been doused from head to toe in icy water.","He gripped Jing Yi's hand tightly, as if letting go would mean losing her forever.","He stared into Jing Yi's eyes, which were slightly red, showing both unease and reluctance. Even his usually cold and detached voice had become hoarse.","He murmured, \"If you don't want me to go, I won't go.\" His voice carried a hint of pleading, \"Okay?\"","Jing Yi gently shook her head, feeling a pang of heartache seeing him like this. Her chest felt heavy, as if something was pressing down on her, making it hard to breathe.","\"It's not about that. Let's both calm down for a few days, okay?\"","Shen Huaichu gazed into Jing Yi's almond-shaped eyes, his own eyes slightly red but filled with seriousness.","He knew that this time, Jing Yi wouldn't let him off easily...","His back slightly bent, as if accepting his fate.","\"...Okay.\"","Shen Huaichu and Jing Yi had a falling out, and the Jing family found out about it the next day.","Lin Ruiqing and others were worried, but seeing Jing Yi eating her meals as usual, they couldn't detect any sadness in her.","That night, Jing Zejun quietly slipped into Jing Yi's bedroom. She was curled up on the sofa watching a movie. Seeing her come in, Jing Yi said, \"Junjun, come watch the movie with me.\"","Jing Zejun sat down beside Jing Yi, occasionally sneaking glances at her.","The frequency of these glances was so high that Jing Yi couldn't ignore them, and she chuckled, \"Are you here to watch the movie, or to watch me?\"","Of course, it was to watch her!","Jing Zejun turned to face Jing Yi, pulling her hand and asking seriously, \"Did you have a fight with Shen Huaichu?\"","【So that's what it is? The news spread pretty fast.】","\"We just had some disagreements.\"","【As for fighting, Shen Huaichu doesn't seem like the type to argue. He usually just goes along with whatever is said.】","Jing Zejun looked at Jing Yi, her eyes filled with concern, \"Just disagreements? But I feel like you're a bit sad.\"","During this time, Jing Yi seemed the same as usual, but Jing Zejun could sense that she must be very unhappy.","Jing Yi sighed, looking at the two figures leaning on each other in the movie, \"Junjun, it seems like dating isn't as easy as I thought.\" Even just dealing with two people, everything was a mess.","They clearly love each other, so why is it so difficult to be together?","Jing Yi stared at the screen, her thoughts drifting, \"Why is he so stubborn? If he had just listened and not come that day, nothing would have happened, right?\"","She was talking about the time Shen Huaichu came to watch her race.","\"He insisted on coming, and now he's uncomfortable, and he's upset with me. His heart must be troubled too.\"","That day, he was right behind her, but Jing Yi didn't dare to look back. She knew she would have given in if she had.","\"Before that, he insisted on coming to the racetrack as some kind of mascot. Why couldn't we meet elsewhere? What was the point of meeting at the racetrack?\"","How could she not be afraid? She was afraid of getting hurt, afraid that Shen Huaichu would worry even more about her.","\"But he's also a bit too much. He promised to trust me before, and now he's changed so quickly. Men just can't be relied on!\"","Worry is a form of love, and so is trust.","Jing Yi's eyes gradually reddened, a sourness welling up in her heart. She leaned on Jing Zejun's shoulder, trying to hide her tears, but they uncontrollably slipped down her cheeks.","Jing Zejun quietly listened to Jing Yi's words, though they were disjointed, she still understood the gist of it.","She gently patted Jing Yi, offering silent comfort.","She had thought there might be some distance between Shen Huaichu and Jing Yi, but she hadn't expected it to be so vast.","When the slight tremor in Jing Yi's shoulders stopped, Jing Zejun softly asked, \"So, what are you going to do?\"","It seemed like an impossible dilemma.","Jing Yi shook her head, continuing to rest on her shoulder, her voice hoarse, \"I don't know. I told him we should both calm down for a few days.\"","Although she said that, Jing Yi knew deep down that there were only two options, and it would likely come down to her giving up.","Jing Zejun's heart skipped a beat. She didn't dare to ask what Jing Yi was planning to give up.","Was it Shen Huaichu, or was it racing...","...","Downstairs, Jing Zeqian paced back and forth restlessly.","Lin Ruiqing, though also worried about Jing Yi's situation, found Jing Zeqian's behavior quite annoying.","\"Xiao Qian, can you calm down a bit?\"","Jing Zeqian finally stopped, but his brows remained tightly furrowed, \"If it were up to me, I'd just drag Shen Huaichu out and interrogate him.\"","If necessary, I'd even resort to some unconventional methods, like a sack!","Jing Zeyou glanced at him, then went back to his work, while Jing Beicheng watched the news, not moving an inch.","Lin Ruiqing couldn't help but roll her eyes.","After all, he was her son, so Lin Ruiqing asked, \"What do you think you're going to achieve by finding out why they're arguing?\"","Jing Zeqian widened his eyes, \"Of course, to resolve the conflict!\"","Lin Ruiqing retorted, \"You, a single man, should stay out of this. You'll only make things worse.\" Jing Zeqian was unconvinced. Everyone says that outsiders see more of the game, and he was the most clear-sighted!","Most likely, it was Shen Huaichu who made Jing Yi angry! A good beating would solve everything!","Jing Zeyou, typing away on his keyboard, said coolly, \"No private vendettas allowed.\" He had every reason to suspect that this was Jing Zeqian's personal idea.","Jing Zeqian paused, well, there was a bit of personal grievance involved, but overall, it was to avenge Jing Yi!","Lin Ruiqing also found it a bit ridiculous, \"Alright, let the young couple handle it themselves. Don't meddle.\"","Her son's plans sounded so unreliable just hearing them.","Jing Zeqian slumped back onto the sofa, his eyes showing a melancholy that no one understood.","He looked upstairs, his eyes filled with worry."]},{"number":202,"title":"Chapter 202: Racing Accident","paragraphs":["Jing Yi looked at her silent phone and muttered to herself in a low voice, \"I told you not to come, but you can't even send a message, can you?\"","\"Yiyi.\"","Jing Yi quickly put her phone away and smiled at the person approaching.","\"Big Brother.\"","Jing Zeyou noticed Jing Yi's evasive action but smiled without pointing it out. \"The coach is asking you to get ready.\" Jing Yi nodded hurriedly, \"Okay, I'm on it!\"","Jing Zeyou watched her retreating figure, his eyes filled with worry. Was his non-involvement really the right choice?","It was impossible for Jing Zeyou to have foreseen the current situation between Jing Yi and Shen Huaichu, but it was indeed a concern of his.","Jing Zeyou had thoroughly investigated the car accident Shen Huaichu was involved in years ago, along with his recent circumstances. To be honest, the situation was far from optimistic, especially since Jing Yi was a race car driver.","Jing Zeyou couldn't help but sigh and followed her with measured steps.","At the Shanchi Racing Track, the noisy stands were packed with people, clearly showing great interest in this public race, or perhaps in Jing Yi, who had won the station championship.","It was just an exhibition race, and Jing Yi hadn't planned to show off. A simple appearance would have been enough, but then she spotted a familiar face.","Song Yuanye? Even after all that exposure, does this guy still dare to show up?","Jing Yi frowned slightly, somewhat surprised to see him here.","Recalling the hot search situation Shen Xi had mentioned to her earlier, Jing Yi couldn't help but complain, the entertainment industry really doesn't discriminate against anything.","On the other side, Song Yuanye had also been looking for Jing Yi.","He walked over, his lips curling slightly, \"Long time no see, Miss Jing.\" The smile didn't reach his eyes.","Jing Yi looked at him, her gaze scrutinizing, \"Mr. Song, what a coincidence.\" Song Yuanye's eyes hid a deep resentment, \"It really is a coincidence. I mentioned before that I wanted to compete with Miss Jing, and now I've found my chance, haven't I?\"","Jing Yi chuckled lightly, her eyes carrying a hint of mockery, \"Compete? You mean in the exhibition race? Mr. Song certainly has high aspirations.\"","If he could appear in the Super Cup, Jing Yi would at least consider him a man, but now he was talking about competing in a public race?","Song Yuanye clenched his fists, his eyes filled with fury.","Laugh all you want, it doesn't matter. Whether it's an exhibition race or not, as long as he can beat Jing Yi, he can reclaim his spot at the top!","Song Yuanye thought almost obsessively.","A few minutes later, Jing Yi looked at the list and smiled. Although she didn't know how Song Yuanye managed it, her opponent was indeed Song Yuanye.","Perfect, she was in a very bad mood right now, and he just happened to be in her way.","At the same time, the Jing family, who also saw the list, reacted.","Jing Zeqian suddenly stood up, \"Song Yuanye? How could it be him?!\"","Jing Zeyou learned from Jing Zeqian about Song Yuanye's schemes against Jing Yi, his brow furrowing, \"He wants to use Jing Yi to climb back to the top?\" His tone was certain.","Both men's expressions darkened, and Lin Ruiqing and others couldn't help but worry.","Jing Zeqian had a bad feeling, \"I'll go and have them reorder the list!\"","The sound of the race starting echoed, and Jing Zeyou gazed solemnly at the red and silver racing cars on the track.","\"It's too late...\"","A sharp whistle broke the silence, and the race began.","The two cars roared out of the starting line like beasts, instantly accelerating, the wind howling past.","The first corner quickly approached, Jing Yi gripped the steering wheel tightly, quickly shifting gears, and gently pressed the brake. The rear of the car swung, and the body slid perfectly into the corner, the tires screeching against the ground.","The smooth drifting action, like flowing water, instantly ignited the passion of the spectators.","Song Yuanye wasn't willing to be outdone, following closely behind. His silver sports car also entered the corner, but Jing Yi's red sports car had already pulled ahead.","The Public Cup was different from the Super Cup; it wasn't just about speed but more about showcasing skills. After the racers completed the fixed skill track, they would head for the finish line.","Jing Yi was already in a bad mood, and now she was going all out, showcasing her skills and experience to the fullest.","She looked ahead, her eyes sharp, and suddenly turned the steering wheel hard, the rear of the car swinging wildly, almost perfectly sliding through the corner. The sound of tires rubbing against the ground echoed in the air, trailing thick smoke.","Seeing Jing Yi's true level, Song Yuanye, who lacked the ability, became even more anxious. At several critical points, he appeared impatient, causing his car to slightly skid and lose the best route.","Jing Yi glanced at the rearview mirror, her lips curling slightly. She firmly gripped the steering wheel with both hands and accelerated toward the finish line.","The cheers of the audience surged like a tide.","\"Jing Yi! Jing Yi! Jing Yi!\" They spontaneously chanted her name again.","Another defeat was unbearable for Song Yuanye.","He had abandoned his dignity, ignoring the ridicule of netizens, just to win in the public race against Jing Yi. But not only did he fail to beat Jing Yi, he couldn't even catch up to her tail!","The more enthusiastic the audience's cheers, the more obvious the madness and despair in Song Yuanye's eyes.","He gripped the steering wheel tightly, his hands trembling, his knuckles turning white, muttering to himself, \"I'm a top star! I can't lose! I'm a top star!\"","A strong sense of loss and anger surged into his mind.","Suddenly, Song Yuanye slammed down on the accelerator, turning the steering wheel. The silver-white racing car, driven with a hint of madness, charged straight toward Jing Yi's red racing car.","Jing Yi had just crossed the finish line and was completely unaware of the danger behind her.","The audience's exclamations exploded in her ears, and she instinctively turned her head to see the silver-white racing car hurtling toward her at an incredible speed.","Jing Yi's pupils contracted, and she immediately turned the steering wheel to try and avoid it.","But it was too late.","The black racing car slammed into the rear of the red car with a violent force, sending Jing Yi's car flying toward the guardrail beside the track.","When she realized the collision was unavoidable, Jing Yi instinctively protected her vital areas, but her head still took a hit.","The track was instantly thrown into chaos. No one had expected such a thing to happen, and the audience's exclamations echoed continuously.","\"Ah! Jing Yi!\"","\"Jing Yi, get out of the way!\"","\"Is that guy crazy?!\"","\"Quick, save her!!\"","\"Call for help right now!\"","\"Yiyi!\"","Jing Zeyou and the others watched this scene in panic, rushing downstairs toward the track.","Her ears were ringing, the distant cries so clear, her vision blurred, and gradually, she lost consciousness.","At the same time, from a nearby stand, the first figure rushed out: Shen Huaichu.","He ran like a madman to the shattered racing car, kneeling on the ground, his hands trembling violently as he tried to pry open the twisted door.","His face was pale, his voice trembling, \"Yiyi, Yiyi, talk to me, don't ignore me, respond to me, Yiyi, say something to me, please...\"","His hands were soaked in blood, the blood soaked his entire palm, his arm veins bulging as he desperately clawed at the door."]},{"number":203,"title":"Chapter 203: Falling into a Coma","paragraphs":["Jing Yi seemed to have lost consciousness, with blood still streaming from the wound on her forehead.","Shen Huaichu carefully carried her out, murmuring, \"We're going to the hospital, to the hospital. Everything will be fine, you'll be fine...\" His voice was soft, as if repeating these words could lessen the fear and despair gnawing at his heart.","The rescue team arrived quickly, but they couldn't pry Jing Yi from Shen Huaichu's grasp.","\"Shen Huaichu, let go! Yi Yi needs to get to the hospital!\" Jing Zeyou's voice, filled with anger, rang out.","Shen Huaichu, as if waking from a dream, strode quickly toward the ambulance with Jing Yi in his arms. He watched as the nurses moved her onto a stretcher, then knelt beside her, his body trembling violently.","Outside the emergency room, Lin Ruiqing's soft sobs could be heard. Her eyes were red from crying, fixed on the direction Jing Yi had been taken.","Jing Beicheng held her, his expression grave, his concern evident in his eyes.","The three siblings stood outside the door, their eyes bloodshot, their anxiety and unease palpable. They all waited for the door to open, and for the doctor's verdict.","In the corner, Shen Huaichu seemed like a lost soul, his gaze never leaving the closed door, as if he could see Jing Yi lying inside.","Then, the doctor emerged, looking slightly weary. Jing Zeyou and the others immediately surrounded him. \"How is Yi Yi?\"","The doctor removed his mask, his expression not exactly reassuring. \"The head injury isn't too severe, but Jing Yi hasn't regained consciousness yet. We need to closely monitor her for the next seventy-two hours. If she doesn't wake up by then...\"","Lin Ruiqing gasped for breath, stumbling back. \"Not wake up? What do you mean, not wake up?!\"","Jing Yi's injuries weren't severe, but the head trauma was significant. If she didn't wake up during the observation period, he couldn't guarantee she would ever regain consciousness.","Lin Ruiqing clutched at Jing Beicheng, as if he were her last lifeline. \"Yi Yi will be fine, won't she? Won't she?!\"","Jing Beicheng suppressed his own emotions, gripping Lin Ruiqing's hand tightly. \"Of course she will. We have to believe in Yi Yi. She's strong. She'll wake up!\"","Jing Zeyou's heart sank, his voice trembling as he struggled to keep it steady. \"If she doesn't wake up within seventy-two hours, what happens then?\"","The doctor looked at Jing Zeyou and shook his head. \"I can't guarantee anything right now. We'll just have to monitor her over the next few days.\"","Shen Huaichu's breath caught, his breathing suddenly rapid. He stepped forward, almost pleading, \"Save her, please, save her...\"","...","Shen Xi stood outside the intensive care unit, her eyes swollen from crying. Chen Yisi stood beside her, offering support, though her expression was far from relaxed.","\"How could I not have gone? What could be more important than Yi Yi's competition? If I had gone, maybe this wouldn't have happened. It's all my fault, my fault.\"","After the Open Cup ended, Shen Xi had just wanted to call and check on Jing Yi's condition. Instead, she received a call from the Jing family, informing her that Jing Yi had been in a car accident.","She ran to the hospital as fast as she could, only to find Jing Yi lying in the ward, her eyes closed.","How could this have happened?","Jing Yi had said it was just an unimportant exhibition match. She had promised to go out and celebrate with her after the competition.","She hadn't even told Jing Yi about her victory over Chen Yisi yet. Jing Yi would have been so interested. How could she just lie there, unmoving?","Chen Yisi sighed inwardly, tightening her hold on Shen Xi's arm slightly, hoping it would offer some comfort.","Watching Jing Yi still unconscious inside, Shen Xi's tears fell like broken pearls, streaming down her face.","She had never seen Jing Yi like this before, so lifeless, so devoid of vitality.","\"Yi Yi, please wake up. I'll apologize, okay? Are you mad at me for not coming to your competition? Please, don't sleep anymore, okay?\"","Shen Xi's voice grew more choked with sobs. Chen Yisi couldn't bear it. \"Xi Xi, Jing Yi will wake up. You mustn't despair like this.\"","Shen Xi didn't respond, her red, swollen eyes still fixed on the figure in the ward.","On graduation day, she had felt utterly devastated, but nothing compared to the pain she felt now.","She had longed for graduation for so long. She had never been interested in finance or management, and the coursework during her university years had felt like a torment.","She wasn't very good at handling interpersonal relationships. She just didn't like how superficial some people were when they declared their 'love' for her. Yet her classmates always accused her of 'fishing for men.'","It was Jing Yi's arrival that brought her her first real friend in university.","Graduating had been a joyous occasion for Shen Xi, but that day, she had felt deeply sad. Jing Yi had been her best friend for so many years, and now they were going to be separated by two countries.","Later, when she heard that Jing Yi had returned home, she had been overjoyed. And when she learned that her best friend had become a wealthy heiress, she had been happy too, though also worried.","Her own family, though only tangentially connected to such circles, had been difficult to navigate. How much harder would it be for Jing Yi, entering the Jing family?","Then, she heard that Jing Yi was doing well, that her family adored her. Shen Xi had been truly happy for her.","But that happiness hadn't lasted long. This was the second time she had seen Jing Yi in a hospital.","All she wanted was for Jing Yi to be safe.","\"If I had known she'd face all this after coming back, I never would have been happy about her return. She was so free and easygoing abroad. She didn't have to deal with all this, or face so much hostility...\"","On the other side, Gu Lin leaned against the wall, his eyes opening to glance at the figure in the ward. His expression was heavy.","He turned to look at the Jing family and Shen Huaichu, who had been waiting outside the entire time.","In just one day, these people had changed so much.","...","\"Hey, brother, is Jing Yi in trouble?\"","The voice on the other end of the line belonged to Wen Yin, sounding very anxious.","Wen Qingyan glanced at Jing Zejun, who looked utterly exhausted and lifeless, her gaze fixed on the direction of the ICU, as if in a trance.","He moved to the side quietly. \"You saw the news?\" The voice on the other end grew more urgent. \"Is it true? Is the news online true?!\"","Wen Yin had been in class when he overheard his classmates discussing something related to Jing Yi.","\"Didn't you hear? Jing Yi was in a car accident.\"","Panicked, he grabbed a classmate's phone. The news had already blown up on Twitter.","Wen Qingyan glanced at the people still waiting outside and spoke softly. \"Yes, she hasn't woken up yet.\"","\"How could this happen? Brother, I'm booking a flight right now!\"","After the variety show, though their meetings had become less frequent, Wen Yin and Jing Yi had kept in touch. They had even made a plan for after Jing Yi's race—she would teach him how to drive.","Wen Yin's call ended abruptly. Wen Qingyan's gaze shifted back to Jing Yi, still unresponsive in the ward.","He thought, if Jing Yi didn't wake up soon, the people outside might truly break down."]},{"number":204,"title":"Chapter 204: That One is Still in the Intensive Care Unit","paragraphs":["The incident involving Jing Yi happened in broad daylight, and the news was impossible to contain. It didn't take long for netizens to find out that the owner of the silver-white car was none other than Song Yuanye.","[What?! That madman is Song Yuanye?! ]","[I remember Song Yuanye previously mentioned he would attend the open race. I thought it was all over after his accident.]","[!!! Song Yuanye, you really are sick!]","[Ah!!!! My Jing Yi, you absolutely cannot be harmed!]","[I heard Jing Yi is still in the ICU...]","[Where is that bastard Song Yuanye?! Shouldn't he pay with his life?!]","[He's already been detained. The Jing family just hasn't had time to deal with him yet. But rest assured, given how much the Jing family values Jing Yi, Song Yuanye is definitely not going to get off easy.]","[So many people witnessed it? The race track's surveillance can be easily retrieved. He deliberately caused harm!]","[Jing Yi, you absolutely cannot be harmed!]","Being a disgraced artist and being a suspect are two different things. Before this news broke, some fans of Song Yuanye still stood by him. But now, with this revelation, those fans have all disappeared. They could accept a morally flawed artist, but a suspect crosses a line that cannot be crossed. Such a person is not someone they want to associate with.","In an instant, many fans began praying for Jing Yi's recovery.","...","\"What did you say? Jing Yi got into a car accident?\"","Upon hearing the news, Cheng Shu abruptly stood up. The assistant next to her sighed.","\"Yes, she's still in the ICU. Oh, and the person who hit her was Song Yuanye.\"","Cheng Shu hadn't fully processed the first piece of news when she was hit with the revelation that Song Yuanye was the culprit.","She stood there in a daze as her assistant handed her the trending topics on her phone.","After a long while, Cheng Shu finally absorbed all the information. She frowned, \"Didn't the company say they were going to freeze Song Yuanye? Why did they still let him participate in the racing competition?\"","Cheng Shu had heard about Song Yuanye's participation in the racing competition. It was nothing more than buying his way in with money. She had assumed that since Song Yuanye had been exposed, the company would have no more use for him.","Why would they still invest money in such a \"racer\"?","The assistant cautiously glanced at her, \"I heard it was because Song Yuanye and Sister Zhao wanted to take a gamble at this competition.\"","Cheng Shu understood what that meant—greed. One couldn't bear to let go of his top-tier status, and the other couldn't bear to lose a cash cow.","\"So, what is the company planning to do?\"","Song Yuanye was from their company, and now their artist had injured the Jing family's daughter. With Song Yuanye already detained, she assumed the Jing family wouldn't let the company off easily either.","\"The company seems to be preparing to throw Sister Zhao under the bus.\"","After all, they could just say it was an employee acting on their own initiative. Sacrificing one person would solve most problems.","Cheng Shu sighed. It was indeed the company's usual practice, but the other party was the Jing family.","Her emotions were complicated as she scrolled through more news about Jing Yi's condition.","At that moment, her agent, Brother Chen, walked in. The subtle change in Cheng Shu's expression didn't escape her notice as she discreetly turned off her phone.","\"Brother Chen, what brings you here?\"","Cheng Shu gave the assistant a look, and the assistant nodded, taking the phone and heading out to prepare tea.","Brother Chen sat on the sofa, crossing his legs in a leisurely manner.","\"Have you heard about the Jing family's daughter?\"","Cheng Shu's eyes flickered as she feigned confusion, \"What happened?\"","Brother Chen glanced at her, \"Cheng Shu, don't play dumb with me.\"","The assistant brought in the tea, sensing the tense atmosphere between the two. She felt a bit nervous.","Cheng Shu smiled and took the tea from the assistant, pouring it herself for Brother Chen.","\"You know me, Brother Chen. I've been preoccupied with Song Yuanye's situation lately. How would I have time to pay attention to other things?\"","Brother Chen stared at Cheng Shu for a while but didn't say whether he believed her or not.","\"Alright, I don't care if you know or not. Song Yuanye is in trouble, and the company's decision is that both he and his agent, Sister Zhao, are done for.\"","Cheng Shu smiled on the surface, \"Then I should congratulate Brother Chen. Now no one is standing above you.\"","She thought she would be happy, no longer having to ride on Song Yuanye's coattails or worry about being scolded by his fans.","But for some reason, she felt a bit complicated inside. Maybe it was a sense of schadenfreude. Perhaps one day, she too would be treated like \"trash\" and disposed of.","Brother Chen lit a cigarette and, after Cheng Shu had lit it for him, he slowly said, \"I didn't come here because of that.\" Though he was indeed very happy about it.","\"With Song Yuanye gone, your popularity hasn't picked up either.\" Cheng Shu's heart skipped a beat, unsure of what her agent was about to assign her next.","The room was filled with the smell of smoke, making her eyes sting, but she still smiled, \"Brother Chen, I don't think riding on someone's coattails is suitable for me. How about I take on some roles...\"","Before she could finish, her agent interrupted her impatiently, \"Roles? Do you think I have the time to wait for you to become popular? Cheng Shu, don't play these little tricks with me. The company isn't raising you to nurture you!\"","Cheng Shu's smile froze, her lips curling down slightly. Signing a contract felt like signing a \"slave contract.\"","The assistant in the corner worriedly glanced at Cheng Shu.","Brother Chen glanced at Cheng Shu and continued, \"You were present when Song Yuanye and Jing Yi met, weren't you?\"","Cheng Shu calmly looked at him, \"Yes.\" So, what did he want?","\"Now that the Jing family's daughter is in trouble, this is your chance to become popular. I've arranged a few interviews for you. They're very interested in the details of what happened. Go talk about it.\"","Cheng Shu suddenly felt extremely exhausted. Riding on someone's coattails! Riding on someone's coattails! How long would she have to keep doing this?!","She took a deep breath, \"Brother Chen, the Jing family's daughter is still in the ICU!\" The girl's life was hanging in the balance, and he was still thinking of exploiting her for profit?","Brother Chen gave her a strange look, \"So what?\" They weren't saying anything wrong, just mentioning it. And even if the Jing family wanted to hold someone accountable, they could just throw Cheng Shu under the bus.","Seeing that Cheng Shu was about to say something more, Brother Chen became impatient. He blew out a smoke ring and stood up.","\"Alright, just do what you're told. Don't act like some saint. You haven't become popular after all this time. Do you really think the company is raising you for free? Oh, and there's a dinner party tonight. Go get ready.\"","Brother Chen left, and the assistant quickly walked over to Cheng Shu, worried, \"Cheng Shu sister...\"","Cheng Shu was still sitting there, her hands gripping her knees tightly, her teeth clenched.","\"To hell with riding on someone's coattails! To hell with these dinner parties! I've had enough!\"","\"Xiao Xiao, I'm done with this. Do you want to leave with me?\"","The assistant was momentarily stunned but then nodded firmly.","\"But Sister Cheng Shu, what about the liquidated damages?\" It would be easy for her to just leave, but Cheng Shu had signed a contract.","Cheng Shu let out a cold laugh. The company wanted her to make money for them but also wanted to sacrifice her? Where was such a good deal?","She wasn't exactly a saint, so she had kept some evidence.","She was gambling.","Gambling that the family of the girl who had smiled at her would be willing to pull her out, just by using the small amount of evidence that they could easily obtain with a little effort."]},{"number":205,"title":"Chapter 205: The Life of 'Jingyi'","paragraphs":["Amidst a hazy mist, Jing Yi looked around in confusion. \"Where am I?\" She tentatively stepped forward, and the mist gradually dispersed.","Jing Yi saw a figure—someone who looked remarkably like herself.","\"Grandma, was that person my father just now?\"","\"Why?! I'm also a young lady of the Jing family. Why should I hide abroad?!\"","\"If you didn't want to acknowledge me, you could've just not adopted me! What does it mean to dump me abroad now?!\"","\"I didn't mean it! Grandma, I didn't mean it!\"","\"Grandma has passed away. Can you bring me back to the country?\"","\"What I have, Jing Zejun has too. What she doesn't have, am I not even qualified to get?\"","\"Why does everything belong to her? Family, identity, this home—it's all hers! What do I have? I have nothing!\"","\"You said it was just a small lesson for them. Why did he get involved with that stuff?!\"","\"I didn't mean to, I didn't want to turn him into this...\"","\"From the beginning, I was just an outsider.\"","Jing Yi quietly watched the scenes unfolding before her, depicting the life of 'Jing Yi'.","Suddenly, a voice came from behind. \"You must be quite pleased, aren't you?\"","Jing Yi turned around.","Staring at the person standing in front of her, who looked identical to herself, Jing Yi felt a mix of emotions.","This was the first time she was conversing face-to-face with 'herself', and it felt rather novel.","\"...Hello.\"","She greeted politely, trying to be courteous.","However, the person in front of her seemed unimpressed by this gesture. She sneered, \"You must be quite pleased. They like you so much.\" Jing Yi thought for a moment and replied earnestly, \"Pleased? Not really. Maybe I'm just more likable.\"","\"You!\"","'Jing Yi' was caught off guard by her straightforward response, her expression contorting for a moment.","Jing Yi smiled indifferently. If she hadn't seen the previous scenes, her attitude might have been more amicable.","Recalling the image of Grandma Jing lying in a pool of blood and Jing Zeqian curled up in pain on the ground, a simple greeting was already the most polite she could be.","It turned out that the brief mention of this plot in the original book concealed such details.","\"Why did you help Wang Boqi?\"","'Jing Yi' raised an eyebrow. \"What? Coming to stand up for them? Do you really see yourself as part of the Jing family? You're just a fake!\" Seemingly recalling something, she smirked mysteriously, \"Do you know why they like you?\"","Unaware of what tricks the other party was planning, Jing Yi calmly watched her.","'Jing Yi' gazed at Jing Yi just as mysteriously, enunciating each word clearly: \"That's because they can clearly hear what you're thinking.\"","Jing Yi frowned slightly. \"What did you say?\" 'Jing Yi' chuckled softly. \"Didn't understand? Let me say it again.\"","\"They can clearly hear your thoughts.\"","Can hear my thoughts?","In an instant, Jing Yi was stunned, her eyes filled with bewilderment.","Seeing her reaction, 'Jing Yi' curled the corners of his mouth with a malicious smile, \"Otherwise, why would they treat you so well? Because you're their script!\"","There's no such thing as unconditional love in this world. What you have that I don't is merely because they can see through your heart.","'Jing Yi' didn't care what the Jing family actually heard. Once the seed of doubt is planted, it can never be uprooted.","Jing Yi stood frozen, memories flashing through her mind.","The peculiar look on Jing Zeqian's face when they first met; the scrutiny from the Jing family upon her return...","'Did you run into someone when you went out?'","'Jing Yi, I know your thoughts like the back of my hand.'","'Don't worry, I'll take care of you for the rest of your life.'","'Why do you have such a strong hostility toward Jiang Miaomiao?'","As Jing Yi gradually recalled past events, 'Jing Yi' grew increasingly triumphant.","\"You're lying.\"","Jing Yi suddenly looked up, her tone firm.","'Jing Yi's face stiffened, trying to maintain composure. \"Don't believe me? Why would I lie to you? You should be well aware of the Jing family's strange behavior lately.\"","Jing Yi gradually regained her composure. \"If they could truly hear all my thoughts, Jing Zeqian wouldn't have been so naive as to fall into someone else's trap.\"","If the Jing family could really hear her thoughts, Jing Zeqian wouldn't have been at odds with her, and she wouldn't have had to go through so much trouble dealing with Jiang Miaomiao.","However, 'Jing Yi' wouldn't have concocted such a lie out of thin air. Maybe they could only hear some of her thoughts?","Which parts?","Jing Yi didn't have time to ponder further, so she decided to address this later.","She gazed at 'Jing Yi' firmly and stated, \"You're lying.\" 'Jing Yi' clenched his teeth and said, \"So what?! In the end, they can still hear your thoughts, can't they?\"","\"How does it feel to have no secrets standing in front of others? You can't possibly be indifferent to it.\"","Jing Yi hesitated slightly. \"This does make me a bit uncomfortable.\" Then, her lips curved slightly upward.","\"But thinking that they like the most honest me, I find it quite heartwarming.\"","'Jing Yi' stared at her, her face filled with gloom, repeating, \"Honest?\"","\"What do you mean by honest? Telling Grandma I wanted to return home isn't honest? Or wanting to become a true young lady of the Jing family isn't honest?\"","Honesty only invites more hostility from the Jing family!","All she wanted was an identity, yet they were unwilling to give even that!","'Jing Yi' eyes turned red, glaring fiercely at Jing Yi. The more composed the other person appeared, the more humiliated and resentful she felt.","\"You asked why I helped Wang Boqi? Because he's the only one willing to love me! Even though I'm just an adopted orphan of the Jing family, he still loves me!\"","Jing Yi's brow furrowed in displeasure. \"Only him? What about Grandma Jing?\"","'Jing Yi' panicked instantly.","Jing Yi suppressed her anger. \"She raised you since you were young. Is this how you repay her?\"","She didn't think there was anything wrong with 'Jing Yi' falling for Wang Boqi, but she regarded him as her only salvation while discarding those who truly cared for her!","'Jing Yi' looked up, her eyes filled with fury.","\"She just wanted to use me as a substitute for Jing Zejun!\"","No one truly cared for her. Not her biological parents, who sent her to an orphanage when she was so young. She was a child unloved and unwanted by her family.","The Jing family too. People always said she was lucky to be adopted by a wealthy family, but for over twenty years, she had only seen Grandma Jing. Was that really good?","Jing Beicheng and the others were like this, and so was Grandma Jing. If they had adopted her, why didn't they allow her to return home? Wasn't she also a young lady of the Jing family?","Jing Yi's eyes instantly turned sharp.","\"Everyone can say that about her, but you can't.\""]},{"number":206,"title":"Chapter 206: Long Time No See, I'm Back","paragraphs":["Grandma Jing adopted Jing Yi, and almost everyone thought she was compensating for Jing Zejun by doing so.","However, no one understood Grandma Jing better than herself. She knew that Jing Yi and Jing Zejun were entirely different people, and she had never treated Jing Yi as a replacement for anyone.","She simply wanted to find redemption for the overwhelming guilt that weighed heavily on her heart. This was her only selfish desire.","All she hoped for was that there would be someone who would treat her granddaughter kindly.","Jing Yi's questioning made Jing Yi feel disoriented, but the anger of being \"usurped\" had already completely taken over her mind.","She forced a smile, one that was sarcastic, \"What? Not satisfied with the Jing Family, now even Grandma is yours?\"","\"Jing Yi! What right do you have to say that to me?! Those are my family! Mine!\"","Jing Yi stood her ground, her almond-shaped eyes cold.","\"You think they're yours now? Did you not feel that way when you watched Jiang Miaomiao drug Jing Zeqian? Did you not feel that way when you helped Wang Boqi target Hengjing? Did you not feel that way when you pushed Grandma Jing away?!\"","Jing Yi's voice grew louder, filled with intense questioning.","The grievances between Jing Yi and the Jing Family, Jing Yi could choose to ignore. She couldn't stand on a moral high ground and demand that Jing Yi be kind to the Jing Family.","As for Jing Yi's involvement with Wang Boqi, she could also choose to ignore. Who someone falls in love with is none of her business.","But she couldn't overlook what Jing Yi had done to Grandma Jing.","Jing Yi gazed at the person in front of her, her lips pressed tightly together, her expression never so forceful before.","\"Even on her deathbed, she was still planning for your future. You wanted to return to the Jing Family, so she let you go and instructed them to treat you well. And what did you do?","\"You only thought about using her death to further your own plans!\"","Jing Yi's voice choked with emotion, her throat bobbing as she suppressed the surge of feelings within her.","\"...She must have regretted adopting you.\"","Jing Yi collapsed to the ground, her eyes reddening as tears welled up and rolled down her cheeks.","\"You're lying, Grandma wouldn't regret it... She loved me, you're lying, you're lying...\"","...","Jing Yi disappeared, and before Jing Yi could ask more, she was gone.","Jing Yi pouted, sitting in place and muttering to herself, \"That was too weak. She got a few words thrown at her and felt so guilty she just vanished? Or is she so angry she's planning to trap me here?\"","She looked around at the misty surroundings, unsure of where she was. She lay down on the ground, lost in thought.","For a moment, Jing Yi felt lost. Not only did she not know where she was, but she also didn't know where she should go.","Her family was something she had unexpectedly gained. Jing Yi wasn't entirely wrong—she had indeed taken over Jing Yi's identity.","If the Jing Family had accepted her as family because they could hear her thoughts,","then what about the future?","After going through this, how could she not reveal anything? Could she just forget it all?","Impossible!","Jing Yi turned over irritably.","Moreover, would they be able to accept this 'outsider'?","What about Shen Huaichu? He witnessed her getting into a car accident with his own eyes, wouldn't he be even more frightened?","What on earth should I do?","The faint hum of the equipment in the ward and the regular \"beep beep\" of the heart monitor.","Jing Yi lay on the hospital bed, her eyes tightly closed, her breathing weak yet steady, as if she were lost in an endless dream.","Jing Zeqian grabbed the doctor anxiously and asked, \"Why hasn't she woken up yet?!\" Two days had already passed, and the time was getting closer to what the doctor had said. Jing Zeqian didn't dare to think any further...","Shen Huaichu sat numbly on the edge of her bed, her hand tightly gripping Jing Yi's, not crying out in pain, nor filled with anger. She simply sat there, her eyes lifeless and devoid of any emotion.","......","In the distant mist, faint sounds could be heard.","A voice was low and sorrowful, he murmured, \"Yiyi, from the day I was with you, I was overjoyed and trembling with fear. I was so afraid that I had to see you safe and sound with my own eyes, but some things seem to slip away faster the tighter you hold onto them.\"","\"Are you very disappointed? On that day, when you won, instead of being happy for you, I felt more of a relief from the fear in my heart.\"","\"I didn't become your strength, nor did I become your armor. I'm sorry, Yiyi.\"","A voice heavy with bitterness said, \"Yiyi, you can't sleep anymore. You still have so many things left to do. Your lonely and affluent remaining years have been interrupted, at least you should live a wealthy life. We agreed that after all this, we would also take good rest and get plenty of sunshine, didn't we?\"","\"Big brother doesn't like basking in the sun alone, could you wake up, please?\"","A voice filled with sorrow and grief, \"Yiyi, you care for your mother the most. Mother has finally gained another daughter with great difficulty, you can't let me experience the disappearance of a daughter in front of me again, can you? Wake up, please?\"","A voice is sad but restrained, \"Yiyi, coming to our home is our fortune. You are the most unique child I have ever seen. This time, you will bring a surprise again, won't you?\"","A voice choked with sorrow, \"Yiyi, you promised that when I win the ultimate Best Actress award, you would be in the audience cheering for me. You said you would always support my dream of being an actress. Yiyi, I'm a little scared, please don't sleep, okay?\"","A voice was anxious and pained, \"Jing Yi Yi, wake up... I'm sorry, it's all my fault, it's because of me that you're lying here. You can hit me or scold me if you wake up. Didn't you say that I would become the manager of the most outstanding race car driver? How can you fulfill your promise if you're lying like this? Please, get up...\"","On the hospital bed, the girl's tightly closed eyes slightly trembled, her long eyelashes gently fluttered, and her fingers involuntarily curled up.","A weak voice came.","“Jing Zeqian, you're so noisy.”","Jing Yi slowly opened her eyes and gradually regained consciousness, her first sight being Jing Zeqian, who had been murmuring by her bedside.","Who is this uncle with a scruffy beard, bloodshot eyes, and disheveled appearance?","Sitting by the hospital bed, Jing Zeqian, who was choked with sobs and mumbling incoherently, was stunned, thinking it was his own hallucination, until he saw Jing Yi awake.","He rubbed his eyes, and after realizing that there was no illusion, he suddenly stood up.","Looking at Jing Yi, who had just awakened on the sickbed, Jing Zeqian was so excited that he couldn't speak a complete sentence and leaned over to the bedside.","\"Jing, Jing Yi Yi! Jing Yi Yi! You're awake?!\"","Jing Yi twitched the corner of her mouth, revealing a bit of weakness from just waking up. \"Second brother, you look so ugly,\" she said. She shouldn't have been asleep for long, so why does he look so much older?","Jing Zeqian's joy was evident on his face. He rushed out of the ward in a panic, shouting as he ran, \"Doctor! Brother! She's awake! Jing Yi Yi is awake!\"","Soon, a crowd gathered around, and Jing Yi looked at the people with bloodshot eyes and haggard faces, feeling a pang of heartache.","A smile crept into the eyes, glistening faintly, and the dimples at the corner of the mouth deepened alternately, \"Although it feels like it shouldn't be long, I still want to say...\"","\"Long time no see, I'm back.\""]},{"number":207,"title":"Chapter 207: They, Waiting for Her to Come Home","paragraphs":["The doctor asked Jing Yi's condition in detail and carefully examined her situation. \"As long as she's awake, there shouldn't be any major issues,\" the doctor thought, feeling a bit relieved.","\"Someone will come to give her a full body check-up shortly.\"","Lin Ruiqing and Jing Zejun stood by Jing Yi's bedside, tightly holding her hands, afraid that if they let go for a moment, they might not see her awake again.","Lin Ruiqing's eyes were red, her voice still a bit hoarse. \"You're back, that's all that matters! You're back, that's all that matters!\" She kept repeating these words.","Jing Yi's eyes welled up with tears, a bittersweet feeling in her heart as she squeezed Lin Ruiqing's hand back.","\"Mom, I'm sorry. I'm sorry for making you worry so much.\"","Lin Ruiqing, though her own eyes were still red, reached out to wipe Jing Yi's tears, as gentle as ever. \"There's nothing to be sorry for. As long as you're awake, Mom would do anything.\"","Several wealthy businessmen stood in a row, their faces pale and haggard, but their excitement and relief were evident in their eyes.","They stood in a line by Jing Yi's hospital bed, a familiar scene.","\"Jing Yi, you're finally awake! If you hadn't woken up, I would have had to slap you awake!\"","As soon as Jing Zeqian said this, the others in the room shot him reproachful glances.","Seeing Jing Zeqian, the first person she saw when she woke up, still looking the same, Jing Yi couldn't help but laugh. She repeated, \"Second Brother, you look so ugly.\"","Jing Zeqian heard this clearly. \"What?! Who am I doing this for?\" He touched his face, asking tentatively, \"Am I really that ugly?\"","Jing Yi's smile widened as she nodded lightly, \"Very ugly.\"","The familiar sounds of bickering filled the room again.","Jing Yi smiled as she looked at the people surrounding her—her family, Shen Huaichu, Shen Xi, Wen Yin, and many others.","Jing Yi had never believed that anyone could love her so much, but they were all waiting for her to come home.","She had heard them, heard that they were all waiting for her to come home.","Jing Yi's heart felt calm again. Suddenly, she paused.","Could they still hear her thoughts now?","...","Jing Zeqian, you big dummy!","Jing Zeqian, you big dummy!","Jing Zeqian, you big dummy!","Jing Zeqian handed Jing Yi the apple he had just peeled, seeing her staring at him, he thought she was moved by his concern.","His lips couldn't help but curl up, the joy in his eyes evident. \"What are you looking at? Eat it, do you want anything else?\"","Jing Yi's eyes lit up. Could they really not hear her thoughts anymore?","Although she had said as much to the original Jing Yi, Jing Yi still felt a bit uneasy. After all, who wouldn't want a little privacy?","\"Then some grapes, please.\"","Jing Yi glanced at him secretly, no reaction? Should she test again?","\"Second Brother, is there anything you want to say to me?\"","If you really can hear me, just 'meow' once, and as a reward, 'Midnight' is yours!","Jing Yi felt a pang in her heart. This was a big deal.","Jing Zeqian's hand paused slightly. Jing Yi's heart skipped a beat. Could he still hear her?","He looked up at Jing Yi, his eyes filled with deep self-reproach and guilt. \"I want to apologize to you.\" Jing Yi was taken aback. \"Apologize?\"","For what?","\"It's all my fault. If I hadn't left Song Yuanye unresolved, leaving you with such a hidden danger, you wouldn't have suffered so much. Yi Yi, I'm sorry.\"","Jing Zeqian looked like he was about to cry. Jing Yi chuckled at her second brother. \"You can't control whether someone else has malicious intentions against me, can you?\"","\"But...\"","Jing Yi put the peeled apple aside and gently patted his head. \"There are no 'buts'. You're all too tense. I'm fine now, the doctor said it's just minor injuries.\"","In truth, the injuries from this car accident were even lighter than those she had suffered when escaping from Wang Boqi, except that she had gained a strange experience.","But, could that have just been a dream?","Jing Zeqian, with red eyes, pushed Jing Yi's hand away and glared at her. \"Jing Yi, I'm your older brother. Don't be disrespectful.\" Jing Yi pouted. \"Crybaby brother.\"","Forget it, whether it was a dream or not, it's all in the past.","The siblings started bickering again. There was a knock on the door, and it was Shen Huaichu.","He stopped at the door, waiting for Jing Yi's permission.","Jing Yi looked at him as if they were separated by an eternity, even though it had only been a few days.","She smiled at Jing Zeqian. \"Second Brother, I want some porridge from that place near the hospital. Could you go buy it for me?\" Jing Zeqian, of course, didn't want to, but Jing Yi's pleading look was too obvious.","He sighed. \"Alright! I'll go buy it now.\" As he left, Jing Zeqian passed by Shen Huaichu and gave him a warning glance.","The room was left with only Jing Yi and Shen Huaichu.","She smiled and patted the spot beside her. \"Come sit.\"","This scene seemed a bit familiar. Wasn't it like this when they first got together?","Jing Yi found it a bit funny and a bit sad. Was their relationship really doomed? Why did every important conversation happen in the hospital?","\"Did I scare you?\"","When Jing Yi was about to lose consciousness from the crash, she saw Shen Huaichu running towards her. He looked desperate.","A heavy sense of oppression filled Shen Huaichu's chest. He opened his mouth, his voice hoarse. \"I thought... I thought you never wanted to talk to me again.\" He felt like he was bound by an invisible restraint, even his breathing was cautious.","Jing Yi wanted to smile to ease the heavy atmosphere in the room, but her lips wouldn't lift.","During her coma, she had thought a lot—about her family, about 'Jing Yi', and about Shen Huaichu.","She wondered if she would become another 'Jing Yi'.","Because of love, would she give up everything?","\"Shen Huaichu, if I said I've considered giving up being a race car driver, you...\" Before she could finish, Shen Huaichu suddenly looked up, his voice trembling. \"No!\"","Jing Yi opened her mouth slightly, stunned for a few seconds.","He stared at Jing Yi, the redness at the corners of his eyes evident. \"You don't need to give up anything.\"","It turned out that when he became the one being chosen, he wasn't as happy as he thought.","A sudden pain struck Shen Huaichu's heart. He carefully held Jing Yi's hand, and she didn't pull away.","\"Yi Yi, that day you said you didn't need me to be there, but I still went. I'm sorry.\"","Jing Yi's lashes fluttered. She had seen it, even though he had hidden it deeply, she had still seen it.","\"My parents died in a car accident, right in front of me. It was a big truck, the car's brakes failed, there was a loud screeching sound, the speed was too fast, out of control, and then the car crashed...\"","This was the first time Shen Huaichu had spoken about this. He tightly held Jing Yi's hand, as if doing so would give him the courage."]},{"number":208,"title":"Chapter 208: Can't Hear the Heartbeat Anymore","paragraphs":["Shen Huaichu had always wanted to hide the part of himself he considered shameful, but Jing Yi always saw through him.","\"You're right, I'm very worried about you, to the point where I can't enjoy the joy of your victories,\" Shen Huaichu paused, \"The young me couldn't save my parents, and that makes me even more worried about not being able to ensure your safety.\"","\"......I'm sorry, I failed to keep my promise to trust you.\"","His voice trembled more and more, as he struggled to suppress the turmoil in his heart, \"Because of my existence, you can no longer do what you want freely...\"","How could he have the right to ask her to give up anything more?","\"I originally thought that not being able to accompany you in doing what you love the most was the most selfish thing I've ever done,\" he swallowed hard, the smile at the corner of his mouth carrying a hint of self-mockery and bitterness.","\"Now it seems, my selfishness goes far beyond that.\"","Jing Yi stared at him without blinking, her eyes seemingly on the verge of tears.","Shen Huaichu paused for a moment, struggling to suppress the endless pain in his heart, he smiled with tears in his eyes, and spoke with difficulty, \"So, I might have to leave for a while.\"","This was the decision Shen Huaichu made during Jing Yi's period of coma.","He had thought about it, if Jing Yi didn't wake up, he would stay here and take care of her for the rest of his life; if she woke up, he would go and get treatment.","Jing Zeyou was right, it was his arrogance to think that as long as he could control himself enough, he could stand by Jing Yi on the racetrack.","But what Jing Yi cared about was never whether he could appear on the racetrack.","He had once trusted her so much that he was willing to give his life to her, how could he now not even trust her to protect herself?","\"When I get better...\" he gently wiped away the tears on Jing Yi's face with a trembling hand, \"When I get better, I'll stand by your side again, okay?\"","By then, he would be able to give Jing Yi a better Shen Huaichu, and he wouldn't be standing at the crossroads of her choices.","As long as he was lucky enough, Jing Yi would still want him by then.","Jing Yi reached out and hugged him, tightening her arms repeatedly, crying and trembling, as if all her grievances were pouring out at this moment.","Jing Yi's voice was choked with sobs, \"Shen Huaichu, I still like you very much, very much, very much, but you said you trusted me...\"","She loved racing, but she also wanted Shen Huaichu to be happy.","Shen Huaichu hugged her tightly in return, as if wanting to merge her into his very bones, \"I know, I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry...\" he kept saying sorry, and never said anything else.","That day, Jing Yi cried until she was exhausted, and after she fell asleep, Shen Huaichu looked at the person on the hospital bed one last time, gazing deeply, as if wanting to etch everything in front of him into his heart.","He gently closed the door of the ward, leaned against the wall, and slowly slid to the ground, covering his face, biting his lips tightly, but it was of no use, the corners of his mouth were already stained with blood.","He tried his best to suppress his voice, but his trembling body couldn't hide anything.","...","Shen Huaichu left, which surprised the Jing family.","During Jing Yi's coma, he had been like a walking corpse, guarding by Jing Yi's bedside without ever taking his eyes off her.","That appearance even made Jing Zeyou a bit worried, worried that before Jing Yi woke up, one of them would go crazy.","But now that Jing Yi was awake, he had left instead.","Jing Zeqian said that before Shen Huaichu left, he had talked to Jing Yi in the ward for a while.","Jing Zeyou wasn't sure if it was because of this, but he felt a little less worried about Jing Yi and Shen Huaichu.","Jing Yi liked Shen Huaichu very much, Jing Zeyou could feel it, he had even thought, if Jing Yi gave up racing for Shen Huaichu, should he break them up?","He didn't want to make his sister sad, but he also didn't want his sister to give up her hard-won freedom for a man.","For Jing Yi, this wasn't just a hobby, but her life after breaking free from her shackles.","Fortunately, Shen Huaichu had truly lived up to his previous promise, that if he became an obstacle, he would solve it himself.","Now it all depended on whether the result of his handling would satisfy them.","There was one more thing, they could no longer hear Jing Yi's thoughts.","Jing Zeyou had specifically confirmed with everyone in the family, and they were all the same.","To be honest, Jing Zeyou didn't feel the slightest bit of regret, instead, he breathed a sigh of relief.","He had been very worried about this from the beginning, and also worried that this would affect Jing Yi's health, otherwise he wouldn't have taken Jing Yi to the hospital right from the start.","\"Not being able to hear is also good, I've always been worried that this would affect Yi Yi.\"","Lin Ruiqing didn't know why she could hear Jing Yi's thoughts, and then suddenly couldn't, but since everything had settled, it was the best outcome.","Jing Beicheng nodded in agreement, no one would like to show themselves completely without any secrets.","Jing Zejun had the same idea.","Jing Zeqian felt relieved, \"Finally, I don't have to hear Jing Yi cursing me in her heart.\" Compared to the others, he was the one who least wanted to hear Jing Yi's thoughts, every time it would make him half-dead with anger.","Although now Jing Yi only cursed him out loud.","\"You haven't even shaved yet, you look so ugly.\"","Jing Zeqian glared at the person on the hospital bed, \"Who do you think I'm doing this for?!\" Although his tone was fierce, his hands still gently peeled the grapes.","Jing Yi's eyes flashed with amusement, and she unceremoniously ate the fruit he placed in front of her.","\"What? Shaving takes that much time?\"","Jing Zeqian glanced at the person enjoying herself unhappily, shaving didn't take much time, but Jing Yi had just woken up, and he really didn't feel at ease, plus Lin Ruiqing and the others were getting older, after staying up for so long, he had them go back to rest first.","The three siblings had agreed to take turns guarding Jing Yi, wasn't it just their turn to start? Even if he wanted to shave, he had to wait for Jing Zejun to bring his equipment.","\"What's wrong with that! Even if I don't shave, I'm still a handsome guy, okay!\" The people chasing him could line up from here to the end of the world!","Jing Yi laughed until her stomach hurt, watching her wobble, Jing Zeqian hurried to support her, afraid that she would fall down if she wasn't careful.","\"Be careful! Don't have such big emotional ups and downs, okay!\"","Jing Yi finally calmed down, wiped the tears from the corners of her eyes, \"Yes, yes, our Jing Shao is amazing.\" With this haggard look, who could recognize him as the second young master of the Jing family if he was thrown on the street?","Jing Zeqian glared at her unhappily, then sat back in his seat, resigned to peeling the grapes.","He occasionally looked up at Jing Yi, his eyes carrying a bit of caution, he had originally been a little worried about Jing Yi's condition, but this person seemed to be fine, wasn't it said that breaking up was like having a serious illness? Some people even felt like the sky had fallen?","Was Jing Yi breaking up?"]},{"number":209,"title":"Chapter 209: Cheng Shu's Visit","paragraphs":["Jing Yi had long noticed Jing Zeqian's gaze and abruptly turned her head to catch him off guard.","\"What is it?!\"","Don't even think about figuring out her little schemes now!","Jing Zeqian quickly averted his eyes, \"Nothing.\" He then changed the subject, \"Oh, by the way, I haven't told you about the outcome of Song Yuanye's case, have I?\"","Talking about Song Yuanye was definitely better than mentioning Shen Huaichu, right?","Jing Zeqian inwardly nodded in satisfaction, thinking he had successfully protected his sister's sensitive and fragile heart today.","Jing Yi furrowed her brows slightly. If he was going to talk about the outcome, why be so secretive about it?","\"So?\"","After being arrested, Song Yuanye still couldn't let go of his dream of becoming a top star, alternating between clarity and madness.","However, even though he didn't make it as a top star, his actions had become known worldwide. Not only did he have some existing fame, but the incident also involved a major racing event, the GT Championship, and the target of his actions was the daughter of a global top-tier conglomerate.","As a result, media outlets of all kinds were reporting on the incident.","In a way, it was a different path to the same destination.","Though he couldn't be a top star in the entertainment industry, with some effort, he could still dream of being a 'top star' in his lifetime—as long as he didn't die too soon.","Jing Yi was uninterested in Song Yuanye's affairs. As for what Jing Zeqian and the others were doing, she had no intention of getting involved.","She wasn't that 'kind'. The guy had tried to take her life, and she wasn't about to feel sorry for him or think the retaliation was too harsh.","Seeing her lack of interest, Jing Zeqian decided not to continue with the topic, lest it tarnish her ears.","He finished peeling the last grape, looking quite satisfied with the lumpy grape flesh in front of him.","Jing Yi's daily intake was strictly regulated, and he dared not let her eat more.","After washing his hands, Jing Zeqian took the tissue that Jing Yi handed him and wiped his hands, not forgetting her playful comment about his disheveled appearance.","He went back to the bathroom, stared at himself in the mirror, and examined himself carefully from side to side.","He muttered to himself, \"I guess I do look a bit scruffy.\"","Jing Yi watched him and couldn't help but smile softly, her eyes filled with warmth and emotion.","How could she not know that Jing Zeqian was guarding her so closely out of fear that something might happen to her again? Every member of the Jing family was like that.","Though her identity was 'Jing Yi', from the moment she boarded the plane, she was no longer anyone else. Her interactions with the Jing family were genuine.","She was the Jing family's youngest daughter, and no one could replace that!","Jing Zeqian came out of the bathroom, and Jing Yi quickly hid her thoughts, teasingly looking at him.","\"What's wrong? Isn't our Jing Shao supposed to be a big handsome guy even like this? Why start caring now?\"","Jing Zeqian coughed lightly, putting his hands down, and retorted indignantly, \"Of course! That's because you haven't seen it. As soon as I step out of this hospital room, there are plenty of people lining up to fawn over me!\"","His voice raised a bit, as if to salvage his image in Jing Yi's eyes.","Jing Yi couldn't hold back her laughter. She thought that compared to the face that revealed Jing Zeqian's identity, if he were completely blackened, even more people would flock to him.","\"Come on! There's a rich, gullible fool over here!\"","...","During Jing Yi's hospital stay, many visitors came to see her, including Shen Xi, who looked even more frail than she was.","After a few words, Jing Yi quickly had Chen Yisi take Shen Xi back to rest. Did she really want to be her hospital roommate?","There was also Li Chengsheng, who was busy cursing on her behalf. Her brother's friend was indeed still a hot-blooded teenager, and his fiery demeanor was unmatched.","Not only Li Chengsheng, but also his brothers. For a moment, Jing Yi felt like she was the big sister of some gang.","It was Jing Zeqian who thought they were too noisy and chased them all away.","There was Wen Yin, who personally made seafood porridge for her, but she couldn't eat it!","Watching Jing Zeqian enjoy it on her behalf and Wen Yin looking guilty, she didn't mind at all, though her tears streamed from the corners of her mouth.","Wen Yin genuinely thought seafood porridge was still porridge and that patients could eat it. Besides, he only knew how to make seafood.","But her brother was really going too far! Why was he enjoying it so much?!","Fortunately, Lin Ruiqing sternly stopped this scene, kicking Jing Zeqian out of the ward.","However, one day, an unexpected visitor arrived—Cheng Shu.","Jing Zeqian had already told Jing Yi about Cheng Shu's recent 'exploits', a person who single-handedly brought down her own company and had been trending on social media for days.","After thinking for a while, Jing Yi finally remembered who Cheng Shu was: \"It's fine, Brother, let her in.\"","Jing Yi was quite surprised. She and Cheng Shu were only nodding acquaintances, and she hadn't expected Cheng Shu to come visit her.","Cheng Shu seemed a bit nervous, and after a few polite exchanges, the room fell into silence.","Jing Yi awkwardly fiddled with her hands, \"I heard things have been lively around Miss Cheng lately.\" Cheng Shu was taken aback and smiled, \"I mainly want to thank Miss Jing.\"","Thank her again?","Jing Yi was a bit puzzled. Why were so many people suddenly thanking her for no apparent reason?","This time, she had even been unconscious; could she still be helping people?","Cheng Shu smiled faintly. She owed her gratitude to Jing Yi. Perhaps it was Jing Yi's experiences that inspired her to want to shine in the sunlight.","Otherwise, she might not have had the courage to rebel.","Moreover, while it seemed she had single-handedly brought down the company, Cheng Shu knew that without the Jing family's backing, with just the evidence she had, she wouldn't have made it out of the company alive.","Jing Yi raised an eyebrow. Alright, since everyone was thanking her, she wasn't losing out.","\"So, what are you planning to do next?\"","With the company gone, Cheng Shu felt a weight lift off her shoulders. The incident had caused such a stir that her popularity had skyrocketed.","Thinking back to what her agent had said, it was a different path to the same destination.","Due to her newfound popularity, many entertainment companies had contacted her, expressing interest in signing her, including Startrack Entertainment.","However, Cheng Shu understood that Startrack's interest was likely due to Jing Zeqian's consideration for Jing Yi, buying her a favor.","But Cheng Shu couldn't bring herself to take advantage of Jing Yi again. She had already been pulled out by Jing Yi; she couldn't ask for more. So, she didn't sign with any company.","She decided to go solo.","It was risky, but with her current popularity, it wasn't impossible.","She still loved acting. Although she might not get the good scripts she had missed before, at least she was moving in that direction, which gave her some hope.","Listening to Cheng Shu's future plans, Jing Yi's lips curved slightly.","Compared to the Cheng Shu who had been behind Song Yuanye, with her flattering and awkward smiles, she preferred this one."]},{"number":210,"title":"Chapter 210: Jing Yi is too scary","paragraphs":["This was Shen Xi's first visit to the Jing family home.","After Jing Yi got injured, Shen Xi had been accompanying the Jing family, waiting for Jing Yi to wake up. However, after just a few days in the hospital, Jing Yi insisted on going home.","If it weren't for the doctor confirming that Jing Yi was fine, Lin Ruiqing and the others wouldn't have agreed.","Shen Xi, however, remained uneasy and started visiting the Jing family every day, almost as if she were living there.","Who could blame her, considering how often this person ended up in the hospital?","Jing Yi savored the dessert made by Aunt Wang, \"Who says I'm in the hospital all the time?\" Shen Xi retorted, \"Don't you remember how many times you've been admitted? Isn't that 'all the time'?\"","She looked at Jing Zejun, seeking support, \"Right, Junjun?\" Jing Zejun just smiled and didn't contradict her.","Shen Xi glanced at Jing Yi, her expression clearly saying, 'See? Everyone thinks so.'","Jing Yi focused on her dessert, and perhaps because she was eating so enthusiastically, Shen Xi also picked up the dessert in front of her and took a taste.","She had often heard Jing Yi praise Aunt Wang's cooking and desserts, claiming there was nothing she couldn't make delicious. Shen Xi wanted to see just how good it was compared to Chen Yisi's cooking.","As the spoon touched her lips, Shen Xi's eyes lit up.","Jing Yi smugly said, \"See? I told you no one can beat Aunt Wang's skills.\" Shen Xi pretended not to hear, burying her head in her dessert.","Jing Yi raised an eyebrow. It seemed Chen Yisi had really captured Shen Xi's heart completely.","Although she had a rough idea of how Chen Yisi had won Shen Xi over, Jing Yi still couldn't help but wonder, \"What kind of magic does Chen Yisi have to make our Miss Shen so infatuated?\"","Jing Zejun quickly leaned in, eager to hear the gossip.","Shen Xi blushed, rarely showing a hint of shyness, which only piqued Jing Yi's curiosity even more. \"Didn't you find it frivolous when he invited you to dinner?\"","Shen Xi quickly defended, \"How could it be frivolous?! He didn't have any ulterior motives like those other guys. He just wanted to invite me to dinner.\"","He would ask her about recipes during their meals, saying he wanted to improve his cooking skills. And then she would always receive small cakes from him.","Jing Yi couldn't help but laugh. She didn't believe that for a second. If he had no intentions, why would he invite Shen Xi to dinner three times a week?","\"And when he confessed to you, didn't you feel any hesitation?\"","She had known Shen Xi for so long, and there were hardly any men who could keep her interest after a confession. So what kind of magic did Chen Yisi possess?","Shen Xi chuckled, \"No, just looking at his face makes me feel butterflies.\"","Jing Yi was stunned, then burst out laughing, collapsing onto Jing Zejun. \"What? So the senior back then just lost to his looks?\"","\"Jing Yi, you're making fun of me!\" Seeing Shen Xi get flustered, Jing Yi quickly wiped her tears and composed herself. \"Sorry, sorry. I'm not making fun of you. I just feel a bit sorry for that senior.\"","Shen Xi huffed. She knew exactly who Jing Yi was talking about. There was no comparison!","Thinking back, that senior was only after the expensive gifts she gave. Chen Yisi was different!","He would make her small cakes!","Speaking of Chen Yisi, Shen Xi remembered something Gu Lin had mentioned recently. She glanced at Jing Yi, who was chatting with Jing Zejun about the reasons Shen Xi had rejected men over the years.","Shen Xi relaxed, relieved that Jing Yi didn't seem too upset. However, she had no intention of telling Jing Yi about Shen Huaichu's current situation.","Gu Lin had said he was very busy, helping Shen Huaichu deal with work at Huarui Group. Apparently, Shen Huaichu had practically moved into the hospital, attending meetings and handling work online, rarely seen by anyone.","She understood what Gu Lin was implying, trying to get some information from her to pass on to Jing Yi, hoping it would make Jing Yi feel sorry for Shen Huaichu.","But Shen Xi was unwilling.","She didn't know what had happened between Jing Yi and Shen Huaichu, nor why Jing Yi had been discharged from the hospital while Shen Huaichu ended up there.","But no matter what happened, she would stand by Jing Yi's side.","Watching Jing Yi's lively expression, Shen Xi smiled.","...","\"Brother.\"","Gu Lin pushed open the door to the hospital room. Shen Huaichu was inside, quietly painting.","Shen Huaichu was undergoing psychological treatment, a secret known only to Gu Lin, not even to Shen Tu.","To the outside world, Shen Huaichu claimed to be on a business trip abroad.","Gu Lin understood why Shen Huaichu was doing this. After all, his long-awaited wish had finally come true. But after seeing Shen Huaichu's state after therapy, he no longer felt so fortunate.","When had he ever seen Shen Huaichu in such a half-dead, pathetic state? So he visited from time to time, mainly to check if the man was still alive.","Earlier, he had inadvertently leaked some information to Shen Xi, but judging by her reaction, she wasn't going to help him.","What a letdown! After sacrificing his pure and innocent friendship, she treated him like this.","Gu Lin leaned in, and sure enough, he saw Jing Yi's radiant smile on the canvas. It seemed that after so many years, his brother's painting skills were still top-notch.","He sighed and shook his head, moving to the sofa. Shen Huaichu's deep affection was downright terrifying, almost too mushy for comfort.","Gu Lin's gaze shifted to the small room inside the ward, its door tightly closed.","The therapist had said it was Shen Huaichu's 'safe room.' Shen Huaichu had requested the most direct form of treatment, and despite the therapist's advice, he had refused to change his mind.","So every time Gu Lin saw Shen Huaichu in this half-dead state, it was like reliving the trauma, not just memories but also using environmental props to 'return to the present.'","The method was cruel, and the 'safe room' was meant to create a secure space for healing.","Just hearing the term 'safe room' made Gu Lin shudder. He had no desire to see what was inside, but looking at Shen Huaichu's paintings, he could guess. Otherwise, where had all those paintings gone?","Thinking about it made Gu Lin shiver. Jing Yi was too terrifying! How could she turn someone into this in such a short time?","He decided he'd better stay away from relationships for now. It was too scary! Too scary!","Shen Huaichu calmly asked, \"Is there something you need?\" His hand holding the brush remained steady as he focused on his painting.","Gu Lin snapped back to reality. \"Ah? Oh, nothing much. Just checking in on you. Also, my mom's starting to get suspicious. You should call her sometime.\"","Before leaving, Shen Huaichu had worried that Shen Tu might disturb Jing Yi, so he had revealed their breakup.","Shen Tu was furious but didn't interfere much. Poor Gu Lin was left at home, enduring his mother's nagging about his brother."]},{"number":211,"title":"Chapter 211: The Unusual Jing Family","paragraphs":["Shen Huaichu stood in front of the easel, holding a paintbrush, meticulously depicting every detail on the canvas.","Gu Lin asked irritably, \"Brother, are you even listening to me?\" Shen Huaichu finally put down the brush and replied indifferently, \"I heard you. I'll make a call later.\"","Shen Huaichu's gaze remained fixed on the canvas, his eyes soft and filled with affection, as if he were seeing the person he missed through the painting.","Watching him like this, Gu Lin sighed, feeling a mix of embarrassment and heartache.","The worst came when Shen Qi'an discovered this weakness of Shen Huaichu and deliberately staged a car accident.","Shen Huaichu was in the car, trembling violently to the point of almost fainting, his eyes bloodshot.","That was the first time Gu Lin realized the impact of that car accident on Shen Huaichu.","He had thought that after so many years, Shen Huaichu's fear had subsided, until he saw Shen Huaichu in a half-conscious state again a few days ago.","Gu Lin had asked Shen Huaichu what was different about this treatment compared to before.","Shen Huaichu replied, \"It's different. Before, it was to remember. Now, it's to forget.\"","Because he had a more important person to protect.","...","Recently, the Jing family has been a bit different.","Jing Yi felt it deeply.","A week ago, Jing Zeqian dragged Jing Yi to 'Startrack' to see the 'S' boy band, which is set to debut next year.","\"This isn't like the last group you saw! These are the real deal, fully packaged and trained by 'Startrack'. You remember, right? I got the list from you...\"","Jing Zeqian was quite enthusiastic, and Jing Yi didn't want to dampen his spirits, but why did they need to come see them specifically?","Jing Yi arrived at the familiar practice room, doing her best to stop Jing Zeqian from pulling her inside, and peeked through the window instead.","Jing Zeqian crouched beside her, watching the sneakily peeking Jing Yi with a complex expression.","Wait, this is his company, why the sneaking around?","Jing Yi put her finger to her lips, signaling Jing Zeqian to be quiet, \"Don't ask, just trust me, I've been through this.\" She leaned in to look at the group of people training inside.","Not bad, they were indeed of higher quality than the last group.","Jing Yi proudly glanced at the person beside her and whispered, \"How is it? Good taste, right?\" These talents were chosen by her from a variety show, and they were bound to be a hit.","Jing Zeqian's eyes sparkled with amusement and he whispered back, \"It's 'Startrack's packaging that's impressive, of course, I'm the one who's really good.\" Jing Yi rolled her eyes at him, \"Yeah, right, you have good taste? What about those who almost debuted before?\"","Of course, it was her taste that was good, she had seen right through those few who were really quite average!","The two of them started arguing by the window, their voices gradually catching the attention of the people inside the practice room. Several of them turned their heads to see their boss crouching by the window, watching them.","The scene was quite unsettling.","The dance teacher came out, looking quite perplexed at Jing Zeqian, who was still half-crouched, \"Mr. Jing, what are you...?\"","Jing Zeqian quickly stood up, \"I'm just showing Yi Yi around, casually looking.\" Jing Yi also quickly added, \"Yes, yes, just casually looking.\"","The dance teacher smiled politely, wondering why they didn't just come in if they wanted to look, instead of peeking from the doorway.","Were they cosplaying as homeroom teachers?","After that, it was only natural for Jing Zeqian to push Jing Yi towards the group of aspiring boy band members, \"This is Yi Yi, my sister. You know she's the one who discovered you, right? You guys can chat, and if necessary, exchange contact information.\"","This time, Jing Yi was truly embarrassed.","A few days ago, Lin Ruiqing and Jing Beicheng took Jing Yi to a gala.","The moment she stepped in, Jing Yi felt something was off, because her dear parents seemed to be extremely, very, and particularly eager for her to meet every single eligible bachelor in Jiangbei.","\"Miss Jing, hello! I'm XXX, I've watched your races, you're really amazing, and I happen to like racing too. Maybe you could teach me sometime?\"","Hmm? This line sounded familiar...","\"Miss Jing! Miss Jing! I'm XXX from XX's family, you look stunning today! By the way, there's a fashion show coming up, are you interested?\"","Why did she have to go to a fashion show just because she looked good? And was this asking her to walk the runway?!","\"Don't listen to him, fashion shows are boring. My family's in the restaurant business, Miss Jing, would you honor us with a visit sometime?\"","What, did she have to specially go and taste his family's food?","\"Miss Jing! My family...\"","Ah!!!!!!","Jing Yi looked pleadingly at Jing Beicheng, hoping someone would save her, or she really couldn't take it anymore!","Instead, she only got an 'I can't help you' look.","Jing Yi: ...Who would've thought, even I have such a day.","After that, Jing Yi became wary of going out, running away like a rabbit at the mere mention of it.","She collapsed on the sofa, looking at Jing Zeqian, who had finally been sent away, feeling quite troubled.","How could she tell them that she really didn't need 'heartbreak therapy'!","Jing Zeyou, sitting nearby, couldn't help but smile, thinking for a moment, he said seriously, \"You don't have anything planned tomorrow, do you? How about going to Hengjing with me?\" Not joining in felt like missing out on something.","Jing Yi leaned back on the sofa, slowly turning her head to look at Jing Zeyou, forcing a smile, \"May I ask what I'm supposed to do at Hengjing?\"","Even her eldest brother wanted to get involved?!","Jing Zeyou thought of the personnel from various departments in the company, and it seemed there were a few good-looking ones, \"There are handsome guys among the tech talents too.\"","Jing Yi couldn't help but roll her eyes.","Jing Zejun, struggling to suppress his laughter, suggested, \"Or why don't you come to the set with me?\" When it came to handsome guys, where else could there be more than in the entertainment industry? Especially since her current crew was brimming with them.","\"Please, don't make it any worse.\"","She was already feeling overwhelmed, and these two were just watching the fun! Where was their conscience? Empathy? Love?","Jing Zeyou and Jing Zejun exchanged glances and both laughed.","Jing Zejun naturally knew that Jing Yi had nothing going on, and compared to Jing Zeqian's concern about her heartbreak, she felt Jing Yi seemed much more relaxed.","As for Jing Zeyou, after guessing Shen Huaichu's intentions, his worry had eased a bit.","Seeing Jing Yi looking utterly defeated, Jing Zeyou finally stopped laughing and couldn't bear to let his sister suffer too much, \"I'll talk to Zeqian.\"","Lin Ruiqing was fine, knowing Jing Yi didn't like it, so she didn't push the idea, but Jing Zeqian was persistent, which was why Jing Yi was so troubled.","Jing Zeyou suspected that apart from worrying about Jing Yi's heartbreak, his brother was at least one-third motivated by the desire to dig the corner of Shen Huaichu."]},{"number":212,"title":"Chapter 212: Are You Going Back to Berlin","paragraphs":["The matter of 'making friends' had finally come to a temporary end, and Jing Yi quietly dropped another 'bomb.'","\"You're going back to Berlin?!\"","Jing Yi was currently discussing the matter of going abroad with her family.","Lin Ruiqing was a bit surprised. \"Why the sudden decision to go back?\" Could it be because of the recent pressure to make friends?","In fact, Jing Yi had thought of this idea since she woke up. Too many things had happened recently, and she suddenly felt the urge to go back and revisit the place where she had first arrived. It was just that she hadn't had the chance to bring it up until now, as she had been busy making new friends...","Jing Zeyou pondered for a moment, then calmly said, \"I'll arrange it, and I'll accompany you back.\" Jing Zejun and Jing Zeqian also nodded hastily, \"We'll go with you.\"","Jing Yi chuckled, \"Why do you all need to accompany me? You all have your own work to do.\"","Jing Zeyou had to go to work, which was a given. Jing Zeqian's 'Startrack' had an important anniversary event, and Jing Zejun also had to join a film crew.","As for Lin Ruiqing and her husband, Jing Yi didn't want them to go through the trouble of accompanying her.","Besides, she wasn't a minor anymore; she was just going abroad to take a look. Why was everyone so worried?","Although Jing Yi said that, the others still couldn't help but worry.","Especially Jing Zeqian and the others, who were already concerned about the impact of Jing Yi's breakup. Now that she was planning to go abroad alone, how could they not be worried?","Jing Zeyou frowned slightly, \"I can arrange my work, or handle it online.\" He knew Jing Yi wasn't that upset, but that didn't mean he was comfortable letting her go alone to recover.","Jing Zejun thought for a moment, \"I can ask the crew to adjust the schedule.\" Jing Yi's injuries had just healed, and he couldn't bear the thought of her going far away alone.","Seeing that he was left out, Jing Zeqian became a bit anxious, \"It's just the anniversary, it's not that important!\" He was sure Jing Yi was going to heal her broken heart, and as her most considerate brother, how could he miss it?","Jing Beicheng comforted the slightly anxious Lin Ruiqing, quietly watching the siblings discuss the matter.","Jing Yi silently looked at Jing Zeqian, pretending to complain, \"The tenth anniversary isn't important? Mr. Jing, how can you be such a CEO?\" Jing Zeqian was rendered speechless; he was just worried about Jing Yi!","Jing Yi looked at everyone and reiterated, \"I really am fine. I'm not going to clear my mind; I just suddenly felt like going back to take a look. Besides, the finals are still months away; I can't be training every day, can I?\"","Moreover, forget about training; she had been busy going out to meet new friends recently.","Jing Zeqian, Lin Ruiqing: ...How much did she resent going out to make friends?","Seeing that they were still hesitant, Jing Yi continued, \"Besides, the finals are also going to be held in Berlin, so consider it me going early to check out the venue?\"","Although this was also a pretext Jing Yi had thought of in advance, it wasn't entirely wrong.","Seeing that Jing Yi had made up her mind, Jing Zeyou and the others didn't say much more.","...","On the day of her departure, Jing Beicheng arranged for the Jing family's private jet, the same one Jing Yi had returned on.","Lin Ruiqing and Jing Zejun held Jing Yi's hand and gave her detailed instructions, covering everything from food to clothing to accommodation, as if they were worried she wouldn't adapt to life abroad.","Even Jing Beicheng couldn't help but add, \"The plane will land in Berlin, and we'll pick you up directly when you return.\"","How had they already started discussing her return?","Jing Yi chuckled, \"Mom and Dad, I'm just going for a short while, and I'm not not coming back.\" But deep down, she felt a warmth in her heart.","Jing Zeyou stepped forward, patted her shoulder, and said, \"Remember to call me if anything happens.\"","Jing Zeqian's reluctance was more apparent, and he was also more verbose, \"...It's an unfamiliar place, so far away, you have to be careful, okay?\"","Jing Yi was helpless. She really had to say, \"Second Brother, have you forgotten that I grew up there?\" Not just Jing Zeqian, but it seemed like the whole family had forgotten this.","She had spent several years there, and even though she had been back in the country for a while, she wasn't exactly a stranger to the place, was she?","Jing Zeqian was stunned, and Lin Ruiqing and the others also seemed to just realize this.","They had been so worried lately that they had actually forgotten about it!","The plane took off, and the sunlight stretched the shadows of the Jing family members, lengthening the melancholy in their hearts.","Jing Beicheng supported Lin Ruiqing and sighed softly, \"Let's go.\"","Jing Zeqian lingered behind, glancing one last time at the disappearing plane before quickly catching up with the rest of the Jing family.","\"Do you think Jing Yi really isn't going there to heal her heart?\" He still felt that Jing Yi was only seemingly fine on the surface, but deep down, she must be terribly upset.","Speaking of this, Jing Zeqian became furious!","Previously, he had thought that Shen Huaichu wasn't worthy of Jing Yi, but he never expected that the guy would actually dare to break up with her!","Jing Zeqian's words left Jing Zejun a bit surprised, with a touch of disbelief, \"Second Brother, what are you talking about?\" After all, he also thought Shen Huaichu wasn't worthy, so now that they've broken up, why is he still angry at Shen Huaichu?","Jing Zeqian still fumed, \"I didn't approve of him, but that guy actually accepted the breakup so easily...\"","Jing Zejun: ...Otherwise? Would he cling to her and beg for a reunion?","Imagining such a Shen Huaichu, Jing Zejun shuddered; she couldn't accept it, let alone Jing Yi.","Jing Zeyou glanced at Jing Zeqian, who was still passionately venting, \"Don't pay attention to him.\" He already found Shen Huaichu annoying, so no matter what, he wouldn't be satisfied.","Seeing the family silently distancing themselves from him, Jing Zeqian quickly moved closer, trying to find an ally.","\"Brother, aren't you going to ask Shen Huaichu what happened?\"","He was afraid of asking Jing Yi and hitting a sore spot, but Shen Huaichu wasn't off-limits. He wanted to see what that guy had to say for himself for breaking up so decisively!","Once again, he didn't approve of Shen Huaichu, but the fact that he left so easily was really infuriating!","Jing Zeyou didn't want to deal with him, opening the car door for Lin Ruiqing and her husband.","After closing the door and turning around, he found Jing Zeqian still blocking him. Jing Zeyou frowned and pushed him into the car in a few quick moves.","\"Brother!\"","Jing Zeyou was too annoyed to ignore him, \"Why don't you go ask him yourself?\" Jing Zeqian leaned forward, still clinging to Jing Zeyou, \"If I knew where he was, wouldn't I have gone already?\"","It was strange. After Jing Zeqian found out about this, he had planned to go find Shen Huaichu and have a showdown, but the guy had disappeared, claiming to be abroad for an inspection, and he hadn't seen him since.","Jing Zeyou remained silent; he had a rough idea of what was going on, but these were things he couldn't tell Jing Zeqian.","After all, this was Shen Huaichu's own business, at most related to Jing Yi, but she hadn't asked about it yet.","Apparently annoyed by Jing Zeqian, Lin Ruiqing couldn't help but speak up, \"Xiao Qian, don't bother your brother while he's driving.\" She softly muttered, \"He's always been like this, from childhood to now, never getting along with Shen Huaichu.\""]},{"number":213,"title":"Chapter 213: Just a Little Missing Him","paragraphs":["“From childhood to adulthood?”","This was the first time Jing Zeqian had heard Lin Ruiqing mention such a thing. He had originally thought that he had only met Shen Huaichu after the latter returned from abroad. Little did he know that they had met when they were kids?","Lin Ruiqing reminisced about the two boys who had cried their eyes out back then, her lips curling into a smile.","“Yes, from the very first meeting, they were at each other's throats.”","Back then, Jing Zeqian was a mischievous little boy, while Shen Huaichu, who had come with his parents, had the demeanor of a little gentleman. Initially, it was thought that since the two boys were of similar age, they would get along well.","However, within minutes of Shen Huaichu arriving, the two started brawling, each grabbing the other's bow tie and wailing louder than the other, refusing to let go.","Jing Zeyou, hearing this story for the first time from Lin Ruiqing, couldn't help but lean in to hear more details.","As Lin Ruiqing described the scene bit by bit, Jing Zejun couldn't hold back a chuckle, laughing out loud.","Someday, he must tell Yiyi about this. Just imagining the two future CEOs as kids brawling made Jing Zejun's eyes sparkle with amusement.","Jing Zeqian crossed his arms and snorted coldly, “It must be because he was jealous that I looked cooler than him!” This made them true rivals, after all!","Jing Zeyou glanced at his younger brother, Jing Zeqian, not that he looked down on him, but if Shen Huaichu knew he was being called a 'rival' by Jing Zeqian, he probably wouldn't be too pleased.","Lin Ruiqing shot a playful glare at Jing Zeqian. Her youngest son had always been like this, but Shen Huaichu had indeed changed a lot.","Thinking of this, Lin Ruiqing's smile softened a bit. She wondered if there was any fate between Shen Huaichu and Yiyi...","Meanwhile, Shen Huaichu was undergoing treatment.","Sweat had soaked through his clothes, clinging tightly to his skin, and his hair was disheveled.","He took a deep breath, as if each breath drained all his strength.","His hands gripped the armrests of the reclining chair, his fingertips turning white, his back slightly hunched, as if bearing some painful memory. This was a sign of his tension and fear.","This was the disheveled Shen Huaichu that Gu Lin had seen before.","Such treatment sessions were nothing new to the therapist, but today, Shen Huaichu seemed different. His heart appeared to be burdened with a different kind of urgency and pain.","When the treatment ended, Shen Huaichu opened his eyes and gazed out the window, lost in thought.","After he had regained some composure, the therapist asked, “You seemed different today. Is something bothering you?”","Shen Huaichu wearily shook his head, “It's nothing.”","The therapist didn't press further. Compared to the Shen Huaichu from over a decade ago, the current one was much more cooperative.","In fact, the therapist had a good guess as to what was troubling him. After all, there was only one factor that affected Shen Huaichu.","It was probably about that young lady.","...","“Hello? Mom, I've arrived.”","Upon reaching her home in Berlin, Jing Yi immediately called home to report her safe arrival.","Lin Ruiqing was still giving her instructions, occasionally interspersed with Jing Zeqian's voice. Jing Yi listened obediently and hung up after a while.","Jing Yi looked out the window, her lips curving into a faint smile, “Long time no see.”","This was Jing Yi's first home, the home she shared with Grandma Jing.","The building was a British-style standalone villa with a red brick exterior, white wooden window frames, and a black wrought-iron porch and balcony. It was surrounded by tall plane trees and ancient buildings.","In front of the house was the garden, Grandma Jing's favorite spot, where she would often chat with Jing Yi.","Both the house and the garden were well-maintained, looking no different from when she left.","The only difference was that the flowers in the garden had blossomed, creating the fairytale garden that the romantic old lady adored.","Jing Yi went downstairs and placed a photo on a reclining chair. The photo featured a dignified and elegant lady, Grandma Jing's favorite.","“Yiyi, when I'm gone, your uncle, that old stick-in-the-mud, will definitely make me move out, but I do miss your grandpa a bit.”","“If you come back, bring my photo and place it under this maple tree. Make sure it's the prettiest one.”","Jing Yi sat cross-legged beside the reclining chair, the gentle breeze caressing her. At this moment, her heart was at peace, a feeling that only her roots could bring her.","She might travel to many places in the future, and while the Jing family was her home, she might also have her own little family someday.","However, nothing could replace the place it held in her heart.","When she first arrived, Jing Yi was also flustered. She didn't know how to play the role of someone Grandma Jing had known for twenty years, but fortunately, they got along well.","Jing Yi had so much she wanted to tell Grandma Jing, to share with her about the Jing family.","“You said Dad is stubborn, but aren't you the same? It's not entirely your fault, but why not explain yourself?”","The maple tree in front of her swayed gently, as if refuting her words. Jing Yi's eyes softened with a gentle smile, “Alright, I know you had your reasons.”","“Oh, and Dad, he may seem so steady, but he really misses you. If you have time, why not visit him in his dreams?” Jing Beicheng was a very reserved man, but Jing Yi could still see his longing.","“You were right, Mom is indeed a very gentle person, and Junjun really takes after her!”","“And about Big Brother, he's truly a ‘workaholic.’ If you were here, you'd definitely scold him for not knowing how to enjoy life.”","\"Oh, and while you're at it, give my second brother a good scolding for me. Although he apologized, I only forgave him because he looked pitiful. You still need to reprimand him. He lacks common sense and didn't even believe me?\"","She sounded like a younger sister who had been bullied by her older brother, complaining to her parent.","She wanted to complain to Grandma Jing about ‘Jing Yi.’","“You don't know how silly she is. If you ever meet her, you must scold her properly. You can't be biased just because she spent more time with you, okay?”","After all, she had also spent over two years with Grandma Jing, so she could at least be considered a granddaughter, right?","She also wanted to tell Grandma Jing about that person.","“It's kind of strange. Before I liked him, everyone thought he wasn't a good match for me, and I thought so too. I found him annoying, arrogant, and rude, incapable of even thanking someone properly. But, I just fell for him.”","Jing Yi gazed into the distance, her lips curving slightly, “Do you think Dad and the others will have a bit more approval of him when I see him again?”","After Shen Huaichu left, Jing Yi never mentioned him to anyone, and no one ever brought him up to her.","Jing Zeqian and the others were worried she would be sad, but in fact, Jing Yi wasn't sad.","She just missed him a little.","Jing Yi leaned gently against the reclining chair, slowly recounting her experiences to Grandma Jing.","The maple leaves in the garden swayed gently, sunlight filtering through the gaps, casting dappled shadows. Time seemed to stand still in that moment."]},{"number":214,"title":"Chapter 214: Where on Earth Did Your Brother Go","paragraphs":["\"Gu Lin, stop right there!\"","Gu Lin froze in his tracks, his fleeing figure coming to a halt. He could have kept running, but his mother was absolutely furious this time—it wasn't just a matter of being grounded for a week.","Shen Tu stormed up to him, her anger palpable, and without hesitation, she grabbed Gu Lin by the ear.","\"Ouch, ouch, ouch!\"","Shen Tu didn't loosen her grip one bit. \"If it hurts, then spill it! Where on earth did your brother go?!\" Gu Lin winced, his teeth clenched, but he stubbornly remained silent.","Seeing his rare moment of obstinacy, Shen Tu tightened her grip even more, but Gu Lin still didn't budge.","After all, he was her own son. Shen Tu finally let go, though not without a sarcastic remark. \"You're quite the loyal friend, huh?\"","Gu Lin quickly backed away, rubbing his now red ear. \"Mom, Gege just didn't want you to worry.\" It wasn't about loyalty; Shen Huaichu truly didn't want Shen Tu to fret over this. Besides, the treatment was going smoothly anyway.","But how did his mom find out?","When did Shen Tu discover the truth?","Shen Huaichu and Gu Lin had been so seamless in their cover-up that Shen Tu initially believed Shen Huaichu was just burying himself in work to distract himself.","However, over the past few video calls, Shen Tu had started to notice something was off.","He had been very well disguised, his usual aloof demeanor intact, but Shen Tu had watched Shen Huaichu grow up. How could she not sense that something was amiss?","Shen Tu sighed, sitting down on the sofa, her expression tinged with sadness. Gu Lin, seeing her distress, hurried over to comfort her. \"Mom, you can rest assured. Gege is really doing fine. I'm not lying to you!\"","As far as the current treatment progress went, even the therapist had said it was going smoothly.","Shen Tu glanced at him. Was she worried about that?","Of course, she was happy that Shen Huaichu was moving in a positive direction. But the fact that she was the last to know about this—that stung.","Gu Lin hesitated. \"Well, not the last, really. Almost no one knows.\" Shen Tu shot him another look, and Gu Lin promptly shut his mouth.","\"He didn't tell Jing Yi?\"","Gu Lin shook his head. \"No.\" If anyone was the last to know, it would be Jing Yi. At least, that's what Shen Huaichu thought.","Gu Lin glanced at Shen Tu's expression, cautiously asking, \"Mom, should we tell Jing Yi?\" He had always felt that having Jing Yi by his brother's side would make him feel better.","At this, Shen Tu frowned. \"Why tell Jing Yi? This is entirely your brother's own affair.\" Not to mention whether their relationship was still on, even if it was, it was still Shen Huaichu's personal matter.","Gu Lin was taken aback. Didn't his mom just seem worried about his brother? How did she suddenly side with Jing Yi?","Besides, wasn't this whole thing because of Jing Yi?","Shen Tu looked at her son, who clearly hadn't grasped the nuances of love yet, and sighed lightly. \"Because of? Luckily, you're the one saying this. If your brother said it himself, I'd have to give him two slaps.\"","Gu Lin reflexively leaned back, putting some distance between himself and Shen Tu.","Alright, he hadn't been in love before, so it was understandable.","\"Tell Jing Yi, and then have her feel guilty and burdened, staying by your brother's side? Making her give up everything for those two heavy words—'because of'? Xiao Lin, that's not love; it's shackles.\"","As Shen Huaichu's elder, she naturally had the responsibility to worry and care for him. But Jing Yi wasn't.","\"Your brother is seeking treatment because he wants Jing Yi to be free to do whatever she wants without worrying about him. If we use this as an excuse to keep her by his side, that would be terrifying.\"","\"Moreover, he's doing this for himself.\"","Gu Lin was left in a daze, unable to process so much at once. He hadn't considered any of this; he just thought that love meant walking together and facing challenges side by side.","Seeing her son's bewildered expression, Shen Tu softened her tone, gently patting his shoulder.","\"You don't understand now, but someday, you'll meet someone like that. Perhaps you two aren't a perfect match, but you'll still be willing to change and move closer to the person she's meant to be.\"","But this change has nothing to do with anyone else, and there's no ulterior motive behind it.","Gu Lin fell into deep thought, his brows furrowed. This topic was a bit too profound for him.","Shen Tu watched him, her eyes suddenly lighting up as if she had just thought of something. She quickly asked, \"So, which hospital is your brother at?\"","Gu Lin was caught off guard, instinctively replying, \"It's at that... Mom!\" Realizing what he had done, he quickly clamped his mouth shut, his eyes expressing his displeasure.","At his age, could he not be so childish?","Shen Tu's eyes gleamed with a hint of regret. Almost got it out of him. His lips were sealed tight.","Shen Tu didn't dwell on it. If he didn't want to say, then so be it. \"When are you going to see your brother?\" Gu Lin eyed Shen Tu warily. Was she still not giving up?","Shen Tu widened her eyes. \"What kind of look is that?! I'm asking because you need to take some things to him. Your brother is out there, and I don't know what the situation is like. Even if I can't go, I have to prepare some things for you to take, like supplements, and maybe some entertainment...\"","Gu Lin's head was spinning from the barrage of items. He muttered under his breath, \"What entertainment? He's there for treatment, not a vacation...\"","\"What did you say?\"","Gu Lin quickly forced a smile. \"I said he has entertainment—drawing! He's been drawing!\" Shen Tu's eyes lit up, eagerly asking, \"Your brother picked up the paintbrush again?\"","Gu Lin nodded. Yes, everyone was happy about it, except for him, the sole 'victim.'","Shen Huaichu's painting was taught by Shen Tu, but ironically, his own son showed no talent or interest in it.","Shen Tu was so pleased that, had it not been for her brother still hoping Shen Huaichu would take over the family business, she would have definitely pushed for him to pursue art.","Alas, life is unpredictable. After that, she never saw Shen Huaichu pick up a paintbrush again.","Shen Tu's eyes glistened with emotion, a tear threatening to spill. She casually wiped at the corner of her eye, though Gu Lin still noticed.","He coughed lightly, pretending to complain. \"You're happy, but do you know what kind of life I've been living? Once he's better, he really should compensate me properly!\"","Shen Tu's lips curved into a smile as she started listing more items for Gu Lin to take to Shen Huaichu. The stream of words continued without pause.","Gu Lin slumped onto the sofa, feeling utterly defeated. He simply couldn't keep track of all this.","When would this ordeal finally end?"]},{"number":215,"title":"Chapter 215: He is the Monster, You are the Rising Star","paragraphs":["The sunlight filtered through the fine floral white gauze curtains, casting dappled patterns onto the carpet in the room.","Outside the window, the sound of the lake gently lapping against the shore created a mesmerizing scene, with shades of yellow and green blending into an elegant oil painting.","However, Jing Yi had no mood to appreciate these sights today. She had arranged to meet with friends, some of the first she had made in this place.","A black SUV pulled up outside the Berlin International Racetrack.","The roar of racing engines filled the air, and Jing Yi, dressed in a casual denim vest and work pants, walked to the edge of the spectator stands.","Her gaze followed the few racing cars speeding around the track, her eyes brimming with a smile.","Perhaps spotting her figure, the cars gradually came to a halt, and the drivers, having removed their helmets, jumped out of their vehicles.","Jing Yi's lips curled into a smile as she walked towards them.","The first to rush over was a young man with honey-colored, curly short hair, a straight nose, and deep green eyes.","The first time Jing Yi met him, he had completely embodied the image of a noble little prince.","But then this little prince gave her a hug, \"Jing! Long time no see! I missed you so much~\" Despite his towering height, he acted like a little kitten, purring with affection.","By the second day of knowing him, Jing Yi's fantasies about him were completely shattered.","\"Henry, long time no see, I missed you too, but could you loosen up a bit?\"","A pale hand pulled the little prince away, and Jing Yi finally breathed a sigh of relief, only to be immediately smothered in another hug!","\"Jing!\"","\"...Marso, I'm really having trouble breathing.\"","This was Marso, whose angelic appearance and devilish figure were Jing Yi's first impressions of her.","After getting to know her, Jing Yi realized that the devilish traits weren't just her figure but also her personality.","\"Jing, you're so heartless. It's been so long since you came back to see us!\" Henry complained around her.","Jing Yi finally managed to escape Marso's tight embrace, took a few deep breaths, and then the last person stepped forward.","Ross, Jing Yi's racing mentor, the holder of the most championship trophies in GT racing, with dark brown short hair, tall and burly yet gentle and refined.","His most distinctive feature was his pair of pale blue eyes that looked deeply affectionate even at a trash can, which was quite deceptive.","He stepped forward with a gentle smile and gave Jing Yi a hug, \"Jing, congratulations.\" He had watched Jing Yi's racing videos and was impressed by her performance. He hadn't been wrong about her potential.","Henry looked dissatisfied, \"Ross, you're really sly. You promised I'd go first!\" Ross's affectionate eyes looked at him, shrugging, \"Who told you to forget? I gave you plenty of time.\"","Marso didn't join their conversation, instead pulling Jing Yi around on her own. Jing Yi asked curiously, \"Marso, is there something strange about me?\" Marso checked Jing Yi as she replied, \"I need to check your injuries.\"","The previous incident had been such a big deal; how could they not know about it?","Although Jing Yi had assured them she was fine, as fellow racers, they knew all too well the potential harm a car crash could bring.","Jing Yi smiled and pressed down Marso's hand, also stopping Henry from coming closer.","\"I didn't lie to you; I'm really fine. By the way, isn't Benjamin here?\" The most shy friend with a serious appearance.","Henry explained, \"He said he was heartbroken about not passing the regional race, so he went on a trip with his sweetheart. He said sorry and promised to bring you souvenirs when he returns.\"","Souvenirs?","Jing Yi's eyes sparkled with amusement. It seemed friends really do rub off on each other.","\"Let's not talk about that. Jing, how about we race?\" Henry's eyes were filled with anticipation.","His regional race hadn't gone well, but what surprised him more was that Jing Yi had become the champion of the Jiangbei regional race.","He knew Jing Yi had talent, but he hadn't expected her to make such significant progress in such a short time.","Jing Yi's lips curved slightly, revealing a helpless smile, \"Henry, we've just met, and we haven't even had a chance to catch up properly. Do we really have to jump straight into a fierce competition?\" The last four words she said in Chinese.","Henry looked puzzled, emphasizing as he repeated, \"Knife, light, hard? Is it very hard?\" Marso gave him an exasperated look, \"Jing means we've just met; don't rush into a decisive battle right away.\"","She also used a four-character idiom with a mischievous intent.","Henry tilted his head, confused, \"Male and female? Do we have to compete to find out?\" He knew the meaning of these two words; he had always thought he was male, but apparently, it was something determined by a contest?","In comparison, Ross's Chinese was better, \"Jing refers to the atmosphere, synonymous with 'at daggers drawn.'\" Henry's brows furrowed even deeper; he just wanted to race, not to debate idioms.","Jing Yi silently looked at these people. Was there really a need to explain idioms with more idioms?","\"My fault. Are there any cars I can use?\" It was better to end this topic quickly; otherwise, she'd have to explain each idiom one by one.","Ross smiled warmly, his eyes gleaming with a hint of cunning, \"Of course.\" Jing Yi raised an eyebrow; it seemed they were all well-prepared.","Ross and the others led Jing Yi to the garage, where a whole row of Ross's racing cars were parked.","If Jing Yi's racing team was backed by the Jing family exclusively for her, Ross's family was no less impressive. Ross's family was a global top 100 insurance and financial company and also the sponsor of Ross's racing team.","So, seeing a whole row of racing cars, Jing Yi wasn't too surprised.","It seemed she had seen enough of the world; Jing Yi mused to herself as she picked a car that looked familiar, \"This one.\"","Henry, who was also selecting a car, wasn't satisfied, \"Jing! Obviously, this one is better.\" He pointed to another car.","Jing Yi leaned against the car door, calm and composed, \"This small difference isn't enough to help me surpass Ross.\"","Ross was Jing Yi's mentor, and she was well aware of the gap between them. Therefore, it was better to choose a model she was familiar with.","Hearing Jing Yi's words, Ross showed no sign of emotion, remaining warm and composed, \"That's true.\" He acknowledged Jing Yi's progress and abilities, but surpassing him still seemed a bit challenging.","Jing Yi was taken aback and then laughed.","It had been a long time since she had talked to these friends; she had almost forgotten their straightforward nature.","Marso pouted, moving closer to Jing Yi, \"He's a monster, and you're a rising star. Just keep at it; sooner or later, he'll...\" What was that phrase she had been trying to remember for so long?","Jing Yi added with a smile, \"Be left on the beach.\" Marso immediately replied, \"Yes, yes, yes! He'll be left on the racetrack.\"","Henry was amused by Marso's sarcasm and leaned against the car, laughing heartily.","\"Jing, keep it up! You're our last hope. Leave him on the racetrack!\" He had always seen this as his goal, but now it seemed more promising to place his hopes on Jing Yi.","Ross didn't mind the three of them talking about this in front of him, even agreeing, \"Indeed, I do plan to retire in a few years. Winning all the time has become rather dull.\"","The other three: ...Fine, you're the best; you get to decide."]},{"number":216,"title":"Chapter 216: Welcome Banquet at the Old Place","paragraphs":["Four race cars lined up at the starting line.","Jing Yi had chosen a black-and-white racing car, and the gaze beneath her helmet exuded the same sharp determination as always. This race was just a friendly match among friends, but they were also the first group of professional racers Jing Yi had ever met. She wanted to see how far the gap between them had widened now!","As the race began, the roar of engines instantly stirred up the heat of the racetrack.","Jing Yi gripped the steering wheel tightly, focusing intently on the track ahead, expertly maneuvering her car. Before long, she had secured the second position.","Henry and Marso were not to be outdone, closely following behind, the racetrack was filled with the intense atmosphere of competition.","However, among the four cars, a racing car with a black main body and red stripes firmly maintained the leading position.","If you enjoy watching racing events, you must be familiar with that car, which has successfully defended its title as the champion of the GT Challenge Cup multiple times.","Ross's driving skills have almost reached the level of unity between man and car. Whenever Jing Yi attempts to accelerate and overtake, he always manages to skillfully maintain his lead.","Until the last lap, Ross's racing car still maintained a steady lead.","Jing Yi crossed the finish line, looked at the figure in front, and smiled wryly.","Indeed, myths are not so easily surpassed.","The other three were indeed surprised by Jing Yi's racing skills. Henry took off his helmet and strode over.","\"Jing! You've really improved a lot!\"","Henry was convinced. He had not failed to consider the level of the contestants from the Jiangbei branch of Huaguo. Now he finally believed that Jing Yi's winning of the branch championship was definitely not by chance.","Marcel also walked over, his expression of surprise matching Henry's, and Jing Yi laughed and high-fived Marcel.","Although she didn't manage to come in first, she was still very happy to have a lively competition with her friends.","Ross walked over with a smile, patting Jing Yi on the shoulder, \"Great, maybe next time you'll surpass me.\" Jing Yi responded with a sarcastic smile, \"Ross, when did you learn to say such polite words?\"","Ross shrugged, not denying it, \"That's how it is in the world.\" Jingyi looked at him, her eyes expressing exasperation.","Rose's lips curled up, and his pale blue eyes seemed even more affectionate. \"Just kidding, but not next time. Maybe the time after next, though.\"","He even emphasized, \"This time it's not just polite talk.\" Jing Yi shook her head in resignation, her cheeks dimpling slightly with a faint smile.","Henry was too lazy to engage in their polite social conversation and directly interrupted their dialogue, \"Stop talking about things I don't understand. Let's go! The usual place!\"","Jing Yi finally managed to return, so the group naturally wanted to give her a warm welcome.","......","Cheers!","A few people's old haunt is Mazzo's bar in Berlin.","The stage featured a band that Jing Yi was not very familiar with. She put down the bottle in her hand and curiously asked, \"Did Chloe and the others leave?\"","Chloe is Matsuo's boyfriend and the bassist of the bar band before Jingyi left.","Masao nodded nonchalantly, \"He went to pursue his dream.\"","Dreams? Jing Yi was puzzled.","Rose raised an eyebrow, still holding the wine bottle, and explained to Jing Yi, \"She's just joking. Chloe thought she was giving too little, so she went looking for another wealthy woman.\"","Maso laughed, his smile bold and unrestrained, as he raised his wine bottle to clink with Ross, as if finding a kindred spirit.","Jing Yi was also accustomed to the personalities of these two, not really worried, after all, Ma Su was much more carefree than her.","What's more, she doesn't seem to be in a state that requires comfort.","Jing Yi looked at the person lazily leaning against the booth, with golden bangs falling over the forehead, appearing even more mysterious and alluring under the dim lighting.","\"Anyway, I'm bored, so it's a good time to try something new.\" Her gaze was fixed on the lead singer on the stage, who seemed to be constantly watching Matsuo. When she looked over, the singer's performance took on a slightly different meaning.","Jing Yi, who understands the lyrics: ...Is this considered a change of taste, switching from a bassist to a lead singer?","Seeing Jing Yi's complicated expression, Henry mocked, \"Jing, why are you still so stubborn after going back for a trip?\" His tone carried a hint of disdain.","\"...I'm not going there to reform.\"","Jing Yi's almond-shaped eyes silently looked at Ross. In just a few words, he had already received several bottles of wine and contact information from different people.","She really is as amazing as ever, she said those eyes are truly deceptive!","As for Henry, the standards are relatively high, but there's never a shortage of people around him.","It must be said that Jing Yi is indeed an outlier among this group.","Masao put her arm around Jing Yi's shoulder and leaned on her, speaking earnestly: \"Jing, you can't go on like this; you're completely like a little lamb in the eyes of those smelly men.\" She had been worried about this for a long time.","Jing Yi was at a loss whether to laugh or cry. \"Masao, it's just a difference in personality. No matter how much I interact with you, I won't become you.\" She was genuinely worried that Masao might make a comeback and start assigning her tasks crazily again.","Ross called the waiter over and gave some instructions. The frequent advances were starting to annoy him, as he was here today to welcome his friend.","The waiter wasn't doing this for the first time either; he nodded and went to the back to make arrangements.","Compared to Matsuo's concerns, Rose is more worried about Jing Yi's life in a wealthy family, which is not an easy place to live, especially in a family like the Jing's.","\"Masao, don't cause trouble for Jingyi, she has to live within the family.\"","Family?","Jing Yi was slightly stunned; this was the first time she had heard such a term since arriving at the Jing household.","Henry was concerned and asked, \"That's right, I haven't asked about your life after returning. How are you adapting?\"","A warm feeling passed through Jing Yi's heart. \"Don't worry, they treat me very well,\" she said. Ross observed her for a few seconds, and seeing that Jing Yi wasn't forcing herself, he nodded.","Given Jing Beichen's character, he probably wouldn't make things difficult for a little girl.","Seeing this, Maza's concern in her eyes eased a bit. Just as she was about to say something, the lead singer of the band came down.","\"Masao, is this your good friend?\" He appeared to be quite the gentleman, as if merely seeking to meet the friend of his beloved.","But none of the people present were fools.","Jing Yi nodded, about to return a greeting, after all, he was Ma Su's newly appointed boyfriend.","But Maltho's expression cooled down first. She didn't speak to the lead singer, but instead waved her hand to call over the manager of the bar.","\"Jade, change a batch.\"","Several burly men then dragged the lead singer away. He frantically called out for Matsuo, but received no response in the end.","Jing Yi looked puzzledly at Ma Suo, while Ross and Henry, unfazed, raised their bottles and clinked them together.","Henry teased, \"Rose and I were still guessing how long it would take you to replace this person, but we didn't expect it to happen so soon.\"","The lead singer's self-assertion is not the first time, as he is dedicated to getting to know every wealthy and influential friend of Matsuo.","Henry had seen him like this before, but he didn't expect Matsuo to be so straightforward this time."]},{"number":217,"title":"Chapter 217: Big Bad Wolf Catches the Little Lamb","paragraphs":["Suddenly, Jing Yi found herself unprepared for what was happening. The lead singer was dragged off the stage by a group of people, and the rest of the band was quickly ushered away as well.","The patrons in the bar seemed a bit surprised, but their gazes only lingered on the group for a few seconds before they moved on, as if they were used to such occurrences.","Soon, another band took the stage, and the music resumed.","“Marso...”","Jing Yi felt a bit uncomfortable with the other person's gaze, but was it really necessary to act so quickly?","“It's fine to be a little playful usually, but today is a special occasion. He was being too arrogant.”","Marso had never expected loyalty from the other person, just as Chloe had found someone else, but it was crossing the line to involve her friends.","“Jing, see? None of these men are any good. You must remember that...”","Marso didn't think there was anything wrong with saying this in front of the two men. She was seizing every opportunity to give Jing Yi a lesson.","Jing Yi's eyes flickered with a hint of helplessness. How much did they worry about her being deceived? Was her face really that deceptive?","No, something felt off. Even if Marso was concerned, she wouldn't lecture so frequently. So, had something happened? Or did they know something?","Jing Yi couldn't figure it out.","Ross placed the wine bottle against his lips, a casual smile playing on his lips, as if he was hiding some great achievement.","The downside of being in the same industry was that, to keep track of other companies' progress, some important changes couldn't be hidden.","For instance, the Huarui Group, which had recently risen to the top of the market—was it led by Shen Huaichu?","He had to make sure Jing Yi was more cautious.","...","“Chen Yisi!”","Shen Xi ran towards the person not far away with a bright smile.","Chen Yisi smiled back, but the smile quickly faded. If it were any other day, seeing his girlfriend would have made him happy.","But today, there was an extra 'baggage.'","Shen Xi only noticed the person behind him when she reached him. Her round eyes widened, and she saw Chen Yisi's apologetic expression.","She stopped in her tracks, ready to turn and run, but the person behind Chen Yisi didn't let her get away. He quickly stepped forward and grabbed her.","“Little niece, where are you going?”","Yes, the person was Gu Lin.","Seeing Gu Lin's rough actions, Chen Yisi stepped forward to shield Shen Xi, “Go easy on her.” Gu Lin rolled his eyes. He couldn't escape the stench of love wherever he went.","Shen Xi hid behind Chen Yisi, clutching the front of his shirt, peeking at Gu Lin with wary eyes.","Gu Lin stuffed his hands in his pockets, glaring at the two who were clearly on guard against him.","“Hey, hey, hey, aren't you guys a bit too ungrateful? If it weren't for me, you wouldn't have had the chance to meet. Now you're treating me like a ghost?”","Not even a thank-you dinner, and now they looked at him as if he were a monster.","Shen Xi did feel a bit guilty. She slowly stepped out from behind Chen Yisi, her fingers twisting together, “Little cousin, I won't pass on any messages for you.”","She was a bit sorry, but she had to stand by her friend.","Gu Lin sighed, “Who said I wanted you to pass on a message?” Then, his tone turned serious, “Sorry, last time was my fault. It won't happen again.”","After being lectured by Shen Tu, Gu Lin had finally understood. Even if he was a bit dense, he realized his previous actions were inappropriate.","Hearing Gu Lin say that, Shen Xi breathed a sigh of relief, \"Why didn't you say so earlier? I thought you were using Chen Yisi to lure me here!\" Chen Yisi paused, a faint smile tugging at the corners of his mouth, his eyes revealing a hint of helplessness.","Gu Lin unconsciously raised an eyebrow. While it wasn't entirely wrong to say that, it was true that after their last meeting, she had treated him like a plague.","However, his purpose today was simple, “So, shouldn't you treat me to a meal as a matchmaker?”","Chen Yisi smiled warmly, holding Shen Xi's hand and explaining, “Lin insisted on tagging along today, saying he deserved a meal for being our matchmaker.” His eyes carried an apology, “I should have told you earlier. I'm sorry.”","Gu Lin had forbidden him from giving any prior notice, claiming he wanted to give Shen Xi a 'surprise.'","Gu Lin complained, “What do you mean by 'tagging along'? You're really ungrateful. Don't you remember what you...” Chen Yisi shot him a warning look, and Gu Lin raised an eyebrow, not continuing.","Shen Xi didn't care about these details. As long as Gu Lin wasn't here to pry into Jing Yi's affairs, everything was fine.","However, hearing Gu Lin's unfinished words piqued her curiosity, “What happened before?”","Chen Yisi looked down at the person beside him, the gentle smile spreading across his eyebrows, “Don't you remember how I asked him to arrange our meeting?” Gu Lin's eyes held a meaningful look.","It wasn't entirely wrong, but he certainly didn't mention how he had carefully led the little lamb into his trap.","Gu Lin was the first to know about Chen Yisi's feelings. He was quite surprised and nearly knocked over his coffee.","“You really like my little niece?!”","Chen Yisi gracefully handed him a tissue, “It's better not to call her that. Otherwise, I always feel like a...” Yes, that's the word you're thinking of.","After all, Gu Lin's little niece was already in her twenties, old enough to date.","Gu Lin took the tissue, still shocked and a bit puzzled, “So, what do you want to know from me?” He felt his friend was going to be disappointed. He didn't know Shen Xi much longer than Chen Yisi.","Chen Yisi shook his head with a smile, “I just wanted to know if she doesn't like...” He frowned, thinking for a few seconds, then continued, “If she doesn't like it when someone expresses their feelings for her.”","The statement was a bit strange, but it was the conclusion Chen Yisi had drawn after several meetings and had been confirmed by Gu Lin.","Everything after that went smoothly. Unlike what Jing Yi had thought, it wasn't that he disliked Shen Xi, but rather that he deliberately avoided the type of people Shen Xi disliked. Step by step, patiently, he brought her into his own world.","Gu Lin had originally thought his friend was the 'little lamb,' since he had never seen him with a girlfriend before. But he was wrong—once Chen Yisi set his sights on a target, he moved quickly.","In contrast, the 'little vixen' Shen Xi, who he had thought was experienced, turned out to be a blank slate. All her previous rejections had been in vain.","Gu Lin sighed and shook his head. But in the end, it was the same result—a big bad wolf had caught his little lamb.","“Let's go. You can't escape this meal.” Since his brother had guests to entertain, he had nothing to do and was determined to make the most of this opportunity to dine with the couple.","Shen Xi puffed out her cheeks, “Fine, I'll treat you. I wasn't trying to escape.” She was just being teased for 'corrupting' his good friend, and it was a bit much.","Chen Yisi held Shen Xi's hand, his eyes filled with a gentle smile. Only he knew that Gu Lin's words were directed at him."]},{"number":218,"title":"Chapter 218: Jingyi's First Choice","paragraphs":["While Gu Lin was enjoying a hearty meal with Shen Xi and the others, Shen Huaichu was sipping tea with Jing Zeyou in the hospital ward.","Shen Huaichu wasn't surprised that Jing Zeyou had found him here, but he had thought their meeting would happen later, perhaps after he had fully recovered. Thanks to his proactive attitude, the treatment process had been smoother than expected, though still far from pleasant.","He picked up his teacup, took a shallow sip, and frowned slightly, clearly not enjoying the taste. Jing Zeyou noticed this and smiled faintly, saying gently, \"You don't have to accommodate me.\"","In truth, Shen Huaichu's decision to bring out the tea set had also caught Jing Zeyou off guard. Shen Huaichu paused, setting the cup down. He could drink tea, just not the kind Jing Zeyou preferred. He had learned about Jing Zeyou's tea preferences from Jing Yi.","Originally, he had planned to thoroughly understand the likes and dislikes of the Jing family members in preparation for future visits, but he hadn't expected to need that knowledge so soon.","The room fell silent again. Shen Huaichu wasn't a talkative person to begin with, and now, in this situation, he wasn't sure what to say. Should they discuss the collaboration between their companies?","\"Huarui Group recently finalized deals with several major domestic banks. The cooperation between our two companies...\"","\"You've misunderstood. I'm not here to discuss business matters.\"","Jing Zeyou had never doubted Shen Huaichu's capabilities. Even with Shen Huaichu away from the company, Huarui Group's operations hadn't faltered.","Seeing Shen Huaichu's expressionless face, Jing Zeyou felt a sudden urge to tease him.","\"Xiao Qian was worried about you, so he asked me to come and check on you.\"","Shen Huaichu's composure cracked slightly, unable to maintain his usual calm.","\"...That sounds familiar. Did he really just want to make sure I was still alive?\"","The two brothers really were alike!","A glint of amusement flashed in Jing Zeyou's eyes as he said with a smile, \"Just kidding. They don't know about your condition, and I really just came to see how you're doing.\"","Though, mentioning Jing Zeqian's concern wasn't entirely a lie, was it? Seeing the displeasure in Shen Huaichu's eyes, Jing Zeyou decided not to push further.","Shen Huaichu regained his usual stoic expression. \"You've seen for yourself, Jing Director. I'm still in one piece.\"","Jing Zeyou studied him carefully, as if genuinely assessing whether Shen Huaichu was indeed \"in one piece.\"","\"Shen's definition of 'fine' is certainly unique.\"","Shen Huaichu opened his mouth, then closed it again, ultimately choosing to take another sip of tea with a resigned expression.","\"Did you know that Yi Yi went abroad?\" Jing Zeyou suddenly changed the topic.","Shen Huaichu's hand paused slightly as he lifted the teacup.","\"...I knew.\"","A ripple of emotion stirred in his usually calm eyes.","\"So, what are your thoughts on that?\"","Thoughts?","Shen Huaichu leaned back slightly, his gaze falling on the door of the adjacent room.","What thoughts did he have now? He just wanted to see her.","But not yet. At least not until he no longer had to stand at that crossroads.","Looking at the relaxed Jing Zeyou, Shen Huaichu sighed inwardly. He couldn't help but feel a bit envious of this man.","Shen Huaichu knew that the Jing family was Jing Yi's top priority. If one day she had to choose between racing and her family, she would undoubtedly choose her family.","Jing Zeyou didn't seem to mind Shen Huaichu's gaze. He calmly poured himself another cup of tea and set a glass of water in front of Shen Huaichu.","\"Mr. Shen, there's no need to underestimate yourself.\"","Shen Huaichu gave a faint smile, his voice low. \"Jing, do you think it's appropriate for someone who is her first priority to say such things?\"","Jing Zeyou raised an eyebrow, a teasing smile playing on his lips. \"Oh? Do you think you'd be happy if she chose you over us?\"","Shen Huaichu's eyes flickered, and he shifted his gaze back to Jing Zeyou, his expression serious. \"No.\" He would rather not be at that crossroads, forcing Jing Yi to make a difficult choice.","Shen Huaichu had once thought that if Jing Yi chose him, he would be overjoyed. But that all changed the day he overheard Jing Yi saying she had considered giving up racing.","In that moment, Shen Huaichu felt nothing but icy dread. He wondered what he had done to push Jing Yi to the point of considering such a sacrifice.","Jing Zeyou seemed satisfied with this answer, his lips curling into a smile. \"So, President Shen, how do you know we're not the same?\"","Whether or not they were each other's first priority was beside the point. Even if he was, Jing Zeyou would never allow himself to be in a position where he forced Jing Yi to choose between him and something else.","And that was exactly what Shen Huaichu was striving for.","Shen Huaichu's lips twitched slightly as he spoke slowly, \"Thank you, Jing Zong.\"","You're welcome, Manager Shen. It's only right to visit a business partner.","With his task complete, Jing Zeyou decided not to linger. Shen Huaichu probably didn't want anyone to see him in his current state.","Shen Huaichu: \"Take care, Jing Zong.\"","...","Meanwhile, after enjoying a sumptuous meal, Gu Lin received a message from Shen Huaichu, instructing him to take care of his dinner later.","Shen Xi glanced over, but Gu Lin quickly pocketed his phone.","\"Little niece, that's not very polite. How can you sneak a peek at someone else's phone?\"","Shen Xi knew she was in the wrong, but she just wanted to see if the message was from Shen Huaichu.","Gu Lin crossed his arms, his tone both teasing and smug. \"You'll never get any information out of me. Didn't you say you wouldn't pass any news to Jing Yi?\"","Shen Xi looked confused. \"I wasn't going to tell Jing Yi. I'm just a junior, so it's natural for me to care about the health of my elders.\" Her parents and brother had also been feeling a bit strange lately, given that Shen Huaichu's supposed business trip had dragged on longer than expected.","But she had been tight-lipped and hadn't told anyone.","After all, she had to address Shen Huaichu as \"Uncle,\" so regardless of her relationship with Jing Yi, she should show some concern.","Gu Lin: ...","He glared at Chen Yisi, who was trying to stifle her laughter, and forced a smile. \"Little niece, you're quite filial indeed.\"","Shen Xi replied earnestly, \"It's only right. How's Great Uncle's health?\" Although Shen Huaichu could be quite intimidating, he had gone out of his way to win her over for Jing Yi's sake. She felt she owed him some concern.","Gu Lin's fake smile was on the verge of cracking. Shen Xi's serious demeanor left him with nowhere to vent his frustration.","He clenched his teeth. \"He's fine. No missing limbs!\"","Shen Xi, still focused on her meal, replied seriously, \"That's good then. As long as he's fine.\"","Gu Lin: ... Are you practicing tongue twisters here?","He officially declared that he and his brother had no such disrespectful niece as Shen Xi!"]},{"number":219,"title":"Chapter 219: The Troubled Jing Zeqian","paragraphs":["Star Track Entertainment","Wen Qingyan's agent glanced at him subtly, then shifted his gaze to Jing Zeqian, who was busy working at his desk.","One was all smiles, the other all seriousness.","The agent's eyes drifted to the pen in Jing Zeqian's hand, fearing the CEO might snap it in half.","Jing Zeqian looked up. \"Are you that bored?\" He was so busy he barely had time to check on his two younger sisters, yet here this guy was, talking about asset reports in his office?","Wen Qingyan's eyes carried a faint smile. \"Better safe than sorry, Second Brother. You should know these things in advance.\" Though he did have an ulterior motive, waiting to see Jing Zejun's reaction.","That calm demeanor only fueled Jing Zeqian's irritation. Wen Qingyan, however, seemed unfazed, like a pig ready for the boiling water.","Jing Zeqian wished Shen Huaichu could see this guy's face, turning the sorrow of their breakup into anger directed at Wen Qingyan! That way, he wouldn't have to deal with it himself.","The agent quietly tried to minimize his presence, lest he get caught in the crossfire.","He had told Wen Qingyan he didn't want to come, but the guy insisted, saying no one knew his assets better than his agent.","While that was true—he had been Wen Qingyan's agent since the start of his career—it wasn't a good enough reason to endure Jing Zeqian's piercing glares!","Jing Zeqian forced a smile. \"At the company, call me CEO Jing.\" Wen Qingyan still smiled warmly. \"Of course, CEO Jing.\"","Jing Zeqian grew even more annoyed. \"So bored, huh? Wen Qingyan, you don't have much work lately, do you?\" He turned to the agent.","The agent hesitated, exchanging a glance with Wen Qingyan before answering honestly, \"Yes, his schedule hasn't been finalized yet.\"","Wen Qingyan was currently in talks for a new script but hadn't started filming.","Seeing Jing Zeqian's smirk, Wen Qingyan's smile faded slightly, a bad feeling creeping in.","\"FA Company is planning a charity film. They've expressed interest in inviting you. Since you're free, go ahead and participate.\"","More work would keep him busy, away from the office talking nonsense.","Wen Qingyan's expression shifted. He didn't mind doing charity films, but this one for FA Company was set in the desert!","This would not only make him miss his scheduled time with Jing Zejun but also delay their meetings even further once his filming schedule was set.","The agent gave Wen Qingyan a sympathetic look. He had warned him not to come; the guy was just too smug lately.","Jing Zeqian looked at Wen Qingyan, his tone drawn out and slow. \"What? Don't you want to go, Qingyan?\"","Wen Qingyan smiled again. \"No, filming a charity film is such a meaningful endeavor. How could I refuse?\"","In truth, he had a promise with Jing Zejun. If she found out he skipped work to see her...","Jing Zeqian's eyes gleamed with satisfaction. As the boss of Startrack Entertainment, he couldn't let one employee get the better of him.","However, while Jing Zeqian could control Wen Qingyan, he couldn't rein in Jing Zeyou.","\"You're saying my brother went to Berlin?!\" Jing Zeqian exclaimed, incredulous.","Lin Ruiqing had anticipated his reaction and wasn't surprised, continuing to tend to her garden.","\"He should be on the plane by now.\"","She explained slowly that Jing Zeyou wasn't going to Berlin just to see Jing Yi; Hengjing had a collaboration with a company there, so it was just a side trip.","But Jing Zeqian didn't buy it. He was sure even if there was work, Jing Zeyou had deliberately taken it!","How could his brother go see Jing Yiyi behind his back? Was he even his brother anymore?","Lin Ruiqing glanced at Jing Zeqian, who was fuming beside her, shaking her head in helplessness. When would this boy grow up?","Jing Zeqian vented his frustration, then moved closer to Lin Ruiqing. \"Mom, wouldn't you like to go abroad for a trip?\"","Lin Ruiqing didn't spare him a glance. She could read her son's mind from eight hundred meters away!","Jing Beicheng, approaching from the side, overheard. \"Don't bother your mom. We have plans too.\"","Jing Zeqian was surprised. \"Dad, you have plans too? What plans?\"","Jing Beicheng glanced at his youngest son. Wasn't it normal for retired people to have their own things to do?","He took the tools from his wife and continued tending the garden.","Seeing his son still waiting for an answer, he finally replied, \"Your mom and I are planning to visit your grandparents next week.\"","Jing Zeqian was momentarily stunned. \"Why not wait until we're all together?\"","Jing Beicheng and Lin Ruiqing exchanged a look. He turned back to Jing Zeqian, his expression nostalgic.","\"This time, it'll just be your mom and me. You can join us next time.\"","This was something Jing Beicheng and Lin Ruiqing had agreed on earlier, though various matters had delayed it until now.","Jing Zeqian sighed inwardly, his tone tinged with grievance. \"So it's just me again?\"","Lin Ruiqing shot him a look. \"You're not a child anymore. Why are you so clingy?\"","Jing Zeqian pouted, his eyes darting, planning something.","But Lin Ruiqing caught on immediately. \"I'm warning you, Junjun is filming. Don't you dare disturb her!\"","Jing Zeqian: Great, I'm the one whose thoughts are being read.","...","Meanwhile, Jing Zeyou hadn't even arrived yet when Jing Yi received a complaint call from Jing Zeqian.","\"...You don't know how outrageous he is!\"","Jing Yi chuckled helplessly at the rambling complaint. \"But Big Brother said it's for work, didn't he?\" She had just received news that Jing Zeyou was coming to Berlin for a business trip.","Jing Zeqian scoffed on the other end. \"You believe that flimsy excuse?\"","Jing Yi thought Jing Zeyou was genuinely there for work, given her brother's workaholic nature.","Jing Zeqian sighed. He had gotten the same response from Lin Ruiqing. They just didn't understand Jing Zeyou.","He felt it necessary to reinforce their understanding of Jing Zeyou's character!","People like Jing Zeyou, so steady and capable, often get away with little schemes because everyone overlooks them.","Jing Yi couldn't help but laugh. \"Second Brother, you're exaggerating. Besides, Big Brother is just here for work and to see me. What's the big deal?\"","Jing Zeqian snorted. He just couldn't stand it. They had all agreed to focus on work, yet his brother went abroad on his own.","\"Alright, I'll be back soon. It's almost time to pick up Big Brother.\"","Jing Zeyou's flight was about to land, so Jing Yi had to cut off Jing Zeqian's complaints.","Thus, Jing Zeqian left, feeling \"no one understands me; only I see through my brother,\" to go complain to Jing Zejun."]},{"number":220,"title":"Chapter 220: On '染指' and '燃脂'","paragraphs":["Jing Yi hung up the phone and called out to the person not far away.","\"Ross, I need to go pick up my brother.\"","The three people who had been playing nearby gathered around.","They had been racing earlier, but when they heard that Jing Yi had family coming to Berlin, they took the opportunity while Jing Yi was on the phone to get the details from Ross.","Henry loved to join in the fun, especially since he hadn't met Jing Yi's family yet, and had heard they were quite impressive.","\"Jing, let's go together!\"","Jing Yi was puzzled. \"Together? You want to come with me to pick up my brother?\"","Marso crossed her arms and gave Henry a strange look. \"Henry, why are you getting involved in the fun? Jing's brother is here for business.\"","Ross thought the same way. They could visit later, but it was better not to disturb the siblings' reunion. Although he was quite curious about Jing Zeyou.","Ross hadn't taken over the family business yet, so his knowledge of Jing Zeyou was limited to just one banquet.","Henry wasn't happy. He hadn't met Jing's family yet, and he was Jing's good friend. He had heard that in Jing's country, good friends were remembered by each other's parents!","Jing Yi was a bit surprised. \"Henry, where did you learn all this?\"","Although it wasn't entirely wrong, he certainly had a lot of cultural knowledge.","Henry snorted with pride. \"I'm very attentive, aren't I? I'm Jing's best friend, so of course I need to know these things!\"","Jing Yi couldn't help but laugh. She hadn't been wrong; Henry really was like a little prince.","She chuckled. \"Don't worry, Henry. I'll bring him to meet you.\" Her older brother would probably want to meet her friends too.","Henry thought about it. Bringing family to meet them seemed about the same. He shrugged and gave in.","...","On the plane, Jing Zeyou was reading a newspaper when he suddenly sneezed. He glanced at his watch.","This time of day should be when Jing Zeqian gets home. It seemed his younger brother probably knew he was coming to Berlin.","A trace of amusement flashed through Jing Zeyou's eyes as he looked out at the clear sky, feeling quite pleased.","As soon as he exited the airport, Jing Zeyou spotted Jing Yi right away.","Jing Yi's eyes scanned the crowd continuously. When she saw the person she was waiting for, her eyes lit up, and a delighted smile spread across her face.","She ran over, \"Big Brother!\" Her voice was filled with excitement.","Jing Zeyou's lips curved slightly as he reached out to hug Jing Yi, gently patting her on the shoulder.","After the brief hug, Jing Zeyou took the time to observe Jing Yi. \"Have you been having fun these past few days?\"","Jing Yi smiled, her eyes crinkling. \"Not bad.\" Jing Zeyou raised an eyebrow. It seemed she had been having a great time, which explained why she hadn't been home for so long.","\"Let's not talk here. Let's head back first.\" Jing Yi wanted to take Jing Zeyou's suitcase, but he dodged her.","Jing Yi smiled, her eyes crinkling, as she linked arms with Jing Zeyou and walked out of the airport.","\"Big Brother, how long will you be staying in Berlin?\" Jing Yi asked, her eyes on the road as she turned the steering wheel.","\"A week.\"","This time, he had indeed used a business trip as an excuse to come see Jing Yi. He would have to return after at most a week.","Jing Yi wasn't too disappointed. \"Then after your work is done, I'll show you around?\" She enthusiastically told Jing Zeyou about the fun places nearby and her friends.","\"When I was coming, Henry and the others were clamoring to come see you...\"","Jing Yi chattered on about what had happened during this period, and Jing Zeyou listened patiently, his eyes warm.","It was good. It seemed Jing Yi had really been having a great time these past few days.","...","Jing Yi didn't go back on her word. The day after Jing Zeyou finished his work, she brought him to meet her friends.","Henry watched as Jing Zeyou engaged in friendly conversation with Ross, nudging Marso with his shoulder and teasing, \"Marso, aren't you interested?\"","Marso glanced at him and casually said, \"Friend's brother, can't lay a finger on.\"","Henry frowned. \"Soiled hands? What does that mean?\"","Ever since Jing Yi returned, Marso and Ross had been showing off their Chinese skills to him!","It was so annoying! It felt like he was the only one left behind!","Marso rolled her eyes, not in the mood to explain to the troubled little prince, and turned her gaze back to Jing Zeyou.","Indeed, he had an extremely handsome appearance and a great figure, but she preferred more controllable partners.","This kind of person? Not to mention his dazzling background, just his looks made it clear he was unmanageable.","Marso looked him over again, clicked her tongue, and couldn't help but shake her head.","Forget it, she liked the controllable kind.","Seeing the two whispering, Benjamin, who had just returned from a trip with his girlfriend, also came over. \"What are you talking about?\" Henry looked mysterious and whispered, \"We're talking about dabbling in something forbidden.\"","The last two words were in Chinese, as Henry wanted to show off his Chinese skills.","His Chinese skills were, after Ross and Marso, the best among them. The little prince was very proud!","Benjamin slightly frowned, his already serious face looking even more fierce. \"Burning fat? Talking about fitness?\"","He understood.","Marso paused, silently moving away from the two big men who had started discussing.","Over there, Jing Zeyou continued to exchange pleasantries with Ross.","Jing Yi was a bit surprised. This was the first time she had seen such a business-like Ross. Their conversation made it seem like they weren't at a racetrack but at an important business meeting.","It only now occurred to her that Ross was also a proper heir to a wealthy family, so handling such encounters would be second nature to him.","It seemed the racer's aura he had was covering up a lot of other things.","\"Then we'll see each other at the event, Mr. Ross.\"","Jing Zeyou knew of Ross, as his father was the CEO of a well-known insurance and finance company. Later, because of Jing Yi, he also heard about Ross's reputation on the racetrack.","Ross was Jing Yi's biggest rival in this GT Super Cup, so Jing Zeyou had done a little research.","However, Jing Yi's friends were quite interesting, like the two men who were talking louder and louder.","\"It definitely doesn't mean what you said!\"","\"It definitely does! I know Chinese!\"","You know nothing! We weren't talking about fitness!","\"Marso must have said Jing's brother has a great figure, but he's not her type!\"","No way! Marso doesn't like 'White Cut Chicken'!","Marso, who was nearby: I really want to give both of you a knockout blow!","\"Shut up!\"","Seeing Henry about to spill all his preferences, Marso had to speak up.","Jing Yi laughed awkwardly and explained to Jing Zeyou, \"They're joking around, no harm meant.\" Though it was a bit embarrassing.","Jing Zeyou chuckled, not minding at all, and actually found it quite nice.","These were Jing Yi's like-minded friends, and she cared about them a lot."]},{"number":221,"title":"Chapter 221: GT Super Cup Finals","paragraphs":["In the blink of an eye, the first snow had already fallen in Jiangbei, while Berlin was still experiencing some heat. The GT Super Cup finals were right on schedule.","Jing Yi had prepared everything and stood beside her racing car, feeling the vibrations from the track. Her heartbeat pounded like a drum, as this was the 'battlefield' she had dreamed of.","As a top-tier global event, the finals had already sparked a series of discussions online and in real life before they even began.","Jing Yi was among those being discussed, but, as usual, there were not many people who believed in her.","Her gaze shifted to the side, where her family and friends were...","What's that banner?!","What caught her eye was a striking banner featuring her face!! Jing Zeqian and Henry were each holding one end, waving it with great interest.","Jing Yi had already anticipated the upcoming 'social death.' She knew the two might become friends, but certainly not in this way!","Ross, on the other hand, seemed quite intrigued, staring at the banner for a long time before saying seriously, \"They're playing favorites. I should have one too.\" Jing Yi's gaze silently shifted to the other side, where the audience in the stands was holding almost all banners of Ross.","\"Do you even need a banner?\"","Please, as a multi-time consecutive champion, this was completely Ross's home ground!","And perhaps due to Jing Zeqian and Henry's actions, the audience's enthusiasm was already ignited before the race even started. One by one, they began waving banners and shouting Ross's name at the top of their lungs.","Ross smiled and waved back at the stands, which only made the crowd cheer louder, and Jing Zeqian and Henry waved even more vigorously.","Before Jing Yi's ears could be deafened by the cheers, Ross finally stopped.","\"That's different. Yours is more eye-catching.\"","Jing Yi politely smiled. Yes, it was very eye-catching, the kind of eye-catching that made her feel like a spectacle.","The race was about to begin, and the drivers were preparing to get into their cars. Ross glanced at Jing Yi one last time.","\"Jing, you know, I'm waiting for you to beat me.\" He spoke very seriously.","Jing Yi smiled, tapping her helmet and pointing forward, mimicking Ross's victory gesture.","She knew the probability of beating Ross this time was very small, but that didn't matter. What mattered was seeing how far she still had to go to reach Ross's level.","Under her helmet, her light blue eyes sparkled with laughter as Ross turned and entered his car.","The race began! Multiple cars roared with deafening engines.","Jing Yi gently turned the steering wheel, skillfully driving her car through the curves at high speed.","The classic black car quickly took the lead, and Jing Yi's gaze was fixed on it. For her, she could only get closer to success by constantly narrowing the distance between them.","In the middle of the race, Jing Yi was still in the middle of the pack, competing with other cars.","Except for Ross's car, the gap between her and the others was very small, and she could easily be overtaken.","The GT Super Cup was a long race, but the audience in the stands didn't feel bored. Instead, they became more and more excited, closely watching their favorite cars.","Jing Zeqian couldn't sit still and stood by the floor-to-ceiling window, watching Jing Yi's car.","\"Brother, do you think Yi Yi can win?\"","Jing Zeyou glanced at the black car leading the pack and replied, \"What's the standard for winning?\" Jing Zeqian was momentarily stumped.","The standard for winning? Isn't it winning by standing on the podium?","Jing Zeyou didn't think so. He believed Jing Yi must have her own standard for victory. She might not be aiming for a medal but for a personal goal.","Moreover, Ross's abilities were superior to Jing Yi's. A racer who had won the GT Super Cup multiple times in a row wasn't easy to beat.","Henry stroked his chin, circling around Jing Zeyou a few times, as if observing some rare phenomenon.","This drew strange glances from those around them. Jing Zeqian asked, \"Henry, why are you circling around my brother?\"","Of course, it was because he was curious about Jing's older brother.","Henry had always been interested in Jing Zeyou, especially after hearing Ross's description.","He had heard Jing Yi describe Jing Zeyou, as if all the best adjectives were used to describe him. At the time, Henry was a bit unconvinced.","After all, he had known Jing longer and spent more time with her than her older brother. How could he lose to Jing's older brother?","But after hearing Jing Zeyou's words, Henry suddenly felt that what Jing Yi said might actually be true.","\"I originally thought Jing had too much of a filter for her older brother, but it seems really... magical.\"","'Magical' was the word Henry had summarized from Jing Yi's many adjectives.","Magical? Jing Zeyou raised an eyebrow. What kind of adjective is that?","Jing Zeqian, however, didn't have the heart to think about it. He quickly asked, \"How did Yi Yi describe me?\"","Henry, with his innocent, prince-like face, said seriously, \"Jing said you're like a little princess, and we'll become friends.\"","Jing Zeqian: ...","In the VIP box, muffled laughter broke out.","Jing Zeyou's lips curved slightly as his gaze shifted back to the race.","...","As the sky gradually darkened, the race was nearing its end.","Jing Yi slowly caught up with Ross's car, now in the front of the pack.","With the finish line in sight, the familiar soreness spread throughout her body, and she knew she was reaching her limit.","Jing Yi gritted her teeth, gripping the steering wheel tightly, summoning all her strength to accelerate and close the gap with the car in front, sprinting towards the finish line.","However, at the last moment, a blue car from behind also surged forward, seemingly determined to overtake her.","The tense and thrilling chase invigorated the already tired audience once more.","Jing Yi felt the blue car almost overtaking her. She knew that reaching her limit wasn't just about her but also her car.","Any further acceleration would only increase the risk.","In that instant, Jing Yi made a decision.","Her red car slightly slowed down.","Jing Yi focused on the finish line ahead, manipulating the throttle, adjusting the speed and position of her car.","The commentators were relaying her actions, which puzzled many.","Why slow down just before the finish line?","Just as everyone was wondering, Jing Yi's red car gradually approached the blue car, which was still sprinting at full speed.","In the crucial moment before the finish line, Jing Yi once again manipulated the throttle. Her car, like a submarine, disappeared from the opponent's sight.","She used the opponent's car's wake to cross the finish line first by a tiny margin.","Henry pressed his face against the floor-to-ceiling window, his eyes wide as he watched this scene. \"Marso! Benjamin! Did you see that?!\" Marso and Benjamin, who had been watching intently, were also very excited.","\"We saw it! We saw it!\"","Compared to the joy of the Jing family, the three were even more thrilled.","Jing Yi's maneuver as she crossed the finish line was brief but required extremely high skill from the driver. No wonder the three were so excited.","The stands and commentators fell into a brief silence, followed by a huge uproar. They praised, marveled, and shouted."]},{"number":222,"title":"Chapter 222: This is Winning","paragraphs":["The race ended, and Jing Yi removed her helmet, gazing at the results displayed on the big screen.","She had come in second again, was her first thought upon seeing the outcome.","However, this time, she had won!","The stands were echoing with chants of \"Jing Yi! Jing Yi! Jing Yi!\"","How familiar these cheers sounded.","Jing Yi waved her hands toward the stands, her smile dazzling.","Instantly, the cheers from the stands grew even louder.","\"Jing Yi crossed the finish line! Second place! Second place!\"","Jing Zeqian was jumping around like a monkey, just as excited as Henry.","\"I knew Jing would be super amazing! I could tell the first time we met!\"","Marso laughed and patted his head, mercilessly debunking his 'lie', \"How could that be! You only wanted to get to know Jing because she's beautiful!\"","How could Henry have truly seen Jing Yi's potential in racing when they first met in such an environment?","Moreover, the sense of someone speaking on behalf of a relative after they've won an award—where did that come from?","Henry remained excited, \"I have excellent eyesight! I could see that Jing was a natural-born racer!\"","Even the usually quiet Benjamin was flushed with excitement, \"Jing is so amazing, she was so close to Ross!\"","Jing Zeyou pushed away the overly excited Jing Zeqian, watching him and Henry howl with joy, a hint of a smile flickering in his eyes.","His gaze shifted back to the track, where Jing Yi and Ross were still interacting with the audience.","Behind them, the excited cheers of Jing Zeqian and the others continued, but Jing Zeyou didn't find it noisy; the smile remained on his lips.","This moment, Jing Yi's second place had stirred up the emotions of everyone present.","No one felt that she had lost just because she hadn't come in first; this was a victory.","On the racing track,","Ross removed his helmet, hearing the cheers echoing throughout the stadium, and felt no displeasure. His pale blue eyes were filled with joy for Jing Yi's success.","This race, he had given it his all, with no hint of holding back. For people like them, this was the basic respect.","He walked over and sincerely said, \"Jing, you're very impressive!\" Henry and the others were right; she was a dazzling new star, and this battle had been beautifully fought.","Who would have thought that in just three years, that reckless girl who had once stood up for another girl had grown into such a dazzling figure?","The acquaintance between Jing Yi and Ross and the others was a coincidence. It was Henry's whim to try street food, an unexpected encounter with a group of drunks, and the sight of a petite girl shielding another girl behind her.","Ross hadn't intended to get involved; his life philosophy was—it's better to avoid trouble than to seek it. Such situations were best left to professionals.","But before he could even dial the number, Marso had already rushed in, and everything else followed naturally.","Jing Yi called it 'meeting through a fight,' and Ross agreed, later discovering that Jing Yi was very interested in racing.","He had only intended to pass the time, but this delicate girl from the East had given him a big surprise.","He had once been deeply regretful and a bit angry, thinking that Jing Yi didn't love racing as much as he had imagined. Fortunately, she hadn't given up.","Ross's eyes flashed with a hint of relief.","He had a feeling that Jing Yi was very close, close enough that he wouldn't have to wait too long.","Jing Yi smiled, her eyes curving into crescents, her dimples deepening on one side of her mouth, excitement still lingering in her eyes.","\"Ross, you'll have to delay your retirement!\"","Ross's thin lips curved slightly, his pale blue eyes particularly striking, \"No need to delay. You'll surpass me.\" He said it with certainty.","The showdown between Jing Yi and Ross made headlines, and the video of her crossing the finish line again garnered high views.","Media outlets were already vying to interview this 'legendary female racer,' Jing Yi, as she was the only female racer to ever stand on this podium.","However, Jing Yi was unaware of this. At this moment, she was standing on the podium, her apricot eyes shining with joy, as bright as the stars, her hands tightly gripping the trophy in front of her, as if trying to contain her excitement.","Her dream was now within reach.","Jing Zeyou and the others stood not far away. Jing Yi knew they could see her, but she still couldn't help but raise the trophy to them in acknowledgment.","In the next second, the happy smile on Jing Yi's face froze.","Why were Jing Zeqian and Henry still holding that banner?!","Jing Zeyou, standing beside her, had a smile mixed with a hint of helplessness. He had tried to dissuade them, but with Jing Zeqian and Henry together, he simply couldn't control the situation.","Jing Yi quickly retracted her hand, pretending not to see.","Surrounded by a circle of photographers, Jing Yi felt that she might become famous, though not as the GT Super Cup's runner-up.","Ross, however, was still staring at the banner, his expression tinged with regret, as if he was really planning to prepare one for the next race.","Thus, Jing Yi heard him say, \"I'll have your brother send me a link later.\"","\"...Alright.\"","Well, if he likes it, then fine.","Apart from the media for interviews, the racing track had mostly cleared out.","Ross's gaze shifted back, and he suddenly thought of the person he had seen before the race began.","He leaned down close to Jing Yi and whispered, \"Jing, it seems you had a mysterious guest.\" He had come silently and left just as quietly.","Jing Yi didn't initially understand his words, but after a moment, she curved her beautiful eyes, her entire being glowing.","\"Yes, he's my mysterious boyfriend.\"","...","Before the GT Super Cup began,","Shen Huaichu mingled among the crowd, his gaze fixed unwaveringly on the red car on the track.","The surrounding noise, filled with the roar of engines, couldn't draw Shen Huaichu's attention.","He could feel his heart pounding violently in his chest, a sensation that felt different from the usual tension and fear—it was excitement and longing.","The race was intense, with Jing Yi's car sometimes leading and sometimes being overtaken. Shen Huaichu watched her intently, and the constant longing seemed to find a brief release in this moment.","He watched very carefully, and the therapist beside him was also recording his current condition.","The therapist breathed a sigh of relief. When Shen Huaichu had proposed coming to this race, he had been a bit worried. The environment was one of the factors affecting the treatment effect, and Jing Yi was another.","When they met, even he couldn't guarantee that the test would go smoothly.","He had even thought about how the treatment might fall into a difficult situation and how he would proceed with the next steps.","Fortunately, it seemed they were lucky. It appeared that the girl named Jing Yi really had a significant impact on Shen Huaichu.","When Jing Yi crossed the finish line, the audience stood up to cheer and celebrate. Amidst the loud cheers,","Shen Huaichu still gazed at Jing Yi. She was standing on the track, waving to the stands, looking very happy, free and unrestrained—this was the world she loved.","Shen Huaichu's eyes were soft, and the smile on his lips spread naturally.","It seemed he could stay in this world she loved."]},{"number":223,"title":"Chapter 223: Do You Have Your Eye on Her","paragraphs":["“Is she your disciple? The adopted daughter of the Jing family?”","Ross's Father watched Jing Yi being interviewed on the news. Having just won second place in the GT Super Cup, Jing Yi piqued his curiosity.","But what intrigued him even more was her identity as the adopted daughter of the Jing family.","Ross focused intently on the interview, his eyes brimming with amusement. “She’s a friend, not a disciple.”","Meanwhile, the reporter in the news asked Jing Yi about her relationship with Ross.","On the screen, Jing Yi smiled confidently, her dimples deepening on one side, making her look particularly charming.","“Our relationship? There are quite a few—friends, mentor, champion and runner-up. You can pick one.”","The mention of their final relationship left many reporters with sour expressions.","The GT Super Cup’s champion had always been from their country. Now, the second-place spot was suddenly occupied by Jing Yi, a female race car driver from Hua Country, who seemed eager to take the top position.","Many of the reporters were hardcore fans of Ross.","But seeing the Jing family members standing behind Jing Yi, and recalling Ross’s long-standing support for her, the reporters suppressed their urge to stir up trouble.","Ross's Father turned to his son, his sharp eyes gleaming.","Was this the “not a disciple” his son had mentioned?","Like Ross, Ross's Father had light blue eyes, though his were sharper and more calculating.","He suddenly said, “Have you taken a liking to her?”","If Ross were to marry her, it wouldn’t be a bad deal. The Jing family, Hengjing—no matter how he looked at it, his family wouldn’t lose out.","Ross’s expression darkened instantly. He smiled, regaining his usual elegance. His deep, affectionate gaze met his father’s, his lips curling into a charming smile.","“Father, you must know about her relationship with the CEO of Huarui Group.” So there’s no need to test me.","Ross’s lips curved upward. “That trick isn’t very clever.” Ross's Father snorted, his brows furrowing slightly, as if he found the whole thing distasteful. “Stop looking at me with that gaze. It’s disgusting!”","Ross’s smile grew even more pronounced, his eyes gleaming with a hint of mockery.","He leaned back, tapping his fingers idly on the sofa.","“Dear Father, instead of being disgusted by my gaze, perhaps you should worry about the market share Huarui has taken from us.”","Ever since Huarui Group got a new CEO, they’ve been unstoppable. While his family’s focus is on insurance and finance, they’ve still been affected—and not in a good way.","Ross's Father’s face remained stern as he stared at Jing Yi on the screen. “When will you fulfill your promise?”","Ross lounged lazily on the sofa. “I’ve said it before—I’ll take over the family business when I lose. And I haven’t lost yet.”","“Besides, you have several other sons, don’t you?”","Ross's Father’s lips pressed into a thin line. “They can’t compare to you. You’re my son.”","He had many sons, but only this one had brought in enough profit for the company and been groomed for the role for long enough.","He was his best heir!","Ross raised an eyebrow, his light blue eyes filled with even more affection. “Father, I’m truly touched.” Ross's Father’s brows furrowed even deeper. “Ross, what exactly are you dissatisfied with?”","Finding the conversation pointless, Ross averted his gaze and glanced at his watch, then stood up to straighten his sleeves.","His tone was devoid of emotion. “Father, you’re still young. I’ll step down and take over the company when the time comes.”","“But not now.”","Ross's Father finally seemed less displeased. Ross had never broken his promises, but there were still some things he needed to address. “Stay away from Henry and those like him. Don’t get involved with them.”","He had said this many times. He believed Ross was a smart man, and as a smart heir, he should know how to maximize his own interests.","But when it came to Henry and his ilk, his son always seemed to make poor decisions.","Ross’s light blue eyes sharpened momentarily before softening into a tender expression.","“Father, Jing doesn’t inherit the family business either.”","Yet his father had just suggested a marriage between them, all with that “for your own good” expression that was so infuriating.","Jing once said that he looked this way even when looking at a trash can. Didn’t his father know that?","Ross's Father was caught off guard by his son’s defense of those who had no claim to the family inheritance. His light blue eyes flashed with anger.","“But her background is the Jing family! Hengjing Group! And she’s connected to Shen Huaichu!”","Jing Yi’s identity was lacking, to say the least. Their family valued bloodlines above all else. Even if the Jing family was wealthy and prestigious, her status as an adopted daughter still made her a questionable match.","But her boyfriend was Shen Huaichu, and that changed things. Rumor had it that Shen Huaichu was deeply infatuated with her, implying he truly loved her.","If they could secure a relationship with her now, what better way to take down Huarui Group?","Besides, Ross had never been one to care much about relationships. What was he playing at now?","Ross chuckled, his light blue eyes sparkling with impatience. He said coolly, “Father, you’re really not interesting to talk to.”","“If you want me to take over the family business, stop bringing up such topics. I’m not in the mood.”","Henry, Jing—they were his friends. Hadn’t he already told his father that?","Why did he have to repeat himself so many times?","Ross's Father was furious. “You!”","Ross calmly cut him off. “If you’re dissatisfied with me, feel free to choose another heir to groom.”","His brothers would surely be eager to take over.","Ross's Father was livid but knew that none of his illegitimate sons could outsmart Ross. Besides, the CEO of Hengjing Group seemed to hold Jing Yi in high regard.","Given Ross’s connection to the Jing family’s adopted daughter, he couldn’t afford to let go of him.","Ross smiled mockingly, his light blue eyes still brimming with affection.","“So, Father, can you stop bringing this up?”","The phone rang, and Ross picked it up without answering immediately. He had to bid farewell to his dear father first.","“That’s it then. Don’t worry, Father, I’ll step down soon. I’m already tired of it. Also, don’t contact me this month. I’m a bit busy.”","Before his father could erupt in anger, Ross strode out of the white villa, not looking back.","He answered the phone. “Hello, Henry.”","Henry’s energetic voice came through the line. “Ross, get ready! We’re meeting at our usual spot. Jing finally shook off those pesky reporters!”","Ross’s lips curved upward, his light blue eyes looking particularly beautiful as some of the coldness around him dissipated.","“Alright, see you at the usual place.”"]},{"number":224,"title":"Chapter 224: Caught Gu Lin","paragraphs":["When they went to Berlin, they were light as a feather, but upon returning, Jing family's private jet could barely accommodate this group of people.","Jing Yi, Jing Zejun, Shen Xi, and Marso were chatting away, with Henry and Jing Zeqian occasionally interjecting a few words. Benjamin, though quieter, also joined in from time to time.","Jing Zeyou and Ross sat on the other side, discussing work matters.","Jing Beicheng accompanied Lin Ruiqing, talking about Hengjing's annual meeting next week, occasionally glancing at the group of young people.","Lin Ruiqing smiled, \"This is the first time I've felt such liveliness on this plane.\"","Jing Beicheng's eyes showed helplessness, but his lips curved upwards, \"Who says otherwise? Maybe it's time to buy a bigger one?\"","Lin Ruiqing chuckled at her husband, \"No need, they just enjoy gathering together to chat.\" But then she thought, \"But it might be good to have a few more, so when schedules clash, it's easier to arrange.\"","The children are all grown up now, each busy with their own work. It's better to prepare more of these things.","Jing Beicheng opened his mouth, unsure if his wife was trying to save money for him or was worried he might be saving too much.","\"...Alright.\"","...","After the Super Cup ended, Henry insisted on coming to Hua Country with her, claiming it was to relax, and even dragged Ross and the others along.","But he hadn't even participated in the competition, so what was there to relax from?","Still, having friends visit, Jing Yi was quite happy.","A few days later, Jing Yi was no longer happy. She knew Henry was a very energetic person, but she never expected his energy levels to be this extreme!","For several days straight, Jing Yi was almost asleep as soon as her head hit the pillow, only to wake up and start a 'special forces' style tour.","So, Jing Yi handed Henry and Benjamin over to her second brother, since they seemed to get along well. As for Benjamin, a slow-to-warm-up person should be paired with a social butterfly.","Ross, on the other hand, seemed quite interested in Hengjing and had been accompanying her older brother to visit Hengjing these past few days.","As for Marso, she seemed to have found another 'toy'—Li Chengsheng.","Jing Yi had reason to suspect that it was definitely his red hair that attracted her friend!","Finally, she could get some rest!","Jing Yi stretched and was about to lie down when her phone rang.","\"Jing Yi Yi, I caught Gu Lin!\"","Jing Yi's eyes snapped open. Well, there's more work to do!","...","\"Little niece! I thought you were a pure and lovely girl, but you actually used the strategy of 'luring the enemy into a trap'!\"","Gu Lin looked at Shen Xi, who stood in front of him, his eyes filled with disappointment.","Chen Yisi, beside him, sipped some water lightly, smiling at Shen Xi's antics, showing no intention of helping his friend.","\"It's 'catching a turtle in a jar'!\"","\"...\"Can't you say something nicer now that I'm caught?\"","Gu Lin didn't expect the situation to reverse so quickly. Not long ago, he was the one using Chen Yisi to ambush Shen Xi, and now Shen Xi had learned to use Chen Yisi to lure him into a trap.","And his childhood friend! The matchmaker for their relationship! His good friend!","What a heartless guy!","Chen Yisi didn't care about Gu Lin's glare at all, even having the mood to fetch juice for Shen Xi.","\"Tired? Have some juice first. Don't worry, I'm watching him.\"","Gu Lin: ...Heartless!","Shen Xi downed the juice in one go, \"Uncle Gu, why were you avoiding me?\" Gu Lin stared blankly, \"Why were you chasing me?\"","\"I wasn't chasing you!\" She was just blocking him, that's all.","Chen Yisi glanced over, smiling elegantly, \"Mind your words.\"","Gu Lin was speechless, \"Why were you blocking me?\"","\"No, I just wanted to ask you something.\" Gu Lin turned away, not looking at Shen Xi, \"Give up, I'll never tell!\"","\"Is that so?\" Jing Yi walked in from outside the restaurant, smiling at Gu Lin, who was surrounded.","Gu Lin: ...This is it, there's no escape now.","Jing Yi sat in the seat Shen Xi vacated, looking at Gu Lin, who had nowhere to hide, and said impatiently, \"Am I a bomb? Why are you avoiding me so much?\"","She didn't really want to ask Gu Lin anything; she could just go ask Shen Huaichu herself if she had the time.","Well, she wanted to know if her mysterious boyfriend was still alive.","Gu Lin widened his eyes, \"...Isn't that a bit too harsh?\"","Jing Yi smiled faintly, \"So he's still alive, huh? It's been so long without a word.\"","It had been so long since her race, and there was no news. She was beginning to think Ross had seen a ghost that day.","Gu Lin stammered but never got to the point. Jing Yi could tell he wasn't going to spill anything, but seeing Gu Lin like this, that person should be fine.","Jing Yi looked at Chen Yisi, who was now huddled with Shen Xi, discussing the menu.","\"So this is the legendary Mr. Chen.\" The master who had captured Shen Xi.","Seeing that Jing Yi had finished her business, Shen Xi grabbed the menu and moved to her side. Chen Yisi realized too late that his little girlfriend had moved to the other side.","Nice to meet you, Miss Jing. I didn't want to disturb you at the hospital, so let me introduce myself properly. I'm Chen Yisi, Xi Xi's boyfriend.","Judging by appearances, the probability of him winning over Shen Xi was as high as 70%.","\"Nice to meet you, I've heard a lot about you.\"","Shen Xi lightly bumped Jing Yi's shoulder. Don't think she didn't hear the teasing in Jing Yi's tone!","Jing Yi chuckled playfully. It seems Xi Xi isn't being fooled.","The three of them started chatting, none of them paying attention to Gu Lin, who was trapped on the side.","He was getting a bit annoyed, \"You called me here just to watch you guys chat?\" There's no way to leave the protagonist out like this.","Jing Yi blinked, smiling, \"So, are you ready to tell me something?\" Gu Lin shut his mouth again, looking away.","Jing Yi said impatiently, \"You don't talk when I ask, and you complain about being ignored?\"","Gu Lin chuckled a few times, \"Can we talk about something else? Like that move you used to ride the slipstream of the other racer during the final sprint in the Super Cup!\"","That move was really cool. No wonder the whole stadium was shouting like that, and he even forgot his original purpose, his mind filled with the image of Jing Yi crossing the finish line.","Jing Yi's lips curved slightly, \"You were at the scene?\" Gu Lin's face changed, \"No! I, I watched the live broadcast!\"","Jing Yi didn't pursue the matter further. Gu Lin's expression was too obvious to fool anyone.","\"It was just a gamble. There wasn't much time to think.\"","She said it casually, but that video was still being deeply analyzed by various racers and coaches, repeatedly watched and studied.","Gu Lin was no exception. However, being a bit of a relative, asking Jing Yi to teach him shouldn't be too much, right?","Jing Yi and Shen Xi finalized the menu, not even lifting an eyelid.","\"Excuse me, what relationship do we have?\"","Gu Lin was shocked. He was almost ready to call her sister-in-law. Wasn't this just waiting for his brother to get some status?","\"It's a bit because of...\" Jing Yi raised an eyebrow, \"Because of what?\"","Gu Lin retracted his words, forcing a smile, \"Because of my mom.\"","Shen Xi, Chen Yisi: ...You really have guts."]},{"number":225,"title":"Chapter 225: She's Seen This Person","paragraphs":["Jing Yi choked for a moment and, along with Shen Xi and the others, turned to look at the person who was standing there with a stiff neck, looking quite shameless.","\"Auntie isn't here, is she?\"","Speaking of which, maybe she should find a chance to visit Shen Tu. With all the trivial matters piling up recently, it had been quite a while since she last paid a visit.","\"Who said she isn't here?\"","The three people at the table stopped using their utensils and spoke in unison: \"Auntie/Aunt Shen is here?\"","Gu Lin looked at them strangely. \"Didn't I mention it? She's shopping in the mall next door.\"","Jing Yi was speechless. \"Auntie is here, and you didn't invite her to join us?\" Eating here while letting his mother shop alone? Was that appropriate?","Chen Yisi stood up. \"Where is she? I'll go pick her up.\"","He had grown up with Gu Lin, and he treated Shen Tu with the same respect he would his own mother.","Gu Lin hurriedly waved his hand. \"No need! She's with her friends. Someone going would just be a disturbance.\" Or did they really think he was that 'filial'?","The three of them relaxed, and even Chen Yisi felt a bit speechless.","\"You should have said it all.\"","Gu Lin also felt wronged. If it weren't for these people dragging him out to block someone, things wouldn't have turned out like this.","\"Do you really not need to ask Auntie if she wants to join us for dinner?\"","Gu Lin hesitated. If it were just his friends, his mother probably wouldn't have the mood to join them, but with Jing Yi, it would be different. He was sure his mother would come.","However, wouldn't Jing Yi feel awkward?","Thinking this, Gu Lin asked it out loud. \"Don't you feel awkward?\"","Jing Yi was puzzled. \"Why would I feel awkward?\"","Gu Lin started stuttering again. \"It's just that, you and that, you know...\"","Shen Xi, watching Gu Lin's awkwardness, continued eating as if using his embarrassment as a side dish.","\"Little Uncle, are you stuttering?\"","Gu Lin felt embarrassed and angry. \"Go, go, go, kids, stay out of this.\" Shen Xi pouted and whispered to Chen Yisi about how bad her little uncle was.","Jing Yi also found it amusing, her eyes full of laughter. \"What's wrong? Is 'Shen Huaichu' a trigger word? Just call her.\"","Even without the Shen Huaichu connection, she really liked spending time with Shen Tu. No one would refuse the company of a warm person.","Gu Lin: ... Fine, he really couldn't understand any of this.","Gu Lin took out his phone, ready to make the call, but Shen Tu's message arrived first.","\"Hey, guess what? My mom already had dinner with her friends and told me to take care of myself before picking her up.\"","See, only he was the one being snubbed. His dear mother didn't even think of him until after she had finished eating.","Jing Yi couldn't help but smile. \"Then I'll go say hello to Auntie after we finish eating.\"","\"Sure, she's been mentioning you a lot lately.\"","Shen Xi quickly looked up. \"Little Uncle, I'm going too!\" Chen Yisi naturally had no reason not to follow.","\"Alright, everyone can go. We'll surprise her.\"","The three of them: ... You really are 'filial.'","...","The mall Shen Tu was shopping in was part of the Gu family's business. According to Gu Lin, it was \"money going from the left pocket to the right pocket.\"","Shen Xi sighed a little. \"This is really the life of the rich.\" Chen Yisi smiled gently. \"If you like it, I have a few malls too...\"","\"Stop! End of topic, let's hurry and catch up!\"","Chen Yisi's eyes showed a bit of disappointment, but he was pulled along by Shen Xi, quickly catching up with Gu Lin and the others.","The mall was quite large, but there were few people, though the difference in status was evident. For example, the doormen were particularly professional, and their attitude towards Gu Lin was very respectful.","\"Seriously, you really should give me an autograph.\"","\"What are you joking about? I'm not a celebrity, what kind of autograph?\"","\"I'm not joking. People in our circle are all waiting for it!\"","Gu Lin was talking about his friends from the racing circle. Ever since they found out that Jing Yi was on good terms with him, they had been pestering him for autographs.","He didn't even dare tell his brother about this, only mentioning it now while they hadn't met yet.","Jing Yi still hadn't gotten used to the idea of people asking her for autographs.","Gu Lin shook his head. \"You really don't know your current influence. Do you know how we refer to you behind your back?\"","\"How?\"","Gu Lin said mysteriously, \"The Purple Star of the Racing World.\"","Jing Yi's runner-up finish in the Super Cup was nothing short of a sudden emergence. That was the GT Super Cup, a crucial race in a racer's career.","Some people might never stand on that podium until they retired, but Jing Yi, with just two races, had completely cleared that track!","\"...\"","Jing Yi was speechless. This phrase sounded more like something an adolescent would say. She seriously doubted that Gu Lin's friends were all underage kids.","\"Don't touch racing if you're not of age. It's dangerous.\"","\"What do you mean by that?\"","\"It's a compliment.\"","Jing Yi was still discussing racing with Gu Lin when the elevator arrived, and a man was standing inside.","He was dressed well, but his slightly long hair looked a bit messy. He stood in the corner, slightly bowing his head.","Jing Yi glanced at him and then looked away.","Gu Lin pressed the button for the elevator and said, \"Mom and her friends should be on the fifth floor. The mall is undergoing renovations, and they love it...\"","As if hearing Gu Lin's voice, the man in the corner suddenly looked up and then quickly bowed his head again, looking visibly flustered.","Jing Yi narrowed her eyes slightly, her gaze probing. She couldn't see the man's face clearly, but she had a feeling that something wasn't right.","Shen Xi followed Jing Yi's gaze and whispered, \"Yiyi?\"","Jing Yi looked back and shook her head slightly, pushing Shen Xi towards Chen Yisi.","Gu Lin probably sensed the strange atmosphere in the elevator and glanced at the only outsider.","The man kept his head down, and Gu Lin tentatively asked, \"Excuse me, which floor are you going to?\"","The man deliberately spoke in a hoarse voice. \"The fifth floor, I'm going to the fifth floor.\"","What a coincidence?","Gu Lin frowned slightly. This voice sounded a bit familiar?","Gu Lin slowly lowered his head, trying to see the man's face, but to no avail.","Jing Yi's eyes remained vigilant, her body tense.","The man was well-dressed, not out of place in this luxurious mall, but something about him felt off.","The elevator soon reached the fifth floor. Gu Lin stood at the elevator door, and the man stood in the corner, waiting for the others to exit first.","Jing Yi stepped out of the elevator, her gaze still fixed on the man.","Should she tell Gu Lin to have the security guard be on alert?","\"Mom and her friends seem to be over there.\"","Just as Jing Yi was thinking this, Gu Lin's voice sounded. Jing Yi hadn't yet turned her gaze when the man in the elevator lifted his head first.","His entire face was revealed.","Jing Yi's pupils slightly contracted. She had seen this man before!","At the entrance of the Huarui Group, the man who had knelt on the ground pleading with Shen Huaichu!"]},{"number":226,"title":"Chapter 226: Shen Qi'an Why are you here","paragraphs":["Shen Qi An didn't know why the girl next to Gu Lin had been staring at him for so long.","He was on the run, and he had to find Shen Tu before Shen Huaichu's bodyguards caught up with him!","He lowered his head, ready to make a dash for it, but was stopped by Jing Yi.","Shen Qi An was already on edge, and being stopped only added to his panic. In his fluster, he prepared to push Jing Yi aside and escape.","If Jing Yi had only been suspicious before, Shen Qi An's move confirmed her suspicions.","Before he could react, Jing Yi reached out and grabbed his wrist!","Shen Qi An instinctively struggled, but Jing Yi quickly grabbed his elbow joint with her other hand. With a slight twist, she turned his arm around, locking it behind his back, and then pressed down on his neck, forcing him back into the elevator.","The whole incident happened so suddenly, and Jing Yi's movements were smooth and efficient, taking only a few seconds.","By the time the other three reacted, Jing Yi had already subdued him.","Shen Xi's eyes widened as she quickly stepped behind Jing Yi. \"Yiyi, he really is suspicious, isn't he?\"","Chen Yisi was stunned, instinctively moving to protect Shen Xi as she muttered, \"It seems Xi Xi wasn't exaggerating at all.\"","Gu Lin was anxious. \"What's going on? Is this guy trouble? Should I call security?\"","Shen Qi An, pinned in the elevator, couldn't struggle free. He shouted angrily, \"What's the meaning of this? Why are you grabbing me for no reason?! Let me go!\"","Jing Yi's expression was calm as she stared at him with her almond-shaped eyes.","\"Gu Lin, come take a look. Do you recognize him?\"","Gu Lin, who was already on the phone with security, turned to look. After taking a few steps closer and seeing the man's face, his expression changed dramatically.","\"Shen Qi An! Why are you here?!\"","Gu Lin instinctively glanced toward Shen Tu's direction, noticing that they seemed to be looking this way. He hurriedly pressed the elevator button.","The doors closed again.","He asked again, \"Why are you here?!\"","Jing Yi looked over, somewhat surprised to see the usually carefree Gu Lin with such a serious expression.","Shen Qi An, realizing there was no point in hiding anymore, stopped struggling and smiled oddly.","\"Little Lin, is this how you talk to your brother? Why can't I be here? Is this Gu family's mall only for your relatives to shop in?\"","Gu Lin frowned deeply and stepped closer to Shen Qi An.","\"Don't give me that nonsense! How did you escape...?\" Gu Lin glanced at Jing Yi, \"How did you get out?!\"","Thinking of Shen Tu shopping in the mall, Gu Lin's mind raced, and his expression grew even more troubled.","\"Are you here for my mom?\"","Shen Qi An chuckled. \"What's wrong with me visiting my aunt?\" He glanced at Jing Yi, who was still holding him down. \"Why don't you let this lady release me first?\"","Jing Yi didn't loosen her grip in the slightest. Now that she had confirmed his identity, she couldn't let go. Even though she didn't know his intentions, they certainly weren't good.","Besides, Aunt of Shen Huai Chu was still outside.","Gu Lin was about to press for more answers when his phone rang. It was Shen Tu.","With Shen Qi An still here, Gu Lin couldn't answer the call. He couldn't risk Shen Qi An causing a scene and his mother finding out about his situation...","While Gu Lin hesitated, Jing Yi had already decided on a solution.","\"Go see Auntie. I'll keep an eye on him until the people you call arrive.\"","Whether it was security or someone else, they had to get this \"escaped\" man back first.","Gu Lin immediately refused. \"No, it's too dangerous!\"","Maybe Shen Qi An wasn't as physically strong as Jing Yi, but he was a man, and a cunning one at that.","Besides, he knew too many secrets about Shen Huai Chu.","\"Auntie is right there. Aren't you worried she'll see him?\" Gu Lin hesitated. \"No way! If anyone should stay, it's me. You go calm my mom down!\"","Jing Yi frowned slightly, feeling that Gu Lin was being indecisive.","\"Instead of wasting time arguing, why don't you just call the people to watch him!\"","Gu Lin paused, then asked, \"Do you know who he is?\" Shen Qi An also looked over curiously, but Jing Yi only tightened her grip further. \"I've heard of him.\"","Chen Yisi, seeing the two still at a standstill, urged, \"Go on, I'll keep an eye on things here.\"","The phone rang again, and Gu Lin seemed to make up his mind as he looked at Jing Yi.","\"Whatever he says, don't believe it!\"","Gu Lin hurried out of the elevator, glancing back at Jing Yi in the elevator with concern in his eyes.","\"Hey Mom? Oh, I suddenly dropped something and had to go back for it. Yeah, I found it already...\"","...","Shen Qi An was held in a security room, surrounded by a circle of security guards, with Jing Yi still watching him from behind them.","\"Miss Jing, why don't you and Yiyi go upstairs to meet Gu Lin? I'll keep an eye on him.\"","Chen Yisi, though not familiar with Shen Qi An, was well aware of the events surrounding the Shen family. She knew about Shen Qi An's relationship with Shen Huai Chu and also knew about Shen Huai Chu's relationship with Jing Yi.","Jing Yi continued to watch Shen Qi An. \"No, I'm a bit curious about this person.\"","Chen Yisi: ...That's exactly why we want to keep you away from him.","Jing Yi stayed, and Shen Xi naturally stayed by her side.","Hearing their conversation, Shen Qi An smiled, his twisted grin still in place.","\"So you're Jing Yi?\"","He had thought she was Gu Lin's girlfriend, but it turned out she was the girlfriend of that other person.","Jing Yi crossed her arms, not at all surprised. \"You know me?\"","Shen Qi An tried to adjust his position to feel more comfortable, but as soon as he moved, the surrounding security guards tightened their circle, brandishing their batons at him.","He didn't care, still smiling. \"It's not strange that I know you. What's strange is that you know me.\"","Jing Yi stepped closer, examining Shen Qi An's face. \"You look much older than before.\" If it weren't for his haggard appearance, she wouldn't have recognized him as the man she saw at the Huarui Group entrance.","\"I had the pleasure of seeing you at the Huarui Group entrance.\"","Shen Qi An's face darkened as he recalled his desperate plea to Shen Huai Chu at the Huarui Group entrance.","He hadn't expected that among the people there, there would be a Jing Yi.","No wonder Shen Huai Chu had taken a liking to her—she was just as annoying!","Shen Qi An's eyes gleamed with malice, and his twisted smile made his already unkempt appearance even more bizarre. His bangs had grown long enough to cover his eyes, and with that smile, he looked downright eerie.","Shen Xi felt a chill and instinctively moved behind Jing Yi.","Jing Yi gently patted her hand and whispered, \"Why don't you let your boyfriend take you to rest over there?\" Shen Xi shook her head quickly. \"No way, this creepy guy might try something to you. I have to stay and watch.\"","\"There are so many people watching him. What can he do? It's really fine.\"","Shen Xi hesitated, not agreeing, but Jing Yi continued, \"Don't worry, it's all in plain sight. Just sit over there.\"","Jing Yi pointed to a spot that was indeed not far away.","Only then did Shen Xi allow Chen Yisi to lead her over."]},{"number":227,"title":"Chapter 227: What do you think of Shen Huaichu","paragraphs":["After Shen Xi walked away, Jing Yi finally spoke up, her tone sharp. \"What are you doing here?\"","Shen Qi An's lips curled into an eerie smile. \"Didn't I just say it? I came to visit my aunt. She's not just Shen Huaichu's aunt, you know.\" His hands clenched tightly at his sides, as if suppressing something.","Jing Yi didn't respond further. She could guess Shen Qi An's intentions—was he trying to use Shen Tu to bring down Shen Huaichu? How naive. Such a simple plan could go wrong, and yet he took on so much.","Standing still, Jing Yi's expression remained calm, though inwardly she was ranting about Shen Huaichu.","Seeing that Jing Yi had nothing more to say, Shen Qi An felt a pang of frustration. \"Don't you want to ask me anything else?\" He prodded, remembering her curiosity earlier.","Jing Yi clicked her tongue. \"Gu Lin said not to trust anything you say, so you should just say less, and I'll listen less.\"","Shen Qi An's smile faded, replaced by a dark scowl. \"You really trust him that much?\"","Jing Yi feigned ignorance. \"Who? Gu Lin? Well, he's a friend, and I've only met you twice. No reason not to trust him.\"","Shen Qi An's face darkened with a hint of malevolence, but then he suddenly laughed. \"Speaking of which, it's been a while since he came to see me. What's he been up to? Watching your competitions?\"","Jing Yi's lips curved into a smile, though her eyes remained cold. \"I don't know. When he visits you next, you can ask him.\" After all, she was curious too about what he was up to.","Shen Qi An seemed intrigued, leaning slightly forward. \"Have you taken him racing? I've always wanted to take him, but I think he's only good enough for a sports car.\"","Jing Yi's expression instantly turned icy.","Shen Qi An continued describing the scene of taking Shen Huaichu for a ride, his voice brimming with unbridled excitement. \"Back then, he was trembling so much, curled up in the backseat. It's a pity, though. I've always fantasized about taking him racing. I had planned to arrange some races, but they never happened. You have no idea how entertaining it would have been...\"","Before he could finish, Jing Yi strode over, shoving past the security guards and landing a punch squarely on Shen Qi An's face.","The surrounding guards stepped back in shock. Shen Xi and the other person noticed the commotion and hurried over.","Shen Qi An, apparently caught off guard, touched his nose and stared at the blood on his hand, stunned.","Jing Yi crouched in front of him, her face expressionless. \"Didn't I tell you to say less? Can't you understand human speech?\"","Shen Qi An licked his molars, wiping away the blood from his nose. The madness in his eyes intensified. \"So it's mutual, huh? I thought it was just Shen Huaichu's one-sided obsession. Guess he really got lucky, hahaha!\"","The thought seemed to amuse him greatly.","After laughing, Shen Qi An calmed down, though the madness in his eyes remained. \"Mutual feelings are good. Very good. That's how I can feel at ease telling you about Shen Huaichu, before the people he sent arrive.\"","Jing Yi's expression shifted slightly, her body tensing as she continued to watch him.","\"Mr. Chen, take Shen Xi to rest!\"","Chen Yisi glanced at Jing Yi, who was still crouched on the ground, then led the worried Shen Xi away again.","Shen Qi An didn't seem to care and continued speaking. \"You know about my parents, right? The ones who killed Shen Huaichu's parents. His uncle and aunt. My aunt probably thinks Shen Huaichu just sent them to prison. But that's not the case at all!\"","He spoke mysteriously, his tone growing increasingly bizarre.","\"Do you know why I'm out here? Because Shen Huaichu said that as long as I'm out here, they have a chance to live. Do you know what that means?","\"It means they dare not die, no matter what kind of torture they endure!","\"Only my presence ensures that!\"","His excitement grew with each word. \"Last time, I skipped a visit because I couldn't bear it. He's too cruel! Those are my parents! How could I watch them suffer? So I didn't go, and you know what happened?\"","His smile grew even more twisted. \"Their hands are gone! Can you imagine? Last time I saw them, they were fine, and then their hands were just... gone!\"","\"So, what do you think of Shen Huaichu? What do you think of him?\"","His voice was urgent, his eyes burning with curiosity.","Jing Yi stared at the nearly deranged man for a moment, then sighed lightly. \"Shen Qi An, you've got the wrong idea. I'm not some rich heiress or a saintly heroine.\"","Shen Qi An's smile froze, his eyes flickering with anxiety and frustration.","\"You don't believe me?! You can check! The Jing Family has so much influence! You could find out with just a simple inquiry!\"","Jing Yi shook her head in helplessness.","\"You're just hoping I'll think he's cruel and cold-hearted. But even if they were blood relatives, or even enemies, his methods are a bit extreme...\"","She paused, then continued, \"But Shen Qi An, your parents killed his parents, and you've bullied him for over a decade.\"","\"Tit for tat, that's all.\"","She wasn't exactly a saint herself. Accidents, bullying—those needed to be repaid. Otherwise, why endure so many years of abuse?","When you have the power, you take your revenge.","Shen Qi An's expression twisted, his eyes bloodshot.","\"Tit for tat?! Why?! It's been over twenty years! I begged him to let me go, to let them go, but he wouldn't! He wouldn't!\"","His voice cracked with desperation.","\"Tit for tat? Why not just take their lives? Why go this far?!\"","Shen Qi An's voice was hoarse with anguish.","Jing Yi remained calm. \"If I'm not mistaken, the key to this plan is you. As long as he can't use you as leverage, and since you don't want them to suffer...\"","Before she could finish, Shen Qi An immediately retorted, \"Why should I pay?! They're dead, but I'm still young! I'm still young!\"","His eyes, red and filled with malice, burned with hatred.","Jing Yi smiled, though it was a test. She was a well-behaved person, after all, and wouldn't have such dangerous thoughts.","She didn't say anything more, her gaze only deepening Shen Qi An's sense of humiliation.","\"Are you done?\"","Shen Qi An lowered his head, silent, his thoughts unclear.","Jing Yi stood up, stretching lazily.","\"If you're done, you can take out the knife you've been hiding.\"","She had noticed it earlier, tucked into his pocket, not caring if it pricked him.","At these words, Shen Qi An's face turned pale. He turned and pressed himself against the wall, pulling out the knife and waving it wildly.","\"Stay back! Or I'll kill you all! Stay back!\"","The security guards, a step behind, held their batons, cautiously watching Shen Qi An's knife.","\"Miss Jing! Miss Jing! Get behind us!\"","They remembered she was a friend of Gu Lin's and couldn't let her get hurt!","Jing Yi sighed in helplessness. She had allowed him to take out the knife because she was confident. Otherwise, letting it stay in his pocket would be like carrying a ticking bomb.","She found an angle and prepared to kick Shen Qi An.","But someone beat her to it."]},{"number":228,"title":"Chapter 228: It's You Who Doesn't Understand Him","paragraphs":["\"Long time no see, Mr. Li.\"","Jing Yi watched as the bodyguard kicked Shen Qi An to the ground, pinning him down with a knee on his back. The knife was kicked away and landed on the floor. Jing Yi's eyes flashed with disappointment—she had wanted to do it herself. After all, Shen Qi An's earlier words had upset her, and she had been looking forward to taking out her frustration on him.","The bodyguard, unfazed, casually exchanged pleasantries with Jing Yi. \"You can just call me Old Li, Miss Jing.\"","Thankfully, he had arrived just in time! If Jing Yi had been injured or, worse, if Shen Qi An had escaped, his career would have been over!","Jing Yi smiled at Shen Xi, who had rushed over. \"I'm fine, not a single hair out of place.\" She glanced at the bodyguard. \"Tell Shen Huaichu that if he doesn't have the energy, he shouldn't take on so much. It's just a hassle.\"","She wasn't defending Shen Qi An, but she felt that as long as Shen Huaichu kept an eye on him, he wouldn't be able to move on. Sure, he could keep seeking revenge, tormenting his enemy, but each act of vengeance only deepened the memories he was trying to escape.","Her words were subtle, but the bodyguard understood. His expression turned troubled. He could relay the message, but with the complicated relationship between Shen Huaichu and Jing Yi, he wasn't sure how to respond.","Fortunately, Jing Yi didn't wait for an answer. After speaking, she turned to leave.","Shen Qi An, still pinned to the ground, struggled violently, his eyes bloodshot as he glared at Jing Yi's retreating figure.","He was filled with unwillingness—he had finally found an opportunity! And now it was all ruined! He was going back to that dark, suffocating house! Back to watching those two hollow shells of people, day after day!","\"Jing Yi! You don't understand Shen Huaichu at all! Do you really think he's some kind of saint?! One day, these same tactics will be used on you! Just wait!\"","He shouted with all his might, but his voice only betrayed his growing despair and collapse.","The bodyguard was furious, twisting Shen Qi An's right arm viciously. \"Shut your damn mouth! You're talking nonsense!\"","He didn't know what had happened between the two, but his boss was definitely not the kind of person Shen Qi An was making him out to be!","\"Ah!\"","Shen Qi An's face contorted in pain.","Jing Yi paused, turning around calmly amidst Shen Xi's worried gaze. She even smiled, her eyes filled with amusement.","\"Shen Qi An, the one who doesn't understand him... is you.\"","Someone who was willing to endure painful memories and physical agony just to protect her—how could he be a bad person?","Besides, she wasn't exactly a saint herself.","...","Meanwhile, upstairs, Shen Tu and Gu Lin, who seemed a bit distracted, were wandering around.","Shen Tu picked up a luxury handbag from the display and examined it. \"What do you think, Xiao Lin?\"","Gu Lin, staring at his phone, frowned deeply, clearly preoccupied.","When no response came, Shen Tu turned confusedly and put the bag back down.","\"Xiao Lin? What's wrong? You've been distracted all along the way.\"","Gu Lin snapped out of it, quickly shutting his phone and forcing a smile. \"Nothing, Mom. What did you ask me? Was it this bag? It's beautiful. It would look perfect with the cheongsam you bought earlier!\"","Shen Tu looked at the bag in his hand, growing even more puzzled.","Earlier, she had seen Gu Lin walking with a group of people, assuming they were his friends. But after calling him, only he had shown up, claiming he had just gone back to pick up something he had dropped. She had even sent her friends away early for this.","As Shen Tu's gaze lingered, Gu Lin's smile grew increasingly strained.","Had he picked the wrong bag?","A store clerk, standing beside Shen Tu, subtly signaled to Gu Lin, indicating he had indeed grabbed the wrong bag.","Gu Lin quickly switched bags, picking up the one Shen Tu had initially held.","\"Just kidding with you, Mom. It's this one, right? I think both are great. Let's take both.\"","Shen Tu crossed her arms, her expression serious. \"Gu Lin, are you hiding something from me?\"","Gu Lin's eyes darted around nervously. \"No way! How could I be hiding anything from you?\"","Shen Tu: ...Honestly, if you're not good at lying, don't try to lie. You have zero convincing power.","Just as Shen Tu was about to press further, Chen Yisi arrived.","\"Aunt Shen.\"","Shen Tu looked over, her expression brightening. \"Xiao Si, what are you doing here?\"","Chen Yisi glanced at Gu Lin, who seemed to relax a bit, and smiled faintly.","\"I was having dinner with some friends nearby. I heard Gu Lin was here, so I came to check on him.\"","Before Shen Tu could say anything, Gu Lin looked past Chen Yisi, searching.","Why was he alone? Where were Jing Yi and the others? Had they really gone home, heartbroken and disappointed, after hearing what Shen Qi An had said?","No way! His brother had finally come out, and he couldn't let Jing Yi leave now. His brother couldn't handle another round of this, and neither could he!","He had already lost so much weight recently!","Shen Tu, noticing her son's changing expressions, asked confusedly, \"What are you looking at?\"","Gu Lin quickly looked away. \"Ah? Didn't he say he was having dinner with friends? I was just checking if they came along.\"","Chen Yisi, who had been calm, now looked a bit exasperated. If he hadn't come, this guy would have been grilled until there was nothing left of his secrets.","Gu Lin had nothing special going for him, and he wasn't good at lying. His face always gave away his secrets. The only thing he had was a stubborn mouth and a 'pure' demeanor that could soften even the toughest interrogators.","For years, Gu Lin had managed to keep secrets under Shen Tu's watchful eye.","Seeing that Shen Tu was about to ask more questions, Chen Yisi spoke first, smiling. \"They've already gone back. Aunt Shen, did you find anything you like? I can help you pick.\"","Hearing this, Shen Tu's face lit up with joy.","\"That would be great!\"","Her husband and son had terrible taste, always picking the options she didn't like. But Chen Yisi was different—he was patient while shopping with her, and his choices always aligned with her preferences, with good reasoning to back them up.","Chen Yisi smiled and gently guided Shen Tu further into the mall.","\"By the way, how's Xi Xi doing lately?\"","\"She's been learning how to manage the company from her brother, but it seems difficult for her.\"","\"Xi Xi is just not finding her strengths yet. She's actually very smart.\"","\"Exactly. Her family just wants her to learn more for now. Once she finds what she likes, they probably won't push her so hard.\"","\"I think that's good. She's so pure, just like Jing Yi.\"","\"Yes. Oh, and Jing Yi said she'll come visit you tomorrow.\"","\"You saw Jing Yi?!\"","\"No, Xi Xi told me. She said it's a surprise for you.\"","\"Then you have to help me pick out something great! I haven't seen Jing Yi in so long...\"","Left behind, Gu Lin: Wait, did they just leave like that? What about their son standing right here? Was the guy next to her actually her real son?"]},{"number":229,"title":"Chapter 229: He Should Go Find Her","paragraphs":["Chen Yisi and Gu Lin accompanied Shen Tu for a while before sending her back to the Gu residence.","As they walked to the villa, Gu Lin glanced back to make sure no one was following them before whispering, \"Did Shen Qi An say anything to Jing Yi?\"","This matter was incredibly important to him, and he had no mind to accompany Shen Tu shopping, his mind fully occupied with this concern.","Chen Yisi looked at him helplessly, \"...Gu Lin, your 'stealthiness' is a bit too much.\" This term was something Chen Yisi had heard from Shen Xi, and he thought it described Gu Lin perfectly.","Gu Lin glared at his friend. How long had he been dating Shen Xi? And already he had picked up all the bad habits from her!","\"Show some respect! You should call me Little Uncle!\"","Gu Lin tried to assert his seniority, but Chen Yisi didn't seem to think there was anything wrong with it.","\"Little Uncle,\" Chen Yisi said calmly, with a hint of respect.","Changing his way of addressing Gu Lin wasn't difficult for Chen Yisi, but the real challenge was with Shen Xi.","That girl seemed to treat their relationship as just that—a relationship—without any desire to deepen it.","\"...I give up. Let's just call each other what we want,\" Gu Lin said, feeling a shiver run down his spine. He had forgotten that Chen Yisi probably didn't mind changing his way of addressing him.","\"Stop sidetracking. I asked you, did Shen Qi An say anything to Jing Yi?\"","Chen Yisi was helpless. Didn't Gu Lin himself lead the conversation astray?","\"What should be said, and what shouldn't be...\" He paused deliberately, and Gu Lin's eyes gleamed with a hint of hope, \"...nothing was said?\"","Chen Yisi smiled elegantly, \"Everything was said.\"","Gu Lin's shoulders slumped instantly. He should have known. How could Shen Qi An let such an opportunity slip by?","Chen Yisi gently patted his shoulder, \"Don't worry. Jing Yi isn't as fragile as you think.\"","Chen Yisi had heard about Jing Yi from Shen Xi and had seen her from a distance, though only in a hospital setting. He had also seen her online.","To be honest, although he didn't know why Gu Lin was so worried, he didn't think it was necessary.","After all, she was indeed a very outstanding girl.","Shen Tu had said that Jing Yi, like Shen Xi, was a very pure-hearted child.","But Chen Yisi felt that Jing Yi and Shen Xi were completely different in personality.","Shen Xi was indeed innocent, her words and actions reflecting her naivety. It was clear she had been pampered by her family.","But Jing Yi was different. The first time they met officially, she had tested him. Chen Yisi believed that at least part of her actions toward Shen Qi An were a warning to him.","Observing Jing Yi's interactions with Shen Qi An, she was calm and collected, even capable of turning the tables on him.","Such a person didn't need Gu Lin to worry about her.","Hearing Chen Yisi's analysis, Gu Lin sighed. How could he not know how capable she was?","The first time they met, she had already managed to handle his older brother. How could she not be capable?","But being capable or outstanding didn't mean she would steadfastly choose to stand by his older brother's side...","Gu Lin looked at the slightly dim sky in front of him, his mind filled with images of Shen Huaichu from childhood to adulthood.","He had lost his parents; his uncle and aunt had killed them. He wanted revenge, but he had to consider his aunt's feelings, the only relative who had ever been kind to him.","He had hidden his intentions for revenge for over a decade, never revealing a single hint of it. Even after avenging his parents, he feared that Shen Qi An, this ' ticking time bomb,' might affect his aunt.","He had concealed everything. He believed that anyone who saw the dark side of him would not steadfastly choose to stand by his side, not even his own aunt.","That was a Shen Huaichu that even Gu Lin found a bit frightening.","Chen Yisi stepped closer and gently patted Gu Lin's shoulder, \"Gu Lin, you can completely relax.\"","Recalling Jing Yi's response to Shen Qi An, Chen Yisi smiled. She was very steadfast, resolutely choosing to stand by Shen Huaichu's side.","...","\"...Brother, don't be so contradictory.\"","Gu Lin stared blankly at Shen Huaichu, who seemed to be in an unusually good mood.","He had been so worried about his older brother's relationship, and this was all he got?","Hmph, don't think he didn't notice how dark Shen Huaichu's tone had been when he first heard about Shen Qi An's news. And now, just how long had passed? He was practically beaming like a flower.","Ignoring Shen Huaichu, Gu Lin turned to the bodyguard standing nearby, asking, \"Did Jing Yi ask you to pass a message to him?\"","He wanted to see what kind of message could have such a magical effect.","The bodyguard looked awkwardly at Shen Huaichu. After all, his boss was right there. How could he speak?","In a good mood, Shen Huaichu didn't mind and nodded, indicating the bodyguard could speak.","Miss Jing Yi said, \"If you don't have the energy, don't take on so many things. It's just troublesome.\" The words were exactly as Jing Yi had said them.","Gu Lin was surprised. That's it? What did it mean?","Shen Huaichu was also taken aback when he heard it. He hadn't expected such a response.","He had even prepared himself for being hated.","For Shen Huaichu, the existence of these words was akin to admitting he had let himself sink into the mud.","But she hadn't left. She was still there, and with a gentle breeze, he could still smell the scent of life.","\"So, how are you planning to handle Shen Qi An?\"","Now that Shen Huaichu seemed fine, Gu Lin had no interest in their relationship.","Shen Huaichu came back to his senses and said indifferently, \"I've called my people back. No one will continue to watch him or that couple.\"","If she didn't like it, then he wouldn't do it anymore. Ever.","Gu Lin wasn't pleased, \"Aren't you worried he'll come after my mom again?\"","He had heard from Chen Yisi that Shen Qi An had even brought a knife with him when he went. If it weren't for Jing Yi, something might have actually happened.","The bodyguard chimed in, \"Don't worry, Young Master Gu. The boss believes Shen Qi An no longer poses a threat. He's currently in a mental hospital.\"","After being brought back, Shen Qi An's condition had been very unstable.","At first, they thought he was faking it, but the medical reports didn't lie.","Unless Shen Qi An had bribed the hospital.","But that was impossible. If he had the ability to bribe the hospital, he wouldn't have been trapped for so long.","Gu Lin's eyes widened in shock. \"He's really gone crazy?\" That didn't make sense. He hadn't gone crazy before, so why now, after meeting Jing Yi?","The bodyguard glanced at Shen Huaichu. \"According to the hospital's report, yes. But whether it's because of Jing Yi, I don't know.\"","Gu Lin didn't say anything else. His mood was a bit heavy. He wasn't feeling sympathy for Shen Qi An, but rather, he felt that after so many years, this ordeal was finally coming to an end.","He shook his head, trying to clear the complex emotions from his mind. \"Brother, are you ready to be discharged?\"","Shen Huaichu stood up and looked out the window at the sunlight streaming in. His mood was excellent.","\"Yes, I'm ready to be discharged.\"","It was time to go find her."]},{"number":230,"title":"Chapter 230: The Grand Finale Part 01","paragraphs":["As night fell, the grand banquet hall was ablaze with lights, the clinking of glasses and the hum of conversation filling the air. Jing Zeyou concluded the speech segment with a few brief words, officially marking the start of Hengjing Group's annual gala.","As in previous years, the stage featured performances by celebrities voted for by the employees, and the crowd was thoroughly enjoying the show.","Jing Yi swirled the champagne in her glass, her gaze landing on Henry, who was scanning the room, Marso chatting with Jing Zejun, Benjamin, whose intimidating appearance left him sipping alone, and Ross, who had a group of Hengjing Group's female employees flocking around him.","Were these four here just to join the fun at Hengjing's annual gala?","\"Henry, are you looking for someone?\"","Jing Yi was puzzled; she didn't know Henry had any acquaintances at Hengjing.","Henry quickly withdrew his gaze, his smile unusually bright, his honey-colored hair swaying slightly. \"No, no, I'm just curious.\"","What was there to be curious about at an annual gala? She should be the one wondering what these people were doing here.","Just as Jing Yi was about to say something, Marso and Jing Zejun approached.","\"Jing, look! The magic show is starting over there!\" Marso raised his voice slightly as he spoke to Jing Yi.","\"What's so great about a magic show?\"","Though she said that, Jing Yi's gaze still turned toward the stage.","Henry quietly breathed a sigh of relief and quietly made his way toward Ross. At a time like this, how could this guy still be flirting!","And Benjamin! Was this really the time to be drinking?","Henry pulled the two aside, glancing at Jing Yi's direction. \"Hey! This is a crucial moment; can you two take it seriously?!\"","Benjamin felt wronged; no one had even come to chat with him.","Ross raised an eyebrow, lifting his glass toward the girls still watching him from a distance, his pale blue eyes filled with tenderness.","\"The main character hasn't even arrived yet; why are you in such a hurry?\" Seeing the girls' smitten expressions, Ross's lips curled up. \"Besides, Henry, you're too obvious.\"","Henry leaned lazily against the wall, his hands in his trouser pockets, looking even more like a dazzling prince under the sparkling lights.","\"I can't miss such a wonderful scene.\" With that, he glanced toward the entrance once more.","...","On the other side, Jing Zeyou whispered something to Jing Beicheng.","He walked over to Jing Zeqian, who was constantly glancing in the direction Henry was watching.","Jing Zeyou handed him a glass of champagne, his gaze inadvertently glancing at Jing Yi, a smile playing on his lips.","\"Are you waiting for someone?\"","Both Jing Zeqian and Henry were so obvious that they might as well have written 'someone's coming soon' on their faces.","No wonder Jing Yi said these two would definitely get along.","Jing Zeqian paused, quickly withdrew his gaze, coughed lightly, and took the champagne.","\"Brother, aren't you just asking the obvious?\" What else could he be doing? Of course, he was waiting for someone.","Jing Zeyou ignored him and exchanged a few words with passing employees.","He was now feeling a bit regretful. Knowing how obvious these two were, he shouldn't have told them. The show hadn't even officially begun, and they were practically giving away the plot.","Jing Zeqian still couldn't help glancing toward the entrance, a hint of impatience in his eyes.","\"Brother, what's he dragging his feet for? The gala is almost halfway through, and he's still not here. Does he even have any sincerity?\"","Jing Zeyou took a leisurely sip of his drink, his long fingers holding the glass, his profile sharp and elegant, exuding a calm and dignified aura.","\"I don't think I ever said he would appear here.\"","Jing Zeqian's expression changed instantly, his eyes widening as he turned to Jing Zeyou. \"What?! He...?\" Realizing his voice was a bit loud, Jing Zeqian quickly glanced at Jing Yi's direction.","Seeing that Jing Yi was still watching the performance and hadn't noticed, he breathed a sigh of relief and whispered, \"He's not coming? You said he would show up at the gala!\"","If he wasn't coming, why had he stood here for so long? He had even thought of several strategies!","Jing Zeyou remained composed. \"He'll show up, just not in the main hall.\" It was obvious that this was Hengjing Group's annual gala; he wouldn't let that person make a grand entrance here.","Jing Zeqian was rendered speechless by his brother. \"Then why did I stand here for so long? Why didn't you tell me earlier?\"","Jing Zeyou certainly wouldn't admit to his mischievous intentions, smiling warmly. \"I just thought you and Henry were expecting a friend.\"","Jing Zeqian: ...I spit!","But he didn't dare push it too far, as he still needed to get some insider information from Jing Zeyou.","\"Brother, where will he be?\"","Jing Zeyou raised his eyebrows, his thin lips uttering two words: \"The lighthouse.\" The place by the riverside behind the banquet.","Jing Zeqian's eyes lit up, and he set down his champagne, heading toward Henry's direction.","Jing Zeyou watched the two conspirators whispering behind their backs, a smile tugging at his lips as he finished his champagne in one gulp.","He had done his part; a little gift shouldn't hurt, right?","On the stage, the lights gradually dimmed, and intense spotlights illuminated the entire stage as Hengjing Group employees cheered and applauded the just-concluded performance.","The members of 'Startrack' stood there, slightly out of breath, fine beads of sweat on their foreheads, their smiles radiant as they greeted the audience.","In the midst of increasingly enthusiastic cheers, the members stepped down.","No wonder it was Hengjing Group's annual gala; the scale was no less than that of a grand event. Lu Yichi thought as he watched the young man rushing off the stage. It wasn't easy; they all had tasks to fulfill.","Before the banquet began, Lu Yichi had seen the company's upcoming boy band standing in front of him, and he hadn't reacted immediately.","He opened his mouth, disbelief evident. \"...Did President Jing send you here?\" The handsome boys nodded shyly.","Lu Yichi's expression grew even more complicated. Just who was this big shot that President Jing would go to such lengths?","...","On the other side, Jing Zejun, who was accompanying Jing Yi to watch the performance, looked at the undercurrents in the banquet hall with a similarly complex expression, even a hint of sympathy.","Maybe Qing Yan should prepare a bit more; this lineup might be too much for him to handle.","Jing Yi noticed Jing Zejun's absent-mindedness. \"Junjun, what's wrong?\" Marso, who was also lost in thought, looked over.","Jing Zejun came back to his senses, smiling gently. \"It's nothing, just thinking about the script.\"","Jing Yi noticed that Henry and Jing Zeqian were nowhere to be seen. She looked around. \"Where are Second Brother and Henry?\"","Jing Zejun's heart skipped a beat. \"Maybe they went somewhere to chat; they seem to get along well.\" Marso chimed in, \"Exactly, don't worry about Henry; he knows how to keep himself entertained. He won't let himself get bored.\"","Jing Yi felt even more uneasy, sensing that everyone seemed to be up to something.","\"Junjun, you guys seem off.\"","Jing Zejun's expression stiffened for a moment, and Marso's eyes also flashed with panic.","Seeing this, Jing Yi was even more convinced of her suspicions. They were definitely hiding something from her!","Jing Yi gave them a triumphant look. \"Gotcha! What are you hiding from me? And what are Second Brother and the others up to?\"","As the two were brainstorming how to cover up, Lu Yichi had already changed into a white suit and walked over, followed by a group of male band members in matching outfits.","Jing Yi: Suddenly, it felt oddly familiar..."]},{"number":231,"title":"Chapter 231: The Grand Finale Part 02","paragraphs":["\"Chen Yisi, hurry up! We're going to be late!\"","Shen Xi shouted to Chen Yisi, who was behind her. He smiled gently and strode over with long steps.","\"No need to rush. Xiao Lin said Shen Huaichu just arrived too.\"","Shen Xi pulled him forward, \"That won't do. We need to secure a good corner first, or there won't be any space for just the two of us.\"","Chen Yisi chuckled helplessly, resignedly holding Shen Xi's hand as they ran toward the Hengjing annual party venue.","Meanwhile, at the lighthouse, Shen Huaichu waited.","He seemed a bit nervous, straightening his collar, adjusting his tie, and smoothing out the creases in his cuffs.","When footsteps echoed from behind, Shen Huaichu's heart raced like a drum. He turned around, and the smile froze on his lips.","He took a deep breath, staring at the two men in front of him. Who else could it be but Jing Zeqian!","Jing Zeqian, seeing the familiar \"ghostly\" expression, looked even more smug.","\"Shen Huaichu, long time no see. Are you happy to see me?\"","Henry, who had been curious about Jing Yi's man for a long time, glanced at Jing Zeqian upon hearing his words. No wonder he was such a good friend; he really suited his taste!","Shen Huaichu's lips curled into a fake smile, \"Long time no see, not at all!\" He said through gritted teeth, and Jing Zeqian's smile deepened.","\"Oh, let me introduce you. This is Yi Yi's friend, Henry.\"","Shen Huaichu was almost out of patience with Jing Zeqian. Where did he have the mood to make new friends now?","\"...Hello, Shen Huaichu.\"","Jing Zeqian nodded in satisfaction, seeing that he was cooperative.","\"Hello, Henry.\"","Henry leaned closer to Jing Zeqian and whispered, \"Aren't you afraid he'll punch you?\" He asked sincerely, and Jing Zeqian raised an eyebrow. \"Why would I? If he dares to raise a hand, I'll go tell Yi Yi.\"","Henry glanced at Shen Huaichu, whose face was slightly pale, and secretly gave Jing Zeqian a thumbs up. He still had a lot to learn; he must ask Jing Zeqian for advice when the opportunity arose.","Shen Huaichu was growing impatient. He glanced behind Jing Zeqian but saw no one, his eyes flashing with disappointment.","Jing Zeqian crossed his arms, looking as smug as ever. \"Oh, I forgot to tell you. Yi Yi is in the hall.\" He emphasized, \"I asked her to guide a few guys from Startrack. She's busy.\"","If he didn't teach this guy a lesson, he'd really think Jing Yi would wait for him forever.","Shen Huaichu paused, \"...You win.\" He strode past Jing Zeqian toward the hall, his steps looking somewhat hurried.","As soon as Shen Huaichu was out of sight, the two men quickly followed, trying to find a good spot to watch the show.","In the banquet hall.","Jing Yi was initially a bit uneasy, thinking it was yet another \"large-scale matchmaking event\" orchestrated by her brother.","But she quite enjoyed chatting with Lu Yichi, and the few male group members seemed even more nervous than she was. Gradually, Jing Yi relaxed.","\"Is that so? I thought you'd be acting next.\"","Lu Yichi smiled brightly, \"My acting skills are nothing to write home about. Next time, I'll let you see how good Jing Zeqian is—he says he could act better with his feet than I can.\"","Jing Yi laughed, her eyes curving into crescents. \"Then next time, I'll have him act with his feet for you.\" Lu Yichi was taken aback, his smile widening. \"No, that's okay. If it comes to that, I wouldn't dare watch.\"","When Shen Huaichu arrived, he saw this \"beautiful\" scene: a man in a straight white suit, Jing Yi standing beside him, wearing a black velvet long dress, her slightly curled hair tied up high, a few strands falling on her cheeks.","She smiled brightly, and one might mistake it for a wedding scene. Shen Huaichu thought sourly.","At that moment, their eyes met, and time seemed to stand still.","Lu Yichi looked toward Jing Yi's direction, where a tall, elegant, and aloof man stood.","Was he the main character of this drama?","Jing Yi stared at Shen Huaichu, her mind blank.","He seemed to have lost some weight.","After a long while, Jing Yi snapped back to reality and continued talking to Lu Yichi, her lips curving slightly, her eyes hiding a smile.","Shen Huaichu's expression faltered for a moment before softening. He slowly walked over to Jing Yi's side.","With the intention of fulfilling his task, Lu Yichi looked at the newcomer, his expression somewhat surprised. He asked Jing Yi, \"Who is this?\"","Shen Huaichu didn't speak, just silently gazed at Jing Yi.","Jing Yi held her glass calmly, seeing that Shen Huaichu didn't respond, she teased, \"Mr. Shen, he's asking you.\"","Shen Huaichu was slightly stunned, his deep eyes brimming with a gentle smile. \"Miss Jing, do I have a title? I need to know before I introduce myself.\"","Jing Yi lightly raised an eyebrow, turning to look at Shen Huaichu. \"And if you don't have a title?\" Shen Huaichu didn't show disappointment. His usually indifferent eyes softened with tender affection.","\"Without a title, I'm just Miss Jing's kept man.\"","Lu Yichi & Male Group Members: ......","Lu Yichi looked at the male group members with a mix of frustration and pity. They were all here on a mission, so why weren't they saying more?!","Male Group: Uh? What were they supposed to say? They hadn't even debuted yet; how could they dare to say such things?","In the corner, the onlookers.","Jing Zeqian looked at Shen Huaichu in shock. Wasn't Shen Huaichu supposed to be better? Why did he seem even crazier now?!","Jing Zeyou thought it wasn't bad without a title; after all, Jing Yi wouldn't lose out either. Jing Beicheng agreed.","Lin Ruiqing found herself more satisfied with Shen Huaichu.","Jing Zejun, on the other hand, was more worried about Wen Qingyan's future situation.","Ross held his wine glass, thinking that if Jing Yi agreed, it would be a rare opportunity to undermine Huarui Group.","Henry was enlightened. This must be the reason why Jing Yi waited for him; he was really impressive.","Benjamin looked serious. Was this why he couldn't be a kept man?","Marso nodded in satisfaction. It was best not to have a title; that way, he could keep the person under control.","Shen Xi tightly held Chen Yisi's hand, covering her mouth to prevent herself from excitedly shouting out. Chen Yisi looked at her helplessly, his eyes full of tenderness.","Jing Yi's smile grew even brighter. She put down her glass and threw herself into Shen Huaichu's arms.","Shen Huaichu's lips curved into a clear smile as he reached out and held Jing Yi tightly.","\"Shen Huaichu, you made me wait too long.\"","Jing Yi's soft voice whispered in his ear, and Shen Huaichu tightened his embrace. \"I'm sorry, it won't happen again.\"","From a distance came the voices of Jing Zeqian and the others, deliberately lowered but still audible.","Jing Yi smiled, her eyes curving into crescents, the dimples on her cheeks deepening.","Family, friends, lover.","The world, it seemed, was silently loving her in its own way.","[The End]"]},{"number":232,"title":"Chapter 232: Extra: Pre-Marriage Daily Life 1: The Legendary Female Racer","paragraphs":["“GT Super Cup: Jing Yi Takes the Crown!”","“GT Super Cup Concludes, Racer Jing Yi Wins on Legendary International Track”","“The Championship Journey of Legendary Female Racer Jing Yi”","“Former GT Super Cup Champion Ross Passes the Torch to Chinese Female Racer Jing Yi!”","“GT Racing World Champion—Jing Yi!”","“The Only Female Racer on the GT Super Cup Championship Podium.”","A flood of news swept across the world the moment Jing Yi secured her victory. The attention on this female racer was unprecedented, not just in the racing community but globally.","In China, trending hashtags seemed endless, with most dominated by the news of Jing Yi’s triumph. Many viewers who watched the live broadcast couldn’t help but shout in excitement, some even moved to tears.","“Jing Yi won! The championship! She actually won!”","“Ah!!!! Jing Yi won!!!”","“No way! A female racer actually pulled it off!”","“Impossible! Ross lost? That’s Ross, the racing demon!”","“This was live! Didn’t you see Jing Yi’s red car cross the finish line first?!”","“I never thought the day would come when a female racer would take the GT Super Cup championship.”","People’s focus on ‘Jing Yi’ shifted. It was no longer about her being the ‘fake heiress’ of the Jing family, nor about her being someone’s sister or daughter.","It was simply because she was Jing Yi, the female racer.","...","After finally finishing her interviews, Jing Yi hurried back to China, only to find that the number of people waiting to interview her hadn’t decreased at all.","The invitations from Jing Zeqian alone were already overwhelming.","Adhering to the principle of fairness, Jing Yi still selected a few authoritative media outlets and granted them interviews.","However, while Jing Yi was busy, the Jing family was far from idle.","Hengjing had recently partnered with the International Racing Federation to develop a holographic racing game. Holographic devices had been a key focus of the group’s recent developments, but the collaboration with the racing federation was unexpected for Jing Zeyou.","This opened up another sector, which was undoubtedly beneficial for Hengjing Group.","Jing Zeqian, aside from managing the schedule of their sole racer, also had to oversee operations at Startrack.","Fortunately, Jing Yi’s schedule was relatively simpler, but why couldn’t these people let his sister rest? Even champions need a break!","What’s more, many artists at Startrack had indirectly benefited from Jing Yi’s popularity, which in turn increased his workload significantly.","“...Additionally, Director Chen wanted to know if Miss Jing Yi would be available for a cameo?”","“Same here. They said even a brief appearance would suffice, and everything else is negotiable.”","“Our side too. The organizers said the compensation is open for discussion...”","“Same here...”","“Me too!”","Jing Zeqian felt a headache coming on and pinched the bridge of his nose. “Reject them all! If they can get her, fine, but don’t use my sister as a bargaining chip!”","The department heads weren’t surprised. They had anticipated Jing Zeqian’s response, and the prepared statements would be sent out shortly.","“Also, the artists we previously contacted are ready to join Startrack. There are also some newcomers in training, but they’re hoping to meet Miss Jing Yi or get her autograph...”","Jing Zeqian looked up, his sharp eyes filled with annoyance and resignation. “...No! Nothing! Take it or leave it!”","He couldn’t believe how spoiled they’d become. Since when did they get to be so picky?","The department heads exchanged glances. They’d just have to keep dangling the carrot. After all, Miss Jing Yi was their boss’s sister. There would be opportunities for her to visit Startrack, and meeting her or getting her autograph would be a breeze then.","But they’d better keep a few for themselves. She was, after all, the first Chinese female racer to stand on the GT championship podium. How cool was that!","Jing Zejun’s situation was similar.","At the moment, several senior actors on set were gathered around her, and she was at a loss.","“I didn’t know you all followed racing...”","The veteran actors smiled warmly. They weren’t exactly racing fans, but their younger family members were absolutely obsessed with Jing Yi, which led them to approach Jing Zejun.","If it were anyone else, Jing Zejun could have brushed them off. After all, Jing Yi wasn’t part of the entertainment industry. But these were respected seniors who had always looked out for her.","“...I’ll ask Jing Yi when I get back.”","Still, the idea of these senior actors asking for her sister’s autograph felt surreal.","No sooner had the seniors mentioned this to Jing Zejun than it became a trending topic.","[I’m tired of saying ‘jealous’...]","[I never imagined my childhood idol would ask my current idol for an autograph!]","[It’s true what they say—‘it’s all about who you know’! @Little Jing, you’re my only connection!]","[Don’t even think about it. I heard Startrack artists have already been turned down by Little Jing.]","[I’m just glad Jing Yi appeared on that variety show once. I’ve rewatched it so many times it’s practically worn out.]","[Same here!]","Some netizens suspected Jing Yi was orchestrating a PR campaign, but the platform’s backend team was overwhelmed. Anything related to Jing Yi these days seemed to trend effortlessly.","The news quickly reached Jing Yi, who called her sister. “...I’ll sign as many as you need!” Jing Zejun smiled gently. “No, just a few will do. It’s for some seniors.”","Jing Zejun knew Jing Yi wasn’t fond of dealing with such matters, and she’d been busy lately.","“It’s fine. I’ll write a bunch, and you can hand them out as you please!”","By the time Jing Zeqian found out, Startrack employees were already gossiping about how close Jing Zejun and Jing Yi were.","Jing Zeqian: ...And here I thought I was the devoted one.","...","Huarui Group","The assistant stood in front of Shen Huaichu’s desk, hesitating.","He had already finished his work report, but there were some requests from his colleagues that he felt compelled to bring up, even under pressure.","Shen Huaichu looked up, noticing the assistant was still there, and frowned slightly. “Is there something else?”","The assistant grew even more nervous, thinking that since the boss had achieved his goals, he might be more lenient with them.","He closed his eyes, lowered his head slightly, and braced himself as if facing certain doom.","“Mr. Shen, will Miss Jing Yi be coming to Huarui to pick you up anytime soon?”","It wasn’t his idea! It was the Huarui employees who wanted to see Miss Jing Yi! They wanted photos! They wanted autographs!","Though, if he could get one too, that would be even better. After all, it was impossible to resist a goddess who raced so brilliantly!","Shen Huaichu was momentarily speechless, his mood instantly souring. Hadn’t they noticed he’d been working overtime lately? Who had time to come pick him up?!","Why bring this up now?","But seeing the assistant’s nervous expression and recalling Jing Yi’s comment about how the employees were afraid of him, he managed to suppress his irritation.","He took a deep breath, his tone less than pleasant. “She’s been very busy lately. No time.”","The assistant was disappointed but, seeing Shen Huaichu’s dark expression, quickly excused himself and left the office.","After the assistant left, Shen Huaichu looked at the photo of Jing Yi on his desk, her smile radiant.","He sighed softly. “She hasn’t even had time to see me, let alone you all.”"]},{"number":233,"title":"Chapter 233: Extra: Pre-Marriage Daily Life 2: About Being 'Beaten to the Punch' in Proposing","paragraphs":["Shen Huaichu had been quite busy lately, busy planning a proposal.","Gu Lin said that girls generally love surprises and romance, so Shen Huaichu decided to propose after the Super Cup exhibition race.","He had been preparing for this plan for a long time—securing the venue, arranging the equipment, and gathering the props.","To ensure the element of surprise, he had to keep Jing Zeqian in the dark, even going so far as to agree to some \"unfair terms\" to ensure his silence.","On the day of the exhibition race, the sun was shining brightly.","\"Shen Huaichu, why are you so nervous?\"","Shen Huaichu watched expressionlessly as Jing Yi executed the final drift.","\"I’m not nervous.\"","Jing Zeqian, standing beside him, chuckled mockingly, \"Your hands are about to crush your knees. If that’s not nervousness, what is?\"","Besides, it’s just a proposal. Why the fuss?","Shen Huaichu slowly turned his head to look at Jing Zeqian, his eyes clearly conveying, \"You know why, so why ask?\"","Jing Zeqian was delighted and smug. Whenever there was an opportunity to give Shen Huaichu a hard time, he was always the first to jump in.","\"By the way, what have you prepared? You should tell me. After all, I’m Jing Yi’s second brother. I might be able to give you some advice.\"","Jing Zeqian was firmly against Shen Huaichu’s plan to propose and had even requested the Jing family’s cooperation.","However, the family had held a meeting...","And once again, he found himself in the minority. What was even more infuriating was that his brother and father had abstained from voting! How spineless!","If only they had shown some \"manly courage,\" like him, it would have been a clear three-to-two vote!","Though after the vote, Lin Ruiqing had scolded him again.","\"What more do you want? Isn’t Huaichu’s sincerity enough?\"","Jing Zeqian muttered discontentedly, \"Transferring his assets to Jing Yi’s name is the least he should do. If Jing Yi’s life after marriage isn’t better than it is now, why should she marry him?\"","\"What’s wrong with making him wait a few more years? Jing Yi is at the peak of her career right now. Getting married would just waste her time.\"","\"And those promises he made—even if he signed them, who’s to say he won’t go back on his word? Businessmen are all cunning!\"","Businessman Jing Zeyou and former businessman Jing Beicheng: \"...\"","Lin Ruiqing looked at him with a complicated expression. \"What kind of nonsense are you spouting? And why do you always have so much to say? It’s the same with Jing Yi and Zejun. You just never listen...\"","Jing Zejun sat quietly beside them, watching as his mother and brother argued, until finally, his mother grabbed Jing Zeqian’s ear, and the latter yelped in pain.","Advice?","As soon as Shen Huaichu heard Jing Zeqian’s offer, he immediately grew wary.","He had already taken a huge risk by telling Jing Zeqian about his proposal plans. There was no way he was going to share the specifics.","Did he want to ruin his proposal?","\"Thank you, Second Brother, but that won’t be necessary.\"","Jing Zeqian still wouldn’t let it go. \"Really, I know Jing Yi’s preferences better than anyone. I might be able to give you some useful suggestions.\"","Shen Huaichu politely declined again.","While the two were going back and forth, Jing Yi’s exhibition race had already ended.","Following the usual post-race procedure, the racer would leave the track, and the audience would gradually disperse.","But today was different. No one moved.","Shen Huaichu, standing on the other side of the stands, felt something was off. \"I’ll go check,\" he said before leaving.","Jing Zeqian was about to follow, but Jing Zeyou stopped him.","\"You don’t need to go.\" Jing Zeqian was puzzled. \"Why not?\"","Jing Zeyou slowly stood up, glanced at the red race car on the track, and sighed almost imperceptibly.","\"Your dear sister has something to say to Shen Huaichu.\"","Jing Zeqian was confused at first, but then his expression darkened, a mix of helplessness and bitterness in his eyes.","...","Jing Yi got out of the car, took off her helmet, and placed it on the roof. She looked at the audience in the stands with gratitude.","Feeling her heart racing, she took a deep breath to calm herself, until she saw Shen Huaichu approaching.","\"Shen Huaichu, stay right there.\"","She didn’t dare let him get too close, or she’d only get more nervous. This distance was just right.","Shen Huaichu was confused but instinctively obeyed, standing still, looking somewhat dazed.","\"I have something to say to you.\"","Shen Huaichu seemed to realize something, his heart skipping a beat before racing uncontrollably.","His breathing grew rapid, and his heart pounded so hard it felt like it might burst out of his chest!","Seeing Shen Huaichu’s stunned expression, Jing Yi calmed down, her eyes curving into a smile, her dimples like hidden sweetness.","\"The first time we met, you were so arrogant.\"","\"The second time we met, you were incredibly rude.\"","Their meeting hadn’t been pleasant—in fact, it had been downright awful.","That day, she had been so angry that she forgot to put on her usual \"well-behaved\" Jing Yi persona.","Before returning to the country, she had reminded herself not to be too outspoken, to always follow the principle of avoiding trouble whenever possible.","As long as she stayed \"invisible,\" she could stay far away from the fate written in the books.","She had never seen a guy with such a handsome face, but who would have thought he could be so arrogant?","\"The third time we met, you were even more insufferably self-important.\"","She had never seen anyone give a gift by taking something from someone else! He was truly too full of himself.","Shen Huaichu stared intently at Jing Yi, watching her slightly annoyed expression, his eyes filled with warmth and tenderness.","From that day on, Jing Yi had harbored a fire in her heart, thinking that once Shen Huaichu’s skilled bodyguard wasn’t around, she’d give him a good beating!","Later, she got her wish.","Thinking of this, Jing Yi suddenly asked, \"Shen Huaichu, did you let me hit you that time because you already had feelings for me?\"","Shen Huaichu was momentarily stunned, his ears turning red, then his entire face flushing.","Even if he had been slow to realize it, the moment he knew he loved Jing Yi, he understood where those strange emotions had come from.","The curve of Jing Yi’s smile deepened, making her look even more vibrant.","Later, she began to think that Shen Huaichu wasn’t so bad after all.","Later, they got together.","She wasn’t naive enough to think she could help Shen Huaichu overcome his deepest fears, so she didn’t want him to keep guarding her over and over.","As long as he believed in her, believed that she could walk away from the racetrack unharmed, that was enough.","Later, he left. Everyone thought she was heartbroken, and yes, she missed him, but her heart was also incredibly soft.","Just how much did this man love her?","Jing Yi smiled, her almond-shaped eyes sparkling with joy.","\"Mr. Shen, I’m here to give you a title!\""]},{"number":234,"title":"Chapter 234: Extra: Pre-Marriage Daily Life 3: The Aftermath of the Proposal","paragraphs":["Shen Huaichu had always known that a person with a dark heart could never truly be considered good.","Why should he be kind to others? The world had already been unkind enough to him.","So, that girl was the young lady the Jing family brought back from abroad? Wasn’t she said to have been raised by her grandmother and known for her gentle personality?","Gentle?","If it weren’t for the bodyguard standing in front of him, her fist might have already been aimed straight at his face.","Shen Huaichu found her somewhat unique, but in their circle, unique people were a dime a dozen. Wasn’t he unique too?","A girl who loved racing? It really showed how inherently incompatible they were.","Shen Huaichu wanted to completely sever these strange emotions, but it seemed to make her even angrier.","He had anticipated this. Probably no one would appreciate such a “thank you,” but he just wanted to see a different side of Jing Yi, one that wasn’t the obedient facade she showed to the world.","Would she be less angry if he let her hit him?","She really didn’t hold back.","That day was the first time he wanted to help Jing Yi, and also the first time he felt a twinge of envy. Jing Yi was just too good to the Jing family.","So good that she didn’t even care about her own safety, solely focused on eliminating any threats to the Jing family.","She was so exhausted she could barely keep her eyes open.","Alright, he lost. He knew the barriers between him and Jing Yi, but he couldn’t stand seeing her hand in someone else’s palm!","Had she not felt anything for him at all? Her kick was way too strong.","It was wonderful—they were together now.","Even though her brothers occasionally showered him with “affection,” he was overjoyed that they were together!","She loved racing, but it seemed like he was affecting her. He had become her obstacle...","She said he was rude, so he learned to be grateful. She said he didn’t know how to speak, so he learned to be tactful. Because he had become her burden, he wanted to become a better person.","He had found someone he cared about in this world, and everything he did was simply to be worthy of that person, nothing more.","...","Jing Yi’s proposal at the racetrack went viral.","In the video, Jing Yi raised her hand, and the previously quiet audience began to stir. They were holding something, unfurling it.","It was a large banner with words written on it:","“Shen Huaichu, let’s get married!”","Shen Huaichu stood there, his eyes red, but his lips curved into a wide smile.","At the end of the video, Shen Huaichu knelt on one knee in front of Jing Yi, his eyes glistening, his hand trembling slightly as he held the ring.","He then tightly embraced Jing Yi, his body visibly shaking.","The video also captured Jing Zeqian and Jing Zejun sneaking into the racetrack to eavesdrop because they couldn’t hear what Jing Yi was saying.","[Wow, wow, wow! Jing Yi is just too cool! Proposing in public like that!]","[Jing Yi is so romantic, it’s absolutely perfect!]","[Honestly, if it were any other guy, the proposal wouldn’t have had the same impact. It’s because it’s Jing Yi that it feels so amazing!]","[He really loves Jing Yi!]","[You can really tell the difference between love and indifference in his actions. He was still trembling afterward.]","[Wait, when did Jing Yi get a boyfriend? I was still shipping her with someone else!]","[Hahaha, I suggest you delete that comment. If Shen Huaichu finds out, you’re done for!]","[Shen Huaichu, who dedicates his life to engraving “Jing Yi’s boyfriend” on every part of his body.]","[It should be changed to “Jing Yi’s fiancé” now.]","[It’s a shame we can’t hear the audio, but just watching the video is enough to feel the emotion.]","[Wait, is no one paying attention to Jing Zeqian in the corner?]","[CEO Jing, you’re really too much of a comedian. You’re the CEO of a listed company!]","[Hahaha, even though we can’t see Jing Zejun’s expression, I’m sure he’s speechless.]","Jing Zeqian glanced sideways at Shen Huaichu, whose lips were still curled into a smile, his displeasure growing more evident.","“Mr. Shen, don’t you have anything better to do? Shouldn’t you be checking if Huarui Group has gone bankrupt yet?”","Shen Huaichu was in an undeniably good mood.","“Don’t worry, Second Brother. Huarui Group’s development is still on the rise. It’s unlikely to go bankrupt for decades.”","This familiar air of smugness was truly infuriating!","Jing Zeqian glared at Shen Huaichu, recognizing that all-too-familiar look of triumph.","What made him even angrier was that he only found out about his dear sister’s proposal after the fact.","Why? Why didn’t anyone tell him!","Jing Yi’s explanation was that she hadn’t told anyone. Jing Zeyou only knew because he figured it out himself, and she had only hinted at it slightly.","Jing Zeqian: “...That’s not the point! The point is, while I’ve been busy fending off Shen Huaichu’s wolfish intentions, how could my sister just walk herself into the wolf’s mouth!”","To this, Jing Yi responded that she had to take control of the situation. That’s how she kept her life and marriage in her own hands.","For example, the place they would live after getting married was a villa just a few steps away from the Jing family home.","Jing Zeqian seemed somewhat satisfied with that.","Meanwhile, Jing Zeyou: “...Wasn’t that already decided before?”","In any case, with Jing Zeyou staying silent, Jing Zeqian let the matter drop.","However, Shen Huaichu’s recent smugness reignited Jing Zeqian’s irritation.","...","The head of the PR department stood in front of the desk, cautiously observing Jing Zeqian’s expression.","“Mr. Jing, should we still suppress that hashtag?” This was a long-term task Jing Zeqian had assigned to them.","If the first time the PR team mistook Shen Huaichu for a no-name trying to ride on the coattails of fame,","then after learning about Jing Yi’s relationship with him and his identity as the CEO of Huarui Group,","they were absolutely horrified. What had they done, treating the CEO of Huarui Group like that?!","But their boss didn’t seem to care at all and even told them to keep going.","So, they had to watch as the hashtag inexplicably gained traction, suppress it, and repeat the cycle.","Even many netizens noticed this strange phenomenon, and the hashtag attracted a group of curious fans.","With Jing Yi and Shen Huaichu’s proposal video going viral, they thought this long-term task would finally come to an end...","Jing Zeqian rubbed his chin, watching the hashtag trending again.","“Of course, suppress it until no one pays attention!” He wasn’t going to let Shen Huaichu keep flaunting his happiness in front of him!","The PR department head was on the verge of tears. The couple was practically official now, so why was their boss still like this?","And so, just as netizens were about to flood into the Shen Huaichu and Jing Yi CP hashtag, they found it mysteriously gone again.","The seasoned fans: I knew this would happen."]},{"number":235,"title":"Chapter 235: Extra: Pre-Marriage Daily Life 4: About Creating a Super Topic","paragraphs":["Many media outlets are aware that Shen Huaichu, the CEO of Huarui Group, is not fond of giving interviews, even personal ones. Yet, there are many intriguing aspects about him that spark curiosity.","For instance, rumors suggest that Shen Huaichu’s parents died in a car accident, with his uncle being the culprit, and that Shen Huaichu spent over a decade plotting his revenge.","Another point of interest is how he managed to revive Huarui Group, which was showing signs of decline, and bring it back to its former glory in just two years.","Additionally, the collaboration between Huarui Group and Hengjing is nothing short of remarkable. How did Shen Huaichu secure this partnership so soon after taking over Huarui?","And then there’s the matter of his relationship with Jing Yi, the youngest daughter of the Jing family.","Most of these topics come from interview outlines submitted by financial journalists, with a few from gossip reporters, though no one has ever gotten answers.","Because Shen Huaichu doesn’t do interviews.","That is, until one day, during a press conference, a rookie reporter from a mainstream media outlet boldly requested an interview, citing a desire to learn more about Jing Yi, the race car driver’s fiancé.","The other journalists scoffed, their eyes filled with disdain, certain that Shen Huaichu would have the reporter escorted out immediately.","After all, this was a Huarui Group press conference, and Shen Huaichu was the current CEO, known for his no-nonsense demeanor.","Gossip had no place here.","Just as the journalists were mentally criticizing the rookie, they noticed Shen Huaichu’s expression soften for a brief moment.","“Alright, after the press conference,” he said.","The journalists were stunned. Wait, what? After the press conference?!","Just like that, the rookie reporter secured Shen Huaichu’s first-ever interview, leaving the others kicking themselves. If only they’d known Shen Huaichu was open to this angle, they would’ve brought banners of Jing Yi to the conference!","The rookie reporter was equally surprised. As a fan of Jing Yi, he had blurted out the request in a moment of excitement, never expecting to actually land the interview.","...","Sitting in Huarui Group’s conference room, the rookie reporter felt a wave of nervousness.","Though he hadn’t interacted much with Shen Huaichu, the CEO’s stern appearance suggested he wasn’t the most approachable person.","The reporter had received numerous interview outlines from seasoned journalists, each version meticulously crafted to avoid any missteps.","The questions were all fairly standard, and he’d even run them by Shen Huaichu’s assistant beforehand to ensure there were no sensitive topics.","However, the assistant seemed to hint at something.","“The questions are fine, but it’s best to remember why the CEO agreed to this interview in the first place.”","If the questions were all so conventional, why would Shen Huaichu have accepted the interview?","Before the rookie could fully process this, the interview time arrived, and he found himself face-to-face with Shen Huaichu, armed with his list of questions.","The interview was tense, to say the least. The rookie had never interviewed such a high-profile figure before, and Shen Huaichu’s imposing presence only added to the pressure.","As Shen Huaichu’s expression grew increasingly stoic, the rookie suddenly had a stroke of inspiration.","“I’ve heard that Jing Yi often comes to Huarui to pick you up?”","Shen Huaichu’s demeanor instantly softened, a faint smile tugging at his lips. “Yes, she comes by when her training ends early...” He even went on to share some office rumors about their relationship.","The rookie reporter’s smile faltered slightly. So, this was what the assistant had meant.","From then on, the reporter peppered the interview with questions about Shen Huaichu and Jing Yi’s relationship, allowing the CEO to openly share their love story.","Feeling more at ease, the rookie abandoned the outline and, in another moment of impulsiveness, asked, “By the way, there was a time when fans were shipping Jing Yi with various people online. My friend even shipped her with you.”","At the time, he’d thought, “Who would ship such a niche pairing?” The photos in the fan community didn’t even show their faces, just vague references to a ‘mysterious boyfriend,’ yet people still shipped them.","Later, after videos of Shen Huaichu rushing to Jing Yi’s side following her car accident and his subsequent proposal went viral, the fan community for their pairing skyrocketed to the top of the charts, surpassing all others.","Though it was quickly pushed down by ‘interference.’","Hearing this, Shen Huaichu’s smile grew even more genuine.","“The fan community must’ve been pretty quiet back then. Please thank your friend for me.”","The reporter was speechless. Did Shen Huaichu actually follow his own fan community with Jing Yi?","The interview flew by, and as Shen Huaichu seemed in good spirits, the rookie reporter grew increasingly uncertain.","Had he asked enough industry-related questions? Was this okay?","When the seasoned journalists reviewed the footage, they were equally stunned.","“This kid’s reporting skills are subpar, but his luck is off the charts! It’s infuriating!”","The rookie hesitantly asked, “Is this content unusable?”","“Of course... of course we’re using it!”","Though it was far from what they’d expected, they knew the video would go viral, bringing massive attention to their media outlet.","Soon, Shen Huaichu’s interview was released, and not just netizens, but industry insiders also flocked to watch it.","Industry insiders: “What is this? A Shen Huaichu interview? Or a celebrity gossip piece? CEO Shen Huaichu, that smile on your face is unfamiliar.”","Twitter was abuzz with reactions.","[Did I click on the wrong media outlet? Or is this a fake account?]","[I knew it! Who else was shipping this niche pairing back then?]","[Wait, CEO Shen, aren’t you busy? You still find time to check the fan community?]","[Let’s be bold here—maybe Shen Huaichu created the fan community himself!]","[You might be onto something. It’s suspicious how such a niche community suddenly appeared. Now it all makes sense.]","[I’m just shocked that Shen Huaichu’s first interview was for this?]","[Hahaha, Shen Huaichu, don’t be too obvious about your love!]","[Other media outlets must be crying. Who knew Shen Huaichu would fall for this?]","Meanwhile, over at Startrack PR, the team was in a panic, standing nervously before Jing Zeqian.","“Sir, we really can’t take down the fan community...”","Why was their CEO still obsessing over his sister and future brother-in-law’s fan community after all this time? Please, just assign them other tasks!","Jing Zeqian glared at the fan community, which was firmly at the top of the trending charts. It had almost been taken down before, but then Shen Huaichu had pulled this stunt.","Shen Huaichu, you’re ruthless!","Shen Huaichu, on the other hand, was scrolling through the comments in his and Jing Yi’s fan community, a satisfied smile on his face.","He had personally created this community, watching it grow from obscurity to the top of the charts, where it remained.","This was exactly what he had envisioned!"]},{"number":236,"title":"Chapter 236: Side Story: The Tale of the Public Relations Plan (Sub-Couple, First Part)","paragraphs":["Wen Qingyan first met Jing Zejun during an audition.","He was only there to assist a senior colleague, wearing a mask and black-framed glasses as a simple disguise, standing in line with the others.","He noticed a girl who, despite his own young age, seemed even more youthful and inexperienced.","She appeared nervous, her voice gentle, yet she was auditioning for the role of a domineering rich girl.","Watching her try to portray arrogance while carefully holding back to avoid actually hitting her scene partner, Wen Qingyan couldn’t help but smile faintly in the corner.","This girl was quite endearing.","When the audition ended, she quickly helped her scene partner up and stood obediently, waiting for the director and others to judge her performance.","His senior colleague told her to wait for further notice, but Wen Qingyan knew she likely hadn’t made the cut.","After watching a few more auditions, Wen Qingyan grew bored and decided to step outside for some fresh air.","To his surprise, the girl was still there, muttering to herself, clearly frustrated.","As he approached, he could hear her reciting the lines from her earlier performance.","“I won’t get to perform this scene again,” she murmured.","Having grown up in the entertainment industry, Wen Qingyan had seen many hardworking individuals, but something about this girl made him want to ease her burden.","The girl seemed slightly startled when she noticed him, her beautiful eyes filled with caution.","But as if sensing his goodwill, her guard softened, and she smiled gently.","“I know the director probably wasn’t satisfied with my performance,” she admitted, unable to hide her disappointment.","Wen Qingyan was curious. “If you knew, why did you hold back so much?” Being overly cautious with a co-actor wouldn’t earn her any points—it might even cost her the role.","The girl sighed softly. “I probably wouldn’t have been chosen anyway, but the actor I was paired with had scraped knees and bruised wrists.”","Wen Qingyan mimicked her sigh. “Little girl, do you think you can survive in the entertainment industry like this?”","Unfazed by his teasing, she continued to smile warmly. “I’m doing alright so far.”","This response amused Wen Qingyan, but before he could reply, he noticed a scrape on her hand.","He pulled a bandage from his pocket and handed it to her.","“If you have the energy to care for others, you should take care of yourself too. You’re injured as well.”","The girl was surprised but accepted it gratefully. “Thank you!” As she carefully applied the bandage, Wen Qingyan asked, “What’s your name? Have you acted in anything before?”","Still focused on the bandage, she looked up, puzzled.","Was this man a talent agent?","“I’m Jing Zejun. I’ve acted in...”","As she listed a few titles, Wen Qingyan tried to recall them but drew a blank. She was truly unknown.","But her name, Jing Zejun, sounded somewhat similar to his boss’s name.","“Little girl, are you some rich heiress here to experience life in the entertainment industry?”","The girl paused, her smile tinged with a hint of sadness. “No, I’m here to make a living.”","Wen Qingyan’s expression immediately turned serious, and he apologized sincerely.","“I’m sorry, I didn’t mean to offend.”","Though he didn’t know her background, her demeanor suggested there was more to her story than he had assumed.","The girl didn’t seem bothered. “It’s alright, you didn’t mean any harm...” She was about to say more when her phone rang. It was her agent, summoning her to another audition.","Her face lit up as she hung up.","“Thank you for the bandage, sir. I have to go now!”","Watching her hurried departure, Wen Qingyan instinctively called out, “Focus on your acting. Worrying too much won’t do you any good.”","She seemed to hear him, as a grateful “Thank you!” floated back.","“You’re welcome, but I hope you actually take my advice,” Wen Qingyan muttered, shaking his head as he headed back to the audition room.","...","“Does President Jing have a sister?” Wen Qingyan’s agent asked casually as they walked, flipping through his recent work schedule.","“I’ve never heard of him having a sister. He has an older brother, though. Why do you ask?”","Wen Qingyan shrugged. “Just curious.”","It was a passing thought. After all, there were plenty of people with similar names.","The agent didn’t press further and led Wen Qingyan to Jing Zeqian’s office.","Today was a routine check-in on the artists’ progress, and since Wen Qingyan was available, the agent brought him along to maintain visibility.","Not that it was necessary—Wen Qingyan was Startrack’s undisputed top star, with both talent and achievements to back it up.","But lately, Jiang Miaomiao and her agent had been overstepping, acting as if Wen Qingyan’s easygoing nature meant they could take advantage. As if he wasn’t the senior artist here!","Unaware of his agent’s internal grievances, Wen Qingyan frowned slightly upon entering the office and seeing who was inside.","The expression was fleeting, unnoticed by anyone.","He shot his agent a look: You didn’t tell me she’d be here.","The agent gave a sheepish smile: If I had, you wouldn’t have come.","Wen Qingyan: ...You’re in trouble now.","Wen Qingyan had joined Startrack after Jiang Miaomiao. He’d heard of her reputation in the industry but hadn’t crossed paths with her until then.","Initially, given their shared company and her comparable fame and talent, his agent had considered a collaboration.","But before any deal could be struck, her agent’s arrogant attitude had been enough to dissuade him.","The idea was never brought up again.","Wen Qingyan wasn’t one to compromise his comfort. He’d chosen Startrack for its reputation and Jing Zeqian’s management style.","At least here, no artist had to resort to socializing or compromising themselves for opportunities.","Plus, he rather liked his boss’s personality. So, as for Jiang Miaomiao, he’d simply pretend she didn’t exist.","When Wen Qingyan and his agent entered, Jing Zeqian raised an eyebrow in surprise.","“Well, look who’s gracing us with his presence today,” he teased.","Wen Qingyan took a seat as far from Jiang Miaomiao as possible, his tone calm. “It’s been a while, President Jing. I was worried you’d forgotten about me, and the resources would stop coming my way.”","Jing Zeqian shot him a glance, their familiarity evident. “Don’t flatter yourself. You only get what’s left after you’ve picked through the best...”","Jiang Miaomiao and her agent observed the exchange, their expressions thoughtful."]},{"number":237,"title":"Chapter 237: Side Story: The Tale of the PR Plan (Secondary Couple, Mid-Length)","paragraphs":["\"...Speaking of which, I recently met someone, her name...\"","Before Wen Qingyan could finish mentioning Jing Zejun's name, he was interrupted.","\"President Jing, I've already reported on Miaomiao's recent work. Additionally, that foreign director has been aggressively inviting Miaomiao to participate, but it conflicts with her current shooting schedule. What do you think?\"","Seeing Wen Qingyan and Jing Zeqian start to chat, Jiang Miaomiao gave her agent a look, and her agent stepped forward.","Wen Qingyan, who had been interrupted, didn't seem to mind. He smiled at Jiang Miaomiao and her agent as if watching a couple of clowns.","A scheduling conflict?","Putting it so delicately, it’s just a ploy to use Jing Zeqian's name to 'legitimately' pressure the director—either to let her go or to use a stand-in. After all, Jiang Miaomiao can’t afford to suffer any losses.","Wen Qingyan could tolerate it, but his agent couldn’t.","Wen Qingyan's agent smiled, \"What does this mean? Are you expecting President Jing to step in and act for Miaomiao?\"","She took on the job herself, and now she wants someone else to clean up her mess while she walks away scot-free. Isn’t that a bit too much?","Jiang Miaomiao and her agent’s expressions turned sour in an instant, and Jing Zeqian’s brow furrowed with displeasure.","Wen Qingyan leisurely picked up his coffee, took a sip, and hid the curve of his lips.","Jiang Miaomiao's agent tried to explain, \"President Jing, it’s not like that...\" Jing Zeqian cut her off impatiently, \"What’s the solution? Do I have to handle this myself?\"","He and Jiang Miaomiao were indeed friends, but that didn’t mean he had to give her special treatment for everything.","Jiang Miaomiao forced a smile, \"Zeqian, it’s not like that. She’s just anxious to help me secure this opportunity. After all, it’s...\"","Jing Zeqian looked at her seriously, \"Miaomiao, I’m not asking you to give up a rare opportunity, but your team should at least manage your schedule properly.\"","In the end, Jiang Miaomiao could only smile and agree before leaving with her agent.","Wen Qingyan's agent watched their retreating figures with a smug look, though he quickly toned it down when he caught Wen Qingyan’s gaze.","He almost forgot—no matter what, Jiang Miaomiao’s relationship with President Jing was still different from the other artists at 'Startrack.'","\"By the way, what were you going to tell me earlier?\"","Wen Qingyan snapped out of his thoughts and shook his head with a faint smile, \"Nothing, just that I met a special girl.\" As for the coincidence of their names being similar, it wasn’t worth mentioning.","Jing Zeqian looked at Wen Qingyan, hesitating to speak.","Rationally, he should advise him to focus on his career. After all, even though he’s been popular for years, he’s still on the rise, and Jing Zeqian was, after all, his boss!","But emotionally, he couldn’t bring himself to stop someone from pursuing love. A young man in his twenties falling in love wasn’t a big deal.","But he was in the entertainment industry, and a top actor at that...","Fortunately, Wen Qingyan's agent quickly picked up on Jing Zeqian’s concern and assured him, \"Don’t worry, President Jing! Qingyan was just speaking offhandedly!\"","He spent almost every day with this guy. If Wen Qingyan were really dating someone, he’d definitely know!","Wen Qingyan realized Jing Zeqian had misunderstood and chuckled, \"Don’t worry, President Jing. Even if I were to start dating, it would only be after the PR plan was in place.\"","Jing Zeqian breathed a sigh of relief and explained, \"I’m not stopping you from dating. Like you said, it’s just a matter of having a PR plan ready.\"","Wen Qingyan was both amused and exasperated. He had only been speaking casually.","But soon, he realized that a PR plan really would be necessary.","...","A few days later, Wen Qingyan saw the girl again. She had come to play the childhood sweetheart of the male lead in the drama.","That is, his character’s childhood sweetheart.","Thinking back to Jing Zeqian’s probing and his agent’s earnest advice, Wen Qingyan felt a little uneasy.","She didn’t recognize him, treating him only as a senior in the entertainment industry.","But, she did look quite stunning in that period costume.","After the day’s filming wrapped up, there was a knock at the door. Wen Qingyan, who had been reading the script, immediately sat up.","His agent gave him a strange look, \"Why so excited?\"","Wen Qingyan tried to cover it up by lying back on the sofa and holding up the script, \"Just stretching after sitting for too long. Aren’t you going to see who’s at the door? Don’t keep them waiting.\"","His agent’s expression grew even more suspicious. It was late at night, and his artist seemed to know who was knocking?","Muttering to himself, the agent went to open the door.","Wen Qingyan slowly lowered the script and looked toward the door, a mix of anticipation and anxiety in his eyes.","Could it be her? He had mentioned that she could ask him if she had any questions, but not this late. She didn’t seem like that kind of girl, right? She wasn’t, was she? But what if it was her?","\"Is Qingyan here?\"","It was the female lead of *The Monarch*. The agent greeted her politely before turning back and saying, \"Qingyan, Miss Li is here to see you.\"","Miss Li?","Wen Qingyan stood up and looked over. Seeing it was the actress playing the female lead, a flicker of disappointment crossed his eyes.","He walked over, a gentle smile returning to his face.","\"Miss Li, what can I do for you?\"","The actress blushed, \"Qingyan, you can just call me Yuyu.\" Wen Qingyan smiled but didn’t respond. His agent, used to this, turned and went back inside.","After all, his artist would never be alone with a female co-star.","Seeing his lack of response, the actress quickly held up her script, \"There’s a scene from today that I’m not quite clear on. I was wondering if you could help me...\"","Wen Qingyan smiled politely, \"I’m afraid that might not be convenient. Besides, if any rumors were to spread, it wouldn’t be good for your reputation.\"","The actress’s expression faltered. Wasn’t that exactly why she had come so late?","But with him putting it that way, she could only leave dejectedly.","Wen Qingyan returned to his room, closed the door, and unconsciously sighed.","His agent looked even more suspicious, \"Were you... waiting for someone?\" Wen Qingyan immediately denied it, \"Of course not. It’s so late. Who would I be waiting for?\"","Really? But he couldn’t shake the feeling that something was off.","Filming for *The Monarch* continued, and Wen Qingyan gradually grew closer to Jing Zejun. At the very least, she no longer treated him like a distant senior.","Today was Jing Zejun’s final scene, the most pivotal moment for her character.","Wen Qingyan did his best to guide her, ensuring that this scene would become a highlight that audiences would remember.","The cameras rolled. Jing Zejun, clad in armor with her hair tied high, collapsed into a pool of blood.","At this moment, Wen Qingyan, playing the male lead, was supposed to rush over in despair—and he did.","But for some reason, watching Jing Zejun fall to the ground like that, he genuinely felt a pang of sadness.","Wen Qingyan was a seasoned actor. He always kept his off-screen emotions separate from his on-screen performance. But today felt different."]},{"number":238,"title":"Chapter 238: Extra: The Story About the Public Relations Plan (Secondary Couple, Middle and Lower Part)","paragraphs":["Wen Qingyan watched from afar as Jing Zejun celebrated the wrap of her scene, holding a bouquet of flowers with a radiant smile on her face. She was still clad in her blood-stained battle armor.","Wen Qingyan didn’t rush to change out of his own dirtied costume, content to simply gaze at her. He felt his heartbeat quicken, a rhythm that grew faster with each passing moment.","“Qingyan, what are you looking at?” someone asked.","“...Brother, we might need to prepare a PR contingency plan,” he replied.","“Huh?!”","From that day on, his manager knew Wen Qingyan had someone he liked. But that PR plan never came into play, even years later.","Wen Qingyan had harbored feelings for Jing Zejun for years, so long that even his manager grew exasperated.","“What are you even doing? If you like her, just confess! All these years of silently watching over her—how is she supposed to know you’re the one behind those opportunities? And honestly...” The manager paused, his expression complicated. “It’s kind of creepy.”","Wen Qingyan sighed. He was well aware of how questionable his actions were.","He always told himself to wait a little longer.","At first, he wanted to give her time to step out of her role, not wanting to appear at her most vulnerable.","Later, he learned about her family situation—her parents were both ill. Helping her secure better medical care was the most straightforward way he could support her without overstepping.","Then, she seemed to go through a tough period, losing weight and her smile dimming.","And then, she became the younger sister of his boss—the heiress of the Jing family.","It turned out the similarity in their names wasn’t a coincidence. If only he had realized sooner, she wouldn’t have had to face so much alone.","His manager was right. If he hadn’t found the courage in all those years, now that Jing Zejun was the Jing family’s heiress, it would be even harder to express his feelings.","She would be surrounded by even more eligible suitors, and he would just be one among many.","Even though he knew the Jing family didn’t judge people based on wealth or status, Wen Qingyan couldn’t help but feel anxious.","He didn’t want to pressure Jing Zejun for a response; he just wanted her to see him as a genuine pursuer.","...","“Qingyan-ge, wait here for a bit. I’ll check how much longer Zejun-jie has on set.”","Wen Qingyan nodded gently and took a seat in Jing Zejun’s dressing room. His eyes wandered until they landed on a small potted plant on the table. He stared at it for a few seconds, his gaze carrying a hint of something deeper.","The assistant returned quickly, and Wen Qingyan shifted his attention.","“Qingyan-ge, Zejun-jie will be back soon. She and Jiang Xu are almost done with their scene.”","Wen Qingyan’s eyes flickered slightly. “Jiang Xu?” The assistant nodded.","Wen Qingyan smiled. “I’ve been curious about him. Would it be alright if I went to take a look?” After a brief hesitation, the assistant led him to the set.","Wen Qingyan stood quietly in a corner, unnoticed as everyone’s attention was focused on the two actors filming.","They were playing a pair of young lovers experiencing their first blush of romance—nothing unusual.","As someone in the entertainment industry himself, Wen Qingyan wasn’t bothered by such scenes. But if the other person harbored ulterior motives...","He stood still, his gentle eyes concealing a glint of something sharper.","“Jiang Xu, your expression is off. You need to relax. If you’re this tense, how can the audience feel the chemistry?”","The director wasn’t satisfied with Jiang Xu’s performance, even after multiple takes.","With a sigh, the director said, “Let’s take a break. Try to get into the right mindset.” He turned to speak to the assistant director but spotted Wen Qingyan in the corner.","His eyes lit up.","“Qingyan?”","They had worked together before, and without exaggeration, collaborating with an actor like Wen Qingyan was one of the director’s easiest jobs.","Wen Qingyan walked over with a soft smile. “Director, it’s been a while.”","The director patted his shoulder warmly. “You rarely come to visit sets! What brings you here?” He glanced teasingly toward Jing Zejun.","The two actors were still discussing how to avoid another NG.","Suddenly, the director had an idea, his eyes brightening further. “Qingyan, could you do me a favor and give a demonstration?”","Wen Qingyan was momentarily taken aback. He had never filmed overly intimate scenes with Jing Zejun—even in their previous drama, *The Reign*, the most they had done was a simple embrace.","Before he could respond, the director called over Jiang Xu and Jing Zejun, who were still practicing.","Jiang Xu stiffened slightly upon seeing Wen Qingyan. It was an open secret in the industry: Wen Qingyan had feelings for Jing Zejun.","Jiang Xu approached and greeted him with a smile, revealing a pair of small fangs. “Qingyan-ge, nice to meet you. I’m Jiang Xu.”","Wen Qingyan nodded politely. “Hello.” Then his gaze shifted to Jing Zejun.","They didn’t exchange words, but the look between them hinted at a connection that set them apart from others.","A shadow flickered in Jiang Xu’s eyes, though his smile remained bright. “I’ve heard a lot about you from Zejun. It’s a shame we’re only meeting now.”","Wen Qingyan’s expression didn’t change, his smile still gentle.","“Is that so? She’s never mentioned you to me.”","Jiang Xu’s smile faltered, unsure how to respond.","The director, sensing the tension, quickly changed the subject.","“Anyway, Jiang Xu, let’s have Qingyan demonstrate that scene for you.”","The director’s reasoning was simple: Wen Qingyan was a decorated actor, a rising star still highly sought after by directors.","If not for their prior relationship, it would’ve been difficult to get Wen Qingyan to do a demonstration.","Jiang Xu’s smile grew uneasy. “Director, isn’t that too much trouble for Qingyan-ge? I think I’ll get the hang of it if I practice more with Zejun.”","Before he could finish, Wen Qingyan interjected, “It’s no trouble at all. I’m happy to help. What do you think, Zejun?”","Jing Zejun, who was still processing the sudden turn of events, replied, “Uh, I don’t mind.” But how had things escalated so quickly?","With the director and the female lead both agreeing, Jiang Xu had no choice but to watch as Wen Qingyan stepped into his role.","Jiang Xu did like Jing Zejun, and while her family background played a part, it wasn’t as if he was solely after her wealth.","His gifts were sincere, and his feelings genuine—though one’s family was an inseparable part of who they were.","Wen Qingyan was indeed a formidable rival, more established in the industry. But since Jing Zejun hadn’t responded to either of them, didn’t that mean he still had a chance?","After all, in matters of the heart, there was no rule about who came first.","Jiang Xu stood where Wen Qingyan had been, watching as the director positioned the other man in his place."]},{"number":239,"title":"Chapter 239: Extra: The Story About the Public Relations Plan (Side Couple Final Chapter)","paragraphs":["Jing Zejun felt a bit nervous. She had never filmed a particularly intimate scene with Wen Qingyan before.","In *The Reign*, her love was one-sided, and the previous infinite flow plot was mainly focused on the storyline.","But why was she so nervous now when she hadn’t been earlier?","Their proximity was startlingly close—close enough for her to feel the warmth of his breath.","Jing Zejun began to feel flustered, her cheeks tinged with a subtle blush.","Wen Qingyan stood across from her, delivering the lines given by the director. His hand gently rose, his gaze firmly locked on her.","At that moment, time seemed to stand still. Wen Qingyan was absolutely certain—he wasn’t acting at all.","Those words were meant for Jing Zejun, and his racing heartbeat was entirely because of her.","Wen Qingyan’s hand slowly approached Jing Zejun’s face, coming to a gentle rest on her cheek.","The rest of the crew watched quietly, as if pink bubbles were floating around them. Even though the two were just standing there, they looked so perfectly matched.","In that moment, Wen Qingyan’s entire focus was on Jing Zejun. He leaned in slightly, using the angle to shield their movements.","His kiss landed softly on his thumb.","Yet, Jing Zejun could still feel it—his tenderness.","Her eyelashes fluttered, and she slowly closed her eyes, reaching up to wrap her arms around Wen Qingyan’s waist.","Behind Wen Qingyan, the crew members covered their mouths, their eyes sparkling as they watched the scene. They couldn’t take photos during filming, so they decided to memorize this moment instead!","The few who could see the angle were even more excited, pinching their thighs in delight.","Nothing was more captivating than such subtle, restrained love—it was simply perfect! They were utterly obsessed!","Time seemed to freeze. No one called “cut,” and everyone, including the director, continued to watch this beautiful moment.","But beneath the director’s excitement, it seemed he was still calculating something.","On the other side, the more excited the crew became, the fainter Jiang Xu’s smile grew.","After a few seconds, Wen Qingyan finally straightened up, looking at Jing Zejun, his hand unconsciously caressing her cheek.","“Great!”","The word “great” broke the lingering tension between them. Wen Qingyan withdrew his hand, composed himself, and then turned to the director.","The director was thrilled. He stepped forward, shaking Wen Qingyan’s hand. “Qingyan, do me a favor—let’s keep this scene as it is.”","Since their faces weren’t fully visible, they could just have Jiang Xu dub a few lines later.","The scene was simply too good to waste. Even from the back, it would captivate the audience, and the director couldn’t bear to let such a gem go unused.","At these words, Jiang Xu reacted the most.","He hurried over. “Director, isn’t this a bit inappropriate? We’re already troubling Qingyan enough, and given his status, he really shouldn’t be my stand-in.”","Wen Qingyan gave an amused glance at Jiang Xu, who was busy “defending” him.","“It’s fine. How could I not help the director? Besides, given my relationship with Zejun, it’s no big deal.”","“Exactly, Xiao Xu. Qingyan isn’t the type to stand on ceremony. Don’t let his status as an award-winning actor intimidate you...”","Jiang Xu wasn’t worried about whether Wen Qingyan was easy to work with. If they used this footage, his own highlight moment would be cut, and his intimate scenes with Jing Zejun would be gone too.","Of course, he was anxious.","Jiang Xu forced a smile. “Director, Qingyan and I have different body types. Won’t that give it away?”","The director waved dismissively. “Don’t worry. Without a full shot, no one will notice Qingyan is taller. As for the body shape, we’ll just slim him down a bit in post-production. It’ll be fine!”","Jiang Xu: ...Was that really the issue?","Then, the excited director made the decision—they would use Wen Qingyan’s footage for that scene.","...","After filming the remaining scenes, Jing Zejun brought Wen Qingyan back to the dressing room.","Honestly, she still felt a bit awkward around him and needed to find a topic to distract herself.","“By the way, Qingyan, are you less busy these days?”","Wen Qingyan’s voice came from behind her. “Yes, I just finished shooting. I’ve got some free time recently...”","He went into detail about his recent work, and Jing Zejun didn’t find anything unusual about this “report.”","It was as if she had grown accustomed to it.","Jing Zejun gradually calmed down and started chatting casually with Wen Qingyan.","“Do you have time to watch Yiyi’s competition next week? It’s in Jiangbei...” As she spoke, she noticed no response from behind her. She turned to look.","Wen Qingyan was staring at the potted plant Jiang Xu had given her. Jing Zejun suddenly realized something.","Wen Qingyan snapped out of it and tried to cover up with a smile. “What? The competition? Of course, I have time. Shall we go together?”","Jing Zejun fell silent. She felt there was something more important she needed to say right now.","“Qingyan, after the Golden Eagle Awards ceremony, can you...wait for me?”","Initially, Jing Zejun had wanted to use “awards” and “status” to create equality in their relationship. But just now, she realized that she and Wen Qingyan were inherently unequal.","For example, she was sure she didn’t love Wen Qingyan as much as he loved her.","Wen Qingyan’s mind went blank. “Don’t we need to wait for the results anymore?” He didn’t think waiting a few more years for Jing Zejun was a big deal. As long as she remembered him, he could wait forever.","Seeing Wen Qingyan’s expression, Jing Zejun suddenly felt a surge of courage. A smile spread across her face.","“No, we don’t.”","Because no matter what, she wanted to be with Wen Qingyan.","Whether it was status or reputation, what she sought was simply the courage to stand by his side.","Now, Wen Qingyan was her courage, and she wanted to be his courage too.","After the awards ceremony, Jing Zejun won the Best Actress award for a TV series. Wen Qingyan was thrilled for her—and for himself.","From that day on, they were together. Although they hadn’t told anyone, anyone who saw Wen Qingyan could tell something had changed.","He had gotten his wish.","His agent looked at Wen Qingyan’s beaming smile and couldn’t help but feel a bit exasperated.","“Alright, my award-winning actor, that’s enough. Your smile is practically reaching the moon. Don’t blame me if you end up with a stiff face.”","“Hehe.”","“...Good thing you’re on vacation right now. Otherwise, anyone who saw you would think you’ve either gone crazy or finally gotten what you wanted!”","“Hehe.”","“...You really look like an idiot.”","Later, the PR plan Wen Qingyan had prepared finally came into use, though in the eyes of countless netizens, it was no longer necessary.","That day, Jing Zejun and Wen Qingyan made their relationship official. Their Weibo post read: “This is a PR plan from many years ago. Thankfully, it hasn’t expired.”"]},{"number":240,"title":"Chapter 240: Extra: Married Life Episode 1 - About Getting Married","paragraphs":["On the day Jing Yi and Shen Huaichu got married, all the media outlets were eager to cover the event, but none of them received an invitation. Moreover, due to the strict confidentiality measures taken by the Jing family, there was no way they could sneak in.","Jing Yi and Shen Huaichu chose to hold their wedding in Berlin. Jing Yi had promised her grandmother that she would bring Shen Huaichu to meet her.","Jing Yi was never fond of attending banquets or wearing high heels, finding them inconvenient and cumbersome. So, on her wedding day, she opted for a white short wedding dress, a veil, and a beautifully done makeup, paired with black boots.","Driving her beloved 'Night', she set off to pick up the love of her life.","Sitting in the driver's seat, her wavy hair fluttered in the wind as the black sports car navigated through every corner of the city, her smile growing wider with each passing moment. She was on her way to pick up her groom!","Shen Huaichu stood at the entrance, dressed in a classic black suit with a black bow tie, accompanied by Gu Lin.","As the car window rolled down, Jing Yi leaned out, her eyes curved into a smile, her dimples showing.","\"Shen Huaichu, I'm here to pick you up!\" she said.","Shen Huaichu looked at her, a smile tugging at his lips, his eyes sparkling with joy.","...","Grandma Jing's home and Jing Yi's place were close to the venue, a sprawling estate that Grandma Jing had gifted to Jing Yi. They had once envisioned Jing Yi's wedding on the vast lawn of that estate.","The venue had been meticulously prepared for nearly a month, a testament to the Jing family's dedication. The lawn, now a vibrant green, was a sight to behold.","The venue was exquisitely decorated, complemented by the majestic mountains in the distance, creating a breathtaking scene.","All the guests had taken their seats, and Shen Huaichu, the groom, stood at his designated spot, waiting for the bride to make her entrance.","Before Jing Yi left her room, Jing Zejun and Lin Ruiqing gave her final touches to her makeup and hairstyle.","Lin Ruiqing's eyes were red as she looked at Jing Yi with admiration. \"Our Yi Yi is so beautiful!\" she exclaimed.","Jing Zejun's eyes were also slightly red, but she had the task of delivering the rings later and was reminding Jing Yi of the wedding procedures.","As Jing Yi stepped out of her room, she was met by Jing Zeqian, who looked unusually serious and formal today.","He extended his hand, and Jing Yi, recalling the procedures, placed her hand in his, even though this wasn't part of the plan.","He led Jing Yi for a short distance, where Jing Zeyou was waiting.","Jing Zeqian said, \"Jing Yi Yi, if you're not happy, I will definitely beat that guy up.\" He added, \"I'm not joking.\"","Jing Yi's heart softened as she looked at Jing Zeqian with tenderness.","\"Okay,\" she replied.","Jing Zeqian handed her hand to Jing Zeyou and turned away discreetly.","Jing Zeyou seemed his usual self, though a bit more silent than usual.","\"Yi Yi, I still say the same thing: I hope you always have the courage to move forward without hesitation.\"","\"And your brother will always be your support.\"","It was he who had agreed to bring Jing Yi back, interrupting her affluent yet lonely life, and he would forever be her safeguard.","Because he was her brother.","Jing Yi's eyes reddened. \"Big brother, I'll come home for dinner in a few days,\" she said, though they lived so close.","Jing Zeyou's lips curved into a gentle smile. \"Okay, we'll be waiting for you at home,\" he replied.","The walk was short, and Jing Zeyou finally handed Jing Yi's hand to Jing Beicheng, watching her walk towards the center of the venue.","Jing Yi, arm in arm with Jing Beicheng, walked carefully, step by step.","The path seemed both long and short, and soon Jing Yi stood before Shen Huaichu.","Jing Beicheng held Jing Yi's hand and solemnly placed it in Shen Huaichu's palm.","\"Shen Huaichu, I have only one thing to say,\" Jing Beicheng said earnestly. \"I entrust Yi Yi to you. She remains the cherished daughter of the Jing family, my daughter. She has parents, brothers, and sisters. She is not alone...\"","In their family, there was no notion of a daughter being like water thrown out after marriage.","Jing Beicheng's voice trembled, and Jing Yi's eyes welled up with tears.","Shen Huaichu held Jing Yi's hand firmly and said seriously, \"You can rest assured. I will always remember that the Jing family's scrutiny lasts a lifetime.\"","The somber mood lightened with a touch of humor, and even Jing Yi laughed, wiping away her tears.","...","The wedding proceeded to the next ceremony. Jing Yi and Shen Huaichu stood at the front, facing their family, siblings, and friends.","Shen Huaichu's hand was still trembling, a fact Jing Yi had noticed earlier.","It turned out that beneath his calm exterior, he was secretly shaking.","He held her hand tightly, his other hand clutching the vows. Jing Yi, with reddened eyes, smiled and reminded him.","\"Shen Huaichu, this isn't convenient,\" she said.","But Shen Huaichu insisted, \"It is convenient.\"","\"Jing Yi, I wrote these vows while you were asleep because you always wanted to copy mine...\"","Jing Yi widened her eyes in mock indignation: Stingy! What harm would it do to let her take a look? And why mention it in front of so many people?","A wave of good-natured laughter rose from the audience.","\"I never imagined that one day I would love someone so deeply, let alone that she would love me back, that I would meet her family, and even marry her.\"","\"How could a bond that even blood ties can't secure be made strong by mere dopamine and pheromones?\"","\"But Jing Yi, you made me meet you.\"","\"At Huarui Group, there's still gossip that I fell for the 'sports car beauty' who drove me every day. Miss Jing, I wish I could tell them how much I schemed to ensure that the sports car beauty would 'coincidentally' pass by the company entrance.\"","\"Everyone who hears about such a terrifying person would be scared, but you, foolishly, told me not to take on too much trouble.\"","\"I had planned a grand proposal, but in the end, you beat me to it.\"","Shen Huaichu spoke with a trembling voice, smiling.","\"I used to hate this world so much, but then you appeared, and I wanted to stay in this world.\"","\"I wanted to become a slightly normal person, to stay in this world that you love.\"","\"Fortunately, I stayed.\"","Shen Huaichu's smile widened, his eyes filled with joy.","\"A week before the wedding, Jing Zeyou and the others took turns talking to me. That's when I realized that while I might have only two brothers-in-law on paper, it took a whole week for them to finish their warnings.\"","Jing Yi was still crying, but his words broke through her emotions.","Shen Huaichu raised his hand holding the vows and gently wiped the tears from Jing Yi's face, his eyes almost melting with tenderness.","\"You love this world so much, and it should love you back. And I am one of those who do.\"","\"Jing Yi, I will love you, deeply and forever.\"","Jing Yi's eyelashes fluttered, her smile soft and radiant, her eyes slightly red but clear and transparent, filled with love.","\"But Shen Huaichu, I will always stand by your side, steadfast and without question.\""]},{"number":241,"title":"Chapter 241: Extra: Married Life 2 - The Meeting Between Wen Qingyan and Shen Huaichu","paragraphs":["For Jing Zeqian, neither Shen Huaichu nor Wen Qingyan were good people! One was a \"smiling tiger,\" and the other was a cold-faced wolf!","Until one day, these two met.","Wen Qingyan had always known that Jing Yi, Jing Zeqian's younger sister, had an impressive boyfriend.","It wasn’t that he was impressive because he was the CEO of Huarui Group, but because he could constantly stand up to Jing Zeqian. That was truly impressive.","Wen Qingyan sat in the Jing family living room, looking at his future brother-in-law and his future brother-in-law’s brother, unsure of what expression to wear.","He couldn’t help but feel that the atmosphere wasn’t exactly pleasant.","Beside him, Jing Zeqian crossed his arms, his face full of mockery. \"Mr. Shen, have you gained any official status today?\"","Shen Huaichu remained calm and composed, raising his hand slightly so that the sparkling ring on his slender finger could be clearly seen by Jing Zeqian.","His face remained expressionless, but the hint of pride was unmistakable.","\"Second Brother, as you can see, I’ve gained some official status.\"","Was this a show of dominance? Wen Qingyan thought to himself.","Jing Zeqian snorted coldly, his expression still displeased as he looked at Shen Huaichu. \"A mere engagement ring doesn’t mean much. I think there’s still some distance before you can claim any real ‘official status.’\"","Shen Huaichu nodded in agreement. He felt the same way. Until he had that red marriage certificate in hand, he didn’t truly have any official status.","Wen Qingyan had thought the tension between the two might ease a bit, but then he heard Shen Huaichu say, \"Thank you for the reminder, Second Brother. I’ll discuss getting the marriage certificate with Yi tomorrow.\"","Jing Zeqian seemed to explode at this, standing up abruptly. \"Dream on! You haven’t even passed the probation period yet. Talking about marriage is way too early!\"","Wen Qingyan was aware of the Jing family’s probation period. He felt like it might take three to five years before Shen Huaichu could pass it.","Shen Huaichu, however, didn’t quite agree with this. He could stay on probation for the rest of his life, but he needed to secure his official status first.","Jing Yi was completely unfazed by the bickering between Shen Huaichu and Jing Zeqian. The Jing family was used to it. They had thought Jing Yi and Jing Zeqian were the pinnacle of sibling rivalry, but it turned out that Shen Huaichu and Jing Zeqian were truly \"natural opposites.\"","Later, Shen Huaichu actually managed to secure his official status first. Wen Qingyan was both shocked and surprised. He began to reflect on his own approach.","Was his method too \"gentle,\" causing him to fall behind? Should he learn a thing or two from his future brother-in-law?","When Jing Zejun found out about this idea, she immediately put on a serious face and stopped Wen Qingyan from pursuing this \"dangerous\" thought.","\"Don’t learn Shen Huaichu’s tricks. They’re dangerous.\"","Her second brother’s situation was truly precarious.","Thanks to his thoughtful sister’s intervention, Jing Zeqian didn’t end up with another \"opponent\" to deal with.","......","Since the two families lived close by, the brothers-in-law occasionally ran into each other, and over time, they began to communicate more.","For example, they discussed who was more difficult to deal with: the elder brother-in-law or the younger brother-in-law.","Wen Qingyan admitted that Jing Zeqian, the younger brother-in-law, was indeed quite a handful. Not only was he his partner’s brother, but he was also his former employer. With all these layers, Wen Qingyan felt that Jing Zeqian was even more challenging.","Shen Huaichu looked up at Wen Qingyan, who was analyzing the situation seriously, and asked quietly, \"Did Jing Zeyou say anything after you two got together?\"","Wen Qingyan shook his head. He had also thought Jing Zeyou would be harder to \"win over,\" but ever since he started dating Jing Zejun, he had been mostly dealing with Jing Zeqian and hadn’t interacted much with Jing Zeyou.","Therefore, he concluded, \"In comparison, the elder brother-in-law is much easier to get along with.\"","Moreover, Jing Zejun greatly admired Jing Zeyou, and over time, Wen Qingyan’s fondness for Jing Zeyou also grew significantly.","Hearing this, Shen Huaichu’s expression became unusually complex.","His elder brother-in-law really knew how to \"make the most of everything.\" No wonder Hengjing had risen to new heights in such a short time.","Thinking about it, it was a bit disheartening.","Not only did he have to deal with the younger brother-in-law’s \"sarcastic remarks,\" but he also had to handle the elder brother-in-law’s \"little surprises,\" as well as occasionally take time to discuss the topic of \"why you’re not the best choice for my sister.\"","Shen Huaichu silently lamented that being a brother-in-law was truly a blessing.","Another example was when their wives returned and immediately clung to their sisters (or sisters-in-law).","At Wen Qingyan’s home, Shen Huaichu observed the director’s team setting up camera equipment.","Wen Qingyan handed Shen Huaichu a cup of coffee. \"Mr. Shen, netizens are saying that my couple’s variety show is turning into a family variety show.\"","Wen Qingyan had struggled for a while with how to address Shen Huaichu. Shen Huaichu had said that since they were brothers-in-law, there was no need to be so formal, and he even called Wen Qingyan \"brother-in-law.\"","However, compared to calling Shen Huaichu \"brother-in-law\" or \"Huaichu,\" Wen Qingyan still felt more comfortable calling him \"Mr. Shen.\"","Shen Huaichu didn’t press the matter further.","Shen Huaichu looked away from the equipment. \"Thank you, brother-in-law.\"","He took the coffee from Wen Qingyan, took a sip, and casually remarked, \"How about you suggest to the director that they film outside?\"","When Shen Huaichu found out that Wen Qingyan and his wife were filming at home, he had anticipated this scenario. He glanced at his watch. It had been almost an hour. What on earth were they talking about?","Shen Huaichu added, \"If they need a location, I have an island abroad.\" It was a place he had bought for his honeymoon with Jing Yi, and she had loved it, but they hadn’t visited it often.","That island would certainly be far enough.","Wen Qingyan’s hand holding the coffee cup paused. He could easily guess Shen Huaichu’s intentions. They were both in the same boat.","However, it wasn’t his place to make the suggestion.","\"How about you suggest it to the director, Mr. Shen? After all, it’s your island.\"","Shen Huaichu set his coffee cup down steadily and replied calmly, \"You should suggest it, brother-in-law. I’m not really connected to this variety show.\"","\"How could that be? If you provide the filming location, you’d be an investor in the show. How could you say you’re not connected?\"","Shen Huaichu paused for a second and said seriously, \"Jing Yi would be upset if she found out.\"","Jing Yi could always guess his thoughts. If she found out he was trying to send Jing Zejun so far away for work, she would definitely be angry.","Wen Qingyan gave him a helpless look. \"Mr. Shen, Jing Zejun is the same.\" It wasn’t as if his wife wouldn’t get upset either. Jing Zejun might usually be gentle, but when she got angry, it took him ten to fifteen days to calm her down.","The two fell into silence, both sipping their coffee.","Wen Qingyan finally said, \"...Then let’s forget it.\"","\"...Agreed.\"","In the background, the crew setting up the equipment couldn’t help but tremble. Why hadn’t they mentioned this before they started filming?!"]},{"number":242,"title":"Chapter 242: Extra: Married Life 3: The Daily Marriage Pressure","paragraphs":["Lin Ruiqing had been feeling a bit troubled lately.","Although she had previously said she wouldn’t meddle too much in her children’s love lives, she wondered if she had perhaps been too hands-off, given that her two sons still showed no signs of romance.","She glanced at Jing Zeyou, who was eating quietly. Her eldest son was handsome and successful in his career, so why didn’t he have a girlfriend?","Then she looked at Jing Zeqian, who was currently bickering with Jing Yi over a piece of food. She paused, her expression complicated.","Surely, there must be someone who would like a lively man like him, right?","“Shen Huaichu, you’re cheating!”","Jing Zeqian glared at Shen Huaichu, who had sneakily helped Jing Yi snatch the chicken wing while he wasn’t paying attention.","Shen Huaichu glanced at Jing Yi, who was proudly showing off her victory, a hint of tenderness in his eyes. “Second brother, didn’t you say ‘whoever’s faster gets it’?”","Jing Zeqian’s eyes widened. This guy was using his own words against him—words he had once used to triumph over Jing Yi.","How sneaky!","Lin Ruiqing heaved a heavy sigh. Jing Beicheng asked, “What’s wrong? Is the food not to your taste?” He noticed the direction of his wife’s gaze and added, “Or are Zeqian and the others bothering you?”","Jing Zeqian and Shen Huaichu: “...”","Lin Ruiqing shook her head and sighed again. “It’s just that with fewer people around, meals don’t feel as lively.”","Jing Zeyou’s hand holding the chopsticks paused for a moment, and he subtly sped up his eating. Jing Zeqian looked up in confusion, staring at the large family gathered around the table.","“Mom, this is too few? We could easily form two mahjong tables with this many people.” How many more did she want? A family meeting that felt like a classroom lecture?","Lin Ruiqing shot her younger son a glare. “Is that what I meant?” Jing Zeqian immediately understood and shut his mouth, lowering his head to avoid further attention.","Jing Yi and Jing Zejun didn’t dare to get involved either, focusing intently on their meals.","Seeing that no one was responding, Lin Ruiqing glanced at Jing Beicheng beside her. He cleared his throat and said, “Your mother is right. It’s about time you two started thinking about your marriage prospects.”","Jing Zeqian silently grumbled to himself. Marriage prospects? There wasn’t even a hint of romance in sight, so how could there be any talk of marriage?","Lin Ruiqing asked, “Who wants to go first?” Even if there were no prospects, they should at least have a plan.","Jing Zeqian lowered his head even further. He was the younger brother, so his older brother should speak first.","Jing Zeyou sighed inwardly and stepped up. “Mom, I’m still focused on my work.”","Jing Yi quietly looked up, giving her eldest brother a look of respect. When others said this, it might be an excuse, but when Jing Zeyou said it, he meant it.","He probably thought that romance would only interfere with his work! A true workaholic!","Lin Ruiqing retorted, “You practically live at Hengjing 24/7. How much more work do you need to do? Besides, Shen Huaichu is also the CEO of Huarui Group, and he manages both his career and family life just fine.”","And as for his father, he had achieved both career success and a happy family life from the same position.","Jing Beicheng: Because he has a wonderful wife.","Jing Zeyou: “...”","And to bring up a closer example, Shen Huaichu was even younger than Jing Zeyou, yet his career was thriving, and he already had a beautiful wife.","Jing Zeqian: “A bit biased there, huh?”","Jing Yi: “Don’t stir the pot!”","Jing Zeyou looked at the so-called “model child” his mother was praising and found it rather amusing. This was the first time he had been on the receiving end of such a comparison.","In the past, he had always been the one held up as an example.","Shen Huaichu understood the look in his brother-in-law’s eyes and smiled gently. “Mom, I was just lucky.” He left it at that, not elaborating further.","After all, the last time he had asked Jing Zeyou for help, things had turned out rather awkwardly. Jing Zeqian still teased him about the “pretty boy” incident to this day.","Jing Zeqian, sitting nearby, rolled his eyes and smirked.","This guy always acted so well-behaved, especially after marrying Jing Yi. He called their parents “Mom” and “Dad” so smoothly it was almost nauseating.","As Jing Zeqian was silently mocking him, Lin Ruiqing noticed his defiant expression.","“Jing Zeqian, do you think I’m only talking about your brother?”","Her eldest son was excused because he was genuinely busy with work, but her younger son worked in the entertainment industry. How come there wasn’t even a hint of gossip about him?","Jing Zeqian quickly straightened his expression and said seriously, “Mom, we run a legitimate entertainment company.”","Not just him, but even the agents and artists under their management had been warned: any hint of “casting couch” behavior would result in immediate termination and a lifetime ban from the industry.","Lin Ruiqing: “...” Was that what she meant?","But Lin Ruiqing’s confusion was shared by many paparazzi.","Unlike other entertainment company bosses, Jing Zeqian was a hot topic himself. Being the youngest son of the Jing family from North River, he had a substantial fan following online. Tracking his personal life was as lucrative as following a top-tier celebrity.","Yet, when it came to gossip about him? There was nothing worth mentioning.","Jing Zeqian took some pride in this. In the eyes of the paparazzi, he was the epitome of a “clean-living” bachelor.","Lin Ruiqing: “Whether he’s a bachelor or not, he’s certainly on his way to becoming an old one.”","Jing Zeyou sipped his soup leisurely. “Don’t worry, Mom. At worst, Jing Yi and Zejun’s children can inherit Hengjing.”","Jing Yi was stunned. How did this suddenly involve her?","Jing Zejun and Wen Qingyan exchanged glances, both seeing confusion in each other’s eyes.","Wen Qingyan smiled and said, “Big brother, Zejun is still focused on her career right now. We don’t have any plans for children yet.” Even if they did, given their personalities, they would likely prioritize their child’s wishes.","Shen Huaichu remained calm, serving Jing Yi a bowl of soup. He said slowly, “Big brother, whether Jing Yi has plans is another matter. She’s preparing for a competition right now. Even if we did have a child, we’d probably consider Huarui Group first.”","For Shen Huaichu, whether they had children or not didn’t matter. Everything depended on Jing Yi’s wishes.","Jing Yi: “Great, this hypothetical child already has two corporations vying for their future.”","Jing Zeyou raised an eyebrow, a competitive spark igniting within him. “Then let the child choose when the time comes.”","He thought that, compared to Shen Huaichu, he would probably be more popular with children. He had that much confidence.","Shen Huaichu paused, understanding Jing Zeyou’s implication. He silently considered the odds of winning against Jing Zeyou and realized they were rather low.","After all, even the child’s mother was biased...","Sometimes he wanted to ask Jing Yi who she would save if he and Jing Zeyou both fell into the water.","But the thought seemed too childish, and there was also the fear of embarrassing himself, so he never dared to ask.","As for why Jing Zeqian wasn’t included in this hypothetical scenario?","If he and Jing Zeqian ever fell into the water together, he’d make sure to “drown” Jing Zeqian first!","Seeing the conversation veering further off track, Lin Ruiqing forced a smile and said threateningly, “Zeyou, you should focus on your own prospects first.” Stop scheming about other people’s children!","Jing Zeyou looked away. “Alright, I’ll do my best.” They could deal with the rest later."]},{"number":243,"title":"Chapter 243: Extra: Married Life 4 - Jing Yi Makes an Appearance","paragraphs":["The marriage of Jing Zejun and Wen Qingyan caused quite a stir. Although everyone had assumed that the two would eventually end up together, the official announcement still managed to create a significant buzz.","As Jing Zejun's career continued to flourish, the \"intense back-and-forth\" between her and Wen Qingyan on a variety show years ago had almost been dissected to the point of becoming a meme among netizens.","Then, one day, it was suddenly announced that Jing Zejun and Wen Qingyan would be appearing on a couples' variety show. The news immediately crashed Weibo.","[Oh my god! This is the kind of thing you only dream of seeing in your lifetime! I never thought I'd get to watch a couples' show featuring the \"Jun-Yan\" duo!]","[Finally, my patience has paid off! I'm ready to ship them to death!]","[Ahhh!!! No more scrounging for crumbs from their rare appearances together!]","[Where are they filming?! Is it at the Jing family estate? Will Jing Yiyi be there?!]","[Hey, fellow shipper! I'm also waiting for any glimpse of Jing Yiyi. Her and General Shen are such a treat to watch!]","[Wait, is General Shen Jing Yiyi's mysterious husband?]","[How long have you been offline? Jing Yiyi is often seen picking someone up at the Huarui Group headquarters.]","[I know this! I watched Shen Huaichu's interview, and I could barely tell it was an economic media piece—it was practically a gossip session about his love life.]","[The best part is that General Shen actually played along. I thought he had a bad temper.]","[Hey, I work at Huarui Group, and trust me, General Shen's temper isn't great. That was just him marking his territory...]","The thread gradually veered off-topic. If it were any other celebrity, they might have been upset about someone else stealing their spotlight, but it was well-known among netizens that Jing Zejun and Jing Yiyi were so close that they wouldn't mind.","When the show aired, the camera once again captured the elegant villa from years ago. However, this time, the crew didn't head toward that villa but instead moved toward a nearby location.","This was Jing Zejun and Wen Qingyan's home.","Wen Qingyan opened the door and welcomed the camera crew inside. Seeing a familiar face, he smiled and said, \"Director Xu, long time no see.\"","The decision to join the show was made by Jing Zejun, as they rarely participated in variety shows these days.","They agreed to this one for two reasons: first, both of them were at the peak of their careers—especially Jing Zejun—and they had been spending less time together; second, it was a familiar production team, so they felt more at ease.","Director Xu's face was creased with smiles. After all, these two were among the people who had helped him rise to fame.","\"Wen Qingyan, it's been a while!\" He stepped aside to chat with Wen Qingyan. \"Is Zejun not here?\"","The filming was meant to be a surprise, and Wen Qingyan had only received the news an hour ago.","Wen Qingyan glanced toward a nearby location and smiled. \"She's over at Jing Yiyi's place.\" A hint of resignation flickered in his eyes.","They had finally found some time together, and just yesterday, his dear wife had affectionately expressed how much she missed him. But as soon as Jing Yiyi returned from her business trip this morning, his wife had fluttered over like a moth to a flame.","This, of course, didn't escape the eagle-eyed netizens.","[Hahaha, I knew it! This couples' show might just turn into a family show!]","[And I'm absolutely here for it!]","[But living together like this, they must really get along well.]","[More like living in a cluster.]","[The word \"cluster\" cracked me up.]","A glimmer of amusement flashed in Director Xu's eyes, but he quickly composed himself when Wen Qingyan looked over. He then grabbed one of the cameramen.","\"Uh, Wen Qingyan, do you think you could ask Zejun if we could come over and film for a bit?\"","Wen Qingyan: \"...You're all heartless.\"","What else could Wen Qingyan do but reluctantly contact Jing Zejun?","Watching Director Xu's hurried footsteps as he practically sprinted ahead, Wen Qingyan sighed. It seemed his couples' show would have to share the spotlight.","What Wen Qingyan didn't know was that after Director Xu left, half of the live stream viewers also switched over.","Meanwhile, Director Xu, feeling like he'd struck gold, eagerly made his way to Jing Yiyi's villa.","He had reached out to Jing Yiyi during the initial guest invitations for the show, but she had declined. Who would have thought things would take such a turn? Even a brief appearance would be a huge win!","Director Xu took a deep breath and knocked on the door.","Jing Zejun answered and exchanged a quick greeting before inviting them in.","In the living room, Jing Yiyi stood there, her beautiful eyes curved into a smile, her signature dimples on full display.","\"Director Xu, long time no see!\"","\"Jing Yiyi, it's been a while!\"","Although they hadn't met in person, Director Xu had often seen Jing Yiyi in various media outlets, such as racing circles and sports platforms.","Noticing the excitement in Director Xu's eyes, Jing Yiyi found it amusing.","The reason she agreed to let Director Xu come over was mainly because she had declined his earlier invitation, even though their previous collaboration had been quite enjoyable.","Still, she didn't mind indulging his and the viewers' curiosity a little.","\"Since you're here, why don't I show you around my place?\"","Director Xu had been wondering how to bring this up, so when Jing Yiyi offered, his eyes lit up, and he nodded eagerly.","The villa wasn't particularly large, as it was just for her and Shen Huaichu. Besides, most of the things they needed were already at the Jing family estate, and she was more accustomed to Aunt Wang's cooking, so she spent more time there.","\"...Downstairs is the basement, where I keep some cars.\"","Over the years, Jing Yiyi had participated in numerous racing competitions. As her fame grew, so did her collection of cars, and she needed a place to store them at home.","Some were gifts from the Jing family, others from Shen Huaichu, and a few from friends.","[What does \"some\" mean?]","[\"Some\"?! I can already see so many in the shot!]","[I want to see! I want to see! Director Xu, show us!!!]","[Who remembers the \"Night\"? I fell in love with it at first sight. How can a car be that stunning?!]","[But in terms of fame, the red Bugatti Jing Yi drove to win the GT championship probably takes the cake.]","Jing Yiyi had assumed the crew wouldn't be too interested, as they were likely more focused on uncovering the \"secrets\" between her and Shen Huaichu.","But after hearing her mention the cars, Director Xu immediately asked, \"Can we film them?\"","How could Director Xu pass up this opportunity? Which director could boast of capturing Jing Yiyi's entire collection of sports cars and race cars on camera?","This was Jing Yi, not just the Jing family heiress, but the champion racer Jing Yi's home!","Jing Yiyi was momentarily surprised but nodded. \"Sure.\"","Thinking about it, Director Xu couldn't help but feel a sense of nostalgia. The last time they met, Jing Yiyi was still the controversial \"fake heiress\" of the Jing family. Now, she was a celebrated racing champion.","Jing Yiyi didn't quite understand Director Xu's excitement, but most of the cars had been featured in the media before, so it wasn't a big secret.","\"I'll take you down to see them in a bit.\""]},{"number":244,"title":"Chapter 244: Extra: Married Life 5 - About Shen Huaichu's Ability to Paint","paragraphs":["Jing Yi's villa wasn’t particularly large, but its interior decoration leaned towards an elegant and understated style. The simplicity of the design made the oil paintings on the walls stand out even more.","From the moment he entered, Director Xu noticed these paintings. Among them were landscapes, but most featured Jing Yi herself, as well as images of her racing.","Director Xu found it a bit strange. After all, in his impression, Jing Yi wasn’t the type to enjoy showcasing herself so prominently.","The landscape paintings were beautiful, and the ones depicting the racetrack offered a refreshing perspective.","“Who painted those?” Director Xu couldn’t resist his curiosity and asked.","Jing Yi turned her gaze toward the paintings, a faint dimple appearing on her cheek, as if filled with a sense of satisfaction.","Jing Zejun, standing beside her, answered, “Those were painted by her fiancé, Shen Huaichu.”","The fact that Shen Huaichu could paint came as a surprise to everyone in the Jing family. But then again, considering that his aunt, Shen Tu, was a renowned painter, it wasn’t entirely unexpected that her nephew might have some artistic skills.","Still, painting seemed somewhat out of character for Shen Huaichu.","Anyone hearing about this for the first time would be shocked, just like Director Xu, who widened his eyes in disbelief. “Shen Huaichu painted these?!” He looked back at the paintings, his eyes filled with astonishment.","No wonder Jing Yi appeared in almost every one of them.","[Wait, who painted them?!]","[I even thought Jing Yi commissioned someone to paint them, but never imagined it was Shen Huaichu.]","[I thought Jing Yi was like Jing Zeqian, enjoying having self-portraits at home.]","[When did you ever see Jing Zeqian’s house?]","[I haven’t, but I just assumed he’d be that kind of person.]","[Poor Jing Zeqian, his reputation is taking a hit.]","[No, the real shocker here is that Shen Huaichu, the CEO of Huarui Group, can paint oil paintings?!]","[Fun fact: Shen Huaichu’s aunt is Shen Tu, a famous oil painting master in the country.]","[Having portraits of your lover at home, painted by your own hand—that’s so romantic!]","While netizens were still immersed in the romantic story of Jing Yi and Shen Huaichu, Jing Yi herself was starting to feel a bit uncomfortable.","Oh no, Shen Huaichu’s dignified image is about to take another hit.","......","Jing Yi hadn’t known about Shen Huaichu’s painting skills much earlier than Jing Zejun and the others. She had only learned about it from Gu Lin.","That day, Gu Lin had been acting extremely mysterious, constantly keeping an eye on Shen Huaichu’s movements, which piqued Jing Yi’s curiosity.","“...That room over there will definitely give you goosebumps.”","Jing Yi stole a glance. She had been to Shen Huaichu’s house several times, and the place Gu Lin was pointing to was just a guest room, wasn’t it?","Gu Lin was still sneaking looks at Shen Huaichu. “It used to be a guest room, but after my brother returned from treatment, it was completely transformed.”","Although, what was with this secretive atmosphere?","Jing Yi glanced at Shen Huaichu, who wasn’t far away, and instinctively lowered her voice. “So, what’s in there now?” Gu Lin replied mysteriously, “It’s my brother’s masterpiece exhibition room!”","Masterpiece? What kind of masterpiece?","Jing Yi frowned. Why couldn’t Gu Lin just explain everything at once?","Instead, Gu Lin acted all profound, telling her she had to see it for herself to fully experience the shock and goosebumps. He even promised to distract Shen Huaichu for her.","Wasn’t it wrong to sneak a peek at someone else’s secret? Even as fiancés, shouldn’t they respect some boundaries?","Without hesitation, Jing Yi said, “Alright! Make sure you keep him occupied!” She climbed the stairs and, while Shen Huaichu wasn’t looking, opened the door.","That day, Jing Yi saw the mysterious room Gu Lin had mentioned. She didn’t feel the goosebumps Gu Lin had promised, but her heart softened, feeling as if it had caved in.","She stood at the doorway when Shen Huaichu hurried over, a hint of fear hidden in his eyes. He didn’t even have time to scold Gu Lin, his entire focus on Jing Yi’s reaction.","Looking at Shen Huaichu, Jing Yi smiled, her eyes curving into crescents.","“Gu Lin! No peeking!”","With that, she wrapped her arms around Shen Huaichu’s neck, pressing her lips to his. They were slightly cool, but that didn’t matter.","Gu Lin: Ugh, yet another overly affectionate fiancé couple!","......","After receiving Jing Yi’s ‘tacit approval,’ Shen Huaichu became more ‘open’ about his hobby.","At the racetrack again, on the same viewing stand, Jing Zeqian glanced at Shen Huaichu beside him, his expression a mix of complexity and exasperation.","He had always thought Shen Huaichu’s ‘illness’ hadn’t fully healed, and now he seemed to have gone completely ‘mad.’","Like right now, holding an oil paintbrush and painting? At a racetrack?","What kind of habit was this?","Jing Zeqian leaned over to take a look. Surprisingly, the painting wasn’t bad. He took another glance—seems like Shen Huaichu hadn’t been idle during his treatment.","One more look, and he realized it was a great way to pass the time. By the time he finished a painting, the race would probably be over.","Shen Huaichu: “...Second Brother, do you need something?”","The subtext was clear: If you don’t have anything important, kindly leave and stop bothering me.","Jing Zeqian pretended not to understand and instead asked curiously, “You can paint? When did you learn that?” Others nearby also pricked up their ears, equally curious.","Although they disapproved of Jing Zeqian’s nosiness, they couldn’t help but want to know the answer themselves.","Shen Huaichu wasn’t oblivious to their curiosity. He sighed inwardly, put down his brush, and resignedly answered.","“Around four or five years old, I don’t remember the exact time.” After all, it had been so long. His memories of learning oil painting were mostly tied to the arguments between his father and his aunt, Shen Tu.","After his parents passed away, he hadn’t thought of picking it up again. But during that dark period, he needed an outlet, something to hold onto, or he might not have made it through.","Jing Zeqian was surprised, looking Shen Huaichu up and down. “I thought you learned it during the time you were gone.” Shen Huaichu fell silent. Aside from Jing Yi, Jing Zeqian was the only one who would so bluntly bring up his ‘disappearance.’","But did Jing Zeqian even realize that he had gone away for treatment, not for a vacation?","“...I’m not that talented.” If it weren’t for the hours he had put in as a child, he probably would have forgotten most of it by now.","The others finally understood—Shen Huaichu’s aunt, Shen Tu, was an oil painter, so it wasn’t so surprising that he could paint.","But if Shen Huaichu were to ask his aunt for her opinion, she would probably criticize his work. Not that it mattered, though, since his audience consisted of only one person.","Shen Huaichu looked at the figure in the painting, wearing a helmet, his deep eyes filled with tenderness.","But of course, there was someone who couldn’t read the room. “What are you staring at? You need to finish this before Jing Yi’s race starts, right? If you have time, how about painting me too?”","Shen Huaichu: ...No, thanks.","“I don’t need all the details or background. Just paint me, okay? Like, just...”","Jing Zeqian was already imagining himself immortalized in a painting, while Shen Huaichu felt completely numb.","He regretted it. He should have taken this secret to his grave.","In the end, Lin Ruiqing couldn’t stand it anymore and dragged Jing Zeqian away."]},{"number":245,"title":"Chapter 245: Extra: Married Life 6 - Recreating the 'Six-Person Team'","paragraphs":["Early in the morning, the recording of the reality show featuring the married couple Jing Zejun and Wen Qingyan continued.","The camera panned, and the first to appear in the frame was Wen Qingyan, who had just finished his workout and was now skillfully preparing breakfast in the kitchen.","Director Xu wasn’t surprised, as he had seen Wen Qingyan cook before, but he couldn’t help but feel a bit nostalgic.","It was hard to believe that so many years had passed, and everyone from back then had undergone significant changes.","“Do you cook often now, Wen Qingyan?”","Wen Qingyan, while expertly frying a sunny-side-up egg, replied to Director Xu.","“Not really, but when I’m with Zejun, I like to make her favorite dishes. We often wake up early to exercise, and I want her to have breakfast ready as soon as we’re done.”","Since marrying Jing Zejun, Wen Qingyan’s daily routine had gradually aligned with hers, including the habit of waking up early for exercise.","[Some people become better after marriage, while others seem to deteriorate...]","[Don’t say that, I’m feeling a bit emotional.]","[Wen Qingyan has truly become more domestic, and what’s more, they seem to bring out the best in each other!]","[So heartwarming! Just seeing them live happily makes me feel content!]","[Same here!]","[I’m different though, I’m just curious about how enjoyable it must be to run in such a luxurious estate!]","[I wonder if they might bump into other members of the Jing family while jogging.]","[Unlikely, but they might end up running into someone else’s property.]","[Hahaha, that’s too funny.]","By now, Wen Qingyan had finished cooking and was plating the food. Jing Zejun had already finished her morning routine and came downstairs.","“Today we’re having egg and bacon sandwiches,” she said.","Wen Qingyan, as usual, sat beside Jing Zejun. Hearing the delight in her voice, he smiled softly, his entire demeanor radiating warmth.","The two enjoyed their breakfast together, as they always did.","As Jing Zejun ate her sandwich, she suddenly remembered something.","“Oh, by the way, your parents are coming back the day after tomorrow.”","She was referring to Wen Qingyan’s parents. She had once worried about how to get along with them, but they turned out to be much more approachable than she had imagined.","Like Wen Qingyan, they were gentle and kind, even more carefree than her own parents.","Since Jing Zejun and Wen Qingyan got married, the couple had almost embarked on a world-touring plan, occasionally traveling with Lin Ruiqing and Jing Beicheng.","Hearing Jing Zejun’s words, Wen Qingyan took a moment to process.","“They’re coming back?” he asked, surprised. Jing Zejun looked up, puzzled. “...Didn’t your mom tell you?”","Wen Qingyan couldn’t help but laugh. He had always been independent, partly due to his parents’ hands-off approach.","Now that he was married, they didn’t even feel the need to inform him of their travel plans.","“You could say that. Ever since they started traveling, apart from messages to assure us they’re safe, they haven’t shared anything else.”","This wasn’t an exaggeration. Wen Qingyan and his parents weren’t the type to share every detail of their lives.","Jing Zejun’s eyes sparkled with amusement, her smile serene. “Well, you can’t compare to me. I get photos and stories from them every few days.”","Wen Qingyan handed her a glass of milk, his gaze tender, feigning resignation. “Yes, yes, I’m always last in this family.”","Though he said that, he couldn’t be prouder or happier.","Listening to their conversation, the production team and viewers could guess who they were talking about and couldn’t help but chuckle.","Perhaps worried that Wen Qingyan might get embarrassed, Director Xu seized the moment to introduce the day’s theme—hosting guests.","The production team had already arranged for guests, but to maintain an element of surprise, their identities were kept secret.","Wen Qingyan handed Jing Zejun a napkin. “Guests? Are they people we know?”","Director Xu chose to remain mysterious but dropped a hint. “Of course, both of you should know them.”","Should know them? That probably meant they weren’t too close.","But Wen Qingyan wasn’t too concerned. He trusted that Director Xu wouldn’t invite someone they disliked.","[Who is it? Who is it? I’m so curious!]","[Could it be Jing Yiyi? Why all the secrecy?]","[Probably not. We just saw her in the prelude, and she lives next door. There’s no need to treat her as a guest.]","[Who could it be?]","[Rumor has it, it’s a popular young actor from the entertainment industry.]","[Oh? That’s disappointing. I was hoping to see Jing Yiyi and Jing Zejun’s families together.]","[And Mr. Jing and Young Master Jing! Life without them feels like an eternity!]","[Who doesn’t feel that way?]","[Young Master Jing is still somewhat visible in the entertainment world, with paparazzi shots here and there, but it’s so hard to catch a glimpse of the eldest brother!]","The conversation gradually veered off track.","But for Wen Qingyan, it didn’t matter who was coming. It just meant an extra person for dinner. His main goal in joining the show was to spend quality time with his wife.","As Wen Qingyan walked over with a plate of freshly washed fruits, he saw Jing Zejun sitting in the living room, talking to Jing Yi on the phone.","To be honest, he wasn’t the type to complain.","But really, what was the point of calling someone you’ve been seeing almost every day?","Wen Qingyan sighed almost imperceptibly, sat down beside Jing Zejun, and began feeding her strawberries while she continued her conversation.","[Hahahahaha, this feels so familiar!]","[Wen Qingyan, you’re not doing great here. It’s been so long, and you still haven’t managed to edge out Jing Yiyi.]","[Hahahaha, that’s too harsh!]","[Isn’t the funny part that they live next door and just saw each other yesterday, yet here they are on the phone?]","[Maybe Wen Qingyan is thinking the same thing.]","Jing Zejun opened her mouth to eat the strawberry, her attention still focused on Jing Yi on the phone.","“Really? Jing Yi, do you know who’s coming?”","Whatever Jing Yi said on the other end made Director Xu visibly nervous, until Jing Zejun spoke again.","“Then it’s not true. Those gossip accounts could come up with dozens of names.”","They chatted for a while longer, and by the time they hung up, Director Xu was almost sweating from anxiety.","Jing Zejun was still wondering who the guest would be. “Qingyan, who do you think the guest is?”","“I don’t know, but my dear Zejun, could you please focus on me for now?”","Jing Zejun was momentarily stunned. Glancing at the cameras and the production team, she blushed and gave Wen Qingyan a playful glare.","“...So, what do you want to do?”","Wen Qingyan felt a little smug. Using his charm occasionally still worked wonders.","He took Jing Zejun’s hand, and the couple leaned close together, planning their afternoon activities."]},{"number":246,"title":"Chapter 246: Extra: Married Life 7 - Reuniting the 'Six-Person Group'","paragraphs":["Until it was almost dinner time, Wen Qingyan and Jing Zejun still didn’t know who the guest was.","However, the couple was happily preparing for the meal and didn’t seem too concerned.","“Qingyan, I’ve washed all the vegetables. Is there anything else I need to do?”","Wen Qingyan took the things from Jing Zejun’s hands and smiled gently, “No, the only thing left is to wait and enjoy the meal.”","Jing Zejun stood beside Wen Qingyan, watching him. In the past, she used to know how to cook some basic dishes, but now, whenever there was a chance to cook at home, Wen Qingyan always took over.","Thinking about it now, Wen Qingyan’s cooking skills had improved a lot.","Jing Zejun stood there, watching Wen Qingyan skillfully handle the kitchen utensils, her lips unconsciously curling into a smile, her eyes filled with tender affection.","The online viewers were absolutely smitten by the sweet moment between the couple when the doorbell rang.","Both of them looked toward the door at the same time.","Jing Zejun walked toward the entrance, “I’ll get it.”","Before opening the door, Jing Zejun had imagined many possible guests—familiar faces, unfamiliar ones, actors, singers—she had thought of them all.","But she never expected to see Wen Yin standing at the door.","He smiled brightly, “Sister-in-law!”","“Wen Yin!”","[Ahhh! It’s Wen Yin! Long time no see!]","[I’ve missed him so much!]","[It’s actually Wen Yin?! They kept this such a secret!]","[Wow, this is going to be so much fun.]","[It’s Wen Yin!!!]","[Please, we need Jing Yiyi and the eldest brother to come too!]","[I’ve been dreaming of seeing them all together again!]","Wen Qingyan walked out of the kitchen and was genuinely surprised to see Wen Yin.","“Wen Yin, so you’re the guest?”","Seriously? They kept it so secret? He’s Wen Yin’s brother, and he didn’t get a single hint?!","Wen Yin scratched the back of his head sheepishly. He had signed a confidentiality agreement, so of course, he couldn’t say anything.","Both Jing Zejun and Wen Qingyan were surprised but also very happy. They were chatting with Wen Yin when the doorbell rang again.","Jing Zejun got up, puzzled, and went to open the door. Before the door was fully open, she could already hear the noisy voices.","“Is your Shen Huaichu throwing a tantrum on purpose?”","“He’s not!”","“Are you sure? The moment I arrived, he handed everything over to me. Why did he buy so much food? Are you planning to stay at Jing Zejun’s for half a month?”","“Then, second brother, let me help you with some of it?”","“No way! If Shen Huaichu could carry it, so can I! That look he gave me earlier was definitely a challenge!”","“Why do you always compete with him?”","“...Lately, I’ve been feeling a bit overwhelmed. Jing Yiyi, can we agree to a one-on-one next time? It’s too much when you two team up.”","“No way! I finally found a partner!”","“...Don’t you realize the whole family is on your side?”","Jing Yi was about to say more when she saw Jing Zejun open the door. She immediately rushed over with a smile.","“Jing Zejun, surprise!”","Jing Zejun could only hug Jing Yi, her only thought being whether they had bought enough food.","But Jing Zejun didn’t need to worry because the guests had brought their own ingredients.","“Ta-da!” Jing Yi made a grand entrance gesture and pointed to Jing Zeqian, who was carrying bags of groceries.","Jing Zeqian cooperatively lifted the bags slightly and said helplessly, “Jing Zejun, Jing Yiyi has brought enough supplies to stay for a while.”","Jing Yi ignored him and linked arms with Jing Zejun, walking toward the living room.","“I knew Director Xu wouldn’t tell you how many people were coming, so I brought my own ingredients.”","Director Xu: ...This girl has no idea how much I’ve sacrificed for this moment!","Wen Yin, who had followed them out, saw the bags in Jing Zeqian’s hands and quickly went to help.","Jing Zeqian breathed a sigh of relief, “Wen Yin, you’re the reliable one!”","Wen Yin smiled and carried the bags to the kitchen to help.","Jing Yi shot a disapproving look at Jing Zeqian, who was already relaxing, looking completely exhausted.","“Second brother, you only carried them for the last bit. It’s not that big a deal.”","Jing Zeqian’s lazy voice came through, “Someone who didn’t lift a finger the whole way has no right to criticize me.”","Jing Yi was momentarily speechless. Fine, she hadn’t carried anything. Shen Huaichu had been the one to bring everything over, and halfway through, he had handed it off to Jing Zeqian.","“Where’s your Shen Huaichu?” Jing Zejun asked, noticing that he wasn’t there despite having helped bring the groceries.","“He just came to drop off the things and left.”","Director Xu, who had just been about to send the camera crew out: ...Well, there goes a major highlight.","Hearing this, Jing Zejun chuckled, “That must be disappointing for Director Xu.” Jing Yi glanced over and saw Director Xu quickly trying to hide his expression. She laughed, “Don’t worry, he’s coming back to pick me up tonight.”","Director Xu, whose mood instantly lifted: \\^o^/","Jing Zeqian, who was resting, couldn’t help but comment, “Your place is just a few steps away...”","Jing Yi shrugged helplessly. What could she do? If she didn’t let him come, he’d make a fuss.","Shen Huaichu might not say much, but his emotions were always very clear in his actions, especially at night. He could be quite intense...","...","Jing Zejun was still surprised. She had just spoken to Jing Yi that morning, and Jing Yi hadn’t mentioned anything about coming.","“You didn’t tell me you were coming. I’ve been wondering all afternoon who the guest would be.”","Jing Yi giggled, “It’s a surprise! How could I spoil it by telling you beforehand?”","She had thought that after Director Xu filmed some scenes earlier, her part was done, since all the curiosity had been satisfied.","But a few days ago, Director Xu had approached her, asking if she could appear in one more episode as a reunion and farewell special for the previous show.","Jing Yi thought it sounded fun, so she agreed.","Honestly, Director Xu was quite bold. He actually trusted her and Wen Yin—one being Jing Zejun’s sister and the other Wen Qingyan’s brother—to keep it a secret.","Well, they did keep their mouths shut.","Jing Yi looked around at all the camera equipment in the room and felt a wave of nostalgia. She walked up to the main screen and waved, smiling brightly, “Hello, long time no see!”","[Jing Yiyi! It’s been so long!]","[I’ve missed you so much!]","[Director Xu, you’re a legend!]","[This is the family reunion I’ve been waiting for!!!]","[The six of them together again! My dream has come true!]","[Where’s the eldest brother?! Director Xu, don’t mess this up at the last minute!]","[Where’s my handsome, never-seen-before, calm and elegant crush, Jing Zeyou?]","As if hearing the viewers’ cries, Jing Yi smiled and said, “The eldest brother will be here later. He has a meeting at Hengjing.”","After chatting briefly with the viewers, Jing Yi headed to the kitchen.","“Second brother, stop resting. Come help me wash the vegetables.”","This team doesn’t tolerate freeloaders!","Well, except for the eldest brother!"]},{"number":247,"title":"Chapter 247: Extra: Married Life 8: Reuniting the 'Six-Person Group'","paragraphs":["The popularity of the variety show livestream featuring Wen Qingyan and Jing Zejun was already high, and with the news of the 'six-member group' reunion spreading, a large number of netizens flooded into the livestream.","Director Xu looked at the backend data and nodded with satisfaction. Fortunately, he had the foresight, otherwise the livestream would have crashed by now.","Over the years, the members of the 'six-member group' had changed in various ways. Jing Zeyou had just arrived, and as Director Xu looked at the six of them, he couldn't help but feel a sense of nostalgia.","When he first started filming the Jing family, he never imagined that years later, there would be such an opportunity again. What's more, it was rare that they had all become better versions of themselves.","The young girl who had been slandered and needed protection back then had now transformed into a legend in the hearts of many.","Watching Jing Yi cooking in the kitchen, Director Xu felt a momentary sense of déjà vu. It was the same boiled fish dish, just like the scene from many years ago.","Jing Yi gently lifted the lid of the pot, and a cloud of steam rose as the boiled fish churned in the pot, filling the kitchen with a rich aroma.","“Second brother, are you done washing?” Jing Zeqian drained the water from the plate and handed the chopped scallions and chili segments to Jing Yi. His movements were so skillful that it was as if he had become a different person.","[Who understands this feeling? It's like nothing has changed, just like many years ago!]","[I get it! They've clearly become better people, but when they come together, it feels just like before.]","[So heartwarming, but it also makes me want to cry.]","[Yeah, I feel like crying too. It's the same boiled fish, but I still can't eat it!]","[Little Jing, have you been secretly practicing washing and chopping vegetables these past few years?!]","[I noticed that too! Look at those scallion segments, they look pretty professional!]","[Hahahaha, secretly practicing washing vegetables, that's hilarious.]","The final step was to pour the hot oil, and it was done!","Jing Yi looked at the fragrant boiled fish with satisfaction, only for Jing Zeqian to immediately take it away.","Jing Yi: \"...Alright, at least he's being enthusiastic.\"","With more people around, dinner was prepared quickly. By the time Jing Zeyou arrived, the last dish was ready.","\"Do you need any help?\" Jing Yi came out of the kitchen.","\"No need, big brother. Just sit and wait for dinner!\" Jing Zeqian, who was passing by, quipped sarcastically, \"Sit and wait for dinner~\" It was truly a treatment only his brother could get. When would he ever get such treatment?","Jing Yi helped set the table. \"Second brother, what are you standing there for? We still need a few more pairs of chopsticks.\"","Jing Zeqian: \"...Waiting!\" He then stomped back to the kitchen in a huff.","What's with his temper this time?","Jing Yi didn't have time to think too much about it as her attention was occupied with setting the table.","She looked at the spread of dishes with satisfaction and noticed that Director Xu was still sitting with the crew.","\"Director Xu, what are you doing? Didn't we invite you to join us for dinner?\"","The other crew members had already been taken care of before Jing Zeyou arrived. This was the standard 'meal provision' during the filming of the Jing family.","As for why Director Xu was invited to join their gathering, it was Jing Yi's idea.","She wasn't accustomed to the entertainment industry or filming, which was why she had turned down many invitations.","But Jing Yi was truly grateful to Director Xu. That period of road trips was a cherished memory for her.","Hearing Jing Yi's words, Director Xu felt a bit embarrassed and pretended to decline, \"No, it's fine. I'll just eat with the crew.\"","The crew members behind him, however, could tell that he wasn't really refusing. They exchanged glances, their eyes filled with mischief.","\"That's right, Yi Yi, Director Xu can eat with us. I've really missed Hengjing's work meals.\"","\"Yeah, Yi Yi, Director Xu doesn't feel comfortable. Let him eat with us.\"","\"Exactly!\"","Director Xu glared at them: Exactly nothing! After all this time, they still couldn't tell when he was just being polite?!","The comments section was also filled with laughter.","[Don't give our Director Xu a hard time, he's feeling shy.]","[Exactly! He loves work meals!]","[Jing Yi is so kind!]","[These people are all so warm-hearted.]","[If Director Xu keeps refusing, the people behind him are going to pounce!]","[Hahahaha, Director Xu looks shocked. Those kids are up to no good!]","Jing Yi watched with amusement as the crew teased Director Xu. \"Alright, hurry up. Dinner is about to start.\"","Director Xu chuckled a few times, helped bring over the last few bowls, and then took a seat.","...","\"Cheers!\"","The seven of them raised their glasses and clinked them together, instantly feeling as if they had returned to the gatherings of many years ago.","At first, Director Xu felt a bit out of place. In his professional field, this kind of discomfort wouldn't exist, but it had been so long since he had eaten with the guests during filming.","Remembering that the cameras were still rolling, Director Xu felt even more uneasy, a feeling that Jing Yi quickly picked up on.","She found it amusing. \"Director Xu, you've been holding a camera for so many years, and you're still afraid of being in front of the lens?\"","Director Xu would never admit it, stubbornly replying, \"Of course not! I'm just thinking about the shooting angles and the next steps. As a director, these are the things I need to consider.\"","Jing Yi saw right through him but decided not to press further. She figured she'd give the director some face.","She shifted her gaze back and reached for the small lobster in front of her.","Watching this, Director Xu recalled how Jing Yi used to praise Wen Yin's cooking skills back in the day, and his professional instincts kicked in again.","\"Yi Yi, it's been a while since you've had Wen Yin's seafood, right? How does it taste?\" Jing Yi gave him a puzzled look. \"Director Xu, didn't you know we meet up often?\"","After graduating from university, Wen Yin had stayed in North River. Jing Yi occasionally taught him how to race, and the group would get together from time to time, just like before.","Director Xu hadn't expected that. He hadn't seen any news about it online and had assumed that Jing Yi only met with her family, given that Wen Yin was farther away.","Glancing at Jing Zeyou across the table, Director Xu suddenly understood.","Of course, with the Jing family's status, dealing with a few reckless paparazzi was a simple matter.","Perhaps the Shen family was also involved. Jing Yi's status was only getting higher.","Jing Yi noticed Director Xu staring at her and asked, \"What's wrong?\" Director Xu sighed with emotion. \"It's just that everyone seems to have changed so much.\"","Jing Yi looked around. \"Have they?\" Perhaps because she saw her family often, she didn't notice any significant changes.","Jing Zeqian casually snatched the shrimp Jing Yi was about to pick up. \"Of course! It's been years. How could there be no changes? You've gone from being a single woman to a married one.\"","Jing Yi glared at him. \"What, are you jealous? I'll tell Mom to prepare a special party for you so you can make more friends!\"","Jing Zeqian paused. \"...You're ruthless!\" He then placed a shrimp in Jing Yi's bowl.","Jing Yi's eyes sparkled with triumph as she began to enjoy her 'spoils.'","Director Xu: \"...Am I seeing things? These are clearly the same people as before. Nothing has changed.\""]},{"number":248,"title":"Chapter 248: Extra: Married Life 9 - Reuniting the 'Six-Person Group'","paragraphs":["As Jing Yi had mentioned, gatherings among the six of them were quite common, and even after years of not seeing each other, there was no trace of awkwardness between them.","The sound of laughter and chatter filled the room as the seven of them engaged in a lively conversation, with even the usually reserved Director Xu joining in.","However, as the saying goes, all good things must come to an end, and Director Xu knew this all too well.","This wasn’t the end of the recording for Jing Zejun and Wen Qingyan, but it was likely the last time Jing Yi and the others would be participating.","“Let’s play one last game,” Jing Yi suggested, leaning lazily against Jing Zejun, having eaten a bit too much and not feeling like moving.","“Classic Director Xu,” someone quipped.","Director Xu retorted, “Don’t worry, it’s a game that doesn’t require any movement. It’s called ‘Five Things About Me Over the Years’...” The idea was for each person to share five things about their experiences or changes in recent years, each starting with “I.”","Jing Yi immediately looked unenthused. Last time, it took her forever to come up with just one thought, and now she had to come up with five!","She tried to hide behind Jing Zejun, “You go first, Second Brother!”","Jing Zeqian, who was also lounging to digest his food, chimed in, “...So you didn’t think of me?”","[Hahahaha, typical Jing Yi!]","[After all these years, Jing Yi still hates answering questions.]","[Young Master Jing’s expressionless face: Why am I always the target?]","[Is this really the last game? Will we not see Jing Yi anymore after this?]","[Be grateful, I think her participation alone is a dream come true.]","Jing Zeqian resignedly sat up, pondering the rules Director Xu had just explained, and extended one hand.","“I am Jing Zeqian.”","Jing Yi burst out laughing, “What’s this? A declaration?” Jing Zeqian glared at her, “What? Can’t I just appreciate how nice my name sounds?”","He needed to come up with five points, and he had to stretch a bit to make it work.","Jing Zeqian bent one finger and continued, “I am still the CEO of Startrack, as I introduced before.”","The others: ...Isn’t that a bit of a cop-out?","Jing Zeqian cleared his throat, “I’ve learned not to turn a blind eye or a deaf ear.” The second statement left the viewers and the production team puzzled, but the people in the room understood perfectly.","He quickly bent another finger, seemingly avoiding the gaze of his family.","“My family has grown by two members.”","Jing Zeqian seemed even more embarrassed, while Wen Qingyan’s expression brightened.","“Finally, I am very satisfied with everything in my life now.” Jing Zeqian lowered all his fingers and waved his hand dismissively, “Alright, alright, your turn!”","Jing Zejun, noticing her brother’s discomfort, naturally stepped in to spare him further embarrassment.","“I’ll go next. I am Jing Zejun.”","“I am still the actor Jing Zejun.”","Jing Zejun smiled gently and bent a third finger, “Jing Yi was there the day I won my award.”","“I have a husband now.”","“I am very satisfied with my current life.”","Next was Wen Qingyan.","Perhaps inspired by Jing Zeqian’s opening, the subsequent speakers followed a similar pattern.","Thus, these statements no longer felt like fillers but instead carried a sense of ceremony.","“I have fulfilled a long-held dream,” Wen Qingyan said, looking at Jing Zejun with tender affection, “I have a wife now.”","“My PR contingency plan, fortunately, hasn’t failed.”","Then it was Wen Yin’s turn.","“I have graduated,” he said with his youthful smile, “My racing skills were taught by champion Jing Yi.”","“I feel very lucky to have participated in this variety show with my brother.”","Jing Yi, who had been secretly preparing, was starting to feel nervous as it was almost her turn.","Jing Zeyou chuckled and took the baton, buying his sister a little more time.","“I am Jing Zeyou.”","“I am still the CEO of Hengjing.”","“I haven’t changed much; I’m still the same as always,” he paused, a slight smile playing on his lips, “I still love going to work.”","“I am grateful that the current situation wasn’t achieved by trading away anyone.”","“Lately, I’ve been getting more sun.”","Hearing this, Jing Yi added, “Yes, even CEOs need to get some sun.”","Jing Zeqian, sitting nearby, urged, “Hurry up, it’s your turn.”","Jing Yi sighed softly and obediently extended her hand, “I am Jing Yi.”","“I am now a professional racer,” Wen Yin interjected, “A champion racer!”","Jing Yi smiled shyly and bent another finger, “I’ve gone through many changes; I’ve participated in several competitions.”","“I married Shen Huaichu.”","“I...” Jing Yi took a deep breath, her dimples showing as she smiled, “I am walking my path with ease and joy.”","After Jing Yi finished, the comments section was filled with both nostalgia and a touch of sadness.","Director Xu also seemed reluctant to let go, and the production team was immersed in the melancholy of the impending farewell.","Jing Yi, too, was affected by this inexplicable mood but joked, “Director Xu, why that expression? Are you not filming anymore?”","Director Xu’s sadness was instantly dispelled, “Who said that! We’re only halfway through the show!”","Jing Yi laughed, determined not to let the moment turn into a sentimental goodbye.","...","It was time for Jing Yi and the others to leave. While the other guests were only seen off at the door, this group seemed different.","Director Xu watched as Jing Zejun and Wen Qingyan changed their shoes, preparing to leave together.","“Are you all heading out too?”","Wen Qingyan neatly placed Jing Zejun’s indoor shoes aside and replied, “It’s a family habit to take a walk together after meals sometimes.”","Jing Yi also contacted Shen Huaichu.","Director Xu, standing nearby, seemed hesitant to speak. Jing Yi, prompted by a subtle hint from Jing Zejun, finally remembered Director Xu’s curiosity about Shen Huaichu.","Jing Yi muttered, “What’s so curious about him? Doesn’t he have two eyes and a nose like everyone else?” As she spoke, she walked toward the door.","The cameraman following her overheard her muttering and thought to himself that Jing Yi probably had no idea how much the media outlet that secured the exclusive interview had profited.","The conversation gradually drifted, and Shen Huaichu appeared on camera. The viewers could clearly see his expression change from neutral to a warm smile the moment he saw Jing Yi, a perfect example of ‘instant transformation.’","Jing Yi held his hand and introduced him to the viewers, “Look, this is my husband, Shen Huaichu.” Her tone was as if she were introducing some rare specimen.","Shen Huaichu’s gaze softened even more, and his voice carried a hint of joy.","“Hello everyone, I am Jing Yi’s husband, Shen Huaichu.”","The others in the room: ...His self-introduction is always a bit different each time.","With everyone present, it was time for the group to head out for their walk.","The camera lingered on the seven of them as they walked away.","It was a summer night, the sky dotted with stars, the evening breeze rustling the leaves, and the moonlight stretching their shadows. They seemed to be chatting, their voices faint and indistinct.","Just like that sunrise many years ago, it was equally beautiful."]},{"number":249,"title":"Chapter 249: Extra: Parenting Daily Life 1 - Shen Muyi is a Sweet Baby","paragraphs":["ManMan was born just as Jing Yi was preparing to retire from the competition. He was a sweet little boy, with the formal name Shen Muyi.","Lin Ruiqing said he was surely going to be a very thoughtful child, and later Jing Yi realized that her son was not only thoughtful but also incredibly sweet.","There was just one thing—he really loved asking all sorts of strange questions.","Jing Yi watched the father and son having a friendly conversation in the living room. The three-year-old boy was well-behaved, his big eyes, so similar to Jing Yi’s, looking intently at his father.","Every time his father spoke, he nodded obediently, the little tuft of hair on his head swaying along.","Shen Huaichu spoke with a serious expression, \"...In conclusion, you’re already three years old. You can’t keep insisting on sleeping with Mommy anymore.\"","ManMan seemed to agree with his father’s words, his chubby little face solemn, as if he were truly pondering the matter.","Every time Jing Yi saw this expression on ManMan’s face, she was reminded of Shen Huaichu.","\"Okay, Daddy!\"","Hearing his son’s response, Shen Huaichu wasn’t entirely reassured, because he knew his son definitely had more to say.","Don’t ask how he knew—he’d been dealing with him for three years now.","Sure enough, ManMan looked up at his father, who was crouching in front of him, and raised his little hand. \"Question.\"","Shen Huaichu sighed inwardly. \"Go ahead.\"","\"How can I grow up to be as big as you and still sleep with Mommy?\"","Jing Yi coughed lightly, moving the glass of juice she was holding farther away and quickly grabbing some tissues to wipe up the spilled juice.","Shen Huaichu’s expression stiffened slightly. \"...She’s not just your mommy; she’s also my wife.\" ManMan seemed to half-understand, his little tuft of hair swaying again.","\"Then, question.\"","He raised his little hand once more. Shen Huaichu paused, glancing at his wife, who turned her head away to avoid his gaze.","\"...Go ahead.\"","\"How can I sleep with your wife?\"","\"...\"","Without context, that question could easily be misunderstood.","Later, Jing Yi managed to steer the conversation away from the topic. Although ManMan was a little disappointed, his mommy promised to come and tell him a bedtime story that night.","Oh well, ManMan was a thoughtful child. He decided not to press further.","After lulling her son to sleep, Jing Yi quietly left the room and returned to the bedroom.","Shen Huaichu was still replaying the day’s conversation in his mind. Jing Yi found it amusing. \"Kids are naturally imaginative. Why are you taking it so seriously?\"","Shen Huaichu moved closer, taking Jing Yi’s hand. \"You’ve had a long day. Was he hard to put to sleep?\" Jing Yi’s bedtime routine with ManMan was a recent development, as Shen Huaichu usually handled it.","To say the least, the boy could ask dozens of questions in a single night.","Jing Yi shook her head, leaning into Shen Huaichu’s embrace. \"Not at all. ManMan was so well-behaved. You always say he’s hard to put to sleep, but he fell asleep really quickly.\"","ManMan had simply smiled at her the whole time, gradually drifting off to sleep as she spoke in her gentle voice.","Shen Huaichu paused. Well, it seemed his son was selective in his behavior.","\"...It takes me at least an hour to get him to sleep.\"","Jing Yi laughed, collapsing into his arms. Shen Huaichu held his wife helplessly. \"If I don’t review these conversations, how am I supposed to handle his next round of strange questions?\"","A while ago, he had picked up a classic father-son relationship book to read as a bedtime story for ManMan. When he got to the part where the father and son were having tea and chatting,","ManMan piped up in his little voice, \"Daddy, does tea taste good with lemon?\"","\"Can you add cream too? Can I try it? I’ll brush my teeth afterward!\"","After that, ManMan was even more awake, showing no signs of wanting to sleep.","Jing Yi looked up at Shen Huaichu, her expression complicated. \"...Are your bedtime stories a bit, um, unconventional?\"","Okay, maybe he had some ulterior motives, but ManMan also had zero interest in the typical bedtime stories meant for three-year-olds.","Once, he dutifully read a standard fairy tale, but ManMan was completely uninterested, playing with his chubby little feet instead.","\"Daddy, why aren’t you sleeping?\"","\"...I’m waiting for you to fall asleep.\"","\"Then why can’t you tell me the story while you’re asleep? That way, you won’t be so tired.\"","\"...I can’t read the words with my eyes closed.\"","\"Then Daddy can memorize the story and tell it with his eyes closed.\"","\"...You’re really thoughtful.\"","Who does this kid take after, anyway?","Sometimes Shen Huaichu wondered if, during the pregnancy, all his attention had been on Jing Yi, and now the consequences were coming back to him.","The moment he found out they were having a child, Shen Huaichu had been at a loss.","He hadn’t initially planned on having children, leaving the decision entirely up to Jing Yi. Compared to a child, he cared more about her.","The baby’s arrival had been somewhat unexpected, but Shen Huaichu quickly composed himself and made a series of plans.","Plans on how to ensure the pregnant woman’s absolute happiness and health, and how to be a considerate husband during the pregnancy.","He even went so far as to consult middle-aged men in his circle who had similar experiences, such as his father-in-law, uncles, and even his assistant.","The only thing he hadn’t planned for was how to be a father.","Jing Yi’s pregnancy had been relatively smooth, and Shen Huaichu breathed a sigh of relief.","But soon, the consequences came back to him.","His son, Shen Muyi, nicknamed ManMan, was a very smart and thoughtful child—a child with many strange questions, but whose thoughtfulness wasn’t directed at him.","Before the pregnancy, Jing Yi had already been a team coach, often flying abroad for meetings. When ManMan was too young to understand, he would cry a bit and then get over it.","Once he started to understand, things became more complicated.","For example, there was a time when Jing Yi had to attend an important conference and went abroad for a few days.","Shen Huaichu had explained to his son many times that Mommy wasn’t abandoning him; she was just away on a business trip.","But ManMan wouldn’t listen, his eyes red and teary as he stared at Shen Huaichu, looking as if he’d been deeply wronged.","And those eyes looked so much like Jing Yi’s.","Shen Huaichu, rarely flustered, found himself at a loss. It took the combined efforts of Jing Zeyou and others to finally calm ManMan down.","And they had Jing Zeqian to thank for that!","\"ManMan, don’t worry. Even if Mommy doesn’t want Daddy, she’ll never not want you. You’re her little treasure.\"","Thinking about it, Shen Huaichu felt both grateful and exasperated.","After that, ManMan really wasn’t upset anymore. He was so happy every day when he video-called with his mommy, his little feet swinging, his eyes crinkling with laughter.","After hanging up the call, ManMan would climb into Shen Huaichu’s lap, patting his shoulder comfortingly and saying in his sweet little voice, \"Daddy, don’t worry. Even if Mommy doesn’t want you, ManMan will still want you.\"","He even patted his little chest as if to promise.","Shen Huaichu held his chubby little body, afraid he might topple over.","\"...If you’re so worried Mommy doesn’t want me, why don’t you leave me some time to talk to her?\" His son had hung up so decisively, not showing a hint of concern.","ManMan frowned, his little hands clutching Shen Huaichu’s shirt as he secretly observed him for a moment.","\"Daddy can’t drag ManMan into this. What if Mommy doesn’t want ManMan anymore? And Mommy works really hard. We can’t waste her time with these things.\"","Shen Huaichu, who was apparently only worth \"these things\" and might \"drag his son down\": Honestly, his son’s logic was impeccable, but could he occasionally be thoughtful toward him too?"]},{"number":250,"title":"Chapter 250: Extra: Parenting Daily Life 2 - Shen Muyi's Kindergarten Routine","paragraphs":["ManMan is extremely popular at the kindergarten, so much so that the first lesson children need to learn when they start kindergarten is \"separation anxiety.\" However, as long as ManMan is around, there’s hardly any separation anxiety to speak of.","At the entrance of a kindergarten in Jiangbei, a chubby little boy is clinging to his mother’s leg, wailing and refusing to go inside.","The kindergarten teacher nearby is also feeling overwhelmed. On one hand, children of this age tend to cry uncontrollably and won’t listen to reason, and on the other hand, once one starts crying, the others are bound to follow!","The chubby boy’s mother is growing increasingly frustrated. “Chen Yuqi! I’m counting to three. Get up and go to kindergarten right now!”","But the little boy is unfazed and only cries even louder. “I don’t want to go to kindergarten! I want to go home! Home!”","As the three parties are at a standoff, Shen Huaichu arrives, holding ManMan’s hand. Seeing the struggling child on the ground, he casually looks away.","He crouches down to speak to his son. “Be good at kindergarten. Mom will come to pick you up this afternoon.”","ManMan’s eyes sparkle, and his slightly curly hair sways as he nods. “Can you tell my uncle to pick me up next time? And let my other uncle know that I have rehearsal tomorrow, so I can’t play with him...”","Shen Huaichu: ...When did he make so many plans without me knowing?","ManMan looks a lot like Jing Yi, especially with those eyes and his curly hair. Add to that his sweet, talkative personality, and it’s no wonder he’s so adored by everyone.","Even Shen Huaichu sometimes finds it hard to stay stern when trying to reason with him.","This has its downsides, like the fact that he and his wife often lose track of their son, who might be whisked away by an uncle, aunt, or other relative.","But there are also benefits, such as never having to worry about who will pick him up or drop him off.","Shen Huaichu sighs inwardly but keeps a straight face. “Alright, I’ll tell them for you.” ManMan obediently gives him a goodbye kiss. “See you this afternoon, Dad!” With that, he follows the teacher into the kindergarten.","As Shen Huaichu watches his son leave, he notices that the crying child’s sobs have quieted down.","The chubby boy’s mother had been waiting, knowing that someone who could calm her son down would arrive soon.","And sure enough, her patience paid off!","“Yuqi, look! Shen Muyi has already gone inside. If you’re late, he’ll be playing with other kids.”","The teacher, understanding the situation, also chimes in. “That’s right, Chen Yuqi. Look, your friend has already gone into the classroom.”","Hearing this, the chubby boy stops wailing, wipes his tears, and looks in the direction where ManMan went.","Seeing that he’s already inside, the boy quickly stands up, even looking a bit panicked. “Mom, give me my backpack! If I’m late, Shen Muyi’s schedule will be full for the day! I still want to race cars with him!”","His mother hands him the backpack, teasing him. “You mean that toy car you still have to pedal to move?”","Watching her son’s hurried little steps as he runs inside, she breathes a sigh of relief. “Thank goodness there’s a Shen Muyi in this kindergarten. Otherwise, I wouldn’t know how to handle this kid.”","The mother glances around and spots Shen Huaichu.","This isn’t the first time she’s seen Shen Muyi’s father while dropping off her son. Most parents at this kindergarten are well-off, but the Shen and Jing families are exceptionally prominent.","She usually doesn’t strike up a conversation with Shen Muyi’s father—he seems rather aloof, though he’s very patient with his son.","On the other hand, Shen Muyi’s mother, the famous race car driver and youngest daughter of the Jing family, is very approachable. They’ve occasionally chatted while picking up their kids.","Though “occasionally” is the key word, since the person who picks up Shen Muyi isn’t always the same. She imagines the teachers must have a long list of contacts for him.","...","In the classroom, ManMan has already settled into his seat, following his usual routine of taking out the things he’ll need for the day and placing them on the table.","Then, he begins socializing with his classmates.","The other kids, familiar with his habits, patiently wait for him to finish, knowing he won’t respond if they try to talk to him before he’s ready.","“Shen Muyi, will you play house with me today?”","Play house? The whole mom-and-dad thing again?","He’ll have to ask his aunt and uncle for advice on what to do if he gets tired of playing the same role repeatedly.","“No! Shen Muyi is playing soccer with us today!”","Soccer? That’s fine too. Uncle Henry is coming to visit next month, and though he can’t take him on a race car ride, they can play soccer together.","“Let’s play video games instead! Shen Muyi, my dad bought me a new gaming set. Come over after school!”","Video games? Are they as fun as the ones at Uncle Gu Lin’s place?","But he’ll have to pass on that. While he enjoys spending time with his classmates, he has a lot of things to do after school.","Like spending time with his parents, grandparents, and all those uncles and aunts...","The afternoon just isn’t long enough. Sometimes, ManMan feels truly troubled.","Why can’t the afternoon be longer? Or why can’t school hours be shorter? Or better yet, why can’t there be more ManMans?","Otherwise, there just isn’t enough of him to go around.","The chubby boy finally manages to squeeze in. “No! Shen Muyi is racing cars with me today!”","ManMan looks at the classmate sitting behind him and patiently explains, “Chen Yuqi, racing cars is too dangerous. There are too many kids in the kindergarten, and someone could get hurt.”","“My mom says if you want to race cars, you should do it at a professional track. Showing off on the road is silly and childish.”","Yes, that’s exactly what his mom said, though he’s not sure why she seemed to hesitate before saying “silly.”","ManMan is especially proud that his mom is a cool race car driver, and all his classmates know it and think it’s awesome.","Hearing this, the kids all gasp in amazement.","Though the chubby boy is a little disappointed, he isn’t upset. “Then let’s race at the track!”","ManMan takes racing very seriously and actually thinks about it for a moment.","“I’ll have to ask my mom if she can take us. But we can’t use the kindergarten cars—they’re too childish, and you can’t go fast just by pedaling.”","The chubby boy’s eyes light up. “You mean real race cars?”","ManMan nods seriously. “Yes, the ones you can control with a remote. They’re really cool.” The remote is always handled by professionals, like his mom, who’s in charge every time.","“Wow! That’s amazing!”","The group of kids gasps in unison again, just as the teacher walks in to start the class, trying hard not to laugh."]},{"number":251,"title":"Chapter 251: Extra: Parenting Daily Life 3 - Shen Muyi's Kindergarten Routine","paragraphs":["At the entrance of Jiangbei International Kindergarten, Jing Yi parked her car and walked over.","Looking at the usual scene that resembled a car exhibition, she couldn’t help but feel a little amazed.","The sight was almost comparable to most racetracks.","However, no matter how expensive the cars were, everyone still had to obediently stand at the gate to pick up their children.","As soon as Jing Yi took her spot, she noticed a familiar figure approaching.","It was the mother of the chubby little boy. Jing Yi smiled and greeted her, “Mrs. Chen Yuqi, are you picking up your child this week too?”","Since ManMan started kindergarten, Jing Yi had gradually gotten to know some of his classmates’ parents, and she was familiar with their routines for picking up and dropping off their kids.","For example, Chen Yuqi’s parents usually took turns each week, and if both were busy, the grandparents would step in.","Chen Yuqi’s mother also seemed delighted. “Mrs. Shen Muyi, yes, I’m on duty this week. It’s been a while!”","Jing Yi felt a bit embarrassed. ManMan’s father usually handled the morning drop-offs, and in the afternoon, it was a rotation of uncles, so she rarely had to worry about it.","Chen Yuqi’s mother didn’t notice Jing Yi’s slight discomfort. She was genuinely happy.","She loved chatting, and she had always enjoyed her conversations with Jing Yi. However, this week, it was mostly Shen Muyi’s uncle who picked up the child, and she didn’t feel comfortable chatting with him.","Now that she ran into Jing Yi, she finally had someone to vent to.","“You have no idea about my son. He’s still as stubborn as ever today. Thankfully, Shen Muyi was there, so he finally agreed to go to school. And when he got home, he wouldn’t stop talking about Shen Muyi...”","Jing Yi’s eyes sparkled with amusement. She quite liked Chen Yuqi and his mother. Watching the enthusiastic mother talk non-stop, Jing Yi wondered if the child had inherited some of his mother’s traits.","While the two mothers chatted about their sons, the three- or four-year-olds emerged, holding hands.","“Mom!”","ManMan immediately spotted Jing Yi and excitedly waved, but he obediently stayed in place, holding the teacher’s hand. When it was his turn, the teacher carefully checked the information before letting him go.","Although they were no strangers to the parents, the kindergarten had strict procedures to follow.","ManMan, with his slightly curly hair just like Jing Yi’s, happily ran into her arms.","“Mom, did you finish training early today?” Jing Yi hugged her son, her eyes crinkling with a smile. “Yes, and I’ll be taking a break soon, so I’ll be able to pick you up more often.”","As for dropping him off at school, that would still be his father’s responsibility—it was just too early!","ManMan was a sweet and easily contented child. Hearing this, he jumped up and down with joy. Although he enjoyed being picked up by different uncles, nothing could compare to his mom.","Jing Yi stood up, holding ManMan’s hand, ready to head home. She was about to say goodbye to Chen Yuqi’s mother when a chubby little boy came running toward her.","Jing Yi wasn’t surprised, nor was Chen Yuqi’s mother, who even looked a little embarrassed as she walked over.","Jing Yi crouched down again and greeted the boy with a smile. “Hello, Chen Yuqi. It’s been a while!”","The little boy’s eyes sparkled with excitement. “Auntie Jing Yi, Shen Muyi and I made a plan to go to the racetrack next time. Can we go?”","The racetrack? These two kids?","Jing Yi was momentarily speechless. She had only taken ManMan to watch races before but never let him drive on a real track.","She glanced at her son with a questioning look.","ManMan obediently explained, “Mom, it’s that place where you can choose lots of cars and drive them on a professional track. Can I take Chen Yuqi there?”","As ManMan provided more details, the chubby boy’s face lit up with even more anticipation.","Finally, Jing Yi understood what her son meant by “racetrack.”","It wasn’t a real racetrack but a large toy track that Jing Zeqian had built for ManMan next to the actual racetrack.","ManMan could decide for himself about that.","The “racetrack” ManMan mentioned was quite large for a child, but it was more like a toy for adults, like her and Jing Zeqian.","Jing Yi said seriously, “Chen Yuqi, before you go anywhere, you need to ask your parents first.”","The boy seemed to remember his mother only then. He looked around but couldn’t find her, his face filled with confusion.","Where was she? She was right there a moment ago!","His mother, who had followed him and was standing right behind him: “...Here I am.”","The boy turned around abruptly and saw his mother standing there. He happily hugged her leg.","“Mom, I’ve been looking for you! Can I go to Auntie Jing Yi’s house to play with the race cars?”","His mother ruffled his hair helplessly and then looked apologetically at Jing Yi. “I’m sorry, he’s always causing trouble.”","Jing Yi stood up, holding her son’s hand, and smiled. “It’s no trouble at all. He can keep ManMan company.” However, she felt the need to clarify that it wasn’t a real racetrack, so the other parents wouldn’t worry.","Chen Yuqi’s mother wasn’t concerned that Jing Yi would let the kids play on a professional racetrack. After all, Jing Yi was a professional racer, and when it came to safety, she was second to none—especially as a champion.","“It’s just going to trouble you.”","“It’s no problem. I’ll be on break soon, so we can arrange a time then.”","However, she might need more hands. She was alone and could only remotely control one car at a time, so she’d probably have to rope Jing Zeqian into helping.","The matter was tentatively settled, and the chubby boy followed his mother home, satisfied.","ManMan also held his mother’s hand and walked to their car, but he looked a little disappointed when he saw it.","“Mom, why is it Dad’s car and not yours?”","Jing Yi chuckled at her son’s sudden pickiness. “What’s wrong with Dad’s car?”","She hadn’t had time to check before leaving, and she couldn’t drive her “Ghost” to pick up her son. Besides, the child seat wasn’t installed in it, so she had to use the car Shen Huaichu had driven that morning to drop ManMan off.","ManMan puffed out his cheeks. It wasn’t that Dad’s car wasn’t good, but Mom’s car was cooler!","He loved cool cars!","Jing Yi felt she needed to defend her husband’s car.","“Dad’s car is pretty cool too.”","Although she knew ManMan was referring to cars like her “Night” sports car."]},{"number":252,"title":"Chapter 252: Extra: Daily Life with Kids 4: Auntie 'Eats' the Kids","paragraphs":["ManMan had always had a special fondness for the cars at home. As soon as he could walk, he would leisurely wander into the garage by himself. Even at around one year old, he loved to linger in the garage, especially in Jing Yi’s sports car. As a result, Jing Yi had no choice but to move several cars out to the yard so the little one could crawl around and play.","Later, when ManMan could express himself more clearly, he repeatedly asked to ride in his mom’s car. Occasionally, it was fine—he could sit in a specially designed child seat and enjoy the ride. However, sports cars are built differently, and the safety of the passenger seat isn’t as high as the back seat. Eventually, they had to buy a four-seater sports car so he could sit in the back with his safety seat. Still, he couldn’t forget the two-seater sports cars at home.","Speaking of this, ManMan’s cheeks puffed out even more as he resignedly climbed into his safety seat. While dutifully fastening his seatbelt, he complained about his mom’s unreliability.","“Uncle said he bought it for me, but Mom’s the one driving it, and there’s no little seat for me in the back!”","Oh, so her son had noticed that. Just as his dad had said, he was no longer easy to fool.","After checking that ManMan’s seatbelt was securely fastened, Jing Yi returned to the driver’s seat and patiently explained, “But you’re the one who said that car was no different from the others and refused to ride in it. Wouldn’t it be a waste to just leave it parked?”","“As for your little seat, it’s custom-made. Putting it in a car you don’t ride in would be a waste, wouldn’t it?”","ManMan tilted his head, seriously considering his mom’s words. It seemed to make sense, but something still felt off.","By the time they were almost home, ManMan was still frowning, trying to make sense of Jing Yi’s explanation.","“Mom, I have a question.”","She knew she couldn’t avoid it. “...Go ahead.”","“Mom, why did you buy a car I don’t ride in? Isn’t that a waste?”","“...Son, it’s because we bought it that you don’t ride in it.”","Even her older brother probably wouldn’t know how to respond to that. And it wasn’t a waste—she still drove it, after all.","“Can’t we sell it and buy a car that ManMan can ride in?”","Jing Yi didn’t want to discourage her son, but according to ManMan’s logic, they’d only end up buying a bunch of toy cars. The regular cars they bought were all driven by her, and she was already overwhelmed with the number of cars they had.","Jing Yi tried to appeal to his sense of whimsy. “That car was the first big car gift you ever received. Don’t you think it would be sad if we sold it so quickly?”","ManMan paused for a moment, his little face showing a hint of conflict.","“Mom, listen to me. It’s just a car. We shouldn’t get too attached to it.”","Jing Yi: “...Okay.” She had been naive to think he’d believe that—he probably stopped believing it by the time he was two.","As she parked the car, Jing Yi couldn’t help but feel a bit emotional. Her son was only three, and he was already so hard to handle. Some questions were better left for Shen Huaichu to deal with.","It seemed a review was truly necessary.","Jing Yi quickly tried to shift ManMan’s attention. She really couldn’t keep up with him anymore.","“By the way, Grandma Wang made your favorite cake today.”","Hearing this, ManMan forgot all about the car. He got out of the car, took Jing Yi’s hand, and headed straight for the Jing family home.","...","Recently, the Jing family dinners had been quite lively.","After finishing his meal, ManMan went over to Jing Zejun, who was pregnant, and as usual, softly chatted with the baby in her belly. He sat obediently beside her, careful not to bump into Jing Zejun’s large belly. Yet, Jing Zejun adored him even more for it, pulling him close and accepting the fruit Wen Qingyan handed over.","She took a bite, then fed one to her little nephew, showing how close they were.","The whole family watched as the little boy cheerfully recounted what had happened at kindergarten that day, their eyes filled with affection.","“...That’s all that happened at kindergarten today. Besides figuring out how to get everyone to play together, everything else was fine.”","When he mentioned how all the kids at kindergarten loved playing with him, his little expression showed just the right amount of helplessness, making everyone smile.","Ever since he learned that Jing Zejun’s pregnancy meant he would have a little sister or brother, ManMan had been acting like a proper big brother.","He looked at Jing Zejun’s belly and asked seriously, “Have you been good today? You mustn’t make Auntie Jing Zejun too tired. Your mom is working hard to carry you...”","His chattering little demeanor melted Jing Zejun’s heart.","She hugged ManMan and sighed, “When your little brother or sister is born, we’ll leave them to you. Then we’ll have the most thoughtful little helper.”","ManMan patted his chest confidently. “No problem! Leave it to ManMan!”","Seeing his confident expression, Jing Zeqian teased, “Oh, so ManMan isn’t saying Auntie ‘eats babies’ anymore?”","That had been ManMan’s reaction when he first heard the news of Jing Zejun’s pregnancy.","At the time, Wen Qingyan was overjoyed, holding Jing Zejun’s hand as he shared the good news with everyone. Everyone was thrilled, including ManMan, who had just learned he was going to have a little sibling.","He went up to Wen Qingyan, looked up with his soft, innocent face, and asked, “Uncle, where is ManMan’s little brother or sister?”","Wen Qingyan picked up his beloved nephew, his eyes still shining with joy. “They’re in Auntie Jing Zejun’s belly. In about eight or nine months, they’ll come out to meet you, and you’ll be a big brother!”","But instead of being happy, ManMan looked at Jing Zejun’s belly in shock, his round eyes filled with a hint of fear.","In a trembling voice, he asked, “Did Auntie eat my little brother or sister?!”","He hadn’t heard the rest of Wen Qingyan’s explanation—all he could think about was the words “in Auntie Jing Zejun’s belly.”","Wen Qingyan’s smile froze, and everyone else was stunned. A few seconds later, the room erupted in laughter.","Jing Zejun was laughing so hard she had to hold her waist, and Wen Qingyan quickly handed ManMan over to Shen Huaichu, who had come over, before carefully helping Jing Zejun sit down.","Later, they explained to ManMan in simpler terms that his little sibling hadn’t been eaten by his aunt but would be born in a few months.","ManMan didn’t fully understand the process, but at least he knew his aunt hadn’t eaten his little sibling.","He also realized everyone had been laughing at him, and now that Jing Zeqian brought it up again, his soft little face turned red with a mix of embarrassment and annoyance.","“Uncle, you promised not to bring that up again! That was when ManMan was little and didn’t understand!”","Jing Zeqian burst out laughing. “Little? I can understand calling two years old ‘little,’ but half a year ago is also ‘little’?”","ManMan proudly puffed out his chest. “Of course! Dad says every day I grow a little bigger. ManMan isn’t the same as before.”","Shen Huaichu looked at his son’s little face, his eyes filled with tender amusement."]},{"number":253,"title":"Chapter 253: Extra: Daily Parenting 5 - Shen Huaichu's Everyday Life with the Kids","paragraphs":["In the early morning, ManMan, still drowsy, sat up in bed. After a moment of adjusting, he reached for the clothes he had picked out the night before—a creamy white pair of overalls.","Shen Huaichu entered the room at his usual time and, as expected, found his son already dressed.","Seeing him come in, ManMan stretched out his little arms and called out sweetly, \"Daddy.\"","This was one of his son's habits.","Shen Huaichu, now accustomed to it, stepped forward and picked him up, receiving an adorable good morning kiss in return.","At first, Shen Huaichu wasn’t entirely comfortable with his son's little quirks and had even tried to be stricter with him.","But those eyes of ManMan’s were so much like Jing Yi’s that anyone who saw the two together would remark how, even though ManMan was a boy, he looked like a miniature version of Jing Yi.","And ManMan, for some reason, was never afraid of Shen Huaichu. Even when he put on a stern face, a little kiss from ManMan would melt it away.","Jing Yi often marveled at how her son had perfectly figured out how to tug at his father’s heartstrings.","But ManMan was a sweet child. Aside from his constant questions and occasional unintentionally blunt remarks, he was obedient and clever, rarely causing them any trouble.","After finishing his morning routine, ManMan held Shen Huaichu’s hand and walked out, his big, dark eyes lighting up with joy when he saw Jing Yi already seated at the dining table, waiting for them.","\"Mommy, you’re up so early today!\"","Jing Yi glanced at Shen Huaichu, who was trying to suppress a smile, and then looked down at her son, who was already starting the day with his usual enthusiasm.","\"Yes, Mommy has something to do this morning, so I had to get up early.\" She wasn’t a fan of early mornings, but that was beside the point.","ManMan didn’t catch the self-deprecating tone in her voice and excitedly pulled Shen Huaichu over to the table.","Since Mommy was up for breakfast today, he wanted to sit right between his parents!","Shen Huaichu lifted his son and placed him in his special chair, then moved the prepared breakfast closer.","ManMan looked at the small bowl of yam and millet porridge in front of him, then at the variety of dishes on Jing Yi’s plate.","\"Daddy, do I still have to eat porridge today?\"","Jing Yi quietly moved her plate further away, not wanting to tempt her son, though his pitiful tone tugged at her heart.","Shen Huaichu also picked up his bowl of millet porridge. It had been prepared by their housekeeper, and ManMan had been eating it for the past few days. Even at kindergarten, the staff had been informed to provide him with a special lunch.","He could hear the disappointment in ManMan’s voice, but he had to stick to the plan. His son loved food, but just a few days ago, he had overeaten and ended up with indigestion, leaving the whole family worried.","\"Yes, just one more day. If your stomach feels better tomorrow, you won’t have to eat it anymore.\"","ManMan looked pleadingly at Jing Yi, but all he got was a sympathetic look. He couldn’t see the delicious spread in front of her anymore.","Jing Yi couldn’t resist her son’s puppy eyes and quickly tried to finish her breakfast.","Seeing her haste, Shen Huaichu frowned slightly and said, \"Take your time.\" Eating too fast wasn’t good for her stomach.","Then he turned to ManMan and said seriously, \"Mommy didn’t overeat, so she can enjoy her breakfast, right?\"","Shen Huaichu and Jing Yi believed in treating their child as an equal, especially now that ManMan could understand them. This approach had proven to be effective.","As expected, ManMan nodded earnestly, his little tuft of hair bouncing.","\"Yes, Mommy. ManMan won’t look anymore. The millet porridge is really good too.\" He scooped up a spoonful and ate it with a smile.","Jing Yi chuckled and gently ruffled his hair.","\"When you’re feeling better, we’ll go to Grandmother Wang’s and make something delicious!\"","At times like this, Jing Yi felt incredibly lucky—she had an angel for a son, and, more importantly, his father was an angel too.","Everyone said ManMan looked like her, but Jing Yi thought he resembled Shen Huaichu, especially when he was deep in thought.","Jing Yi watched as Shen Huaichu continued to eat his porridge with ManMan, occasionally wiping his son’s mouth, his eyes filled with tender love.","People often joked that \"as long as the dad keeps the kid alive, it’s a win,\" but in their household, it was a completely different story.","Ever since ManMan was born, Shen Huaichu had been the one taking care of him more often. He always said he hadn’t had time to prepare for fatherhood, but he had adapted to the role faster than she had.","While she was still figuring out how to be a mom and worrying about every little detail, Shen Huaichu had already taken charge of everything.","No one could compare to her husband in terms of dedication.","Shen Huaichu looked up and noticed Jing Yi staring at him. \"What’s wrong? Don’t you like the breakfast?\"","That couldn’t be—it was all her favorite dishes. He had even asked their housekeeper to learn some recipes from Aunt Wang.","Jing Yi smiled, her dimples showing. \"No, I just wanted to try your millet porridge.\"","Shen Huaichu gave her a helpless but affectionate look and was about to scoop some for her when someone beat him to it.","ManMan, with his little tuft of hair, happily looked up at Jing Yi. \"Mommy! ManMan will feed you! ManMan and Daddy have the same thing!\"","He carefully lifted the spoon toward Jing Yi, his other hand protectively underneath it, looking utterly adorable.","\"Thank you, ManMan!\"","Jing Yi ate the porridge and lovingly patted his curly hair.","Meanwhile, Shen Huaichu, holding his spoon, froze for a moment, watching the mother-son interaction with a mix of amusement and resignation.","Well, he’d been beaten to it again.","Jing Yi noticed Shen Huaichu’s expression and teased, \"What about you, Daddy?\" Shen Huaichu’s lips curved into a smile as he scooped some porridge and fed it to Jing Yi.","Jing Yi pretended to savor it and nodded approvingly. \"Not bad, very good.\"","ManMan’s eyes lit up, and he turned to Shen Huaichu. \"Daddy, can I try yours too?\"","Shen Huaichu chuckled and fed him a spoonful. It was all from the same pot—how could it taste any different?","ManMan imitated Jing Yi, tasting it carefully. \"Not bad, very good!\"","The mother and son, with their strikingly similar eyes, looked at Shen Huaichu with laughter in their gaze. Shen Huaichu’s smile deepened, his entire demeanor soft and warm.","After breakfast, it was time for ManMan’s usual kindergarten routine.","He obediently gave his mom a goodbye kiss and waited for her to return the gesture. Then, after watching her give Shen Huaichu a goodbye kiss, he took his father’s hand and headed out.","\"Daddy, last week you didn’t take me to school, and my classmates kept asking about you.\"","\"What did they ask?\"","\"They asked why you didn’t take me to school.\"","\"And what did you say?\"","\"I told them you were on a business trip. Daddy, will you have to go on more trips?\"","\"Probably, yes.\"","\"Okay, but try to come back early, okay? Otherwise, they keep asking me, and it makes me think of you. When I think about coming home and not seeing you, I feel a little sad.\"","\"...Okay, I’ll always come back early.\""]},{"number":254,"title":"Chapter 254: Extra: Daily Parenting 6: Jing Yi's Everyday Life with the Kids","paragraphs":["ManMan's words kept Shen Huaichu in a good mood all day, and even the employees of Huarui Group could easily notice his cheerful demeanor.","The first to notice was his assistant, right after he left Shen Huaichu's office.","Within half an hour, people waiting to report their work had quickly gathered at the office door.","Each person waiting watched as employees came out, and with every one they saw, their confidence grew. It seemed the CEO was in an unusually good mood today!","However, Shen Huaichu's good mood only lasted until he got home. He arrived early today, but his wife wasn't there, and his three-year-old son had also been taken somewhere else.","\"Huaichu, I took ManMan and his classmate to Shanchi. We won’t be back for dinner tonight.\"","Jing Yi had previously promised Chen Yuqi's mother that she would take him to ManMan's small racing track, so after picking him up, she headed straight there with the two kids.","Listening to the faint sound of his son and another child chatting on the phone, Shen Huaichu sighed. Coming home to find neither his wife nor his son was truly disappointing.","...","At Shanchi, next to the small racing track, Jing Yi and Jing Zeqian were each remotely controlling a small car.","Jing Yi was in charge of Chen Yuqi's car, while Jing Zeqian controlled ManMan's.","The two small cars were 'speeding' along the track at a very safe pace—at least that’s what the two kids thought.","Chen Yuqi had been excited all day because he finally got to visit the professional racing track that Shen Muyi had talked about!","No little boy could resist cool cars, especially race cars.","Chen Yuqi, with his chubby hands on the steering wheel, felt the thrill of speed as described in cartoons, occasionally letting out excited shouts, yelling, \"Faster! Faster!\"","ManMan, on the other hand, was much calmer. With both hands on the wheel, he looked seriously at the track ahead, cautiously turning the wheel as the course demanded.","Meanwhile, Jing Yi and Jing Zeqian were also fully focused. Although the cars weren’t moving fast, remote control required skill, and the outcome depended on the controller's technique.","Chen Yuqi's car was the first to cross the finish line, and his excited cheers grew even louder.","Jing Yi looked smugly at Jing Zeqian, \"Second brother, you owe me three forehead flicks!\" Jing Zeqian retorted, \"Let’s go again!\"","Jing Zeqian had secretly practiced with ManMan for a long time, but he still lost to Jing Yi!","This small racing track was a gift from Jing Zeqian to ManMan. While there were smaller race cars available, ManMan would have to wait until he was a bit older, or else the whole family might gang up on Jing Zeqian.","For now, they could only 'race' with remote-controlled cars on this track.","But it was still a lot of fun.","Jing Zeqian rolled up his sleeves, ready to give it another shot. ManMan, who had lost the race, wasn’t upset. Instead, he seriously discussed strategy with Jing Zeqian.","Standing next to him, ManMan only reached Jing Zeqian's thigh. He tugged on Jing Zeqian's clothes, pointing at a curve on the track.","\"Uncle, it was right there where we fell behind...\"","Jing Yi, holding Chen Yuqi's hand, watched her son’s analysis with a soft, proud smile.","ManMan was very smart. At first, he might have been excited about the racing track, but later he noticed something was off when he couldn’t fully control the car.","Jing Yi had to explain to him that this was the most professional track a three-year-old could have, which finally put his questions to rest.","Even though he knew his control was limited, he still took it seriously, and Jing Zeqian listened intently.","The uncle and nephew even high-fived, determined to beat Jing Yi (Mom) at least once!","Jing Yi chuckled, her almond-shaped eyes sparkling with amusement, and her cheeks dimpled.","\"Chen Yuqi, they’ve challenged us. What should we say?\"","The chubby little boy jumped up excitedly, looking thrilled, \"Bring it on! There’s only one winner on the battlefield!\"","Jing Yi paused, looking down at the three-year-old with his clenched fists and an inexplicably intense 'ready for battle' expression.","Was he already entering his edgy phase this early?","Chen Yuqi had no idea what 'edgy' meant. All he knew was that today he got to play with Shen Muyi—just the two of them! This was something he could brag about in class for a long time!","Plus, he got to play with Shen Muyi's mom, who was a champion racer!","And she was really pretty!","She had almost everything a kindergarten kid would envy, so whenever Shen Muyi's mom came to pick him up, many of the kids were excited too.","Of course, Shen Muyi's dad was also very handsome, but he seemed a bit intimidating. Chen Yuqi had never seen him smile, not even during parent-teacher meetings.","But Shen Muyi didn’t seem afraid of his dad. If it were Chen Yuqi’s dad looking serious and not smiling, he’d be wondering if his dad had found out about the time he secretly drew on his face.","Yet Shen Muyi always said his dad wasn’t scary—he was actually super gentle.","Chen Yuqi wanted to believe it, but he wasn’t entirely convinced.","Every time he saw Shen Muyi's dad, he still felt a bit scared, but he instinctively felt that Shen Muyi wouldn’t lie. If Shen Muyi said his dad wasn’t scary, then he wasn’t scary.","...","Not far from the racing track, the glow of the setting sun bathed the area as ManMan's car crossed the finish line, marking the end of their 'professional racing' adventure.","\"Alright, kids, how about we think about getting some dinner and then heading home?\"","After taking the two kids out for dinner, Jing Yi would have to safely return Chen Yuqi to his family.","The kids were reluctant to leave, while Jing Yi and Jing Zeqian’s fingers were starting to ache.","Although they enjoyed this large-scale remote-controlled car race, it was still tiring after a while.","ManMan and Chen Yuqi ran back, looking up with soft, pleading eyes. \"Mom, can we watch you race before we go?\" The chubby little boy beside him also gazed at Jing Yi with starry eyes.","Their expressions were so endearing that Jing Yi couldn’t resist gently pinching their cheeks.","\"Ha, so you want a closing performance, huh? You guys really know how to have fun.\"","But it would only take a few minutes, and Jing Yi was happy to oblige.","\"Alright, just one lap.\"","The two kids were thrilled, especially Chen Yuqi.","Now he would be the only kid in class who had seen Shen Muyi’s mom race!","The small racing track was right next to Shanchi. As Jing Yi and Jing Zeqian prepared to take the kids over, they spotted Shen Huaichu approaching from a distance."]},{"number":255,"title":"Chapter 255: Extra: Daily Life of Raising Kids 7: Shen Muyi's Dad","paragraphs":["ManMan was the first to spot Shen Huaichu and immediately rushed towards him.","Shen Huaichu’s eyes sparkled with amusement as he crouched down, arms open wide, ready to catch his son, who was charging at him like a little cannonball.","ManMan wrapped his arms around Shen Huaichu’s neck and asked cheerfully, “Dad, why are you here?”","What could Shen Huaichu say? That he felt like an empty-nest middle-aged CEO? Or that he missed his wife and son so much that he chased after them?","“I just got off work and happened to pass by,” he replied.","Jing Zeqian, who had just arrived, overheard this and crossed his arms, teasing, “Mr. Shen, that’s quite a detour for a ‘pass by,’ isn’t it?”","Jing Zeqian couldn’t help but think to himself, after all these years, Shen Huaichu was still as serious as ever, and still terrible at making excuses.","Shen Huaichu pressed his lips together, thinking the same about his second brother—after all these years, Jing Zeqian still hadn’t learned to hold his tongue.","Jing Yi walked over, holding Chen Yuqi’s hand. “Why are you here?” Shen Huaichu glanced at the child hiding behind his wife, who was sneaking peeks at him.","It was the same child who often cried and made a scene at the kindergarten gate.","Shen Huaichu shifted his gaze back to Jing Yi, his eyes softening as he looked at his wife. The tough words he had prepared seemed to melt away in an instant.","“I came to pick you up,” he said.","Of course, the more tender words would be saved for when he and his wife were alone later that night.","ManMan was overjoyed, thrilled that his mom was playing with him and that he had run into his dad.","“Dad, Mom’s going to race for us later. Can we watch before we go home?”","Shen Huaichu adjusted the button on his son’s shirt, which had come undone from all the playing. “Sure, we’ll watch first and then go home.” He turned to Jing Yi. “Have you eaten yet?”","Jing Yi shook her head. “Not yet. We were planning to grab something later. Have you eaten?” Shen Huaichu shook his head honestly. He had gone home to find the house empty and came out to look for them.","Though Shen Huaichu’s face remained expressionless, Jing Yi could sense a hint of grievance in his demeanor.","“Sorry, I should’ve told you earlier. Next time, I’ll take you with us, okay?”","He wasn’t a child.","Both Shen Huaichu and Jing Zeqian thought the same thing, though one felt a surge of happiness while the other was filled with disdain.","...","When Jing Yi put on her helmet and got into the race car, the last rays of the setting sun bathed the track, illuminating the dazzling red car.","The two adults and two children stood on the viewing platform. While the kids were excited, the adults remained calm.","As they watched the figure on the track, they chatted casually.","“What do you want to eat later?”","“Jing Yi mentioned wanting to try that private kitchen near the post office yesterday.”","“Let’s go there, then.”","“Ask the kid if there’s anything he doesn’t eat.”","Shen Huaichu was referring to Chen Yuqi, who stood beside Jing Zeqian, gripping the railing with excitement, his chubby face beaming.","Jing Zeqian raised an eyebrow, his tone casual. “Why don’t you ask?” Shen Huaichu gave him a look—couldn’t his second brother see that the child was afraid of him?","Jing Zeqian smirked, never missing an opportunity to tease Shen Huaichu.","“I told you your face is too serious. Only our ManMan is brave enough to handle it.”","Shen Huaichu remained expressionless. If he had the time and energy, he would’ve already asked.","In the end, Jing Zeqian only got a “he eats everything” response. He glanced at the little boy, whose attention was entirely on the race car.","Forget it, he’d ask later. The kid didn’t look like he was in the mood to answer now.","The sunset bathed the race car as it roared down the track, executing a clean drift that sent the kids’ cheers to a new decibel level.","Shen Huaichu sat beside ManMan, gently supporting him while occasionally glancing at the little boy next to them.","When Jing Yi crossed the finish line in the car that had won multiple GT Super Cup championships, ManMan turned to his father, still bursting with excitement.","He threw himself into Shen Huaichu’s arms. “Dad, Mom is so amazing! She’s the best racer ever! Mom’s the coolest!”","Shen Huaichu carefully held his son and looked at Jing Yi as she stepped out of the car. His gaze was tender and intense.","Under the sunset, she waved at them, and the cheers continued. Shen Huaichu could feel Jing Yi’s joy.","He had seen this scene many times, but it never got old.","Shen Huaichu lifted ManMan up so his waving would be more visible to Jing Yi. Mother and son waved at each other from a distance.","Shen Huaichu’s expression softened even more.","“Hey, kid, what are you looking at?”","After tearing his gaze away from his sister and nephew’s enthusiastic waving, Jing Zeqian noticed Chen Yuqi had quieted down.","His heart skipped a beat—was the kid envious that ManMan was being held? Should he pick him up too? But they weren’t exactly close.","While Jing Zeqian was lost in thought, Chen Yuqi gestured for him to bend down, looking mysterious.","The little boy had no idea what the handsome uncle was overthinking. He had just discovered a secret.","Jing Zeqian leaned down curiously.","As if afraid others might hear, Chen Yuqi whispered into Jing Zeqian’s ear, “I was watching Shen Muyi’s dad. Turns out Shen Muyi was right—his dad isn’t scary at all.”","He had seen it himself. Shen Muyi’s dad didn’t scold him for shouting, and he even lifted him up so he could wave better.","Children’s worlds are simple. They see a smile as a sign of friendliness and tears as a sign of reluctance.","But beyond these expressions, Chen Yuqi could also sense the emotions Shen Huaichu didn’t openly show.","It was like what his mom had said—even if Shen Muyi’s dad didn’t smile often, he was still much better than his own dad.","At the time, Chen Yuqi had defended his dad with all the seriousness a child could muster, but it hadn’t earned him the ice cream he wanted.","In retaliation, he had secretly drawn little figures on his dad’s stomach that night.","Shen Muyi’s dad gave him the feeling that Shen Muyi didn’t need to say anything nice to get ice cream. Even if he didn’t get it today, he’d get it tomorrow.","Jing Zeqian, who had been expecting some tear-jerking backstory: That’s it?","Jing Zeqian chuckled and looked at Shen Huaichu, who was still holding ManMan as the boy waved energetically at Jing Yi.","Even if he still couldn’t stand Shen Huaichu, he had to admit that Shen Huaichu was a great dad.","Jing Zeqian never imagined Shen Huaichu would become such a patient and caring father. Even if he didn’t smile much, he was still gentle with ManMan, making sure the boy felt loved.","ManMan idolized Jing Yi, but he also fiercely defended Shen Huaichu. He loved his parents deeply, and they loved him just as much."]},{"number":256,"title":"Chapter 256: Extra: Daily Life with Kids 8 - Uncle Takes Care of the Baby","paragraphs":["At Hengjing Group, Assistant Chen arrived at the company half an hour earlier than Jing Zeyou, as usual.","Normally, he would be preparing all the materials for Jing Zeyou's work for the day, but today was the day the boss's beloved little nephew was coming to the office.","So, he had to first prepare everything the little boss might need—some small toys to pass the time, the 'homework' the CEO had assigned to the little boss last time, and some carefully prepared snacks.","In short, on the days the little boss came, even the CEO's work had to take a backseat.","Assistant Chen was the best representative of Jing Zeyou, so the employees could roughly guess the CEO's schedule for the day by observing his actions.","It was obvious that the small items he was preparing indicated that the CEO's little nephew would be visiting today!","For a moment, the employees who heard the news were all delighted. After all, who wouldn't love a beautiful and well-behaved child?","Every time they heard the CEO's little nephew call them 'big brother' or 'big sister,' their mood would stay uplifted for the entire day.","Assistant Chen calmly watched the cheerful chatter of the employees and remembered the CEO's recent reminder.","\"Don't say I didn't warn you—no feeding him anything today.\"","The little boss had recently suffered from indigestion, and for several days, Assistant Chen had seen books like 'How to Relieve Child Indigestion' on the CEO's desk.","Although the little boss had recovered, the CEO had specifically instructed that no one in the office should feed him snacks anymore.","The employees were a bit disappointed, but since the CEO had spoken, they had no choice but to comply. It seemed they would be missing out on one of their daily joys—watching the CEO's little nephew snack away was something they could do all day!","After delivering the CEO's instructions, Assistant Chen took the items prepared for the little boss and headed back to his workstation. The CEO had a meeting in the morning, and some documents needed to be prepared.","...","While the employees were still discussing, Jing Zeyou walked into the company carrying a three-year-old child in one arm. The little boy obediently rested his head on Jing Zeyou's shoulder, a small tuft of hair tied up on his head.","As they passed the reception desk, the child waved and greeted the receptionist.","This was the sister who had given him a small jelly last time!","Jing Zeyou carried the child, noticing that the Hengjing employees were much more cheerful than usual. They were greeting him, but their eyes were all fixed on his little nephew.","It wasn't until they entered the elevator that they were shielded from the employees' eager gazes.","No matter how many times he witnessed this scene, Jing Zeyou still found it amusing.","ManMan was on vacation, and with so many people at home, they didn't want to restrict him. So, they decided to bring ManMan to work.","Of course, Jing Zeyou also wanted to expose ManMan to more things as early as possible, given how clever his little nephew was.","But the next day, he couldn't find ManMan. According to Aunt Wang, Jing Zeqian had taken him away.","That was fine; there was no rush anyway.","On the third day, ManMan was again nowhere to be found—he had gone out to play with his uncle and aunt.","The fourth day, the fifth day, the sixth day...","Jing Zeyou fell silent.","So, he decided to bring ManMan to his house the night before, and only in the past few days had he successfully brought ManMan to work.","ManMan was also very well-behaved. Occasionally, when Jing Zeyou had meetings and couldn't take him along, ManMan would entertain himself or go out to 'socialize.' The employees who greeted him were the fruits of his 'efforts.'","This wasn't ManMan's first time at Hengjing. After being set down, he happily greeted the familiar Assistant Chen and sweetly thanked him for the snacks and toys he had prepared.","Even the usually composed Assistant Chen couldn't help but smile, softening his voice as he replied, \"You're welcome. It's part of my job.\"","After ManMan's first visit, Jing Zeyou had arranged a dedicated spot in the office for him.","The spot had a small table, a small chair, toy facilities, and even a small sofa—all brightly colored and impossible to miss upon entering.","ManMan didn't head there immediately. Before coming, his uncle had told him that he had a small task today.","He was here to accompany his uncle to work and to help him!","Jing Zeyou unfolded the day's work report and began to read it slowly, trying to make the three-year-old sitting on his lap understand.","His voice was so gentle that one might mistake it for a bedtime story.","Although it wasn't the first time Assistant Chen had seen this scene, he still felt a complex mix of emotions.","If you thought the CEO was hoping his nephew would become a prodigy, he wasn't exactly forcing the three-year-old to truly understand his work—he was just narrating it like a story.","If you thought the CEO was simply playing with his nephew, well, who else would have a three-year-old listen to a corporate CEO's work report?","What was even more absurd was that ManMan actually had something to contribute.","Jing Zeyou was discussing the results of the testing team, his tone still calm, but a hint of displeasure gradually darkened his eyes.","ManMan furrowed his little brows. Assistant Chen thought he didn't understand and silently criticized the CEO for being a bit unreliable this time.","Then ManMan spoke, his voice tinged with hesitation, \"So, what did these big brothers and sisters actually do?\"","ManMan couldn't understand terms like 'completed metrics' or 'technological innovation.' After listening, he felt like they had done something, yet nothing at all.","The displeasure in Jing Zeyou's eyes faded, replaced by pride and joy as he looked at his little nephew.","\"ManMan is absolutely right. You're so clever.\"","ManMan adored his uncle the most. Hearing Jing Zeyou's praise, he smiled, his eyes curving into crescents, the little tuft of hair on his head swaying slightly.","When Jing Zeyou looked up again, the joy in his eyes had disappeared.","\"Tell the testing team that I expect a reasonable explanation during the morning meeting.\"","Assistant Chen clearly sensed the displeasure in Jing Zeyou's tone and responded seriously, \"Understood.\" He couldn't help but feel a bit of sympathy for the team. Did they really think the CEO was easy to deal with?","After Assistant Chen left, ManMan looked up at Jing Zeyou, who had returned to his usual gentle demeanor.","\"Uncle, did ManMan help?\"","His round eyes sparkled with anticipation for praise. Jing Zeyou gently ruffled his curly hair.","\"Of course, ManMan helped a lot.\"","ManMan's smile widened, and he tilted his head, giving Jing Zeyou a sweet grin.","\"Then can ManMan go play with the big brothers and sisters later?\"","Jing Zeyou could easily tell that his little nephew was planning to 'forage for snacks.' A hint of amusement flashed in his eyes.","\"Sure, but remember to be careful, okay? If anything happens, go find Assistant Chen.\"","He was glad he had given the heads-up earlier. It seemed his nephew's 'snack hunt' would be unsuccessful this time.","So, while Jing Zeyou was in the meeting, ManMan found the group of big brothers and sisters who had fed him last time. He leaned on their desks, his soft little face glowing with anticipation.","The employees, inwardly weeping: ...ManMan, we really can't give you anything this time. The boss has spoken!"]},{"number":257,"title":"Chapter 257: Extra: Daily Life with Kids 9 - Uncle's Day with the Kids","paragraphs":["At the Jing household, Jing Yi and her husband were both busy with work, so during the day, ManMan mostly stayed at the Jing residence. After all, the families lived close by.","ManMan was sitting on the sofa playing with a Rubik's Cube, while Lin Ruiqing sat beside him, smiling as she watched him and occasionally feeding him some fruit.","\"Thank you, Grandma!\"","ManMan tilted his head and gave Lin Ruiqing a sweet, soft smile.","Lin Ruiqing smiled even more, the corners of her eyes crinkling with joy. She softened her voice, \"You're welcome, ManMan. Would you like some more grapes?\"","Jing Beicheng, who was nearby, glanced over, a hint of amused helplessness in his eyes. Ever since ManMan came into their lives, his wife's attention had completely shifted to the little boy.","Perhaps because Jing Beicheng had been watching for a while, ManMan looked at him, then at the fruit in Lin Ruiqing's hand.","He took the fork from Lin Ruiqing, speared a piece of fruit, and with his little topknot bouncing, he trotted over to Jing Beicheng. Looking up at him, he offered the fruit.","\"Grandpa, eat this.\"","Grandpa had been watching for so long; he must want some fruit!","ManMan held up the fruit, his eyes, which looked so much like Jing Yi's, gazing at him.","Jing Beicheng chuckled with a mix of helplessness and affection, opening his mouth to eat the fruit. \"Thank you, ManMan.\" His actions were practiced, clearly not the first time this had happened.","Lin Ruiqing, her eyes filled with warmth, deliberately coughed lightly. ManMan immediately turned around, speared another piece of fruit, and brought it to Lin Ruiqing's mouth.","\"Grandma, you eat too!\"","Mom had said not to favor one over the other.","\"Ahem, is there any for me?\" A clear, cheerful voice rang out.","ManMan immediately looked over to see Jing Zeqian, who had just returned. His round eyes sparkled with excitement as he put down the fork and rushed over.","\"Uncle Zeqian!\"","Jing Zeqian crouched down, catching the little \"missile\" that came barreling toward him, and lifted him up.","\"Whoa, it's only been a few days since I last saw you, and you've already gained weight?\"","Jing Zeqian settled ManMan on his arm and playfully pinched his little belly.","ManMan immediately protected his stomach, his soft cheeks puffing out. \"Uncle Zeqian, ManMan isn't heavy. Dad says you're just too weak.\"","Jing Zeqian: \"...He's been talking about me again, hasn't he?!\"","ManMan quickly covered his mouth, his little eyes darting around. He had forgotten that Mom said not to mention that.","ManMan knew exactly who to turn to for help. He looked at Lin Ruiqing, but before he could say anything, she cut off Jing Zeqian's attempt to press the matter.","\"Alright, you're old enough now. When are you going to stop bickering with Huaichu and grow up?\"","Jing Zeqian dodged Lin Ruiqing's attempt to take ManMan from him, shifting the boy to his other arm. \"Mom, I'm taking ManMan out for a bit.\"","Hearing this, ManMan let go of Lin Ruiqing's hand, his eyes lighting up as he clung to Jing Zeqian's arm, his face beaming with the joy of going out to play.","Lin Ruiqing shot Jing Zeqian a stern look. \"Don't take ManMan to bother Huaichu again.\"","This wasn't an unfounded warning, as Jing Zeqian had indeed taken ManMan to Huarui Group to see Shen Huaichu before, and the two of them had left happily after annoying him.","Jing Zeqian looked aggrieved. Wasn't it his nephew who wanted to see his dad? How had it turned into his own selfish scheme?","Lin Ruiqing rolled her eyes. She knew her son all too well.","Jing Zeqian sighed in resignation. \"My status has really plummeted!\"","Before ManMan came along, he and Shen Huaichu were on equal footing. But now, with ManMan in the picture, Shen Huaichu had completely risen in status because of his son! The more Lin Ruiqing adored ManMan, the kinder she became toward Shen Huaichu!","Even worse, his father was the same. Whenever Shen Huaichu showed up with ManMan, his dad's expression visibly softened!","It was so unfair!","ManMan, sitting in Jing Zeqian's arms, mimicked his uncle's sigh, his little brow furrowing as he said in his childish voice, \"Plummeted!\"","Lin Ruiqing couldn't help but laugh at the little boy. \"Don't learn these things from your uncle.\" Then she turned back to Jing Zeqian. \"Where are you taking ManMan?\"","She needed to make sure her younger son wasn't up to something irresponsible.","Jing Zeqian did feel a bit guilty. He wanted to take ManMan to Shanshi for some fun, but he couldn't admit that. After all, it was even worse than going to Huarui Group to annoy Shen Huaichu—or rather, to visit ManMan's dad.","Lin Ruiqing could tell from Jing Zeqian's expression that he wasn't being entirely honest. This guy could never be trusted!","Before Lin Ruiqing could press further, Jing Zeqian dashed out the door with ManMan in his arms.","ManMan wasn't new to being carried off like this. He giggled happily, waving goodbye to Lin Ruiqing and Jing Beicheng.","ManMan was a polite child.","Before Lin Ruiqing could react, the two were already gone. Jing Beicheng, used to this, steadied his wife as she began scolding their younger son.","\"How can he still be so irresponsible? Ever since ManMan was less than a year old, he's been taking him out to play every other day...\"","Jing Beicheng's eyes twinkled with amusement, but when his wife looked at him, he immediately put on a serious expression, as if to say, \"I'm on your side.\"","Though, if he were to be honest, Shen Huaichu was also quite laid-back, trusting Jing Zeqian to take care of their son.","Shen Huaichu: ...When had he ever been trusting? He had even started resorting to badmouthing Jing Zeqian.","...","Meanwhile, Jing Zeqian, who had \"stolen\" ManMan away, carried the boy on his shoulders as they headed out.","ManMan placed his hands on Jing Zeqian's head, his face alight with excitement. \"Uncle Zeqian, where are we going today?\"","He knew that whenever Uncle Zeqian took him out, it was always for something fun!","Jing Zeqian walked steadily, mindful of the three-year-old perched on his shoulders.","\"First, Uncle Zeqian will take you to eat something delicious, and then we'll go see your mom, okay?\" This was likely the time when Jing Yi would be training at Shanshi.","ManMan was even more thrilled. He had seen his mom race cars before, and she was super cool!","He raised his chubby little hand and exclaimed, \"Uncle Zeqian, can I drive a car at the big racetrack today?\"","Hearing this, Jing Zeqian nearly stumbled in his guilt. It was his fault for taking ManMan to the racetrack in the first place, sparking the boy's fascination with racing.","\"ManMan, remember what we agreed? You have to wait until you're at least eighteen to even think about that.\"","Please don't let this slip in front of his mom or Jing Yi, or he'd be in big trouble!","ManMan was a little disappointed but didn't fuss. \"Then, Uncle Zeqian, can I ride in Mom's race car today?\"","Oh no, he couldn't promise that either. ManMan was only three, and all the cars at home had special child seats. Who would dare let him sit in a race car?","Jing Zeqian chuckled nervously. \"ManMan, today we'll go to the special track just for you, and we'll drive the little red car, okay?\"","ManMan sighed like a little adult. It seemed Dad was right—Uncle Zeqian really couldn't make any decisions.","Still, he really liked Uncle Zeqian! And Mom had said that Uncle Zeqian was like a little princess inside, so as a little knight, he needed to take care of him!","\"Okay, Uncle Zeqian! Let's drive the red car today!\"","\"Alright! Let's go!\""]},{"number":258,"title":"Chapter 258: Extra: Daily Life of Raising Kids 10: The Ownership of 'Night'","paragraphs":["Jing Zeqian leaned in close to ManMan, watching as his little nephew skillfully played with the Rubik's cube in his hands.","\"ManMan, who do you like more, Uncle Zeqian or Uncle Zeyou?\" This time, he put himself first, hoping for a different answer.","ManMan didn’t pause for a moment, his voice soft and sweet, \"I like both!\" His mom had told him not to favor one over the other, so when faced with such questions, he should always say he likes both.","Jing Zeqian was momentarily speechless.","It wasn’t that he was dissatisfied with the answer, but it seemed all too much like something Jing Yiyi had coached him to say. And the response felt so insincere.","Shen Huaichu, who was sitting nearby playing with his son, couldn’t help but smirk, his eyes filled with amusement. Jing Zeqian caught it immediately.","With a huff, Jing Zeqian turned back to ManMan and asked, \"ManMan, who do you like more, Uncle Zeyou or Daddy?\"","ManMan finally solved the Rubik's cube, let out a small sigh of relief, and smiled brightly.","\"I like both!\"","Shen Huaichu: \"...Jing Zeqian, you’re really childish.\"","How did Jing Zeqian and the others discover ManMan’s fondness for Jing Zeyou?","It was obvious. Whenever Jing Zeyou was around, ManMan wouldn’t cling to anyone else for attention.","When ManMan was just under two years old, if he was placed in a circle of people without Jing Yi, he would toddle straight toward Jing Zeyou.","Shen Huaichu had even complained to Jing Yi about it a few times.","...","\"Uncle Zeyou!\"","Jing Zeyou picked up ManMan and carried him upstairs to change into his home clothes.","There was no other choice—if he made ManMan wait, the little one would definitely get upset.","Jing Zeyou carried him back down, and ManMan was still chattering away about what he had done that day.","The clingy, affectionate little boy always made Jing Zeqian feel a pang of jealousy whenever he saw them together.","ManMan’s daily routine was pretty much the same, but today was a bit different.","He had asked his mom for something, but she hadn’t given it to him.","Jing Zeyou raised an eyebrow, looking at his well-behaved nephew sitting on his lap. \"What was it?\" If necessary, he could try to find something similar.","ManMan looked up at him with his soft, round face and said, \"It’s that really cool black car.\" Jing Zeyou was momentarily stunned. A really cool black car?","Could he be talking about the 'Midnight'?","......","Earlier that morning","\"Mom, is there a car in the garage that’s mine?\"","ManMan snuggled into Jing Yi’s arms, pouting. He had been eyeing the cars in the garage for a while, but he knew they all belonged to his mom.","Jing Yi pinched his chubby little cheek, her eyes—so similar to ManMan’s—filled with laughter.","\"Shen Manman, I can’t believe you’re already trying to claim my things at such a young age!\"","Shen Huaichu, who was sitting nearby, didn’t even look up as he chimed in, \"Of course there is. Isn’t your toy car parked in there?\"","Shen Huaichu was referring to the toy cars ManMan’s uncles had given him. They could have been kept in the playroom, but for some reason, they were deliberately parked in the garage.","Every time Jing Yi and Shen Huaichu walked past, their eyes would linger for a moment, worried they might accidentally crush the tiny cars.","ManMan puffed out his cheeks, \"Dad, I’m asking Mom!\" His dad was so mean—he knew that wasn’t what he meant!","Shen Huaichu raised a hand, signaling for ManMan to continue, while he went back to whatever he was working on.","Jing Yi watched the little exchange between father and son with amusement, then turned her attention back to her persistent son.","\"Alright, which one do you want?\"","Her son was just too adorable, and she could hardly refuse such a small request. After all, even if he got it, he couldn’t drive it—he’d still be stuck with the toy cars taking up space in the garage.","ManMan’s face lit up with excitement, but before he could say anything, Jing Yi added,","\"Except for the shiny black sports car. That one’s off-limits.\"","ManMan’s smile faded, replaced by a look of confusion and disappointment. \"Why can’t I have the shiny black car?\"","So he really did want the 'Midnight'?","Jing Yi held her son close and patiently explained, \"That car was a gift from your Uncle Zeyou, and I’m not ready to part with it.\" She was glad she’d clarified that upfront, or else she might have ended up giving the 'Midnight' away.","Shen Huaichu, enjoying the little drama, decided to pass the problem along to Jing Zeyou.","\"Or, you could go ask the person who gave it to her?\"","Jing Yi shot Shen Huaichu a look. She knew exactly what he was up to—he was being so childish!","......","\"...So, your dad sent you to ask me?\"","ManMan nodded obediently. \"Yes, Daddy said if I couldn’t decide, I should ask the person who gave the gift.\"","Shen Huaichu, you’re something else.","Jing Zeyou sighed in resignation.","Seeing his little nephew still waiting for an answer, he spoke gently, \"ManMan, I can’t make the decision for your mom about whether she can give it to you.\"","ManMan tilted his head, his little face full of confusion as he listened to his uncle continue, \"But since your mom doesn’t want to part with it, shouldn’t you respect her feelings?\"","ManMan wasn’t happy about it. This was the first time in his life that both his mom and uncle had said no to him at the same time.","He clung to Jing Zeyou’s arm and pleaded, \"Not even for me?\" Jing Zeyou smiled at his nephew’s attempt to win him over with cuteness.","If there had been a second 'Midnight,' he would have done everything in his power to get it for ManMan, but unfortunately, there was only one.","\"No.\"","ManMan cupped his chubby little face in his hands, his brows furrowed as if he were pondering some great dilemma.","But instead of being upset about the rejection, he was more troubled by something else.","...","When Jing Zeqian returned home, he found his little nephew sitting by the door, his chubby cheeks resting in his hands, his eyebrows knitted together in a serious expression.","Jing Zeqian chuckled and scooped him up. \"You’re waiting for me today? How sweet!\"","ManMan’s face remained serious. \"I’m thinking about something.\" Jing Zeqian teased, \"Oh? What’s got our little ManMan so deep in thought?\"","ManMan, still looking very serious, recounted his earlier conversation with Jing Zeyou.","Then, he came to a conclusion. \"In Uncle Zeyou’s heart, Mom is more important than me!\"","Even though he was only three, he knew it! Uncle Zeyou always gave him whatever he wanted—except this time.","Jing Zeqian was both amused and impressed. His three-year-old nephew’s logic was surprisingly sharp.","But what did he want with a sports car? His little legs couldn’t even reach the pedals—what was the point?","Jing Zeqian carried the boy inside, seizing the opportunity to cement his place as ManMan’s favorite uncle.","\"See? Uncle Zeqian is the best, right?\"","ManMan immediately replied, \"Uncle Zeyou is great too!\" Jing Zeqian pinched his chubby cheek in mock annoyance. \"You’re such a loyal fan of your Uncle Zeyou!\"","Seeing that ManMan was still a little down, Jing Zeqian gently ruffled his hair and, for once, said something nice about his \"rival.\"","\"ManMan, your Uncle Zeyou loves you very, very much. But your mom isn’t just your mom—she’s also his sister.\"","\"You’re his nephew because of her, but she’s been his sister for much longer.\"","These words were a bit complex for a three-year-old to fully grasp, but ManMan soon stopped worrying about it.","A few days later, ManMan received a custom-made miniature version of the 'Midnight' from his Uncle Zeyou. Even Jing Yi couldn’t help but admire it, circling the tiny car several times."]},{"number":259,"title":"Chapter 259: Jing Zeqian Side Story: On How to Become Jing Yiyi's Favorite Brother","paragraphs":["When Jing Zejun went missing, Jing Zeqian was old enough to remember. He was devastated—the sister he had been longing for was suddenly gone.","During that time, he cried and threw tantrums until his voice turned hoarse, and he even developed a high fever. But no matter how much he cried, his sister didn’t return.","Then, one day, his brother told him they had found her. Overjoyed, Jing Zeqian rushed to meet her.","The little sister he had once carried around had grown into a graceful young woman, but she was no longer familiar with him.","He was thrilled to have found her, but also heartbroken. He wanted to compensate her, to give her everything she could ever want.","Yet, she didn’t seem to want anything—not even to join his company or accept any resources.","Their interactions were awkward, filled with a sense of distance.","Jing Zeqian was troubled, but he knew that rebuilding a bond with his sister couldn’t be rushed.","Before he could even begin his plan to reconnect with her, Jing Yiyi suddenly appeared.","Jing Zeqian wasn’t happy about it. He didn’t want to bring Jing Yiyi into the Jing Family. There could only be one young lady in the Jing Family—his sister!","Even if it was his grandmother’s dying wish, he lost the argument due to the family’s majority rule.","Hmph! They’ll regret this!","To ensure Jing Zejun’s absolute position in the Jing Family, Jing Zeqian took it upon himself to keep an eye on Jing Yiyi. She wasn’t going to take his sister’s place!","But Jing Yiyi turned out to be not only eccentric but also strangely perceptive. For the first time, he found himself able to hear others’ thoughts.","At first, it felt novel, but the novelty quickly wore off.","“‘Wind oil essence’? ‘Brother-obsessed princess’? How many nicknames is she going to give me in her head?!”","And why was it that all he could hear were her sarcastic remarks?","Later, his sister and Jing Yiyi became incredibly close. His brother even accompanied her to bask in the sun! His parents also started treating him less favorably!","He could understand the two girls growing closer, especially since Jing Yiyi seemed to genuinely understand Jing Zejun and had even saved her.","He could also understand his parents treating their adopted daughter well—after all, the Jing Family had a tradition of being particularly kind to girls, and Jing Yiyi had accidentally saved his mother.","But his brother? Why was he acting like that? His brother had never even sunbathed with him!","Jing Zeqian couldn’t understand it. Jing Zeqian was furious!","Well, having another sister in the family wasn’t so bad, even if this sister didn’t show him much “respect”! She loved to argue with him and often played dangerous games.","But, ahem, having another sister wasn’t so bad after all.","This sister wasn’t exactly well-behaved. Despite her innocent appearance, her hobbies were wild, and she was surprisingly skilled, completely defying his expectations.","But since he had already accepted her as his sister, he had to protect her.","She could go on TV—he’d make sure everyone knew Jing Yiyi was also a child of the Jing Family! She could race cars—he’d keep an eye on her! She could argue with the company’s artists—after all, she was his sister!","Jing Zeqian thought this new family dynamic wasn’t so bad, and he could adapt to having another sister.","But he never expected that soon, he wouldn’t need to adapt anymore—because he was “kicked out” of the house.","When Jing Yiyi and Jiang Miaomiao had their first argument, Jing Zeqian didn’t pay much attention. It was just a parking spot—he could buy the surrounding area and turn it into parking spaces if needed.","They only argued that one time, and Jing Zeqian thought it would blow over.","But soon, he kept hearing Jing Yiyi’s complaints about Jiang Miaomiao. He didn’t understand why, but since they were in different circles, he didn’t worry too much.","However, things escalated quickly.","Jing Yiyi insisted on attending Jiang Miaomiao’s party. Jing Zeqian was worried she might cause trouble, but since she wanted to go...","He thought he could keep things under control, but it still ended in disaster.","Jing Zeqian was angry. He had warned her repeatedly, but Jing Yiyi still “caused a scene,” and her performance was rather clumsy.","He was such a blind fool.","He had known Jiang Miaomiao for nearly a decade. She wasn’t just a colleague or a subordinate to him—she was his pride from his younger days.","He was stubborn by nature, and once he set his mind on something, he wouldn’t budge. He saw Jing Yiyi as his sister, and Jiang Miaomiao as a crucial friend in his life.","He was stubborn, refusing to rely on the Jing Family, and he had still managed to thrive in the entertainment industry. Jiang Miaomiao was talented, but he was the one who discovered her and elevated her career at Startrack.","How could he accept that his pride from his youth had stabbed him in the back?","He had a temper, but when he heard Jing Yiyi say, “If you can’t find evidence, then kneel and apologize,” he already knew he had lost.","Anyone who could say something like that must be deeply hurt.","Later, the truth came out. He had been the fool all along, the one who was self-righteous. Jing Yiyi had only ever been concerned for him, her brother who talked a big game but never truly cared for her.","He had been self-righteous, guarding against Jing Yiyi, who had never wanted anything from him. He had been self-righteous, becoming an obstacle to her dreams. And he had been self-righteous, hurting Jing Yiyi for the sake of someone who wanted to harm him.","He never thought he’d be kicked out of the house, but more importantly, he hadn’t even apologized to Jing Yiyi! Whether she wanted to hit him or scold him, he needed to let her vent first!","Over time, he learned how to be a good brother instead of a self-righteous one.","He also gradually realized that what he thought was “good” wasn’t necessarily what his sisters wanted.","Jing Yiyi loved racing, so he learned how to be a proper racing manager, building an entire racing team just to pave the way for her career.","But! Could someone please tell him why Jing Yiyi liked his brother so much?!","He went through “great lengths” to sneak her snacks, enduring the “unjust accusations” from their mother, only for her to turn around and share them with his brother!","Couldn’t she spare some for him after all his hard work?!","What? He had already eaten some? That wasn’t the same—snacks he got for himself versus snacks given by his sister were completely different!","And last time, he was the one who saved the barbecue for her—he had put his heart into grilling it!","He just stepped away for a moment, and suddenly his brother got all the credit!","Jing Yiyi, don’t push it! He was the one who treated her the best!","Later, Jing Yiyi brought home a boyfriend—his “rival.” He was going to thoroughly vet him! But before the vetting period was over, they got married, and they even brought a little one into the mix! And guess what? The little one also adored his brother!","Being the sisters’ favorite brother was really hard!"]},{"number":260,"title":"Chapter 260: Jing Zejun Side Story: The Only One Who Truly Understands Me in This World is Jing Yi","paragraphs":["Jing Zejun had always known that the parents who raised her were not her biological parents, but she never imagined she would become the heiress of a top-tier wealthy family.","This felt somewhat surreal to her.","Even more surreal was the fact that before she could fully accept her new identity as a wealthy heiress, she gained a sister.","According to her mother, that sister had been raised by their grandmother.","She couldn’t help but wonder why her grandmother had brought in a girl of similar age after she had gone missing.","It wasn’t that she didn’t care, but curiosity simply got the better of her.","It was later that Jing Yi explained it to her—it wasn’t the so-called “replacement drama” everyone speculated about, but rather an old woman’s prayer.","After meeting Jing Yi in person, Jing Zejun became even more curious. She could actually hear Jing Yi’s thoughts!","It turned out that Jing Yi wasn’t as obedient as she appeared to be.","This only piqued Jing Zejun’s curiosity further.","At first, Jing Zejun felt a little uneasy about having a sister. She was new to the world of wealth herself and worried that her actions might make her sister laugh at her.","But Jing Yi turned out to be much easier to get along with than she had imagined!","Jing Zejun found it hard to believe that even though they had only known each other for a short time, Jing Yi understood her so well.","She knew about Jing Zejun’s determination to become an actress and would stand up for her when their second brother questioned her, helping her get through it.","She could sense Jing Zejun’s discomfort and would mediate between her and the family.","Jing Zejun was supposed to be the older sister, yet it was always Jing Yi who worried about and took care of her.","Jing Zejun had always known that the entertainment industry was far from clean, but she never expected to encounter such a situation so soon.","The director she admired had sold her out for a bit of money.","At that moment, Jing Zejun felt utterly hopeless. She smashed a glass in despair—it was her only hope.","When Jing Yi walked in, Jing Zejun felt like she had been saved, but the next second, she worried again. How could Jing Yi, also a young woman, possibly stand up to the burly investor?","What followed was a one-sided beating—a side of Jing Yi Jing Zejun had never seen before, all for her sake.","Later, her brothers arrived.","Jing Zejun instinctively wanted to hide because she knew what they would say.","And indeed, it was her fault. Her repeated refusals had led her into danger.","Was she being too pretentious? Now that she was a wealthy heiress, why was she still clinging to her dream of becoming a famous actress through hard work?","Why reject her family’s goodwill when she could have everything handed to her?","Even those who knew her identity were saying the same thing.","Jing Zejun could predict that once her identity was revealed, most people would think the same way.","Her brothers were indeed furious, even asking her why she refused to accept their help.","She felt guilty and even thought about giving up. After all, her dream of becoming an actress couldn’t compare to the family she had just regained.","But once again, Jing Yi stood by her side. Jing Yi understood her feelings and knew that all she wanted was to fulfill her dream of being “Jing Zejun, the actress.”","Call her naive or foolish, but she just wanted to try once—to see if the name Jing Zejun could be heard by more people.","At least she had Jing Yi’s support, and that was enough.","Jing Yi was different. She had family, a lover, and friends.","But only Jing Yi could give her the sense of security she needed.","They got along much better than anyone expected. When the truth about the “real and fake heiress” came out, Jing Zejun was anxious, eager to prove Jing Yi’s worth to everyone.","Her brothers also did their best to come up with a plan, but Jing Yi remained as calm as if nothing had happened.","Perhaps it was Jing Yi’s calm demeanor that helped her settle down, though she still felt the need to clarify things.","Before going on the variety show, Jing Zejun only wanted to clear up the misunderstandings about Jing Yi, but that period turned out to be the most peaceful and happiest time for her.","Many years later, viewers were still watching that show, and she occasionally revisited it herself.","She saw the viewers’ teasing comments about her and Wen Qingyan.","Back then, she didn’t know how to race cars—even go-karting was her first time. She was afraid she might lose control and crash, as the speed seemed too fast.","Wen Qingyan came over and gave her a lot of advice. She was grateful to this senior in the entertainment industry, but her nervousness made it hard for her to fully absorb his words.","Then, Jing Yi arrived.","People said that what Jing Yi told her wasn’t much different from what Wen Qingyan had said, and they teased her about how her demeanor changed instantly.","Occasionally, Wen Qingyan would see those comments, his eyes filled with amusement and a hint of hidden grievance. She felt guilty but had to admit it.","She admitted that just seeing Jing Yi made her feel at ease—a sense of security that even her now-husband, Wen Qingyan, couldn’t surpass.","Later, she gradually came to understand Jing Yi’s passion for racing.","Perhaps Jing Yi wasn’t aware of it, but Jing Zejun knew that racing wasn’t just a simple hobby for Jing Yi.","Jing Yi loved it like a cherished possession she couldn’t bear to touch—or perhaps, something she couldn’t touch.","Jing Yi once said that a racer’s hands on the wheel would waver if they were afraid of something.","At that moment, Jing Zejun understood why Jing Yi was reluctant to pursue it. Jing Yi was afraid—afraid of her family’s worries, and those worries were the chains that held her back.","Jing Yi cared deeply about their family.","Though she always seemed detached, she was always the first to step in when danger arose.","Whether it was their mother, Jing Zejun, their second brother, or Hengjing, Jing Yi was always there.","Even her beloved racing had to take into account her family’s feelings.","Jing Yi, there’s only one thing I wish for you: that your desire to live freely and boldly outweighs your worries.","Later, Jing Yi seemed to face a dilemma, and those chains seemed to tighten again.","Jing Zejun could see how much Jing Yi loved Shen Huaichu, so she was deeply concerned when Jing Yi mentioned giving up.","Giving up always comes with pain, and it’s even more painful when the choices on both sides are equally beautiful.","On one side was Jing Yi’s rediscovered passion for racing, and on the other was Shen Huaichu, whom Jing Yi loved deeply.","No matter which side she chose, Jing Yi would suffer. During that time, Jing Zejun even wished that the choices weren’t so evenly balanced, so that Jing Yi’s pain might be less.","But she had seen the joy in Jing Yi’s eyes when she rediscovered racing and the smile on her face when she talked about Shen Huaichu.","Fortunately, in the end, Jing Yi didn’t have to give up anything, because Shen Huaichu resolved the issue that stemmed from himself.","Jing Zejun breathed a sigh of relief.","Later, Jing Yi attended Jing Zejun’s Best Actress award ceremony, and Jing Zejun went to watch Jing Yi win the GT Super Cup Finals.","They lived so close to each other that a short walk was all it took to visit one another.","No one talked about the “real and fake heiress” anymore. Instead, they marveled at how they must have been sisters in a past life."]},{"number":261,"title":"Chapter 261: Jing Zeyou Side Story: I Will Forever Be the Guarantee of Her Prosperous Later Life","paragraphs":["Jing Zeyou only found out later that his grandmother had brought back a granddaughter.","By the time he learned of it, the girl had already gone abroad with his grandmother and had been raised overseas ever since.","Unlike Jing Zeqian, who was furious and resentful, Jing Zeyou didn’t see the girl’s arrival as a significant event.","From a young age, he knew he bore the responsibility for the Jing Family and Hengjing. As long as he didn’t acknowledge her, no one could take away what belonged to Jing Zejun.","In his youth, Jing Zeyou often visited his grandmother abroad with his father, yet he never once saw the girl, which surprised him.","His father had mentioned getting to know her, as so many years had passed, and calmness had eventually overcome anger. After all, the little girl was not at fault.","But his grandmother had always refused. Now, looking back, perhaps both they and Jing Yi should be grateful to her, as it might have prevented a much worse first meeting.","It was during the time of his grandmother’s passing that he first met Jing Yi.","At the time, she appeared well-behaved, fitting the image of an ‘adopted daughter’ perfectly—unassuming, obedient, and sensible.","However, he had come across records of her active achievements abroad, which suggested she was far from ordinary.","If he hadn’t heard her inner thoughts, he might have believed that.","That first meeting left a deep impression on him. She was visibly heartbroken, inside and out. After recovering slightly, she took a moment to silently admire his appearance.","When his father suggested bringing her back, Jing Zeyou was initially hesitant.","But Jing Yi was shrouded in too many mysteries, and someone like her was safer kept close.","Watching her lament her affluent yet lonely future on the plane, Jing Zeyou found it both amusing and guilt-inducing.","She genuinely didn’t want to return, but he couldn’t let someone like her remain unsupervised.","At the very least, he needed to figure out what had caused her transformation and why he could hear her thoughts.","Later, none of these questions were answered, and Jing Yi only grew more intriguing to him.","She had some peculiar hobbies, like sunbathing while fully covered, enjoying car racing, and practicing martial arts.","Though she always seemed detached, it was she who discovered his mother’s illness, Junjun’s danger, and even Zeqian’s troubles.","That incident had indeed angered him—both at Jing Zeqian and himself.","The Wang Family had always targeted Hengjing, and their focus on Jing Zeqian was ultimately because of him. He had underestimated their petty schemes, which had endangered his family.","Jing Zeyou valued his family deeply and would always stand in front of them when danger arose.","But one day, Jing Yi declared that she would be the one to shield them.","That was unacceptable. Even if he had brought her back with some intentions, none of them included putting her in harm’s way.","“Big brother, how do you know I don’t want to become the sharpest blade of the Jing Family?”","At that moment, Jing Zeyou felt both ashamed and awestruck.","When Jing Yi first arrived, they had never truly given her anything. Even their kindness was superficial. If she had remained aloof, he wouldn’t have felt this way.","But her heart was just too soft.","Because of this, he always wanted to protect her a little more.","Shen Huaichu wasn’t the ideal match. His sister deserved the best—someone who was considerate, capable, gentle, and deeply in love with her.","Jing Zeyou thought about it a lot but knew such a person might not exist. Even if they did, he would have to thoroughly investigate their motives.","Perhaps it was fate, but the two ended up together.","Soon, his fears came true, but before Shen Huaichu could find a solution, Jing Yi was involved in an accident.","That night, he stood outside the hospital room, looking at Jing Yi lying there, lifeless.","His heart was filled with fear and regret.","He overheard Shen Xi’s words: “If I had known you’d face so many troubles after returning, I would never have wished so eagerly to see you again.”","On that variety show, he had asked Jing Yi if she would still board the plane if she could do it all over again.","Jing Yi said she would.","The joy he felt then was matched only by the sorrow he felt now, standing outside her hospital room.","Their relationship had grown close so quickly, as if they were always meant to be family.","But if becoming family meant she would lie motionless in a hospital bed,","he wished he had never met her.","Perhaps the heavens heard their prayers and returned Jing Yi to them. They could no longer hear her inner thoughts, as if everything had returned to normal, and the weight on his heart finally lifted.","Later, Jing Yi became the champion of the Super Cup, standing in the place of the previous legend.","His little sister had grown up, step by step, to stand in a position bright enough to dazzle the world. Her love for racing had become a treasure she could boast about for a lifetime.","His little sister had indeed grown up, even knowing to propose in a significant setting.","He was a little displeased, though not as visibly as Jing Zeqian, but he was still deeply reluctant to let her go.","Even if she would only live a few steps away in a villa after marriage, it felt the same.","He had always found Jing Yi extraordinary. He prided himself on being someone who hid his emotions well, yet she seemed to sense them almost immediately.","That day, she lay outside the manor, sunbathing, still fully covered.","Another lounge chair was beside her, and when she saw him approaching, she wasn’t surprised at all, her voice lazy.","“Big brother, come on, I’ve been waiting for you to join me.”","He smiled and obediently lay down on the chair Jing Yi had prepared for him.","Jing Yi fell silent, and he thought she had really just called him over to sunbathe.","“Big brother, you know what? You’re the person I admire most in this world.”","Jing Zeyou was slightly taken aback, a smile tugging at his lips as he gazed at the warm, gentle sunlight. “Why bring this up so suddenly?”","Jing Yi’s voice remained lazy. “Because the person I admire most is incomparable to anyone else.”","“So, big brother, don’t act like I’m leaving the family, okay? That would make me really sad.”","At the time, he was both amused and exasperated. “Who said getting married means leaving the family? Whether you marry or not, you’re still a child of the Jing Family, my little sister.”","She seemed satisfied with this, the dimples on her cheeks deepening.","“It’s settled then. Even after I get married, I’m still going to cling to you all. You promised to take care of my affluent life for the rest of my days.”","“It’s settled.”","The sunlight that day was truly comforting, just like the first time he had sunbathed with Jing Yi.","Later, as Jing Yi had said, their relationship didn’t change much.","The only difference was that the family had grown a little larger."]},{"number":262,"title":"Chapter 262: If Line: When the Jing Family Travels to Jing Yi's World 01","paragraphs":["The warm sunlight filtered through the windows of the orphanage, casting a gentle glow on a little girl.","The girl sat alone by the window, her hair tied into two adorable buns. She gazed quietly at the world outside, her eyes reflecting a calmness that seemed beyond her years.","\"Jing Yi.\"","An elderly voice broke the silence.","The girl turned her head and flashed a bright smile, \"Grandma!\" She hurried over to support the approaching old woman.","This was the Grandma of the orphanage, the matriarch of this small haven and Jing Yi's only family.","Grandma lovingly patted her small hand and allowed herself to be guided to a seat by Jing Yi.","Jing Yi stood obediently beside her, her almond-shaped eyes sparkling with liveliness. \"Grandma, did you need me for something?\"","The old woman's smile softened, and her aged eyes carried a hint of reluctance. \"It's about your parent-teacher meeting tomorrow...\"","The orphanage was managed only by her and her daughter. She had originally arranged for her daughter to attend, but her daughter suddenly had to work overtime tomorrow, leaving her to stay and watch over the orphanage.","After all, the orphanage wasn't just home to Jing Yi.","Jing Yi was momentarily taken aback, a flicker of disappointment crossing her eyes, but it vanished almost instantly. She continued to smile sweetly.","\"It's okay, Grandma. The meeting won't be about anything important anyway. If the teacher says anything, I'll just relay it to you later. Oh, by the way, the teacher praised me for improving my grades last time. Let me tell you about it...\"","Jing Yi deftly changed the subject.","She understood. Grandma was busy, taking care of the other children. She wasn't just Jing Yi's Grandma.","It seemed like tomorrow would bring yet another round of teasing from her classmates.","Under the sunlight, Jing Yi chatted with her kind-hearted Grandma, both of them smiling, though their smiles seemed strained.","In a primary school classroom, desks and chairs were neatly arranged, and a notice about the parent-teacher meeting was written on the blackboard. The meeting began as scheduled.","The classroom buzzed with excitement as students eagerly shared stories of school life and academic progress with their parents.","But all of this had nothing to do with Jing Yi. She began packing up her things, accustomed to leaving early.","The teacher approached her and gently patted her head, comforting her, \"Jing Yi, don't be sad. Even though your parents aren't here, they must love you dearly from wherever they are. I know you're a strong child, and you've been doing exceptionally well in school. The teachers and classmates all like you very much...\"","This wasn't the first time Jing Yi had heard these words. She was grateful to the teacher, as it was one of the few kind remarks she ever received.","But why did people always assume that parents must love their children? Had the teacher forgotten?","She was an orphan.","Honestly, it didn't bother her much. Unlike her classmates who had to wait for the meeting to end, she could return to the orphanage early and help Grandma with the chores.","But Jing Yi couldn't say this to the teacher. It would only elicit more pity. She smiled politely, thanked the teacher, and continued packing her things after the teacher turned to attend to other parents.","\"Sweetie, who's that little girl? She's quite cute.\"","\"That's Jing Yi, the orphan in our class.\"","\"An orphan? That's so sad. Does that mean no one came for her parent-teacher meeting?\"","\"Yeah, even when her Grandma came before, she was asking about it...\"","Jing Yi sighed softly. How many times would she have to hear the same things?","The sky had turned a deep orange, the setting sun casting its final glow.","Jing Yi slung her backpack over her shoulders and prepared to leave the school grounds. She felt a bit nervous, wondering if the others would tone down their teasing after the parent-teacher meeting.","Lost in thought, she quickened her pace toward the school gate.","But, as usual, fate wasn't on her side.","Jing Yi stopped in her tracks, her eyes wary as she faced the group of classmates blocking her path.","These were the classmates the teacher claimed \"all liked her.\"","\"Jing Yi, why are you leaving so early? Isn't it parent-teacher meeting time?\"","A few boys, who others said \"liked\" her, were teasing her.","But Jing Yi hated this kind of \"like.\"","She remained silent, her round almond eyes filled with caution.","\"Don't you remember? Jing Yi doesn't have parents! She was picked up from the orphanage!\" one of the boys behind her shouted loudly, as if ensuring everyone nearby could hear.","\"But didn't she say her Grandma would come?\"","\"I checked. Her Grandma didn't show up! Her seat was empty. No one came for her.\"","\"She's a liar! Jing Yi is a liar!\"","\"Let's tell the others not to play with the liar tomorrow!\"","The boys laughed mockingly. Jing Yi tightened her grip on her backpack strap, trying to slip past them, but they blocked her way.","\"You're not going anywhere!\"","One of the boys grabbed her backpack. Jing Yi felt a mix of helplessness and fear.","She forced herself to stay calm. \"Let go, or I'll tell your parents!\"","But the boys weren't intimidated. \"Go ahead! At most, we'll just say sorry. Big deal.\"","This wasn't the first time. Whether she told the teacher or their parents, it always ended with an apology. Nothing more.","They yanked her backpack off and rummaged through it, scattering her belongings on the ground.","Jing Yi was pushed to the ground by the group.","...","\"Bro, where is this place?\"","Jing Zeqian followed closely behind Jing Zeyou, feeling uneasy as he looked at the unfamiliar surroundings.","After waking up, Jing Zeqian found himself in this strange place with Jing Zeyou. Everything was unfamiliar, and to make matters worse, both he and his brother seemed to have regressed in age!","When he first saw Jing Zeyou, who looked no older than twenty, he was as shocked as if he'd seen a ghost.","Then he looked in the mirror and realized he himself looked like a high school student.","Jing Zeyou calmly observed the buildings around them. The architectural style was very different from that of North River. This place resembled a small town in a third-tier city.","\"I don't know either.\"","Jing Zeyou was just as puzzled by this strange turn of events. He decided to explore the area to see if they could contact anyone.","The two stopped at the entrance of a primary school. It was dismissal time, but there weren't many people around. Instead, a group of students stood at the gate, talking about something.","Jing Zeyou didn't pay much attention and was about to walk in another direction when, out of the corner of his eye, he noticed a little girl on the ground. She had her hair in two buns and was sitting there, her eyes filled with defiance.","Jing Zeqian also looked over, his brow furrowing. A group of boys surrounding a little girl didn't seem like a good situation."]},{"number":263,"title":"Chapter 263: If Line: When the Jing Family Travels to Jing Yi's World 02","paragraphs":["Jing Yi silently picked up the things they had thrown on the ground.","They didn’t seem satisfied. “There’s nothing decent here! No money, not even anything valuable!”","Finally, her backpack was tossed onto the ground as well.","A little boy stepped forward and kicked away the book Jing Yi was about to pick up. “Hey, liar!”","“Liar! Jing Yi is a liar!”","“The unwanted liar! The unwanted liar! The unwanted liar!”","Behind her, Jing Zeyou suddenly turned his gaze to the girl on the ground, his expression changing abruptly.","What did they just call her?","Jing Zeqian had initially thought to help the little girl being bullied, but when he heard them calling her “Jing Yi, the liar,” his mind went blank.","Instinctively, he pushed the surrounding kids aside and stood in front of Jing Yi. “What’s going on here?!”","Jing Zeyou quickly walked over, intending to help Jing Yi up, but she dodged his hand.","He crouched down, looking at Jing Yi’s young face, a flicker of surprise in his eyes.","Her eyes... they looked so much like Jing Yi’s.","Jing Zeyou’s throat felt dry. “What’s your name?”","Jing Yi studied the person in front of her. He was a very handsome older brother, but the wariness in her eyes didn’t fade, even though these two seemed to want to help her.","“...Jing Yi.”","Hearing this, Jing Zeqian’s face showed disbelief. He leaned in and asked urgently, “Which ‘Yi’?!”","Jing Yi found these two people a bit strange and instinctively took half a step back, whispering, “The ‘Yi’ from ‘the beginning.’”","‘Grandma named me Jing Yi, the ‘Yi’ from ‘the beginning,’ hoping I’d have a fresh start.’","‘Liar! Jing Yi is a liar! The unwanted liar!’","Jing Zeyou stared at Jing Yi, a dull ache spreading in his chest.","The moment he got his answer, Jing Zeqian’s expression turned icy. He turned and grabbed the two little boys who were cautiously hiding nearby.","“You were the ones bullying her, right?”","How dare they bully Jing Yi, his sister?!","The thought of such a thing happening to Jing Yi made Jing Zeqian’s anger almost uncontrollable.","“Let me go! Let me go!”","“Hey! What are you doing?!”","A school security guard ran over, demanding an explanation.","Jing Zeqian ignored him, still glaring at the group. “I’m asking, was it you who bullied her?!”","The boys were terrified, tears streaming down their faces as they sobbed, “We’re sorry, we’re sorry, we were just joking.”","The guard pointed his baton at Jing Zeqian, warning, “I’m telling you, let the kids go, or I’ll call the police!”","Jing Zeqian shot the man a furious look. “When they were bullying her, why didn’t you say anything about calling the police?”","The guard’s eyes shifted uneasily. Everyone at the school knew Jing Yi was an orphan. It was just a little teasing, and no parents would come to complain. Better to avoid trouble.","Jing Zeyou helped Jing Yi pick up her things from the ground, ignoring how Jing Zeqian was dealing with the situation. His eyes were gentle.","“I’m Jing Zeyou, your older brother. He’s Jing Zeqian, your second brother. Let me take you home, okay?”","Home?","Jing Yi stared blankly at the older brother in front of her, hesitating. “Are you trying to kidnap me?”","They were very handsome, but Grandma said that if someone wanted to take her away, they were probably kidnappers.","But he said he wanted to take her home...","Jing Zeyou was momentarily stunned, then smiled gently. “No, I can prove it to you later.” Jing Yi looked into his eyes and seemed to believe him.","“Are you going to adopt me, then?”","Jing Zeyou’s heart ached. He forced a smile, though it didn’t quite reach his eyes. “It’s not adoption. I’m your older brother, and you’re my sister. We’re already family.”","He didn’t like the word “adoption.” Not at all.","Jing Yi didn’t fully understand but obediently let him take her hand.","Jing Zeyou stood up, his expression darkening as he looked at the still-crying boys.","“Zeqian.”","Jing Zeqian issued a final warning. “This is the last time. If I ever see you bullying someone again!” He let go, and the two boys fell to the ground, scrambling to get away from him.","By then, the parent-teacher meeting had ended, and more people began to notice the commotion, including the parents of the boys.","They rushed over, shielding their children and angrily confronting Jing Zeqian.","Jing Yi felt uneasy. She had never been in a situation where parents came to complain.","What should she do? She couldn’t let Grandma have to deal with this!","Jing Zeyou noticed Jing Yi’s anxiety and leaned down to reassure her. “Don’t worry, Yiyi. Your brother will handle it.”","Perhaps it was the confidence in Jing Zeyou’s eyes that gave her strength. Jing Yi relaxed a little and stood quietly by his side.","“Who are you?! How dare you barge into our school?!”","“What kind of people are you, bullying children?!”","“Call the police! Call the police!”","Jing Zeqian wasn’t fazed. His sharp eyes gleamed with anger.","“Go ahead! Let’s see how your sons bullied our sister! Better yet, call some reporters and take pictures of these little brats. Let everyone see what a born troublemaker looks like!”","The parents hesitated. They knew their sons’ behavior, but usually, a quick apology was enough. Since when did this girl have someone backing her up?","“Who are you?”","Jing Zeyou stepped forward, still holding Jing Yi’s hand, his expression calm. “Jing Yi’s brothers.”","The parents exchanged glances. “Impossible. She’s an orphan. Where did these brothers come from?” One parent glanced at Jing Yi’s face and sneered, “Are you some brothers she picked up in an alley?”","Jing Zeyou’s cold gaze swept over them, and the parent involuntarily took a step back, trying to sound brave. “What? Can’t handle the truth?!”","Jing Zeqian rolled up his sleeves, ready to charge forward, but Jing Zeyou stopped him. Given their current situation, getting into a fight would only make things worse, especially with Jing Yi there.","The crowd around them grew larger, and the security guard, seeing the situation was out of control, quickly contacted the school administration. Even the principal arrived.","He was slightly out of breath but before he could ask what was happening, he caught sight of Jing Zeyou’s face.","His eyes widened in disbelief, and he rubbed them as if to confirm what he was seeing.","“Are you Jing Zeyou?” he asked, his voice tinged with excitement and disbelief.","The principal’s voice stood out, and Jing Zeyou frowned, looking in the direction of the sound.","Someone here recognized him?","“Yes, I am.”","Hearing the confirmation, the principal’s face lit up with excitement. He pushed through the crowd and hurried over.","He looked thrilled, wanting to shake Jing Zeyou’s hand, but the latter was holding Jing Yi’s hand in one hand and her backpack in the other.","The principal didn’t mind and retracted his hand.","“I never thought I’d see Mr. Jing here. What an honor! What an honor!”"]},{"number":264,"title":"Chapter 264: If Line: When the Jing Family Travels to Jing Yi's World 03","paragraphs":["The principal was just a school leader in a small town, with no real opportunity to know the president of the Hengjing Group. He had only happened to read about him in the news, given how prominent the man was.","From the principal’s words, Jing Zeyou gradually understood his identity in this world. It seemed there wasn’t much difference from his original identity, though he wondered if his parents and Junjun were here too.","Seeing the principal ramble on about trivial matters, Jing Zeyou interrupted him, “Principal, let’s save the small talk for another time. These parents mentioned calling the police. Could you help arrange that?”","He looked down at Yiyi, who was standing obediently by his side, and a softness flickered in his eyes. Now that his identity was clear, he preferred to handle things through formal channels.","The parents, noticing the principal’s deferential attitude toward Jing Zeyou, grew increasingly uneasy. When they heard he was serious about calling the police, they panicked.","“It’s a misunderstanding, just a misunderstanding! We were only worried about our children!”","“Yes, yes! Since Yiyi’s family is here, and we’re all in the same class, there’s no need for this!”","Seeing that Jing Zeyou and the others remained unmoved, one parent turned their attention to Jing Yi.","“Yiyi, you know we’ve always cared for you. Could you ask your brother to let this go? After all, you’re...”","Before she could finish, Jing Zeqian stepped forward, his expression fierce. “I’m warning you, keep your thoughts to yourself when it comes to her!”","The parent stumbled back, as if one more word would provoke Jing Zeqian to tear them apart.","Jing Zeyou shielded little Jing Yi, soothing her nervousness.","The principal, watching the tense standoff, felt a headache coming on. He hadn’t expected Jing Yi to be Jing Zeyou’s sister, let alone for her to be bullied in front of her family.","But he knew where his priorities lay. “Mr. Jing, rest assured, I’ll make sure you and Miss Jing are satisfied with the outcome.”","He gestured for the security guards to escort the parents away, ignoring the children’s cries and the parents’ shouts and curses. A few students were nothing compared to Jing Zeyou’s sister.","If necessary, he’d give up the entire school for this opportunity. He just couldn’t believe Jing Yi was Jing Zeyou’s sister! All these years, he’d wasted such a valuable connection!","The principal didn’t care why Jing Yi was related to Jing Zeyou, nor whether she was a biological sister or adopted. As long as Jing Zeyou acknowledged her, Jing Yi’s status as his ‘sister’ was solidified.","Seeing the greed and flattery in the principal’s eyes, Jing Zeyou’s gaze turned cold.","Little Jing Yi looked up at the unfamiliar principal, unsure of what to make of him. She’d never seen him like this before. Was this change because of the two older brothers?","They must be very important people.","Jing Yi lowered her head, staring at her slightly worn canvas shoes, lost in thought.","Jing Zeyou didn’t have time to waste on the principal. He crouched down and asked gently, “What’s wrong?” Jing Zeqian also stepped closer, a bittersweet smile tugging at his lips.","He didn’t want to scare Jing Yi, but he was heartbroken.","Jing Yi bit her lip, her eyes reddening as she looked up with determination. “I’m Jing Yi, not the ‘Miss Jing’ you’re talking about.”","She understood the principal’s words. That ‘Miss Jing’ sounded like someone pampered and privileged, like a precious jewel.","But she wasn’t that. She was Jing Yi, the child her mother had abandoned at an orphanage on a cold winter’s day.","Jing Zeyou felt a sharp pang in his chest. Jing Zeqian’s eyes reddened, and he was about to say something, but Jing Zeyou signaled him not to scare Jing Yi.","Still crouching in front of Jing Yi, with her little pink backpack on his back, Jing Zeyou spoke softly.","“I can’t explain everything right now, but you’re the person I’ve been looking for. Not some ‘Miss Jing,’ but my sister.”","Jing Yi stared at Jing Zeyou, who patiently explained, but she remained silent.","Jing Zeyou smiled and took her hand. “Just trust me for now, okay?”","“...Okay.”","Jing Zeyou gently ruffled her hair. “Good girl.”","He stood up and handed her over to Jing Zeqian, then went to discuss the matter of the other children with the principal. Jing Yi couldn’t stay at this school, but the withdrawal process would have to wait until he contacted the Jing family.","Jing Zeqian held Jing Yi’s hand tightly, his gaze fixed on her as if afraid she might slip away.","Jing Yi looked up at him and said earnestly, “I won’t run away.” So there was no need to hold her so tightly.","It took Jing Zeqian a few seconds to understand what she meant, and he quickly loosened his grip. “Sorry.” Jing Yi shook her head obediently. “It’s okay.”","This was the well-behaved Jing Yi he’d always dreamed of, but Jing Zeqian only felt more heartache and sorrow.","Jing Yi looked up again and asked, “Are you going to cry?”","Jing Zeqian quickly turned his head away, hiding his face. “No, I’m not.” Jing Yi knew adults didn’t like children seeing them cry, so she comforted him, “I know, it’s just the wind.”","Jing Zeqian’s heart ached even more. He quickly wiped the tears from the corners of his eyes and crouched down. “Jing Yi, I’m your second brother. If anyone ever bullies you, you have to fight back. I’ll stand up for you. If you can’t fight, we’ll learn martial arts together...”","Jing Zeqian paused. Did Jing Yi want to learn martial arts because of this?","Jing Yi’s round eyes lit up. “How did you know I wanted to learn martial arts?” She’d wanted to for a long time, but she didn’t have the money, so she kept the idea to herself.","Jing Yi was about to share her future dreams with Jing Zeqian, but for some reason, he looked like he was on the verge of tears again.","She panicked and used her small hands to wipe his tears. “Don’t cry! The wind is just too strong today.” Jing Zeqian couldn’t help but laugh and gently hugged her. “Yes, the wind is too strong.”","Jing Zeyou walked over to see Jing Zeqian both crying and laughing. “What’s going on?”","Jing Zeqian quickly wiped his tears and stood up. “Nothing. Is everything settled?” Jing Zeyou nodded. “First, we’ll see if we can contact our parents, then we’ll go to the orphanage with Jing Yi.”","Jing Zeyou took Jing Yi’s other hand and was about to leave the school when he noticed the hesitation on her face.","“What is it, Yiyi?”","Jing Yi seemed to struggle with her words, clutching her uniform nervously. “Could you... come to my parent-teacher meeting?” She wanted to know what it felt like to have someone attend a meeting for her.","The moment Jing Zeqian heard this, he couldn’t hold back. He picked her up and rushed toward the school building.","They’d go! They had to go! Right now! They could stay for days if needed!","Jing Zeyou, realizing what had happened, shook his head with a wry smile and hurried after them."]},{"number":265,"title":"Chapter 265: Alternate Timeline: When the Jing Family Enters Jing Yi's World 04","paragraphs":["Amidst a whirlwind of chaos, Jing Zeqian and the others finally located Jing Yi's classroom. Fortunately, the teacher was still inside, overseeing the other students as they tidied up their desks and chairs. Upon seeing Jing Zeyou and the others, she was momentarily stunned. She had just heard about the commotion at the school gate and hadn’t expected these two to show up. Her heart skipped a beat, knowing that even the principal treated them with great respect.","Jing Yi’s eyes sparkled as she pulled the two over, “Teacher, these are my two older brothers. They’re here for the parent-teacher meeting!”","Jing Zeyou and Jing Zeqian felt a pang of emotion, their gazes softening as they looked at Jing Yi.","“...Parent-teacher meeting?”","Jing Zeyou stepped forward, his tone gentle, “Hello, I’m Jing Yi’s eldest brother. We were delayed by some matters, so we’re a bit late for the meeting.”","The teacher looked even more bewildered, staring at the man who could easily pass for a movie star. She instinctively replied, “No problem, no problem.”","Meanwhile, Jing Yi had already led Jing Zeqian to her seat.","“This is my spot!”","“Can you see well from so far back?”","“Of course! My eyesight is great.”","“Has your desk mate ever bullied you?”","“No, my desk mate is also a girl...”","The teacher felt a bit dazed. They truly seemed like parents attending a parent-teacher meeting, concerned about their child’s well-being at school and worried about any potential bullying.","“Teacher, could you please fill me in on Jing Yi’s performance at school?”","The teacher snapped out of her thoughts and naturally didn’t refuse. She began to explain Jing Yi’s academic progress to Jing Zeyou, just as she would with any other parent.","When it was over, the teacher watched Jing Yi’s retreating figure. It was the first time she had seen Jing Yi look so happy.","She held onto each of her brothers’ hands, her steps light and full of joy.","“...The teacher said your grades are good, but math is a bit of a weak point.”","“I didn’t do well in math this time. It’s so hard.”","“What’s there to fear? Your eldest brother was the top scorer in the college entrance exam back in the day. He’ll teach you, and you’ll get it in no time.”","“Really? Eldest brother is amazing!”","“Hey, I’m pretty great too!”","“Alright, alright, second brother is also amazing.”","...","Jing Zeyou managed to contact Jing Beicheng and his wife, who were with Jing Zejun in North River.","They had experienced the same strange phenomenon, though everything around them remained largely unchanged, except that they had become much younger.","They had also been searching for Jing Zeyou and the others and were overjoyed to hear that Jing Zeyou had found Jing Yi.","Lin Ruiqing and Jing Zejun even wanted to come and pick up Jing Yi themselves, but Jing Zeyou refused.","He was worried that meeting too many family members at once might make Jing Yi uncomfortable. It was better to let her adjust gradually, especially since they would all be returning home eventually.","After hanging up the phone, Jing Zeyou looked over at the two by the roadside. Jing Zeqian was playing with Jing Yi.","It was a bit heartbreaking. He had made the call not only to reassure his parents and Jing Zejun but also to ask for money. Both he and Jing Zeqian were completely penniless.","Otherwise, Jing Zeyou wouldn’t have had to leave Jing Yi waiting by the roadside.","“Let’s go, it’s time to eat.”","Jing Zeqian’s face lit up with surprise, “Brother, is everything settled?”","When had the young master of the Jing family ever been in such a situation—without a cent to his name, unable to even treat his sister to a meal at McDonald’s or KFC!","“It’s settled.”","Jing Yi, holding Jing Zeyou’s hand, looked up and said, “Actually, we could go back to the orphanage to eat.” She had noticed the awkwardness on her brothers’ faces, but it didn’t matter—she didn’t have any money either.","At this, Jing Yi’s expression turned hesitant, “But the orphanage doesn’t take in kids as old as you.” With nearly ten years of ‘seniority’ at the orphanage, she might be able to exchange it for a meal.","However, children at the orphanage were usually expected to fend for themselves by the age of fifteen or sixteen. As for someone as old as her brothers...","Jing Yi’s face grew more troubled.","She was thinking about how she could support her brothers.","Jing Zeyou found her serious expression amusing, “Jing Yi, your eldest brother can take care of himself.” Jing Zeqian, not wanting to be underestimated, quickly added, “I can too! I can even take care of you.”","Jing Yi looked at them with a mix of belief and doubt.","She didn’t seem to fully grasp their plans. Jing Zeyou crouched down, carefully choosing his words to soften the impact.","“Jing Yi, we’re going back to the orphanage to let your grandma know. Remember what I told you before? You have parents and a sister waiting for you, so...”","Jing Zeyou couldn’t bring himself to continue, as Jing Yi’s happy expression slowly faded.","It dawned on her that while she was gaining family, she was also losing her grandma.","Jing Yi’s eyes welled up with tears, which soon began to fall in large drops.","Jing Zeqian was both heartbroken and panicked, “Brother! Why did you have to tell her so soon?!”","Jing Zeyou wrapped his arms around her, gently patting her back as she sobbed into his shoulder.","Jing Yi wasn’t an ordinary child. She understood what gaining new family members meant, but in the excitement, she had momentarily forgotten.","Jing Zeyou knew this, which is why he didn’t try to sugarcoat it.","From every angle, taking Jing Yi to North River was the best option. The only issue was the grandma who had raised her.","Jing Yi, still crying on his shoulder, managed to choke out, “Will I... will I still be able to see Grandma?” Jing Zeyou continued to pat her back, softly replying, “Of course. You can visit her anytime you miss her.”","After all, the Jing family had the means to make it happen.","What followed was a natural progression. They went to the orphanage.","...","The grandma at the orphanage was shocked to learn that Jing Yi had brought back a family to adopt her. Her expression was tinged with wariness.","However, the evidence Jing Zeyou presented was too detailed, and his demeanor was far from that of a suspicious character.","In the end, it was her daughter who recognized Jing Zeyou and showed her the online reports, finally dispelling her doubts.","It was for the best. She couldn’t possibly provide the same level of care for every child.","For Jing Yi to be adopted by such a family was a blessing.","It was for the best.","“...The funds will be transferred next week. Please don’t refuse. Hengjing has a dedicated charity organization, and they will bring over detailed plans for the support. Everything will be done in full compliance.”","The grandma looked at Jing Zeyou, his features calm and noble, his demeanor sincere. He even treated her with the respect due to an elder.","“...And as for Jing Yi, you’re welcome to visit her at the Jing family anytime. The contact information I gave your daughter is my personal number. You can reach me at any time.”","“...Jing Yi will also visit you often. Once she’s settled, I’ll have her contact you.” The grandma’s eyes glistened with tears, her face full of love and years of hardship. “Alright, then I’ll leave Jing Yi in your care.”","Jing Zeyou slightly bowed, “You’re too kind. She’s already our family. This is just a reunion.” Jing Zeqian quickly followed with a slight bow of his own.","The grandma thought it was because Jing Zeyou held Jing Yi in such high regard.","Jing Yi left the orphanage, the place she had called home for ten years.","That day, she cried heavily in Jing Zeyou’s arms."]},{"number":266,"title":"Chapter 266: If Line: When the Jing Family Travels to Jing Yi's World 05","paragraphs":["The plane was a bit bumpy. Jing Zeyou glanced at Jing Yi beside him and gently tucked her in. Her eyes were still slightly swollen.","Jing Zeqian approached, and Jing Zeyou signaled him to talk in the rest area. Before getting up, he took one last look at the sleeping Jing Yi and quietly walked out.","Jing Zeqian looked like he had just \"come back to life,\" lazily leaning on the sofa.","Everything that had happened in the past two days had drained all his energy.","\"Brother, what are we going to say when we get back?\" Jing Zeyou poured himself a glass of red wine and swirled it casually.","\"Say about what?\"","Jing Zeqian reached out his hand, clearly asking for something. Jing Zeyou, as usual, handed over what he was holding.","\"Of course, about Jing Yiyi's identity? Don’t let there be another rumor about a fake heiress like before.\"","Jing Zeyou glanced at him, \"I remember, back then, someone didn’t even want her to have the title of 'fake heiress.'\"","Jing Zeqian seemed to bristle, sitting up straight abruptly, almost spilling the wine in his hand. \"Brother! Don’t bring up old wounds like that!\" How long was this going to be brought up? Couldn’t they just chalk it up to his youthful ignorance?","Jing Zeyou smiled faintly and downed his glass of wine in one go. \"We’ll say what needs to be said. Since when does the Jing Family care about what others think?\"","As long as they stood firm, no matter who it was, they’d have to accept that Jing Yi was the Jing Family’s heiress.","Jing Zeqian raised an eyebrow. Arrogant enough—just the way he liked it!","\"However, I think you should start thinking about your own problems now.\"","Jing Zeqian moved the glass away from his lips, puzzled. \"What problems?\" Jing Zeyou studied the person in front of him. \"Don’t you think you look like a high school student right now?\"","Jing Zeqian wasn’t aware, but Jing Zeyou knew his appearance all too well.","Jing Zeqian paused, then gasped, frantically looking for a mirror to check his reflection.","He couldn’t accept it. \"No way! I should’ve graduated by now, right?!\" Please tell me I’m not stuck in my senior year of high school!","Jing Zeyou remained calm, pouring himself another glass of wine, leisurely watching his brother, who looked like he’d just stepped on a tail.","Jing Zeqian slumped on the sofa, muttering, \"This is bad. Am I really going to have to go through it all over again? Brother, hurry and tell Dad I know what I’m doing. There’s no need for me to relive it.\"","Jing Zeqian had genuinely gone through three years of high school, but he’d been severely unbalanced in his studies, with math and science almost completely eluding him.","The thought of going through it again made him feel utterly defeated.","Jing Zeyou seemed to agree, swirling his wine glass. \"That makes sense, but what if Jing Yi asks?\" He watched as Jing Zeqian immediately became alert, a hint of amusement in his eyes. \"What if she asks why Second Brother doesn’t have to go to school? What if she asks about your grades?\"","As if that wasn’t enough, he added, \"What if she asks you elementary school questions and you can’t answer them?\" He even emphasized the word \"elementary.\"","Seeing the despair growing in his brother’s eyes, Jing Zeyou smiled. \"Alright, I’m just teasing you. You’ll just have to stay at school a bit longer to look after your two sisters.\"","Jing Zeqian didn’t have to go to school, but his sisters still did. Nothing made for a safer school life than having an older brother as a \"bodyguard\" at the same school.","...","Little Jing Yi had just recovered from the shock of riding a private jet.","Her big brother had told her this was a private jet that could take her to the orphanage. Whenever she missed her grandma, she could just say the word and they’d go—quick and easy.","Little Jing Yi was happy. When she had a break, she could go back to see her grandma! That way, she could have her family without having to give up her grandma!","But there was still one thing troubling her.","Her big brother had said her parents and sister were waiting for her. She didn’t know if they’d like her, or if it would be better not to call them Mom and Dad right away.","Hearing Jing Yi’s thoughts, Jing Zeqian immediately said, \"Of course not! They’ve been waiting for you for so long. If they don’t hear you call them Mom and Dad, they’ll be heartbroken!\"","Jing Zeqian spoke earnestly, and Jing Yi seemed to understand, her round eyes peeking at Jing Zeqian. \"Like when Second Brother cries?\" That did seem pretty sad.","Jing Zeqian paused, looking a bit uncomfortable. \"That wasn’t crying! It was just windy!\"","Jing Yi nodded understandingly. She knew how to be considerate of adults.","Jing Zeyou, standing nearby, smiled, while Jing Zeqian just wanted to move past the topic.","\"Anyway, just remember they’re your parents, and they’ll definitely like you as much as I do!\"","Little Jing Yi’s nervousness eased a bit, but as they approached the Jing Family home, those feelings resurfaced.","The wealthiest people she’d ever seen were the kids who used to bully her. They had cars to pick them up and lived in fancy neighborhoods.","But even they didn’t have private jets or such a big mansion.","Little Jing Yi instinctively held onto Jing Zeyou, as if that would make her feel safer.","Lin Ruiqing and Jing Beicheng, now decades younger, along with Jing Zejun, were waiting at the entrance.","When Lin Ruiqing woke up, the first thing she saw was the young Jing Zejun, and tears immediately streamed down her face. Not being able to witness Jing Zejun’s growth had been her greatest regret.","She never thought that one day, that regret would be filled.","After the initial joy subsided, she began to worry about Jing Yi and the others who weren’t there yet. But soon, she received a call from Jing Zeyou.","She had wanted to go pick up Jing Yi herself, eager to see her youngest daughter, but after hearing Jing Zeyou’s reasoning, she decided against it.","For the first time in a long while, she felt nervous, constantly checking her outfit and Jing Zejun’s.","Jing Beicheng teased, \"Why are you so fidgety now that you’re younger?\" Lin Ruiqing shot her younger husband a glare. He seemed to have regained his youthful mindset, even finding time to tease her.","Jing Zejun held Lin Ruiqing’s hand and reassured her, \"Mom, don’t be too nervous. Otherwise, Jing Yi might get nervous too.\"","In truth, she was also a bit nervous. She hadn’t seen Jing Yi as a child before. She must be even cuter than she was when she grew up.","The three of them waited with anticipation until they saw Jing Yi, clinging tightly to Jing Zeyou, trying to appear calm but clearly frightened.","Jing Zejun finally saw Jing Yi as a child, and she was indeed adorable.","But her heart ached.","Jing Zejun walked up to Jing Yi, forcing a smile, her eyes red and filled with tenderness.","\"Jing Yi, welcome home.\""]},{"number":267,"title":"Chapter 267: If Line: When the Jing Family Travels to Jing Yi's World 06","paragraphs":["“Grandma, look, this is my room, and next door is my sister’s...”","Little Jing Yi excitedly held up her phone, showing her new room to the grandma from the orphanage. The room had been prepared in advance, but the overall style was finalized only after Jing Yi returned.","Most of the room’s arrangements were done with Jing Yi’s input, and she absolutely loved it.","In the video, the orphanage grandma smiled, the wrinkles at the corners of her eyes deepening. It was clear that Little Jing Yi had found a family who truly cared for her.","To be honest, even now, she couldn’t quite figure out what the Jing Family saw in Little Jing Yi. She prayed and worried at the same time.","She feared that the Jing Family might have ulterior motives, and she also worried that Little Jing Yi might only share the good news and hide any troubles. But the joy on Jing Yi’s face seemed genuine.","“And this, this little table was picked out by Mom and Dad when they took me shopping...”","The grandma listened quietly as Little Jing Yi shared every detail of her life since returning to the Jing Family. Her aged eyes were filled with affection.","She needed to live a little longer, at least long enough to see Little Jing Yi enjoy more good days.","Most children in the orphanage were unfortunate, and like many others, Little Jing Yi had her share of misfortune, though hers was a bit different.","It wasn’t uncommon for children to be left at the orphanage’s doorstep. Most parents did so with a hint of pity; otherwise, these children might have been left in some forgotten corner.","Unnoticed, until they vanished from the world.","Little Jing Yi had also been left at the orphanage’s doorstep, but it was during a harsh winter, wrapped in a thin little quilt, placed there in the cold.","“Mom, do you see a child over there?”","The world outside was blanketed in snow, so bright it made the grandma’s eyes water. Her vision was already poor, and in such conditions, she could barely see.","She and her daughter supported each other as they walked over. The child was so cold that her cries were faint, almost inaudible.","The grandma took the child back, and fortunately, she survived—a healthy little girl.","She never hid this from Little Jing Yi. All the children in the orphanage had the right to know their origins. Only by knowing where they came from could they let go of their worries and move forward.","This was what made Little Jing Yi different. Even she couldn’t understand whether the person who left her there wanted her to live or not.","She thought this mystery would never be solved, but then she met that couple.","The news of Little Jing Yi being adopted by such a family couldn’t be kept quiet. After Jing Zeyou and the others left, the principal of the local elementary school was quickly replaced.","Now, everyone in town was talking about how Little Jing Yi had been adopted by a wealthy family.","The orphanage grandma had been focusing on taking care of the remaining children, as the Jing Family had donated a large sum of money, enough to provide a better and larger home for the kids.","She and her daughter were discussing these matters when the couple showed up.","“Who are you?”","The man was tall, scanning the orphanage with a calculating look in his eyes.","The woman was thin, her chin sharp. When she saw the orphanage grandma and her daughter, she seemed disappointed but also peered behind them, as if searching for someone.","“Hello, we are...”","The woman seemed hesitant, glancing at the man beside her. He spoke impatiently, “Did you have a girl adopted from here?”","The grandma’s daughter didn’t like their attitude. The man’s imposing figure made her instinctively shield the grandma, her eyes wary.","“This is an orphanage. It’s normal for children to be adopted. Who are you, and what do you want?”","Seeing their reaction, the woman quickly stepped in, her voice soft, “You’ve misunderstood. We’re here to find our daughter. You must have taken in a girl about seven or eight years ago, on the 25th of the twelfth lunar month, wrapped in a floral quilt...”","As the woman provided more details, the grandma’s heart grew heavier. Her daughter also realized who they were looking for.","The two exchanged a glance, their eyes filled with concern.","These were Little Jing Yi’s parents.","“Big Brother said I can start school next week with my sister, and we’ll be in the same class. Second Brother is also at that school...”","Little Jing Yi was still excitedly telling the grandma about everything that had happened since she returned. She didn’t notice the growing weight in the grandma’s expression.","“Oh, Grandma, Big Brother said I can visit you during the holidays. Mom and Dad have a big plane, so I can fly to see you. It’ll be so convenient!”","The grandma looked at Little Jing Yi with a warm smile. “Alright, I’ll be waiting for you, Yi Yi.” But as she watched Jing Yi’s joyful expression, her heart ached.","Her Little Jing Yi had only just started to enjoy a good life.","The grandma smiled, though her lips trembled slightly. “Yi Yi, is your Big Brother around?”","She couldn’t tell Little Jing Yi; she was still just a child. She could only hope that the young man would handle this matter properly.","Little Jing Yi nodded obediently. “Yes, Big Brother is probably in his study. Do you need to talk to him, Grandma?” The grandma nodded with a smile. “There’s something I need to discuss with him. Could you ask if he has time?”","“Sure!”","Little Jing Yi climbed down from the sofa and headed to Jing Zeyou’s study with the phone in hand.","Just as she reached the door, she ran into Jing Zeqian, who was coming out. He crouched down and scooped her up.","“What’s up? Are you looking for Second Brother? Where do you want to go today?”","Before Little Jing Yi could explain that she was looking for Jing Zeyou, Jing Zeqian had already thrown out several suggestions. “How about the water park? Or should we sign you up for martial arts first? Or maybe bumper cars?”","Little Jing Yi shook her head seriously. “Second Brother, I’m not a little kid anymore. Besides, I’ll be starting school soon, so I need to focus on studying. And I’m here to bring Grandma to talk to Big Brother.”","She waved the phone, and the kind old woman on the screen smiled at him.","Jing Zeqian’s smile froze. “Hello!” Oh no, would she think he wasn’t mature enough?","He obediently led her inside, but as soon as Little Jing Yi handed the phone over, she pulled him back out.","After closing the door, Little Jing Yi motioned for Jing Zeqian to lean in closer.","He crouched down. “What’s up? Don’t you want to hear what Grandma and Big Brother are talking about?” Little Jing Yi shook her head and whispered, “Second Brother, let’s go play bumper cars today.”","Jing Zeqian was stunned for a moment, then burst into laughter, startling Little Jing Yi, who nearly covered his mouth, her eyes darting toward the study door.","“Second Brother, Big Brother and Grandma are discussing something important!”","“Well, well, Jing Yi Yi, weren’t you just talking about focusing on your studies?”","Little Jing Yi felt a little guilty. Grandma always said she should study hard no matter what, but she hadn’t even started school yet! And there were so many fun things she hadn’t tried.","Jing Zeqian laughed and ruffled her hair. “Alright! After lunch, we’ll go out and play! Bumper cars it is!”","“And Sister too.”","“Yes, and Sister too.”"]},{"number":268,"title":"Chapter 268: If Line: When the Jing Family Travels to Jing Yi's World 07","paragraphs":["In the study, Jing Zeyou listened as the grandmother from the orphanage spoke about the couple, his expression gradually darkening.","\"Do you think they have ulterior motives?\"","In the video call, the grandmother hesitated for a moment. They might be Jing Yi's biological parents, and she shouldn't speculate like this, but their behavior left her no choice.","If they had been more discreet, she wouldn't have come to Jing Zeyou for help.","\"They only said they wanted to see Jing Yi, but they also asked for your address. I thought it couldn't be that simple, so I brushed them off and came to ask you.\"","She hoped the couple was just trying to deceive them. If they were truly Jing Yi's parents, what would happen to the child?","Over the years, she had seen many parents come to reclaim their children. If their intentions were genuine, she didn't mind them taking the child back after leaving them at the orphanage.","After all, giving those children a home was a good thing. But this couple didn't seem to be here for Jing Yi.","They hardly asked about Jing Yi, instead focusing on the family who had adopted her. Combined with the recent rumors in town about the Jing Family, she couldn't help but think deeper.","Jing Zeyou had never met Jing Yi's biological parents before, so after bringing Jing Yi home, he hadn't expected anyone to come looking for her.","Was it because their identity had been exposed?","He narrowed his eyes, thinking for a moment. \"It's fine. Give them the address. I'll handle it.\" First, he needed to figure out what they wanted.","As for Jing Yi, he wouldn't let them involve her.","A sharp glint flashed in Jing Zeyou's deep eyes.","The grandmother sighed, her tone heavy. \"This is troublesome.\" Jing Zeyou quickly shifted his gaze back, his voice respectful. \"You're too kind. This is what the Jing Family should do. I promised to protect Jing Yi.\"","The elderly woman's expression finally relaxed a little. She wasn't afraid of anything except the adoptive family growing tired of Jing Yi because of this matter.","...","In a small house in the town near the orphanage, a woman stood in the kitchen, snapping beans. Beside her was a middle-aged woman.","\"Third Aunt, are you sure the one who was adopted is my daughter?\"","The middle-aged woman added some water to the pot, her voice loud. \"Of course! Why else would I have you come all this way?\"","She even sounded a bit proud. \"Don't underestimate your Third Aunt. The girl is the same age as your daughter, and that orphanage is so run-down. There haven't been many children there over the years—it has to be her! I haven't seen her, but I'm almost certain!\"","She glanced out the window, then leaned closer to the woman, lowering her voice. \"Besides, you're not losing out. You have no idea about the family that adopted her. Their demeanor is extraordinary—even the school principal is wary of them. If it really is your daughter, you've hit the jackpot!\"","\"And did you hear? The family that bullied her was kicked out of school and even got a formal warning. Just imagine how powerful that family must be!\"","Even though she spoke softly, the excitement in her voice was undeniable.","She never imagined that her relative's child could have such a bright future. If she had known, she would have taken the girl in herself. A little girl wouldn't have eaten much.","But raising her in her own home probably wouldn't have led to such luck. It was better to leave her at the orphanage—no cost to them, and now they could benefit from her success!","The woman still hesitated, glancing at the man lying outside. He was lounging on the bed, humming a tune, seemingly in a good mood and not paying attention to them.","The woman lowered her voice further. \"But when I left her there, it was the middle of winter. I thought she wouldn't survive.\"","Back then, she and the man outside weren't married yet. They had no money for the hospital, and her family wouldn't help raise the child. She had to hide at the man's relative's house to give birth.","It was winter, and she had just given birth, unable to rest properly. Because it was a girl, the man disliked her even more, telling her to get rid of the child.","They had planned to leave for another province to work right after the birth, so she didn't have much time. She quickly bundled the child up and went out.","Luckily, there was an orphanage nearby. She didn't dare get too close, fearing someone might see her, so she left the child in a corner.","\"It's just fate. If you had been a boy, he might have taken you with him.\"","She tucked the thin blanket around the baby, then turned and ran off. It was almost time to catch the bus.","The middle-aged woman washed vegetables, water splashing from the faucet and soaking her clothes. Her mood remained cheerful.","\"Why worry about that? The girl was destined to survive. Besides, if she had died, wouldn't the orphanage have told you? Just relax and wait for your fortune. And don't forget your Third Aunt when the time comes!\"","\"Of course! If it weren't for you, we wouldn't have known about this from out of town.\"","The woman smiled, feeling a surge of joy. After all these years, she might finally become a wealthy lady. Ten years ago, she had left the child at the orphanage because they couldn't afford to feed her.","It was a pity for the child, but perhaps this was her destiny.","The adoptive family must be willing to give them some money, right? Everyone in town said they were very wealthy.","With that money, she could buy a bigger house, send Little Baby to a better school, and stop working so hard!","The woman handed the prepared beans to the middle-aged woman, then turned to her son, who had just bitten into an apple and thrown it on the ground.","She called out softly, her voice gentle, \"Little Baby, don't make a mess.\" The boy ignored her, continuing to rummage through the fruit bowl.","Not finding what he wanted, he pouted and tossed the rest of the fruit onto the floor.","The man outside opened his eyes lazily, glanced over, and then went back to humming and lying down.","\"Third Aunt, when will Third Uncle be back?\"","The middle-aged woman looked out the kitchen window, her brow furrowing briefly in displeasure.","This child really has no manners, does he?","She quickly smiled again. \"It's fine, it's fine. He's just a child! Let him play!\" Then she turned back to answer the woman. \"He's probably playing cards at Old Zhang's place. I called him earlier—he should be on his way back.\"","Seeing that the middle-aged woman didn't mind, the woman ignored her son.","Her thin face was filled with barely contained joy. \"I wonder how big the girl is now.\"","\"I heard she's grown into a graceful young lady. Why else would that family take her in?\"","\"That's good. It's a life of luxury.\"","\"Exactly. When she's wealthy, you won't have to work so hard anymore.\"","\"We don't matter much. It's mainly for her younger brother—he's still so young.\"","\"Don't worry. He's her brother—she'll definitely help him out.\""]},{"number":269,"title":"Chapter 269: If Line: When the Jing Family Travels to Jing Yi's World 08","paragraphs":["That evening, the Jing family held their first family meeting since the unexpected turn of events.","The teenage boy's face was dark and stormy, his voice low, as if afraid of disturbing his two younger sisters playing upstairs.","\"What a load of crap! Jing Yiyi is a Jing! A member of the Jing family! What kind of fraudsters are these?!\"","No one had come forward to claim Jing Yiyi as their biological daughter before, so why now, just days after he brought her home? What kind of nonsense was this?","Jing Beicheng's expression wasn't much better, his tone grave. \"Have you already looked into it?\"","He knew his eldest son's habits. If it were truly a scam, there would be no need for a family meeting.","The fact that it had come to this meant that the other party might indeed be Jing Yiyi's biological parents.","Jing Zeyou remained calm, his eyes reflecting a maturity beyond his years.","\"I've looked into it. The timing, location, and details all match what the woman said,\" he paused, \"If it comes to a DNA test, I don't want to hide it from Yiyi.\"","This step wasn't part of Jing Zeyou's plan. No matter what, he would deal with these two first.","Jing Zeqian suddenly stood up, his narrow eyes filled with wariness and displeasure. \"I don't care if it's true or not, Jing Yiyi isn't meeting them!\"","Lin Ruiqing frowned, her face filled with worry. After all, blood ties were stronger than anything.","Jing Beicheng patted his wife's hand and turned to his hot-tempered youngest son. \"Keep your voice down. Listen to your brother.\"","Jing Zeqian opened his mouth to argue but, seeing Jing Zeyou's calm demeanor, slowly settled down.","That's right. His brother wouldn't let this slide.","Jing Zeyou's lips curled into a faint smile, though it didn't reach his eyes. If the couple truly wanted to see Jing Yiyi, he might have allowed it.","But they didn't.","\"The town isn't big. Word spread quickly after we took Jing Yiyi, and then this couple came specifically. They're probably after the Jing family's status and money.\"","So, there was no need to worry about them taking Jing Yiyi away.","Lin Ruiqing breathed a sigh of relief, though a hint of sadness lingered. It was good that no one was trying to take Jing Yiyi from the Jing family, but what if little Jing Yiyi found out her parents were like this...","\"What about Yiyi?\"","Jing Zeyou's voice was calm. \"She won't find out.\" Not just anyone could claim ties to his sister.","Jing Zeqian seemed uneasy.","\"If she can't know, then we can't let those people come to North River!\"","Jing Beicheng's brow remained furrowed with concern. \"No, we have to meet them. Otherwise, this will always be a lingering issue.\" Only by meeting them could they control the situation; otherwise, they might pop up again at any time.","Lin Ruiqing agreed with Jing Beicheng. After all, their current conclusions were just speculation. They needed to meet the couple to understand their true intentions.","Jing Zeqian leaned back in his chair, frustrated. North River wasn't that big—what if they ran into each other?","What if Jing Yiyi wanted to leave with her biological parents? What if the couple treated Jing Yiyi poorly? What if they had ulterior motives that would hurt Jing Yiyi?","For a moment, the Jing family living room fell into silence.","...","\"Little Bao, we're going to see your sister today. Be good, okay?\"","The little boy impatiently shook off the woman's hand, his voice shrill. \"What sister?! We don't have any useless girls in our family!\"","The woman flinched, glancing at the indifferent man before hesitantly urging, \"Little Bao, today is different. You can't say things like that, understand?\"","She knew the term \"useless girl\" likely came from the boy's grandmother. It was one thing for him to say it at home, but what if the family who adopted the girl didn't like such talk?","She had heard that the family was quite protective of the girl.","The man, in a rare good mood, took his son's hand and chimed in.","\"That's right, Little Bao. Your sister isn't useless. She's here to bring us money, so behave yourself.\"","The boy, who usually ignored his mother, was somewhat intimidated by his father. He pouted and reluctantly said, \"Fine.\"","The family of three followed the address given by the welfare home, growing more and more astonished as they walked. They were from a small town, and even though they had worked in other provinces and seen tall buildings, they had never encountered such luxurious architecture.","But beneath their astonishment was an uncontrollable excitement.","The man looked around, his eyes wide. \"Looks like that girl really landed in a good place! This is so rich—could they be the richest family around?!\"","The woman was also excited, though more nervous. \"I don't know. Could we have the wrong address?\" She had imagined the family was wealthy, but not this wealthy.","The man's excitement grew, his eyes gleaming with greed. \"No way! They must be here! Hurry up!\" The woman quickly followed, pulling her son along.","But after just a few steps, the man was stopped by the security at the Jing family's gate.","\"Stop! What are you doing here?\"","The security team stood sternly in front of them, dressed in crisp uniforms.","The man took a half-step back, rubbing his hands together and hunching slightly as he smiled obsequiously.","\"Gentlemen, we're here to see someone.\"","The security captain, who had been briefed about the visitors, stepped forward, his expression still stern.","\"See someone?\"","He looked the man up and down, then glanced at the woman and child behind him.","\"There's probably no one here you're looking for.\"","The man anxiously tried to step forward, but the security team slightly raised their weapons, causing him to retreat again.","He forced a smile. \"Sir, I really am here to see someone. I’m here to see... to see...\"","He had been about to say he was here to see his daughter but remembered the welfare home's warning.","'The family who adopted Yiyi must be very powerful. You don’t have any proof, so if you’re wrong and they get angry...'","He changed his words. \"We're here to see Mr. Jing. The welfare home in Nanyue should have contacted him.\"","The security captain didn't respond, but his gaze alone was enough to make the couple feel humiliated.","The man felt a surge of anger, silently vowing to replace these arrogant guards once he reclaimed his daughter.","He glared at the woman behind him, who shrank back before mustering the courage to step forward.","\"Please, could you check? We really need to see Mr. Jing. This is the address he gave us.\"","The security captain seemed to believe her, his brow furrowing slightly in annoyance. He uttered two words.","\"Wait here.\"","He turned and walked to the communication station, his demeanor instantly sharpening.","The call connected, and his tone became respectful. \"Young Master, the people you were expecting have arrived.\"","\"Good. Let them wait a little longer.\"","\"Understood.\""]},{"number":270,"title":"Chapter 270: If Line: When the Jing Family Travels to Jing Yi's World 09","paragraphs":["During the noon break at the welfare home, after putting all the children to sleep, the elderly matron of the welfare home sat in the courtyard, gazing at the plane tree in front of her, lost in thought.","Her daughter, who had just finished handling the expansion matters of the welfare home, came over and saw her mother’s worried expression.","She knew what her mother was concerned about. By her calculations, it was about time for that couple to visit the Jing Family.","She sat down and comforted her, “Mom, don’t worry too much. With Mr. Jing’s family background and capabilities, dealing with that couple won’t be a problem.”","The elderly matron sighed, “I’m not worried about whether he can handle it. I’m worried about how it might affect Jing Yi.”","Jing Yi was more thoughtful and quieter than anyone else. It had been so hard for her to find a family that truly cared for her, and now that couple had to barge in like this.","She was afraid that the Jing Family might come to dislike Jing Yi after learning about her parents’ character, and she was also afraid that Jing Yi would be heartbroken if she found out about the couple’s identity.","The elderly matron’s daughter sighed as well, “True, those two might as well have written ‘we want money’ on their faces.” Even she could easily see through their intentions.","She had practically watched Jing Yi grow up. Surviving that harsh winter had already been a miracle, and now she had to deal with such troublesome parents.","“But Mr. Jing really likes Jing Yi. He won’t mind.”","When it came to Jing Yi’s adoption, aside from feeling reluctant, she was mostly happy. For one, the family that adopted Jing Yi was exceptionally wealthy, so Jing Yi would have a much better environment to grow up in.","Secondly, for the welfare home, it was indeed a substantial amount of sponsorship money.","The welfare home was only supported by her and her mother. Even with some financial aid from society, truth be told, these years had been really tough. She had even considered giving up at one point.","Running a welfare home was too difficult. How could her meager salary and her mother’s retirement pension possibly be enough?","That was when Jing Zeyou appeared.","The amount of money allocated to the welfare home was unusually high this time. She knew that Jing Yi had played a big part in it.","For this reason alone, she hoped that the couple wouldn’t cause any trouble for Jing Yi.","The elderly matron continued to gaze at the plane tree and sighed softly.","“Let’s hope so.”","......","“Jing Yi, are you sure you’re okay? Big Brother and the others are busy. We don’t have to go back so early.”","Jing Zejun held Jing Yi’s hand as they got out of the car. The two delicate little girls walked hand in hand toward the manor.","Jing Zeyou and the others seemed to have some important matters to attend to today, so they had Jing Zejun take Jing Yi to the amusement park. However, Jing Yi didn’t play for long before saying she wanted to go home.","Jing Zejun wasn’t really a child anymore, so she wasn’t particularly interested in those things either. She decided to take Jing Yi back early.","Jing Yi was in a good mood, her skipping steps full of joy. “It’s okay, Sister. I’ve already tried all those rides, and they’re not that fun anyway. I’d rather stay at home with Mom, Dad, and you.”","She had always heard her classmates talk about how fun the amusement park was, but it wasn’t all that great. She much preferred being at home with her family.","“Sister, let’s sneak back and surprise Mom and Dad, okay?”","Jing Zejun never refused Jing Yi’s ideas. She smiled gently and said, “Alright, let’s give them a surprise.”","......","After a while, the family of three, who had been left waiting outside for quite some time, were finally allowed to enter.","The woman wiped the sweat from her forehead and breathed a small sigh of relief. If they hadn’t been let in soon, she really wouldn’t have been able to handle the stares from the people passing by.","The man was no longer as cheerful as before. He gritted his teeth, his eyes filled with a mix of resentment and humiliation.","These rich people really look down on others! Just wait, I’ll make them pay dearly for this!","The little boy, who was being led by the woman, had no idea what his parents were thinking. Once they entered the manor, he was immediately captivated by the surrounding buildings.","“I want to play here! I want to play here!”","He broke free from his mother’s grip and threw a tantrum, refusing to move.","The security guard who had escorted them in stood still and said, “The main house is just ahead. Mr. Jing is waiting for you inside.” Before leaving, he glanced at the couple and added with a meaningful tone, “Also, don’t touch what you shouldn’t touch, and don’t take what you shouldn’t take.”","The man’s face stiffened. After the security guard walked away, he started cursing, “Who do they think they are? Once I get my daughter back, the first thing I’ll do is fire that guy! Just a lowly gatekeeper...”","He ranted for a while, but when he saw that the woman was still crouched on the ground trying to coax their son, his expression turned even more displeased.","“What the hell are you dawdling for?! Forget about him! With so many people around, he’s not going to get lost. Let’s focus on the important matter!”","Reluctantly, the woman left her son in the garden and followed the man into the beautiful villa.","The more the Jing Family’s wealth was on display, the faster the woman’s heart raced. Her excitement was almost uncontrollable, but she walked with careful steps.","......","“Sister, is that a child over there?”","In front of the Jing Family villa, a boy of about five or six years old was standing there, kicking at a sculpture.","The flowers and plants in front of him were torn up and scattered all over the ground.","Jing Zejun looked over, her little face filled with displeasure. “Where did that kid come from?”","This shouldn’t be happening. Security wouldn’t just let anyone in, and the housekeeper seemed to be nowhere in sight.","Jing Yi was also upset. Those were the flowers that Lin Ruiqing loved and often tended to herself. Now they were ruined by this little boy.","Jing Yi ran over and asked, “Did you destroy these flowers?”","The boy, who was used to being domineering, stopped kicking the sculpture and said arrogantly, “None of your business! This is my house, and I can do whatever I want!”","He snorted, turned around, and stepped into the flower bed, stomping and kicking at the plants. Jing Yi’s face turned red with anger, and she tried to pull him out.","Even though she was a year or two older than the boy, her frail body was no match for his chubby frame.","He pushed Jing Yi to the ground.","Jing Zejun’s expression changed instantly, and she rushed over.","“Jing Yi!”","She helped Jing Yi up and, seeing the red marks on her sister’s hand, grew angry. She grabbed the boy and said, “Who said you could touch her?!”","The boy’s face turned red as he struggled to break free. “Let go of me! I’m warning you, my sister is the daughter of this family. If you don’t let me go, I’ll have her beat you up!”","At such a young age, he was already spewing foul language and talking about violence.","Sister? Who was his sister?","Jing Zejun wrestled with him, but when Jing Yi saw that her sister was losing the upper hand, she quickly stepped in and pushed the boy to the ground.","She was breathing heavily but still spread her arms to protect Jing Zejun behind her.","“Don’t bully my sister! I’ll call my brother!”","Seeing that he couldn’t win against the two of them, the boy started wailing and thrashing on the ground.","“Waaah! Dad! Xiao Bao is being bullied! Xiao Bao is being bullied! Come and beat these two worthless girls!”","Jing Yi stared at him in confusion. “...Sister, he looks like that fat-headed fish I saw on TV last time.”","Jing Zejun held Jing Yi’s hand, her brow furrowed, her eyes filled with suspicion.","Who was this kid talking about when he mentioned his sister?","A bad feeling suddenly crept into Jing Zejun’s heart."]},{"number":271,"title":"Chapter 271: If Line: When the Jing Family Travels to Jing Yi's World 010","paragraphs":["The living room of the Jing family.","The couple stood before the Jing family, their hearts filled with unease. Even without much worldly experience, they could sense the extraordinary aura emanating from the family members.","The man took a step forward, a smile plastered on his face, his eyes darting around nervously.","\"Mr. Jing, I've heard so much about you! It's such an honor to finally meet you. You have no idea how much this trip means to me...\"","Good heavens! This family was even wealthier than what he had seen on TV! This was truly a jackpot!","Jing Zeqian sat impatiently on the sofa, his arms crossed, his expression clearly annoyed. \"Which Mr. Jing are you talking to?\"","The man paused, scanning the room before his gaze settled on Jing Beicheng, the eldest among them.","He must be the one who adopted that girl.","With a sycophantic grin, he said, \"Everyone says it, Mr. Jing, you are truly blessed. Your two sons are both handsome and accomplished. A successful man like you, with such a big heart...\"","\"Enough, Mr. Chen. Take a seat. Let's skip the small talk,\" Jing Beicheng interjected, his voice carrying an air of authority as he straightened up.","The man quickly complied, nodding eagerly. The woman behind him shrank back, her neck stiff, sneaking glances around. Seeing her husband sit, she hurriedly followed suit.","\"Mr. Chen, you're not from Nanyue, are you?\"","\"No, no, I just have relatives there. That's why I say it's fate that brought us together. I...\"","\"Which relative brought you back this time?\"","\"Huh? Oh, no! Although we work away from home, we still care about our elders, so we often come back to visit...\"","\"How did you confirm Yiyi's identity?\"","\"Well, it was all our carelessness. We came back to visit my aunt, and before we knew it, our child went missing. Thank goodness for Mr. Jing! That's why they say success follows people like you...\"","Jing Zeyou, sitting nearby, had his eyes closed, leaning back on the sofa, silent throughout the exchange.","As the man's answers were peppered with flattery, Jing Zeyou felt a growing irritation.","\"Don't you want to know about her?\" His clear voice carried a hint of coldness.","The man was taken aback, momentarily confused.","\"Who?\"","Jing Zeqian had long since had enough. He shot to his feet, his eyes blazing with anger.","\"Who?! You don't even know who you're here for?\"","Even the usually gentle Lin Ruiqing was furious. If they were just an ordinary adoptive family, given these two's attitude, who would dare take in Yiyi?","The man and woman looked flustered. The man hurriedly explained, \"Of course we do! She's our flesh and blood! But with a family like yours...\"","Jing Zeyou opened his eyes, his gaze piercing as it landed on the man, who gradually fell silent under the intensity.","Why did this young man, who looked no older than twenty, have such a commanding presence?","Seeing the man quiet down, Jing Zeyou spoke coldly, \"Two things. Once you leave this door, she has no connection to you...\"","How could that be? They had come precisely because they were the girl's biological parents. If they couldn't get any benefits, what was the point of coming?","\"Young master, do you doubt our identity? We can take a DNA test! The girl was found at the gate of the Nanyue orphanage, wasn't she? It was the middle of winter...\"","All the details his aunt had mentioned matched. They were definitely the girl's birth parents!","And now, they were still trying to use Jing Yiyi's identity to their advantage!","Jing Zeqian's eyes turned bloodshot as he ground out through clenched teeth, \"You... don't even think about it! Jing Yiyi will never have parents like you!\"","The woman turned pale, tugging at her husband's sleeve. The man, realizing he had been too hasty, wiped the sweat from his forehead, his eyes betraying his guilt.","Jing Zeyou didn't stop Jing Zeqian. Once the man quieted down, he continued, \"Second, after taking the money, you are never to set foot in North River again.\" His tone was emotionless.","The man and woman exchanged glances, their eyes lighting up with excitement.","Suppressing his glee, the man put on a facade of reluctance and said with a fake smile, \"We didn't come all this way for money. We just wanted...\"","Before he could finish, Jing Zeqian cut him off, \"Enough nonsense! Do you not want the money?!\"","The man quickly shut his mouth, offering a few ingratiating smiles.","Jing Zeqian closed his eyes in frustration, turning away, his fists clenched tightly.","The man didn't care about their attitudes. His goal was achieved, but he still wanted to know how much they were willing to offer.","Just as he was about to speak, the sound of crying came from outside. The woman's expression changed as she recognized her son's wails and rushed out.","...","In the garden, Jing Zejun seemed to have noticed something and was about to lead little Jing Yiyi away.","A thin woman suddenly dashed out, and Jing Zejun instinctively shielded Jing Yiyi behind her.","\"Xiao Bao! Xiao Bao! What's wrong? Are you hurt?\"","The woman rushed to the little boy, her eyes filled with worry.","The boy continued to cry, refusing to get up. \"Mom! Those two worthless girls hit me! Tell Dad to beat them up!\"","Only then did the woman notice the two girls standing nearby. She paused.","One of them must be her daughter, right?","Judging by the timeline, the girl should be around seven or eight years old. The one behind seemed younger, so it must be the one in front.","The woman's face lit up with joy as she helped her son up and turned to Jing Zejun, her voice soft and pleading.","\"You're Yiyi, right?\"","Jing Zejun's unease grew. She tightened her protective stance around little Jing Yiyi.","\"I don't know what you're talking about. Yiyi, let's go!\"","Little Jing Yiyi glanced at the woman, puzzled. Was this auntie calling her? But why was she talking to her sister?","Jing Yiyi didn't ask. She could sense Jing Zejun's tension and obediently prepared to leave with her.","From the villa, Jing Zeyou and the others rushed out.","Seeing Jing Yiyi and Jing Zejun outside, their expressions changed drastically.","Why were they back?!","The man also noticed the two girls. Ignoring his crying son, his eyes gleamed with greed and excitement.","He stepped toward Jing Zejun, who stood protectively in front.","\"You're Yiyi, right? You've grown so much. I am...\"","Jing Zeyou immediately interrupted him, \"Both of you, get inside now!\" His voice carried a rare trace of panic.","The man wasn't pleased. Compared to a one-time payout, building a relationship with his daughter was far more important! What could be better than having a daughter raised in a wealthy family to secure his future?","She was a living, breathing cash cow!","Before the man could act, Jing Zeyou seemed to sense his intentions and warned in a low voice, \"Mr. Chen, if you say one more word, I guarantee you'll never speak again.\"","\"You can tell I have the means to make that happen.\"","The man's pupils contracted in fear, his trembling fingers betraying his terror.","At the same time, the woman, having just calmed her son, made her move."]},{"number":272,"title":"Chapter 272: If Line: When the Jing Family Travels to Jing Yi's World 011","paragraphs":["The woman crouched in front of Jing Zejun, her eyes slightly red, her voice gentle.","\"You must be Yiyi, right? I can't believe you've grown so big.\"","She gazed at the beautiful Jing Zejun, her eyes carrying a hint of nostalgia.","Jing Zejun's expression remained stern, unmoved. She only wanted to take Little Jing Yi and leave this place.","\"I told you, you've got the wrong person!\"","Jing Zejun held Little Jing Yi's hand, ready to turn and leave, but her younger sister didn't follow.","Little Jing Yi's gaze shifted between the woman and the little boy who was still crying and making a fuss.","He continued to shout, \"I'll tell my sister to kick you all out! This is my home now! You two good-for-nothings!\"","The woman panicked, covering the boy's mouth, her eyes timidly darting toward Jing Zeyou's direction.","Jing Zejun forced a smile and tugged at Little Jing Yi's hand. \"Little sister, let's go home. The kitchen made your favorite beef stew today. Let's hurry.\"","Jing Zeqian rushed over and stood in front of Little Jing Yi, trying to pick her up.","\"Didn't we say we were going to the amusement park? Was it not fun without your second brother? Let me take you back for more fun, okay? You...\"","\"Second brother, are they here for me?\"","The woman's words sounded familiar, like something an elder would say to a long-lost younger relative. Little Jing Yi had heard similar words at the orphanage.","Jing Zeqian's steps faltered, and he forced a smile. \"No way! They were clearly talking to Zejun! They must have mistaken you for someone else! Don't mind them, second brother...\"","Little Jing Yi patted Jing Zeqian's shoulder gently. \"Second brother, put me down.\"","Jing Zeqian's eyes reddened at the corners. \"Be good, they got the wrong person!\" Little Jing Yi simply repeated, \"It's okay, second brother. I just want to ask.\"","Jing Zeqian stood frozen. If possible, he wished Little Jing Yi would never have to learn about that couple.","He glanced at Jing Zeyou, whose expression was also grim, but he nodded nonetheless.","Little Jing Yi patted Jing Zeqian's shoulder as he crouched down, her eyes curving into a smile. \"It's fine, I just want to ask a few questions.\"","Jing Zejun stepped forward, holding Little Jing Yi's hand, and accompanied her as they approached the woman.","By now, the woman realized her mistake. Her face flushed red, and her eyes filled with deep guilt and remorse.","\"Yiyi, I'm sorry! I didn't mean to. I just thought a seven- or eight-year-old would be...\"","Little Jing Yi smiled, unfazed. \"It's okay. Maybe the nutrition at the orphanage wasn't great. I am smaller than other kids my age, so it's possible to mistake me for someone else.\"","The woman was stunned, staring at the child in front of her, unsure of what to say.","Jing Zeyou and the others watched Little Jing Yi, who remained calm and even managed to smile, their hearts aching even more for her.","Little Jing Yi turned to the little boy, who seemed frightened by the tension, and asked the woman, \"Why did he say his sister would kick us out?\"","The woman's lips trembled, hesitating. \"He didn't mean it. He's just, just...\"","Little Jing Yi calmly looked at her, and when the woman stammered without finishing her sentence, Little Jing Yi completed it for her.","\"Just because he has a sister with some blood relation who was adopted by a wealthy family, so he thinks he's entitled to their money too.\"","Having lived in the orphanage for several years, Little Jing Yi had seen this kind of reunion drama play out countless times.","The woman bit her lower lip tightly, her face pale, her voice shaking. \"No! That's not what he meant!\" But Little Jing Yi's gaze only made her feel more ashamed.","She turned to the man, who, under Jing Zeyou's threatening glare, remained cowering in the corner, not daring to speak.","Little Jing Yi's expression was calm, but Jing Zejun could feel the grip on her hand tightening. She stepped closer, wanting to give her little sister some strength.","Little Jing Yi took a small breath. \"Let's not talk about that. Are you here to take me back?\"","In an instant, the hearts of the Jing family tightened. Jing Zeqian rushed forward, his face filled with anxiety.","\"Yiyi!\"","Little Jing Yi lifted her small face, smiling softly at Jing Zeqian. He forced a smile, his eyes brimming with heartache.","Reluctantly, he stayed behind Little Jing Yi, standing guard.","The woman hesitated, glancing at the man, who was shaking his head frantically.","They had come for money, not to take a child back.","Little Jing Yi also looked over and smiled. \"So, you're not here to take me back?\"","The woman seemed conflicted, lowering her head slightly, her hand tightly gripping the little boy's.","\"Yiyi, the Jing family can give you a better life, so...\"","\"Enough!\" Jing Zeyou interrupted her, stepping in front of Little Jing Yi and crouching down. His voice was gentle. \"Yiyi, they're not your parents. We haven't even done a DNA test. They're not. Please stop asking, okay? Be good.\"","Little Jing Yi's almond-shaped eyes, slightly red, looked at Jing Zeyou with determination.","\"Big brother, I'll just ask a few more questions, then we'll go back.\"","Jing Zeyou pursed his lips and stepped aside.","Little Jing Yi looked at the woman, her smile fading slightly. \"Whatever my big brother promised you, it doesn't count. You won't get anything from us.\"","At this, the man grew anxious. Ignoring Jing Zeyou's threat, he stepped forward, towering over Little Jing Yi.","\"Child, you might not know this, but we're your birth parents...\"","Little Jing Yi's gaze remained calm, unlike that of a typical seven- or eight-year-old.","\"Proof?\"","\"We can go to the hospital for a test!\"","\"Why should I? Based on just your words?\"","The man's frown deepened, his expression growing more displeased as he looked at Little Jing Yi.","\"What's wrong? Now that you've climbed to a higher branch, you don't want your birth parents anymore? You're so ungrateful...\"","The man was silenced by the glares from Jing Zeyou and his brothers, taking half a step back and swallowing the rest of his words.","Little Jing Yi repeated her question. \"So, are you taking me back? You're both alive, not dead or disabled. Why should someone else raise your child?\"","The man stole a glance at Jing Zeyou and muttered, \"How can you talk like that? Besides, we still have to take care of your brother...\"","Little Jing Yi ignored him, turning to the woman behind him.","\"I'll say it again. Even if we do a test, you'll only get me. Not a single penny. So, are you taking me back?\"","The woman's eyes grew redder, her voice trembling. \"Yiyi, your brother is still young...\"","\"One last question.\"","Little Jing Yi cut her off. She hadn't held much hope to begin with, and the woman's answer was expected.","\"Why couldn't you wait until the weather got warmer before abandoning the child?\"","This was something she had never understood since she became aware of her situation.","The man raised his head, his deliberately gentle expression nauseating. \"Child, you've misunderstood. It was an accident...\"","Little Jing Yi's gaze remained steady. \"I was asking her.\"","The man's pupils contracted, unnerved by the composure of a seven- or eight-year-old. But with the Jing family present, he held back his anger.","He muttered to himself, wondering if they had indeed mistaken the child. She didn't resemble him at all—in fact, she looked more like Jing Zeyou."]},{"number":273,"title":"Chapter 273: If Line: When the Jing Family Travels to Jing Yi's World 012","paragraphs":["The woman looked at Little Jing Yi with guilt in her eyes.","“It was a last resort back then. I had no money, the train was about to leave, and your grandparents couldn’t take care of you either...”","The woman’s words were incoherent, her voice trembling as if she were being interrogated.","“Alright, I don’t want to hear anymore. Big Brother, I’ve asked all I needed to.”","Little Jing Yi turned around, holding Jing Zejun’s hand as they prepared to enter the house, but suddenly she stopped.","“Big Brother.”","Jing Zeyou glanced at the two people across from them and crouched down in front of Little Jing Yi.","She whispered, “Big Brother, we can’t give them anything. That money is for me and my sister’s education.” Grandma had said that raising children and paying for their schooling required a lot of money.","Jing Zeyou smiled gently. Just moments ago, he had been firm, but now he seemed so childlike.","“Alright, that money is for your schooling. Go on.”","Only then did Little Jing Yi feel reassured, holding Jing Zejun’s hand as they ran toward Lin Ruiqing and the others.","The four of them went home, ignoring the commotion outside.","......","At night, Little Jing Yi stayed in the tent that Jing Zeqian had set up on the balcony of her room, gazing at the night view of the river.","A knock came at the door. “Yi Yi, can I come in?” It was Jing Zeyou outside.","The little one in the tent poked her head out, slipped on her shoes, and ran to open the door.","She looked up, her smile adorable. “Big Brother!”","Jing Zeyou smiled, holding her hand with one hand while carrying a dessert in the other.","“What are you up to?”","“Watching the scenery on the balcony.”","The balcony?","Jing Zeyou walked over and only then noticed the tent on Jing Yi’s balcony. The corners of his lips curled up. “Why did you set up a tent on the balcony? Did your second brother do this?”","Little Jing Yi looked at him with admiration. “How did Big Brother know? You’re amazing!”","Jing Zeyou’s eyes sparkled with amusement as he led her over.","Probably no one else in the family, aside from Jing Zeqian, would do something like that.","The two of them, one big and one small, nestled by the tent, quietly watching the night view of the river.","Little Jing Yi held the dessert in her small hands, occasionally glancing up at Jing Zeyou beside her.","“What is it? Do you have something to say to me?”","Little Jing Yi’s admiring gaze grew even more evident, and Jing Zeyou’s smile deepened.","His little sister was so cute when she was young.","“Big Brother, why did you adopt me?”","The Jing family treated her so well, as if she were truly one of their own. But earlier that day, she had seen something that made her wonder—even biological parents could treat their children like that, let alone someone without blood ties.","At the same time, Little Jing Yi was also worried. She had seen children in the orphanage who had been adopted and then sent back.","Little Jing Yi loved the Jing family and every member of it. If she couldn’t see them anymore, she would be heartbroken.","Jing Zeyou turned to look at the little girl. “I’ll only answer this question once, okay?”","“Wait!”","Little Jing Yi carefully placed the dessert on a small table nearby, sat up straight, and put on a serious expression.","“Big Brother, go ahead!”","Seeing this, Jing Zeyou’s eyes overflowed with tenderness.","He spoke softly, “Because our relationship isn’t about adoption. It’s about reunion.” Little Jing Yi didn’t quite understand and repeated, “Reunion?”","Jing Zeyou continued to gaze at the scenery outside, his mind filled with memories of the moments he had shared with Jing Yi.","‘Hello, Big Brother, I’m Jing Yi.’","‘Big Brother, do you want to sunbathe?’","‘Big Brother, you’re such a workaholic. Keep it up, my future depends on you.’","‘Big Brother, how did you know I didn’t want to become the sharpest sword of the Jing family?’","‘Big Brother, being your family must be such a happy thing.’","Jing Zeyou gradually snapped out of his reverie and looked at the expectant Little Jing Yi.","“You don’t know this, but we’ve known each other for a very, very long time. So long that we’ve become the closest of family. That’s why this is a reunion.”","After meeting Jing Yi, Jing Zeyou had come to understand that blood ties only represented one layer of a relationship. Only mutual care and affection could truly make someone family.","Little Jing Yi’s small brows furrowed. Had she known Big Brother and the others for a long time? She remembered their first meeting at the elementary school gate.","And before that, she had lived in the orphanage. She had never met Big Brother before.","Jing Zeyou reached out and gently ruffled Little Jing Yi’s hair. “These are things that happened before you went to the orphanage.”","“The Jing Yi I knew was an amazing girl. Her hobbies were cool, her personality was cool, and she was cool in every way.”","“She was a remarkable person. So many people admired her and liked her. There were even people who came to me asking for her autograph.”","“She was a strong-willed person. Despite her soft appearance, she had her own convictions. Once she set her mind on something, no one could change it.”","“She was a gentle soul. Even when she could have stayed out of trouble, she would step forward to shield others, which often led to her being hurt.”","Little Jing Yi really liked the girl Jing Zeyou was describing. She asked excitedly, “Is this the Jing Yi from Big Brother’s dreams?”","Jing Zeyou smiled warmly. “Yes.”","“So, Yi Yi, we are bound by fate. This kind of connection isn’t measured by blood. This is a reunion—a reunion between you, me, our parents, and everyone else.”","Little Jing Yi suddenly felt her eyes grow warm, and she buried her face in Jing Zeyou’s lap.","Her voice muffled, she said, “Big Brother, what if I can’t become that amazing Jing Yi from your dreams?”","Did this kind of fate truly belong to her?","Could it be that she had taken someone else’s place?","Jing Zeyou gently patted Little Jing Yi, as if to comfort her.","“Little Jing Yi doesn’t need to become anyone else. You just need to grow up happily. That kind of Jing Yi is the most amazing of all.”","Little Jing Yi remained lying there. “But the person Big Brother described is so incredible...”","Jing Zeyou chuckled. “Little Jing Yi is incredible too. You waited safely for Big Brother to find you, and now you’re growing up happily. Isn’t that amazing?”","Little Jing Yi, still lying there, secretly smiled. She loved those words. It felt as though they were always meant to be a family, even if their meeting had come a little later.","“Jing Yi Yi, open the door!”","Outside, Jing Zeqian’s voice rang out. Little Jing Yi got up and ran over to open the door.","Before he even entered, Jing Zeqian’s voice was already filling the room.","“Did you sneak in to play without waiting for me and Jun Jun? Jun Jun only took a little. You didn’t need to help her carry it. If you’re so thoughtful, why not help your second brother out a bit? Oh, never mind. With your tiny arms and legs, what could you even carry? I’ll just do it myself. By the way, I couldn’t find Big Brother. Who knows where he’s gone off to work again...”","Jing Zeqian rambled on as he carried snacks toward the balcony, only to find Jing Zeyou standing there with an amused expression.","“Brother, so you’re here! Quick, quick, take these things off me!”","Jing Zeyou looked at him, laden with bags and boxes, and though he was a bit exasperated, he still kindly took the items from Jing Zeqian.","“Why did you bring so much stuff?”","“Isn’t it obvious? I wanted to make Jing Yi Yi’s tent even cozier!”","“Jing Yi Yi, Jun Jun, what are you two doing? Come and help!”","Under the night sky, the bustling city had quieted down. The sounds of laughter drifted from the balcony of a manor, and the leaves rustled in the wind, as if responding to the joy within."]},{"number":274,"title":"Chapter 274: If Line: When the Jing Family Travels to Jing Yi's World 013","paragraphs":["Life at the Jing household turned out to be easier to adapt to than Little Jing Yi had imagined.","Her parents were wonderful, her older brother was wonderful, and her older sister was wonderful too. It felt as though they were always meant to be a family.","The only slight trouble was that they were too good to her.","Lin Ruiqing held Little Jing Yi in her arms and gently asked, \"Yi Yi, how about sleeping with Mom tonight?\"","Little Jing Yi nestled obediently in Lin Ruiqing's embrace, her expression slightly conflicted. \"Mom, I promised Sister I'd sleep with her today.\"","Lin Ruiqing quickly came up with a solution. \"That's no problem. Both of you can sleep with me.\"","What could be better than two sweet and soft daughters? The middle-aged man could just roll to the side.","Jing Beicheng, the middle-aged man who had just managed to feel young again: Although... it had already been a week since he last slept in the master bedroom...","The matter of who would attend the parent-teacher meeting also troubled Little Jing Yi.","She rested her chin on her hands, watching as the family held a meeting to decide who would go to her parent-teacher meeting.","Lin Ruiqing was the first to speak. \"This is Yi Yi's first parent-teacher meeting. I must go!\" Wasn't it only natural for a mother to attend her child's meeting?","Jing Beicheng set down his teacup and cleared his throat. \"Actually, I could go too.\" After all, it was their youngest daughter's first meeting. Shouldn't the father attend to show how much they cared?","Jing Zeyou remained calm and composed. \"I should go. After all, I'm the one tutoring Yi Yi. I know her situation best.\" With their parents so busy, it made sense for the eldest brother to handle such matters.","Jing Zeqian, not wanting to be outdone, slammed the table and stood up. \"Of course, it should be me! It has to be me!\" There was no particular reason, but he *had* to go!","The Jing family: ...","At first, Little Jing Yi was a bit worried. She glanced in Jing Zejun's direction. They were in the same class, so her parent-teacher meeting was also Jing Zejun's.","That was, until she saw Jing Zejun joining the discussion.","Jing Zejun stood up, feeling her small stature might not be enough to make her voice heard. She climbed onto a chair.","\"I should go. Mom, Dad, and my brothers all have their own things to do. Since Yi Yi and I are in the same class, it’s more convenient for me.\"","She wasn’t really a child anymore, so why would she care about a parent-teacher meeting?","Compared to such matters, Jing Zejun cared more about Jing Yi. She had heard from Jing Zeyou about what had happened to Little Jing Yi at school before. She wished she could grow up faster to better protect her.","The Jing family: What happened to our gentle and obedient Jun Jun?","Jing Zeqian had a look of disbelief. \"Jun Jun, you still need someone to attend *your* parent-teacher meeting...\" A seven- or eight-year-old shouldn’t be running for this position, right?","Jing Zejun, unwilling to back down, was about to argue further when Little Jing Yi chimed in, thinking it was a great idea.","Her eyes sparkled, and the dimples on her cheeks deepened as she smiled. \"That sounds good! Why don’t Sister and I switch and attend each other's parent-teacher meetings?\" She had never done something like this before.","The idea was, of course, unanimously rejected. They couldn’t let *none* of them go, could they?","In the end, it was decided that Lin Ruiqing and Jing Beicheng would attend together, while the two brothers could accompany them and listen from outside the classroom.","On the day of the parent-teacher meeting, Little Jing Yi was visibly happy. She held Jing Zejun's hand and skipped into the classroom.","The school Jing Yi and Jing Zejun attended was a well-known international school in North River, catering to students from elementary to high school.","Apart from its excellent faculty, it was also a school that many prominent families in North River vied to send their children to.","Though Little Jing Yi's classmates were just elementary school students, most of them were sharp and knew who not to mess with.","For example, the newly transferred Jing Yi.","They had learned from their parents that Jing Yi was the youngest daughter of the Jing family. Whether she was biological or adopted didn’t matter—what mattered was that she wasn’t someone to provoke.","Not to mention the outwardly gentle but fiercely protective Jing Zejun, who had already shielded her completely. Then there was Jing Zeqian, the heartthrob and school bully of the high school division, who visited their class at least twice a day just to make sure no one was bullying his little sisters.","Jing Zeqian carried two backpacks, one in each hand, as usual, escorting his sisters to their classroom.","Before leaving, he reminded them, \"Big Brother will come to your parent-teacher meeting later. Wait for me, okay?\"","Jing Zejun couldn’t help but shudder at the cheesiness. Her second brother was finally getting his fill of being an overprotective older brother.","Jing Yi obediently replied, \"Okay!\" Jing Zeqian beamed, patting both their heads before leaving with a satisfied expression.","Jing Zejun sighed, ignoring Jing Zeqian's smugness, and led Little Jing Yi to her seat.","A few classmates gathered around. Over time, Little Jing Yi had noticed their friendliness, though it seemed to come with some ulterior motives.","But she didn’t mind. As long as they didn’t bully her like her previous classmates had, Little Jing Yi was easy to please.","\"Yi Yi, is your brother coming to your parent-teacher meeting this afternoon?\"","Jing Zejun glanced at the group of girls surrounding them, silently noting how her second brother's looks seemed to attract endless attention.","It was no wonder that even as the boss of 'Startrack,' he garnered more attention than most of the artists.","Little Jing Yi, following her sister's lead, took out her textbooks and stationery, smiling sweetly. \"No, it’s Mom and Dad who are coming.\"","The kids looked puzzled. \"But your brother just said...\" Little Jing Yi blinked her innocent eyes. \"Oh, Mom said Brother can only listen from outside. But we have to save face for him, or he’ll cry.\"","The kids were stunned. The big brother from the high school division... cried?","Jing Zejun couldn’t hold back her laughter, turning her head to hide her smile.","It wouldn’t be long before rumors spread through the school that Jing Zeqian from the high school division was a crybaby.","When the bell rang, Jing Zeqian slung his backpack over his shoulder and dashed out of the classroom. His classmates were used to it—it was obvious he was off to pick up his sisters.","By the time Jing Zeqian arrived, the parent-teacher meeting had already started, and Jing Zeyou was standing at the door, listening intently.","Catching his breath, Jing Zeqian noticed a group of kids whispering not far away, their eyes darting in his direction.","He frowned. Were they talking about Jing Yi?","The memory of Little Jing Yi being bullied was still fresh in Jing Zeqian's mind. He made sure to visit her class punctually every day to ensure she wasn’t being mistreated.","Sometimes, the harm caused by words could be just as damaging as physical harm."]},{"number":275,"title":"Chapter 275: If Line: When the Jing Family Travels to Jing Yi's World 014","paragraphs":["Jing Zeqian was worried that little Jing Yi might get hurt again in places he couldn't see.","He quickly walked over to the group of elementary school students and grabbed one of them, demanding, \"What are you whispering about?\"","The child, who was caught, looked scared and hurriedly said it was nothing.","Seeing this, Jing Zeyou walked over, signaling Jing Zeqian to calm down. He seemed to be overreacting.","Compared to the fierce-looking Jing Zeqian, Jing Zeyou was much gentler. He asked, \"I'm Jing Yi's older brother. Would you mind telling me what you were just talking about?\"","The child, who had been released, stood timidly to the side, sneaking a glance at Jing Zeyou.","Feeling slightly less intimidated, the child stammered, \"...We were talking about Jing Yi's little brother.\"","Earlier that morning, the whole class had been gossiping about how Jing Yi's brother cried a lot and how Jing Yi always made sure not to upset him.","But they also knew Jing Zeqian, who was practically their idol—a cool and impressive high school senior!","Hearing that their idol was a crybaby, the kids couldn't accept it. Coincidentally, Jing Zeqian showed up, and they couldn't help but argue about it.","Little did they know, they’d been caught by the person they were talking about.","The child's voice was soft, but Jing Zeyou could still make out that they were discussing Jing Zeqian.","He looked up at Jing Zeqian, who seemed just as confused. Clearly, Jing Zeqian hadn't expected to be the topic of conversation.","Jing Zeyou lowered his head and asked, \"What's wrong with him?\" The child grew even more nervous, glancing around as if trying to figure out the best escape route.","\"They said... they said Jing Yi's brother is a crybaby!\" With that, the child bolted, afraid of being chased.","Jing Zeqian: Huh???? A crybaby? What the heck?!","Despite his confusion, the kid was already long gone, and there was no way to drag him back for an explanation.","Jing Zeqian crossed his arms and stood outside the classroom again.","He couldn't wrap his head around it and muttered angrily, \"It must be Jing Yi. That little rascal must have told her classmates something about me!\"","He, the school heartthrob and tough guy, being labeled as a 'crybaby'? How was he supposed to maintain his reputation at school? How could he continue to be the boss of those little brats?!","The thought of his classmates spreading rumors about him being a crybaby the next day made Jing Zeqian furious.","Jing Zeyou, on the other hand, had a hint of amusement in his eyes. As long as they weren't talking about Jing Yi, he was fine. He decided to focus on listening to the teacher during the parent-teacher meeting.","...","Meanwhile, little Jing Yi and Jing Zejun came running over, hand in hand.","They had been peeking through the window at Lin Ruiqing and Jing Beicheng attending the parent-teacher meeting. To be precise, Jing Yi was the one watching, while Jing Zejun couldn't refuse her request and joined her at the windowsill for a while.","As a result, Lin Ruiqing and Jing Beicheng kept glancing toward the window during the meeting.","There were two adorable little girls out there.","When they noticed the adults looking their way, Jing Yi excitedly waved at them, melting quite a few hearts.","Other parents couldn't help but think to themselves, no wonder the Jing family had made such a big deal about welcoming her back. It was their way of telling everyone in Jiangbei not to mess with their little princess.","After watching for a while, Jing Yi finally decided to leave the windowsill and go find her brothers.","As they approached, they noticed Jing Zeqian looking upset.","Jing Yi walked over, tugged at Jing Zeqian's sleeve, and looked up at him with concern. \"Second Brother, are you unhappy? Who made you angry?\"","Jing Zeqian glanced at her.","Who else could it be but Jing Yi? Who else had the power to upset him like this?","He crouched down, gently pinched Jing Yi's cheek, and asked sternly, \"Tell me, did you say something to your classmates?\"","Jing Yi tilted her head in confusion. She talked to her classmates about so many things—which one was he referring to?","Jing Zeqian sighed, exasperated, and clarified, \"...Did you say anything about me crying or something like that?\"","Jing Zejun, standing nearby, couldn't help but smile. It seemed the news had spread quickly.","Jing Yi suddenly understood and explained, \"I didn't say you cry a lot. I just told them to give you face in public, or else you might cry.\"","Jing Zeqian: ...Wow, thanks for that.","Jing Yi was quick to pick up on his mood. Seeing that Jing Zeqian wasn't happy, she immediately came up with a solution.","\"Second Brother, don't worry. I'll explain to my classmates tomorrow that you're not a crybaby—it's just that the wind is too strong!\"","Even Jing Zeyou couldn't hold back his laughter at this point.","Jing Zeqian, annoyed, pinched Jing Yi's cheek again. \"Thanks a lot!\" Jing Yi, thinking she had helped, cheerfully replied, \"You're welcome!\"","Jing Zeqian: ...What could he do? He couldn't bring himself to scold her, so he just had to endure it!","At that moment, the parent-teacher meeting ended, and Lin Ruiqing and Jing Beicheng walked out.","\"What are you all talking about?\"","Jing Yi eagerly took on the task of explaining, buzzing around Lin Ruiqing like a little bee.","Even Jing Beicheng was amused, and Lin Ruiqing couldn't stop laughing.","Jing Zeqian: Great, once again, I'm the only one suffering!","He quickly picked up the chattering Jing Yi and started walking ahead.","\"Just stop talking, will you?\"","\"Why, Second Brother? Mom and Dad are laughing so happily!\"","\"...Of course they are!\"","\"Then why can't I talk? Everyone should be happy.\"","\"...They can be happy, but please don't use my misery as a punchline, thank you.\"","\"I didn't! Brother, don't worry. I'll definitely explain everything to my classmates tomorrow!\"","\"...I'm afraid the more you explain, the more my reputation as a crybaby will grow!\"","\"Don't worry, Brother! I'll tell them it's because of the strong wind!\"","\"...I can't hear you! The wind's too loud!\"","The handsome teenager carried the little girl as they bickered.","Behind them, the couple held hands with another little girl, while the tall young man stood protectively by their side. They all laughed, their voices clear and joyful.","The sun was setting, casting a warm glow over them.","They were heading home."]}]);
